ex:Ev2_Page_Ch09 a backlog:TestEvidence ; rdfs:label "Chapter check for Page Ch09"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:attestsCriterion ex:AC_Chapter, ex:AC2_Admission ;
    backlog:evidenceVerified true ; backlog:hasTestId "Page/Ch09" ; backlog:hasTestSpec "08-tooling/sen0401_lineage_chapter_check_v1_1_0.py" ;
    backlog:hasVerificationMethod "python3 -B 08-tooling/sen0401_lineage_chapter_check_v1_1_0.py Page/Ch09 > /tmp/claude-0/s/bl_p9/$(echo Page/Ch09 | tr / _).log 2>&1 exited 0 Disclosed by the research run, kept with this evidence: Agent-reported disclosures for the chapter 9 page (from the course coordinator's relay of the builder's report, not re-verified here). The chapter check ran the newest page test, 9.35.0, and passed; the builder reports that 9.34.0 also passes completely (370 passed, 0 failed, longest task 172 ms), so this page does not depend on the 9.35.0 relaxations. Template 9.46.0. 67 of 69 examples run in the browser; 2 (CarveOutRule and FeeFilterMessage) are Recorded because the research package's example text is not valid Python, a research defect to be fixed by a new research version, reported only. One agent name was shortened from 43 characters to 'Lock time defense agent'. The question bank was generated: 96 Remember-level items. The test key was used, which proves page logic only. OPEN LICENCE QUESTIONS: the wheel embeds three third-party texts of unclear redistribution (Carlsten et al. 2016, Moeser and Boehme 2015, the Corallo list post of 2018-12) and mempool.space data with no stated licence. The page is 3.97 MB and its main-thread time is 172 ms, close to the 200 ms limit. (the page test ran against a copy of the page carrying a TEST release key: it proves the page logic, not the instructor's real key)" ;
    backlog:verifiedByTool "backlog_evidence_bridge_v1_1_0 with the course repository as workspace" ;
    backlog:verifiedAt "2026-10-15T11:59:58"^^xsd:dateTime .
