ex:Gap_OutScope_Lineage2 a backlog:PartialScopeDeclaration ;
    rdfs:label "Out-scoping of the work of the second lineage that is not finished"@en ;
    backlog:declaresGapFor ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner ;
    backlog:outScopes ex:TK_Deck_Ch01_CheckFix, ex:TK_Deck_Ch02_CheckFix, ex:TK_Deck_Ch03_CheckFix, ex:TK_Deck_Ch04_CheckFix, ex:TK_Deck_Ch14_StaleFixtures, ex:TK_Licence_BOLT_Ch09, ex:TK_Licence_Mempool_Ch09, ex:TK_Licence_Texts_Ch09, ex:TK_Page_Ch13_Build, ex:TK_Page_Ch13_Verify, ex:TK_Research_Ch02_Stage3F, ex:TK_Research_Ch03_Stage3F, ex:TK_Research_Ch04_Stage3F, ex:TK_Research_Ch08_Stage4, ex:TK_Research_Ch09_Stage4, ex:TK_Research_Ch10_Stage4, ex:TK_Research_Ch11_Stage4, ex:TK_Research_Ch12_Stage4, ex:TK_Research_Ch13_Stage4, ex:TK_Research_Ch14_Stage4 ;
    backlog:describesUncoveredScope "Not Done in this register at the time of this declaration and created during the second lineage: 20 tasks (the deck-check fixes of chapters 1 to 4, the stale-fixture work of the deck of chapter 14, the three licence questions of page 9, the stage-4 courseware artefacts of chapters 8 to 14, the Stage3.F failures of the research of chapters 2 to 4, and the build and verify tasks of the page of chapter 13, held open on purpose with the page of chapter 6: their load-time budget and test-design ruling are owner decisions). The open stories, epics and initiative of the first lineage (the pages of chapters 6 and 13, three epics, one initiative) belong to the first lineage, were out-scoped by its own declaration and stay carried by the Backlog output of the second lineage. Two link passes (decks and pages of chapters 1 to 14) were done after their stories were Done; ruling G125 says a link pass is a story of its own, so they are not added to this lineage, whose Backlog stage is closed and digest-verified. All of this leaves the second lineage unchanged and unfinished so that it closes with no unfinished work inside it; the successor lineage under the same mission takes the open work in and admits the two link passes as finished work with their real dates from git. The route is the owner decision of 2026-10-18 for the route \"out-scope, close, succeed\" of ruling G125 (G105): the owner confirms it by accepting this record." .

ex:Lineage3 a backlog:Lineage ;
    rdfs:label "Third lineage run for the SEN0401 decks: the link passes done after the second lineage planned its stories, and the work still open"@en ;
    backlog:lineageForMission ex:Mission ; backlog:lineageOrdinal 3 ; backlog:lineageArchived false ;
    backlog:hasLineageStatus backlog:LS_Scoped ;
    backlog:adoptsObligationSet backlog:OS_SDLC_v2 ; backlog:adoptionRecordedAtOpen true .

ex:Succession_Lineage2_3 a backlog:LineageSuccession ;
    rdfs:label "Succession that takes in the open work of the second lineage and the two link passes"@en ;
    backlog:succeedsLineage ex:Lineage2 ; backlog:successorLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:resolvesGap ex:Gap_OutScope_Lineage2 ;
    backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner ;
    backlog:successionRationale "After the Backlog stage of the second lineage was closed and digest-verified, the decks and pages of chapters 1 to 14 were rebuilt so that every link names its resource and goes straight to it. That work has its own criterion, so it is two stories (ruling G125); a story the closed Backlog stage did not admit moves its digest, so it cannot be added to the second lineage, and a task cannot carry it. The second lineage was therefore left unchanged: its unfinished work was out-scoped in the previous event, it closes complete on what it finished, and a successor under the same mission opens with the Scope of admitting the two link passes as finished work (real dates from git, evidence run through the evidence bridge) and of carrying the open follow-up work. The Mission is continued unchanged; its re-affirmation is the owner's act (G14). Cost of waiting: the register cannot state the link passes or start the follow-up of the open parts without breaking the digest; cost of acting: one succession and five stage commits; enforcement value forgone: none, the chains of the first two lineages stay untouched." .

ex:Out3_Mission a backlog:StageOutput ;
    rdfs:label "Closure of the Mission stage of the third lineage"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:outputOfStage backlog:Stage_Mission ;
    backlog:hasStateDigest "0d854051ea52ba05ebfa85367b4701e4214ec57fd2345b6c7567cbdde32d9595" ;
    backlog:closedAtCommit "9c616bd" .

ex:Area3_LinkPass a backlog:ScopeArea ;
    rdfs:label "The link passes over the decks and pages of chapters 1 to 14 admitted into the register"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:areaLocation "07-lineage (this register); the rebuilt files are in 03-materials and the link registers in 08-tooling, chapters 1 to 14" ;
    backlog:areaMeasure "2 stories (a deck link pass and a page link pass), each recorded Done with its real dates from git and evidence verified by the evidence bridge" ;
    backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Work .
ex:Del3_DeckLinkPass a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ;
    rdfs:label "The deck link pass recorded Done"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:derivesFromMissionClause "Every SEN0401 lecture teaches what the third edition of Mastering Bitcoin teaches"^^xsd:string ;
    backlog:hasDeliverableText "The decks of chapters 1 to 14 rebuilt so that every READ card and resources link names its resource and goes straight to it, each deck with a link register, recorded Done with its real dates from git and evidence that was verified against the course repository; the decks of chapters 1 to 4 fail the lineage deck check and are admitted failing, with the reasons." ;
    backlog:deliverableForArea ex:Area3_LinkPass ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Work ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_Functional .
ex:Del3_PageLinkPass a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ;
    rdfs:label "The page link pass recorded Done"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:derivesFromMissionClause "Every SEN0401 lecture teaches what the third edition of Mastering Bitcoin teaches"^^xsd:string ;
    backlog:hasDeliverableText "The interactive pages of chapters 1 to 14 rebuilt with the deck link labels, recorded Done with their real dates from git and evidence that was verified against the course repository; the page of chapter 13 fails its one check and is admitted failing, and the page tests ran with a test release key." ;
    backlog:deliverableForArea ex:Area3_LinkPass ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Work ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_Functional .
ex:Del3_OpenWorkCarried a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ;
    rdfs:label "The open work of the second lineage carried"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:derivesFromMissionClause "Every SEN0401 lecture teaches what the third edition of Mastering Bitcoin teaches"^^xsd:string ;
    backlog:hasDeliverableText "The 20 open tasks of the second lineage are admitted open, each with an executor, to be finished or ruled on; the page of chapter 6, the page of chapter 13, the three epics and the initiative that the first succession carried stay as they are." ;
    backlog:deliverableForArea ex:Area3_LinkPass ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Work ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_Functional .
ex:Excl3_NoRebuild a backlog:ScopeExclusion ;
    rdfs:label "The admission rebuilds nothing and decides nothing for the owner"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:excludesConcern "Any change to the decks or pages of chapters 1 to 14 made in order to admit them: they enter this register exactly as they stand in the course repository, and a deck or page that fails its check is admitted failing. Also the owner decisions the open items wait for (the licence questions, the load-time budget of the page of chapter 6, the test-design ruling of the page of chapter 13)." ;
    backlog:hasExclusionRationale "The link passes were done before their stories existed. The admission records them; it does not redo them, and a record that changed its subject would not be evidence of it. The rulings belong to the owner." ;
    backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Work .

ex:Scope3 a backlog:ScopeStatement ;
    rdfs:label "Admit the deck link pass and the page link pass as finished; carry the open work"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:scopeForMission ex:Mission ;
    backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_OwnerStated ; backlog:scopeCompletionState backlog:Proposed ;
    backlog:hasScopeStatementText "IN: (1) the admission of the deck link pass and the page link pass over chapters 1 to 14 of Mastering Bitcoin's 3rd edition, done after the stories of those decks and pages were Done and recorded as finished with their real dates from git and evidence run through the evidence bridge - a deck or page that fails its check is admitted failing and named, not Done; (2) the open work of the second lineage, carried in unchanged and with an executor: 20 tasks. OUT: rebuilding any deck or page in order to admit it; the owner's decisions (the licence questions, the page of chapter 6 and the page of chapter 13). Nothing else of the first two lineages is open." ;
    backlog:coversArea ex:Area3_LinkPass, ex:Area_Deck, ex:Area_Research, ex:Area_Page ;
    backlog:hasScopeExclusion ex:Excl3_NoRebuild, ex:Excl_OldStructure ;
    backlog:producedByStage ex:Out3_Scope ;
    backlog:requiresDeliverable ex:Del3_DeckLinkPass, ex:Del3_PageLinkPass, ex:Del3_OpenWorkCarried .

