    backlog:hasAuditNote "The decks of chapters 1 to 4 are admitted but FAIL the lineage deck check: deck_check_v1_0_0.py is missing in the deck folder of chapters 1 and 2, the stale fixtures of chapter 2 are not refused, the notes of chapters 1 to 4 carry SAY/ASK/STORY labels, and the old deck_check hits a NameError and merkle_root refusals on chapters 3 and 4 (it also failed on the old decks); their evidence here is the hash of the deck and its link register only. The decks of chapters 5 to 14 pass the check through the evidence bridge. Agent-reported, not verified from here: 403 or a bot challenge for the CNBC and CoinGecko links (chapter 1), the NYT and learnmeabitcoin HD-wallets links (chapter 5), the learnmeabitcoin Transaction link (chapter 6) and the Schnorr 1991 article (chapter 8), so those links were not verifiable by the builders; archive.org copies were used for hashcash, b-money, the bitcoinfoundation 2014 post and the Spilman reply, and raw.githubusercontent.com for GitHub files; Wikipedia stays for the Mt. Gox card (chapter 13) and the Lightning Network, Trezor and Casascius wiki cards (chapter 14); the agent that rebuilt chapters 8 to 14 edited the committed sen0401_links_v1_0_0.py (the Hashcash entry) after its commit, which breaks the no-edit rule; corrected on the way: the chapter 2 slide 12 linked bitcointalk topic 141 (wrong) and now links topic 183, and the chapter 3 slide 6 date changed from 9 January to 8 January 2009 after Satoshi's post header (Thu Jan 8 14:27:40 EST 2009), \"Six days\" became \"Five days\"; the older chapter 3 pages and the materials register sen0401_materials_v1_4_* still say 9 January (open). Dates: first and last git commit of the listed rebuild commits (deck rebuilds); the commits are 63f135e, 6df5c90, 895cf99, 3d5e489, 2e5c3bd, 7bef4cf, 1093656, 1be22b9, 0f432f8, b4369a8, d9de650, 74f559b, c918ccc, 09c008c." .
