ex:TK_Licence_Texts_Ch09 backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-18T22:50:00"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:startedAtIsEstimate true ; backlog:startEstimateBasis "Not witnessed: the work and its files first appear in one commit (065b1a7, 2026-10-19T02:22:10 UTC). Estimated as the latest owner message of the day before the work, the confirmation of 2026-10-19 01:50 Istanbul (2026-10-18T22:50:00 UTC); the owner's question that started the work is dated 2026-10-19 and its time was not relayed." ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-19T02:22:10"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:lastAuditedAt "2026-10-19T03:42:56"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasExecutionModality backlog:Mode_Hybrid ; backlog:hasAcceptanceCriterion ex:AC_Chapter ; backlog:hasEvidence ex:Ev3PG_Licence_Texts_Ch09, ex:Ev3PG_Page_Ch09, ex:Ev3PG_Prov_Ch09 ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Done, recorded 2026-10-19: the three third-party texts without a clear licence (Carlsten et al. 2016, Moeser and Boehme 2015, Corallo 2018) are left out of the page's wheel, under the standing rule that no text without a clear licence is shipped; the five examples that read them are shown as Recorded, not run. The evidence bridge ran the physical licence check (it opens the page's embedded wheel and lists its files) and verified the SHA-256 of the page sen0401_ch09_page_v9_68_0.html (commit 065b1a7) and of the provenance file. Owner-directed: \"Can we collect our own statistics from the network or alternative resources?\" (2026-10-19; the time was not relayed)." .
ex:ST_Page_Ch09 backlog:hasEvidence ex:Ev3PG_Check_Ch09, ex:Ev3PG_Page_Ch09 ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Correction recorded 2026-10-19 (G125 option 1, new evidence on the same Done story): the page was rebuilt as sen0401_ch09_page_v9_68_0.html (commit 065b1a7) to carry the course's own census and no text without a clear licence. The chapter check Page/Ch09 was run again through the evidence bridge on the rebuilt page (a TEST release key: it proves the page's logic, not the real instructor key) and the page is cited by SHA-256. The earlier evidence of the replaced page stays as the dated record. Owner-directed: \"Can we collect our own statistics from the network or alternative resources?\" (2026-10-19)." .
ex:ST_Page_Ch06 backlog:hasAuditNote "Owner-directed work, recorded 2026-10-19: \"Keep the same standards with all other pages.\" (2026-10-19) - the same standards as all other pages, no relaxation. Page 6 is a lighter page on the new template (page 9.67.0, commit 44642d3): same content as 9.63.0, tests 9.34.0 and 9.35.0 374 pass 0 fail, five runs each, load-task median 95-129 ms against 169-248 ms before (agent-reported)." .
ex:ST_Page_Ch13 backlog:hasAuditNote "Owner-directed work, recorded 2026-10-19: \"Keep the same standards with all other pages.\" (2026-10-19) - the same standards as all other pages, no relaxation. Page 13 is page 9.69.0 (commit 5533071) built on research 13 v1_0_2 and deck 13 v1.2.0: tests 9.34.0 and 9.35.0 368 pass 0 fail; 14 varied questions drawn, 21 examples can vary; the question bank covers 84 of 84 concepts; 51 examples run, 11 Recorded (agent-reported). The load-time budget failed once on the first run and passed on the rerun with an 88 ms median: disclosed." .
ex:ST_Deck_Ch01 backlog:hasAuditNote "Agent-reported weak spots of the deck, recorded 2026-10-19 from the builder's review file 08-tooling/ch01-deck/REVIEW_v2_11_0.md (not re-verified here beyond the nine checks). Not done, in the builder's words: The PayPal Form S-1 of 2001 (sec.gov, 403) has no reachable copy: no mirror other than web.archive.org, which is blocked here. The `genesis_hexdump.png` licence (CC BY 4.0, the course's own licence under Yusuf Altunel) is the course's declaration, not a third party's; the owner may want to confirm it. The StoneMoney date is the release date of the free ebook (2024-01-30), the only day-precise date of that story; the visit (1903) is in the subtitle. Links replaced or blocked: sec.gov (PayPal S-1), cnbc.com, coingecko.com and web.archive.org answer 403 or no connection here. Replaced by reachable pages of the same resource or event: PayPal story -> encyclopedia article on PayPal; Ukraine story and card -> CNBC's own article of 2022-03-03 as republished at nbclosangeles.com (the first CNBC article is not republished there; this one is the same reporter's report of the donations); CoinGecko price page -> CoinGecko's own data feed (api.coingecko.com); Hashcash and b-money -> the Satoshi Nakamoto Institute's copies (cdn.nakamotoinstitute.org); the YouTube watch link -> its embed URL (oEmbed title read: \"But how does bitcoin actually work?\", 3Blue1Brown). Labels are ke Pictures: David Chaum 2018 (Harry Murphy / Web Summit, CC BY 2.0), Mt. Gox logo (author not recorded on Commons, public domain text logo), Hal Finney 1972 (Daily News-Post, public domain), Papa John's plaque (Sanjev Rajaram, CC0), Fedorov (U.S. Embassy Kyiv, public domain; a 720 px copy, because the deck's case card already uses the original and a deck may not carry one file twice). The other stories keep their pictures (rai stone, Cleveland stater, PayPal logo, genesis hex dump) with new short credits. The one question left for the owner: the credit of genesis_hexdump.png, the course's own CC BY 4.0 under Yusuf Altunel, which is the course's declaration and not a third party's. Also: the coingecko API link answers 429 or 403 intermittently, so the links check may fail on a live host once and pass on the next run." .
ex:ST_Deck_Ch02 backlog:hasAuditNote "Agent-reported weak spots of the deck, recorded 2026-10-19 from the builder's review file 08-tooling/ch02-deck/REVIEW_v2_3_0.md (not re-verified here beyond the nine checks). Not done, in the builder's words: Nothing fails. The bust stands for the author of the white paper (whose face is unknown) and the Bitcoin logo for the overflow: neither shows the event. Links replaced or blocked: none reported. Pictures: bust of Satoshi Nakamoto, Budapest (Fekist, CC BY-SA 4.0, copy of the chapter 7 asset); Gavin Andresen at Web Summit 2014 (Stephen McCarthy, CC BY 2.0); the Bitcoin logo (Grayliptrot, public domain) as an announced stand-in for the value overflow, for which no free photograph exists." .
ex:ST_Deck_Ch03 backlog:hasAuditNote "Agent-reported weak spots of the deck, recorded 2026-10-19 from the builder's review file 08-tooling/ch03-deck/REVIEW_v2_3_0.md (not re-verified here beyond the nine checks). Not done, in the builder's words: Andresen's original post (bitcoinfoundation.org) cannot be read from here; the story's date rests on the Bitcoin Wiki page's statement of 7 April 2014 and Wikipedia gives 8 April for the day van der Laan took over. The Bitcoin Wiki date is used. Links replaced or blocked: the web.archive.org copy of the 2014 post is replaced by the Bitcoin Wiki page on Wladimir van der Laan (reachable), whose text carries the same fact and cites the post. Pictures: Gavin Andresen at Web Summit 2014 (Stephen McCarthy, CC BY 2.0); bust of Satoshi Nakamoto, Budapest (Fekist, CC BY-SA 4.0); the GNU Guix logo (author GNU Guix, public domain text logo; replaces the project's own icon on slide 10, which is MIT licensed and therefore cannot be the story's picture)." .
ex:ST_Deck_Ch04 backlog:hasAuditNote "Agent-reported weak spots of the deck, recorded 2026-10-19 from the builder's review file 08-tooling/ch04-deck/REVIEW_v3_3_0.md (not re-verified here beyond the nine checks). Not done, in the builder's words: The Bitcoin logo and the Satoshi bust are stand-ins. Links replaced or blocked: learnmeabitcoin.com keys guide (403) -> Bitcoin Wiki \"Technical background of version 1 Bitcoin addresses\" (label changed). Watch group: \"Elliptic Curves - Computerphile\" as `https://www.youtube.com/embed/NF1pwjL9-DE` (oEmbed title read). The \"Checked\" date on the resources slide is 2026-10-19. Pictures: Whitfield Diffie, 2017 (Duncan Hull, CC BY-SA 4.0, a 500 px copy of Commons File:Whitfield Diffie Royal Society.jpg, which replaces the unusable GFDL composite on slide 6); bust of Satoshi Nakamoto, Budapest (Fekist, CC BY-SA 4.0); Bitcoin logo (Grayliptrot, public domain, a stand-in: an address has no picture)." .
ex:ST_Deck_Ch05 backlog:hasAuditNote "Agent-reported weak spots of the deck, recorded 2026-10-19 from the builder's review file 08-tooling/ch05-deck/REVIEW_v2_3_0.md (not re-verified here beyond the nine checks). Not done, in the builder's words: Business Standard shows only the opening of Popper's article; the 2011 video reward is in Finance Magnates (named in the story's source), not on the linked page. The Mt. Gox logo is a stand-in for the event. Links replaced or blocked: nytimes.com (403) -> the New York Times article's opening as republished by Business Standard (labelled \"NYT via Business Standard\"); learnmeabitcoin.com HD wallets (no connection) -> the Bitcoin Wiki page on deterministic wallets (label changed). Watch group: \"BIP-39 mnemonic words\" as `https://www.youtube.com/embed/hRXcY_tIlrw` (oEmbed title read: \"Blockchain tutorial 28: Bitcoin Improvement Proposal 39 (BIP-39) mnemonic words\", Mobilefish.com). Pictures: Stefan Thomas (Lift Conference, CC BY 2.0), Trezor One devices (Gage Skidmore, CC BY-SA 3.0), the Mt. Gox logo (author not recorded on Commons, public domain text logo)." .
ex:ST_Deck_Ch06 backlog:hasAuditNote "Agent-reported weak spots of the deck, recorded 2026-10-19 from the builder's review file 08-tooling/ch06-deck/REVIEW_v1_3_0.md (not re-verified here beyond the nine checks). Not done, in the builder's words: The Mt. Gox logo and the Satoshi bust are stand-ins for the event and the patch author; no free photograph of either exists. Links replaced or blocked: learnmeabitcoin.com transaction guide (403) -> Bitcoin Wiki \"Transaction\" page (label changed). Watch group: \"Blockchain tutorial 26: Bitcoin transaction\" as `https://www.youtube.com/embed/PrcJD4rznyA` (oEmbed title read; Mobilefish.com). The \"Checked\" date on the resources slide is 2026-10-19. Pictures: Hal Finney, 1972 (Daily News-Post, public domain); the plaque at Papa John's, Jacksonville (Sanjev Rajaram, CC0); the bust of Satoshi Nakamoto, Budapest (Fekist, CC BY-SA 4.0, copy of the chapter 7 asset: it replaces the Andresen photograph on the value-overflow slide, because Satoshi wrote the patch; it is also the credit the fixtures tool needs to make stale_credit and stale_date); the Mt. Gox logo (author not recorded on Commons, public domain text logo, a stand-in)." .
ex:ST_Deck_Ch07 backlog:hasAuditNote "Agent-reported weak spots of the deck, recorded 2026-10-19 from the builder's review file 08-tooling/ch07-deck/REVIEW_v1_3_0.md (not re-verified here beyond the nine checks). Not done, in the builder's words: Nothing fails. The mining-farm photograph is a general view of 2014 hardware, not of the 2015 pools; the credit says so. Links replaced or blocked: none reported. Pictures: see the review file." .
