ex:CR_SEN0401 rdfs:comment "Corrected caveat, 2026-10-21 (it supersedes the caveats of v0.121 and v0.135; v0.135 still said that chapter 5 fails Stage 3.F, which the register no longer holds). Measured on this date, after research v1.1.1 of chapter 5 (commit 76d6083), with 08-tooling/sen0401_stage4_gates_v1_1_0.py for all fifteen units, RDODI's validator unchanged (the current one, v1.13.0), on main: every run exits 0 and reports 0 failing gates. Per unit: chapter 1: Stage3.F PASS, Stage4.cov PASS, Stage4.sub PASS, Stage4.src PASS; chapter 2: Stage3.F PASS, Stage4.cov PASS, Stage4.sub PASS, Stage4.src PASS; chapter 3: Stage3.F PASS, Stage4.cov PASS, Stage4.sub PASS, Stage4.src PASS; chapter 4: Stage3.F PASS, Stage4.cov PASS, Stage4.sub PASS, Stage4.src PASS; chapter 5: Stage3.F PASS, Stage4.cov PASS, Stage4.sub PASS, Stage4.src PASS; chapter 6: Stage3.F PASS, Stage4.cov PASS, Stage4.sub PASS, Stage4.src PASS; chapter 7: Stage3.F PASS, Stage4.cov PASS, Stage4.sub PASS, Stage4.src PASS; chapter 8: Stage3.F PASS, Stage4.cov PASS, Stage4.sub PASS, Stage4.src PASS; chapter 9: Stage3.F PASS, Stage4.cov PASS, Stage4.sub PASS, Stage4.src PASS; chapter 10: Stage3.F PASS, Stage4.cov PASS, Stage4.sub PASS, Stage4.src PASS; chapter 11: Stage3.F PASS, Stage4.cov PASS, Stage4.sub PASS, Stage4.src PASS; chapter 12: Stage3.F PASS, Stage4.cov PASS, Stage4.sub PASS, Stage4.src PASS; chapter 13: Stage3.F PASS, Stage4.cov PASS, Stage4.sub PASS, Stage4.src PASS; chapter 14: Stage3.F PASS, Stage4.cov PASS, Stage4.sub PASS, Stage4.src PASS; numbers page: Stage3.F PASS, Stage4.cov PASS, Stage4.sub PASS, Stage4.src PASS. Chapter 5 failed Stage 3.F until 2026-10-21 (15 dangling citations, because the validator's resolver reads only a standalone four-digit year from a source label and the labels 'Lightning Labs, 2026a' and '2026b' carry none); the labels now state the retrieval date; no source was added, no citation or claim removed. Chapter 1 and the numbers page (Stage 3.F and Stage 4) and chapters 2 to 7 (Stage 4 page ABox) were repaired or built by the gap tasks of the third lineage; chapter 5 also by its Stage 3.F task; chapters 8 to 14 pass without a gap task. Not claimed: the gates Cross.B, Cross.C, Stage1.C, Stage1.E, Stage3.E, Stage4.L are NOT_MEASURED or CANNOT_RUN in the units that report them (no concept inventory in the research data; no hybrid chains) and are not passes. The two validators differ: the Stage 4 runner reads the current validator (v1.13.0) and the lineage chapter checks read the pinned one (v1.6.0); both now pass for chapter 5. Items the evidence bridge could not verify and the register does not claim: the Research chapter check of chapter 1 (the check has no verify script for chapter 1; the Stage 1 to 3 gates of the runner pass) and the first bridge run of the Stage 4 runner for chapter 5 in v0.134 (it failed Stage 3.F then; the rerun of v0.136 verified). The numbers page has no chapter check. The page tests use a TEST release key and prove page logic only. Timing noise on the page checks of chapters 3 and 7 occurred in earlier runs. The other caveats of the summary stand unchanged. Neither the Mission outcome, nor closureCommittedAt, nor the achievement of the third lineage is recorded: they are the owner's."@en .
ex:Obj3_Stage3FPass backlog:hasAuditNote "Label correction 2026-10-21: chapter 5 became a third Stage 3 document of the Stage 3.F objective (the scope change of v0.132, target 2 to 3), but this label, the measurement query and the metric label, and the sprint goal of Iter_12, still named chapter 1 and the numbers page. They now name chapters 1 and 5 and the numbers page. A label edit in a new version was used, not a StageRevision: labels are not in the stage digests (subject IRIs only), so no digest moves; the pipeline verifier confirms it. The Stage 4 objective needs no change: chapters 1 to 7 and the numbers page are 8 units, from 0 to 8. The historical records (change request, impact assessment, scope and deliverable texts) keep the wording of the moment they were decided." .
ex:Iter_12 rdfs:comment "Label correction 2026-10-21: chapter 5 became a third Stage 3 document of the Stage 3.F objective (the scope change of v0.132, target 2 to 3), but this label, the measurement query and the metric label, and the sprint goal of Iter_12, still named chapter 1 and the numbers page. They now name chapters 1 and 5 and the numbers page. A label edit in a new version was used, not a StageRevision: labels are not in the stage digests (subject IRIs only), so no digest moves; the pipeline verifier confirms it. The Stage 4 objective needs no change: chapters 1 to 7 and the numbers page are 8 units, from 0 to 8. The historical records (change request, impact assessment, scope and deliverable texts) keep the wording of the moment they were decided."@en .

ex:Lineage3 rdfs:comment "Owner-directed question, not yet answered by a decision. Owner's message, relayed by the course coordinator on Wednesday 2026-10-21 08:12 Istanbul (05:12 UTC), quoted: \"Do we have any solutions for older template pages? Do we have work items for these chapters? If they are not matching with the standards how can we say the mission is reached? Is it about a gap in the goals or mission? If you think it is better to close the current lineage and start a new one for those quality enhancements, we can consider on that. But my current feeling tells me to finish them first before the final closure. What do you say?\" Measured on 2026-10-21 (coordinator; the strings re-checked by the builder session in the newest page HTML of each chapter): pages 8, 10, 11, 12 and 14 (page versions 9.51.0, 9.53.0, 9.54.0, 9.55.0, 9.57.0) do not contain the template 9.50.0/9.51.0 code ('const LBLRE=LBL.map' and 'function edVars()' are present in pages 1 to 7, 9 and 13 and absent in 8, 10, 11, 12 and 14): they lack the label-aware ERD untangle of 9.50.0 and the faster load of 9.51.0. Their content matches the decks (0 not carried on all five); their test counts do not change on 9.51.0 (regression, commit 0f7d21f). Page 8 also fails page test 9.34.0 (113 pass, 1 fail, then a crash): no chapter 8 example has a number in its code. The register holds no work item for any of this. The question is open, not decided: this note records the message and the facts; it opens no story, changes no scope and records no outcome. The Mission outcome stays the owner's act and is not recorded."@en .
ex:CR_SEN0401 rdfs:comment "Before the closure act: Owner's message, relayed by the course coordinator on Wednesday 2026-10-21 08:12 Istanbul (05:12 UTC), quoted: \"Do we have any solutions for older template pages? Do we have work items for these chapters? If they are not matching with the standards how can we say the mission is reached? Is it about a gap in the goals or mission? If you think it is better to close the current lineage and start a new one for those quality enhancements, we can consider on that. But my current feeling tells me to finish them first before the final closure. What do you say?\" Measured on 2026-10-21 (coordinator; the strings re-checked by the builder session in the newest page HTML of each chapter): pages 8, 10, 11, 12 and 14 (page versions 9.51.0, 9.53.0, 9.54.0, 9.55.0, 9.57.0) do not contain the template 9.50.0/9.51.0 code ('const LBLRE=LBL.map' and 'function edVars()' are present in pages 1 to 7, 9 and 13 and absent in 8, 10, 11, 12 and 14): they lack the label-aware ERD untangle of 9.50.0 and the faster load of 9.51.0. Their content matches the decks (0 not carried on all five); their test counts do not change on 9.51.0 (regression, commit 0f7d21f). Page 8 also fails page test 9.34.0 (113 pass, 1 fail, then a crash): no chapter 8 example has a number in its code. The register holds no work item for any of this. The question is open, not decided: this note records the message and the facts; it opens no story, changes no scope and records no outcome. The Mission outcome stays the owner's act and is not recorded."@en .

ex:CR3_Pages a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "Rebuild the pages of chapters 8, 10, 11, 12 and 14 on the current page template, and give chapter 8 real examples with numbers, before the Mission is closed"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR_SEN0401 ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Owner's message of Wednesday 2026-10-21 08:12 Istanbul (2026-10-21T05:12:00 UTC), relayed by the course coordinator and recorded by the builder session, quoted: \"Do we have any solutions for older template pages? Do we have work items for these chapters? If they are not matching with the standards how can we say the mission is reached? Is it about a gap in the goals or mission? If you think it is better to close the current lineage and start a new one for those quality enhancements, we can consider on that. But my current feeling tells me to finish them first before the final closure. What do you say?\" He asked what we say; the coordinator and the builder session answered to finish before the closure, which is his own stated lean, and this plan follows that lean and that recommendation. Under the standing rule that work following the owner's direction is recorded as owner-directed, it is not listed as an open owner confirmation. His earlier direction of 2026-10-19 00:42 Istanbul, quoted: \"Keep the same standards with all other pages.\" is the origin of the standard written below. Measured 2026-10-21 (coordinator; strings re-checked by the builder session in the newest page HTML of each chapter): pages 8, 10, 11, 12 and 14 (page versions 9.51.0, 9.53.0, 9.54.0, 9.55.0, 9.57.0) do not contain the code of the page template 9.50.0/9.51.0 ('const LBLRE=LBL.map' and 'function edVars()' are present in the pages of chapters 1 to 7, 9 and 13 and absent in these five): they lack the label-aware ERD untangle of 9.50.0 (the defect that left 6 labels out on chapter 3 under 9.48) and the faster load of 9.51.0 (the stability fix for the load-time budget; noisy first runs happened on chapters 11 and 13 and a chapter 11 test hung). Their content matches the decks (pages_deck_match_verify: 0 not carried on all five); the regression (evidence commit 0f7d21f) showed their test counts do not change on 9.51.0. Page 8 also fails page test 9.34.0 (113 pass, 1 fail, then a crash): no chapter 8 example has a number in its code; chapter 13 solved the same check by research v1_0_2 examples with editable numbers (commit 43886764) and a new inputs maker. The register had no work item for any of this. The change grows the scope: the third lineage's scope admits the two link passes, the 20 carried tasks and the Stage 3.F and Stage 4 gap closure, and names no page rebuild (its exclusion ex:Excl3_NoRebuild excludes rebuilding a page in order to admit it; this rebuild is not for admission, it is the owner's direction, and the new files stand beside the old ones). Pending until the ScopeChange that admits the stories is recorded in the Backlog version." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .

ex:IA3_Pages a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What rebuilding the five pages and giving chapter 8 its examples costs, measured before it is started"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR3_Pages ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage3 ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_Gaps, ex:CR_SEN0401 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "Measured 2026-10-21 (coordinator; strings re-checked by the builder session in the newest page HTML of each chapter): pages 8, 10, 11, 12 and 14 (page versions 9.51.0, 9.53.0, 9.54.0, 9.55.0, 9.57.0) do not contain the code of the page template 9.50.0/9.51.0 ('const LBLRE=LBL.map' and 'function edVars()' are present in the pages of chapters 1 to 7, 9 and 13 and absent in these five): they lack the label-aware ERD untangle of 9.50.0 (the defect that left 6 labels out on chapter 3 under 9.48) and the faster load of 9.51.0 (the stability fix for the load-time budget; noisy first runs happened on chapters 11 and 13 and a chapter 11 test hung). Their content matches the decks (pages_deck_match_verify: 0 not carried on all five); the regression (evidence commit 0f7d21f) showed their test counts do not change on 9.51.0. Page 8 also fails page test 9.34.0 (113 pass, 1 fail, then a crash): no chapter 8 example has a number in its code; chapter 13 solved the same check by research v1_0_2 examples with editable numbers (commit 43886764) and a new inputs maker. The register had no work item for any of this. Answers to the owner's questions, from the register: (1) Do the goals and the Mission cover the standard? They ask for existence (G_PageForEveryDeck: every renewed deck has its interactive page; the Mission outcome: a deck, an interactive page and the sources for each chapter); the five pages exist and pass the chapter check (AC_Chapter). No goal, objective, criterion or Done story states a template or a uniform standard; the owner's direction of 2026-10-19 \"Keep the same standards with all other pages.\" is recorded only as notes on the stories of the pages of chapters 6 and 13. So it is a gap in the stated standard (goals and criteria), not a contradiction of the Mission. (2) Route: a standard added after a story is Done does not reach into it (G133); the work is a story of its own (G125); it is a new deliverable, so a StageRevision from the Scope stage (G127), which rebuilds the Scope, Goal, Objective and Backlog stages once and lets a goal for the standard be added in the same revision. Cost: the earlier Scope revision of this lineage took eight versions to work begun (v0.122 to v0.129); this one takes seven (change, retraction, four stages, work begun). (3) Closing now and a successor taking the work (G125 route 3) costs about ten versions plus the owner's closure act with the gap on record; finishing first costs seven plus the recording of Done and a refreshed caveat, and leaves the Mission outcome unrecorded, which is the owner's stated lean. What moves: the digests of the Scope, Goal, Objective and Backlog stages of the third lineage move once, when the stages are closed again; the first and second lineages are not touched; no Done story is re-dated or re-opened. New work, planned in the Backlog version: a story for the five pages with one acceptance criterion per page (G133) and a story for chapter 8 with one criterion, 12 execution tasks (a build and a verify task per page, a build and a verify task for the chapter 8 examples). Iteration: the work is planned into the twelfth iteration of the third lineage, ex:Iter_12, which ends 2026-10-23T06:00 UTC (09:00 Istanbul), the owner's own confirmed end date; about 48 hours remain. The end does not have to move for the plan to be valid; if a story is still open when the iteration ends, the register shows it as spillover (L4) until the owner rebaselines the iteration or recommits the story, and only the owner decides that. Risks: the chapter 8 examples are new research content, so the deck of chapter 8 may have to carry them for the page and the deck to stay equal (pages_deck_match_verify); if so that is stated and decided, not hidden; a unit whose gate fails is named failing and is not Done. Not in the standard: the connectedness repair of the T-Box files; the concept-inventory gates (Stage1.C, Stage1.E, Stage3.E, Stage4.L, which the runner reports NOT_MEASURED because the research data holds no concept inventory) and Cross.B/Cross.C; any change to a gate, a test or a threshold; any change to the content, the decks or the research (except the chapter 8 examples); the owner's open rulings (load-time budget of the page of chapter 6, test-design ruling of chapter 13). Cost of waiting: the Mission outcome stays unrecorded; cost of acting: one change request, one assessment, one stage revision (retraction and four rebuilt stages, one commit each), two stories, 12 tasks. Nothing is waived and no digest is re-recorded outside the revision." .

ex:Revision_Lineage3_Scope2 a backlog:StageRevision ;
    rdfs:label "Revision of the third lineage from the Scope stage: the pages of older templates are rebuilt before the Mission outcome is recorded"@en ;
    backlog:revisesLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:revisesFromStage backlog:Stage_Scope ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_Pages, ex:IA3_Pages ;
    backlog:revisionReason "Owner's message of Wednesday 2026-10-21 08:12 Istanbul (2026-10-21T05:12:00 UTC), relayed by the course coordinator and recorded by the builder session, quoted: \"Do we have any solutions for older template pages? Do we have work items for these chapters? If they are not matching with the standards how can we say the mission is reached? Is it about a gap in the goals or mission? If you think it is better to close the current lineage and start a new one for those quality enhancements, we can consider on that. But my current feeling tells me to finish them first before the final closure. What do you say?\" He asked what we say; the coordinator and the builder session answered to finish before the closure, which is his own stated lean, and this plan follows that lean and that recommendation. Under the standing rule that work following the owner's direction is recorded as owner-directed, it is not listed as an open owner confirmation. His earlier direction of 2026-10-19 00:42 Istanbul, quoted: \"Keep the same standards with all other pages.\" is the origin of the standard written below. The work adds two deliverables to the scope of the third lineage (pages rebuilt on the current template; chapter 8 examples); the lineage is in its closed Backlog stage, and a deliverable added to a closed scope statement is a revision from the Scope stage (ruling G127). The change request ex:CR3_Pages and the impact assessment ex:IA3_Pages were recorded first, in the previous version. This version retracts the Scope, Goal, Objective and Backlog outputs and rebuilds nothing; they are rebuilt one stage and one commit at a time, each consuming the last unretracted output above it; the goals, objectives, stories and tasks already in the register, Done ones included, re-enter by admission and are not re-dated. The retracted outputs and their digests stay as history (L-112). The interim versions are the declared transition (G129). The revision is recorded as decided by the builder role: the route is what the owner's direction needs; the stage revision itself he did not decide." ;
    backlog:retractsOutput ex:Out3_ScopeR2, ex:Out3_GoalR2, ex:Out3_ObjectiveR2, ex:Out3_BacklogR3 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:revisedAtCommit "ffab2d6" .
ex:Out3_ScopeR2 backlog:outputRetracted true .
ex:Out3_GoalR2 backlog:outputRetracted true .
ex:Out3_ObjectiveR2 backlog:outputRetracted true .
ex:Out3_BacklogR3 backlog:outputRetracted true .

ex:Area3_PageTemplate a backlog:ScopeArea ;
    rdfs:label "The pages of chapters built on older page templates"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:areaLocation "03-materials: the page folders of chapters 8, 10, 11, 12 and 14 (the pages, the page ABoxes) and the research folder of chapter 8; the page builder and the Stage 4 builder in 08-tooling" ;
    backlog:areaMeasure "14 chapter pages of which 9 carry the code of the page template 9.51.0 today; after the work all 14 do" ;
    backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Work .
ex:Del3_PageTemplate a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ;
    rdfs:label "The pages of chapters 8, 10, 11, 12 and 14 are rebuilt on the current page template with the same content, the tests unchanged"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:derivesFromMissionClause "the research behind it and an interactive page"^^xsd:string ;
    backlog:hasDeliverableText "The pages of chapters 8, 10, 11, 12 and 14 rebuilt as new files on the page template 9.51.0 with the same content (the deck's lecture export and stories), the page tests 9.34.0 and 9.35.0 unchanged and reporting counts equal to or better than the stored result of each page, a Stage 4 page ABox rebuilt from each new page that passes the Stage 4 gate run. The written standard of a page, each element a fact the page can be measured against and none a taste: (1) template: the page is built from the current page template, 9.51.0, the one the newest pages of chapters 1 to 7, 9 and 13 use; measured by the two code markers 'const LBLRE=LBL.map' and 'function edVars()' present in the page HTML; (2) content: the page carries the deck's lecture export and stories; measured by pages_deck_match_verify, 0 not carried; (3) ERD: the relationship labels are shown after Untangle; measured by the existing page test 9.35.0, the feature 'the on-choice labels mode ... Untangle finishes and leaves no more lines through unrelated entities than the grid had', which compares the labels shown after Untangle with the grid (at least 95 percent) - no new test is written, the template carries the fix; (4) tests: the page tests 9.34.0 and 9.35.0, unchanged, report no failure and counts equal to or better than the stored result of the page as it stands; (5) Stage 4: the page ABox is rebuilt from the new page as a new file and the Stage 4 gate runner v1_1_0 for the chapter exits 0 with Stage3.F, Stage4.A, B, cov, sub and src PASS; the Research, Deck and Page chapter checks of the chapter still pass. NOT part of the standard: the connectedness repair of the T-Box files; the concept-inventory gates (Stage1.C, Stage1.E, Stage3.E, Stage4.L, which the runner reports NOT_MEASURED because the research data holds no concept inventory) and Cross.B/Cross.C; any change to a gate, a test or a threshold; any change to the content, the decks or the research (except the chapter 8 examples); the owner's open rulings (load-time budget of the page of chapter 6, test-design ruling of chapter 13)." ;
    backlog:deliverableForArea ex:Area3_PageTemplate ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Work ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_Functional .
ex:Del3_Ch08Examples a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ;
    rdfs:label "Chapter 8 has real executable examples with numbers, so its page passes page test 9.34.0"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:derivesFromMissionClause "the research behind it and an interactive page"^^xsd:string ;
    backlog:hasDeliverableText "A new version of the chapter 8 research with real executable examples that have numbers in their code (editable inputs), following chapter 13 (research v1_0_2, commit 43886764, and an inputs maker); the chapter 8 Stage 3.F and Stage 4 gates re-run clean, the Research, Deck and Page chapter checks pass, and the chapter 8 page passes page test 9.34.0 (now 113 pass, 1 fail, then a crash); no test or gate is changed. Measured 2026-10-21 (coordinator; strings re-checked by the builder session in the newest page HTML of each chapter): pages 8, 10, 11, 12 and 14 (page versions 9.51.0, 9.53.0, 9.54.0, 9.55.0, 9.57.0) do not contain the code of the page template 9.50.0/9.51.0 ('const LBLRE=LBL.map' and 'function edVars()' are present in the pages of chapters 1 to 7, 9 and 13 and absent in these five): they lack the label-aware ERD untangle of 9.50.0 (the defect that left 6 labels out on chapter 3 under 9.48) and the faster load of 9.51.0 (the stability fix for the load-time budget; noisy first runs happened on chapters 11 and 13 and a chapter 11 test hung). Their content matches the decks (pages_deck_match_verify: 0 not carried on all five); the regression (evidence commit 0f7d21f) showed their test counts do not change on 9.51.0. Page 8 also fails page test 9.34.0 (113 pass, 1 fail, then a crash): no chapter 8 example has a number in its code; chapter 13 solved the same check by research v1_0_2 examples with editable numbers (commit 43886764) and a new inputs maker. The register had no work item for any of this." ;
    backlog:deliverableForArea ex:Area3_PageTemplate ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Work ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_Functional .
ex:Excl3_NoConceptGates a backlog:ScopeExclusion ;
    rdfs:label "The page standard does not include the connectedness repair, the concept-inventory gates, or any change to a gate, a test or a threshold"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:excludesConcern "Anything that changes a gate, a test or a threshold in order to make a page pass; the connectedness repair of the T-Box files (deferred by the owner on 2026-10-20 09:19 Istanbul); the concept-inventory gates Stage1.C, Stage1.E, Stage3.E, Stage4.L and Cross.B/Cross.C, which the runner reports NOT_MEASURED or CANNOT_RUN; a change of content, decks or research other than the chapter 8 examples; the owner's open rulings (load-time budget of the page of chapter 6, test-design ruling of chapter 13); recording the Mission outcome and the Achieved status of this lineage, which wait for the owner's act." ;
    backlog:hasExclusionRationale "A standard made of facts the pages can be measured against stays measurable only if the measures are not changed to fit; the concept-inventory gates report NOT_MEASURED for every unit because the research holds no inventory, which is a research-design matter the owner has not asked for; the connectedness repair was deferred by the owner on 2026-10-20 09:19 Istanbul." ;
    backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Work .
ex:Scope3 backlog:requiresDeliverable ex:Del3_PageTemplate, ex:Del3_Ch08Examples ;
    backlog:coversArea ex:Area3_PageTemplate ; backlog:hasScopeExclusion ex:Excl3_NoConceptGates ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_Pages, ex:IA3_Pages .
ex:Scope3 rdfs:comment "Revised 2026-10-21 by the stage revision ex:Revision_Lineage3_Scope2 on the owner's message of Wednesday 2026-10-21 08:12 Istanbul (2026-10-21T05:12:00 UTC) (quoted in the change request ex:CR3_Pages). The statement above is unchanged (L-112). It now also requires ex:Del3_PageTemplate and ex:Del3_Ch08Examples, covers the area ex:Area3_PageTemplate and carries the exclusion ex:Excl3_NoConceptGates. The exclusion ex:Excl3_NoRebuild stands: it excludes rebuilding in order to admit; these rebuilds are the owner's direction and are new files beside the old ones."@en .

