    backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-21T08:24:15"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-21T19:49:53"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:lastAuditedAt "2026-10-24T02:19:03"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasExecutionModality backlog:Mode_Hybrid ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Not scored: the owner's lean of 2026-10-21 08:12 Istanbul is to finish this before the closure, so there is no ranking left to compute." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Created by the stage revision ex:Revision_Lineage3_Scope2 on the owner's message of Wednesday 2026-10-21 08:12 Istanbul (2026-10-21T05:12:00 UTC) (quoted in ex:CR3_Pages), which follows his stated lean. One criterion per page (G133). The written standard of a page, each element a fact the page can be measured against and none a taste: (1) template: the page is built from the current page template, 9.51.0, the one the newest pages of chapters 1 to 7, 9 and 13 use; measured by the two code markers 'const LBLRE=LBL.map' and 'function edVars()' present in the page HTML; (2) content: the page carries the deck's lecture export and stories; measured by pages_deck_match_verify, 0 not carried; (3) ERD: the relationship labels are shown after Untangle; measured by the existing page test 9.35.0, the feature 'the on-choice labels mode ... Untangle finishes and leaves no more lines through unrelated entities than the grid had', which compares the labels shown after Untangle with the grid (at least 95 percent) - no new test is written, the template carries the fix; (4) tests: the page tests 9.34.0 and 9.35.0, unchanged, report no failure and counts equal to or better than the stored result of the page as it stands; (5) Stage 4: the page ABox is rebuilt from the new page as a new file and the Stage 4 gate runner v1_1_0 for the chapter exits 0 with Stage3.F, Stage4.A, B, cov, sub and src PASS; the Research, Deck and Page chapter checks of the chapter still pass. NOT part of the standard: the connectedness repair of the T-Box files; the concept-inventory gates (Stage1.C, Stage1.E, Stage3.E, Stage4.L, which the runner reports NOT_MEASURED because the research data holds no concept inventory) and Cross.B/Cross.C; any change to a gate, a test or a threshold; any change to the content, the decks or the research (except the chapter 8 examples); the owner's open rulings (load-time budget of the page of chapter 6, test-design ruling of chapter 13)." .

