    backlog:hasScopeChangeRationale "Owner's message of Wednesday 2026-10-21 08:12 Istanbul (2026-10-21T05:12:00 UTC), relayed by the course coordinator and recorded by the builder session, quoted: \"Do we have any solutions for older template pages? Do we have work items for these chapters? If they are not matching with the standards how can we say the mission is reached? Is it about a gap in the goals or mission? If you think it is better to close the current lineage and start a new one for those quality enhancements, we can consider on that. But my current feeling tells me to finish them first before the final closure. What do you say?\" He asked what we say; the coordinator and the builder session answered to finish before the closure, which is his own stated lean, and this plan follows that lean and that recommendation. Under the standing rule that work following the owner's direction is recorded as owner-directed, it is not listed as an open owner confirmation. His earlier direction of 2026-10-19 00:42 Istanbul, quoted: \"Keep the same standards with all other pages.\" is the origin of the standard written below. The boundary moved outward by two stories because the owner leaned to finish this before the Mission outcome is recorded. It is paid for by running the work inside the twelfth iteration, which ends at the owner's own confirmed date, by building new files beside the old ones, and by leaving every gate, test and threshold as it stands." .
ex:CR3_Pages rdfs:comment "Disposition set to Accepted on 2026-10-21 in the version that records the ScopeChange ex:SC3_Pages and the stories it admits; it was Pending before. The owner's message of Wednesday 2026-10-21 08:12 Istanbul (2026-10-21T05:12:00 UTC) is the direction, and his stated lean to finish first is the decision."@en .

