    backlog:closedAtCommit "aade2cb" .

ex:Lineage3 rdfs:comment "Owner-directed corrections. Owner's message, relayed by the course coordinator on Wednesday 2026-10-21 10:14 Istanbul (2026-10-21T07:14:00 UTC), quoted: \"I think you need to correct the stories appropriately and connect the tasks with the stories and run them per sprint rather than ad hoc initiation of the agents out of the lineage. It is a drift to find a solution to an issue after the happening. We have a clean discipline first to plan and decide, later execute and control. Your approach is to start unconditionally and find a way to deal with. This makes the progress much more complicated. Why don't you keep the lineage standards? If you can find the root-cause we can ask BRSF to build preventive measures against such cases.\" Recorded as owner-directed work: the corrections below follow it. No work agent had started on the template work; the root cause was written as a handover to the BRSF package (pending in its handover inbox, 2026-10-21)."@en .
ex:CR_SEN0401 rdfs:comment "Before the closure act: Owner's message, relayed by the course coordinator on Wednesday 2026-10-21 10:14 Istanbul (2026-10-21T07:14:00 UTC), quoted: \"I think you need to correct the stories appropriately and connect the tasks with the stories and run them per sprint rather than ad hoc initiation of the agents out of the lineage. It is a drift to find a solution to an issue after the happening. We have a clean discipline first to plan and decide, later execute and control. Your approach is to start unconditionally and find a way to deal with. This makes the progress much more complicated. Why don't you keep the lineage standards? If you can find the root-cause we can ask BRSF to build preventive measures against such cases.\" Recorded as owner-directed work: the corrections below follow it. No work agent had started on the template work; the root cause was written as a handover to the BRSF package (pending in its handover inbox, 2026-10-21)."@en .
ex:CR3_Pages rdfs:comment "Owner-directed corrections to the execution of this change: Owner's message, relayed by the course coordinator on Wednesday 2026-10-21 10:14 Istanbul (2026-10-21T07:14:00 UTC), quoted: \"I think you need to correct the stories appropriately and connect the tasks with the stories and run them per sprint rather than ad hoc initiation of the agents out of the lineage. It is a drift to find a solution to an issue after the happening. We have a clean discipline first to plan and decide, later execute and control. Your approach is to start unconditionally and find a way to deal with. This makes the progress much more complicated. Why don't you keep the lineage standards? If you can find the root-cause we can ask BRSF to build preventive measures against such cases.\" Recorded as owner-directed work: the corrections below follow it. No work agent had started on the template work; the root cause was written as a handover to the BRSF package (pending in its handover inbox, 2026-10-21)."@en .

