    backlog:hasObservationMethod "Measured 2026-10-21: the newest page of each of the 14 chapters contains both template markers: 14 of 14 (all). This objective counts the code of the template only; it does not say that every page meets every element of the written standard (see the notes of the criteria)." .
ex:ST_Page_Template backlog:hasAuditNote "Control 2026-10-21: criteria met: AC3T_Ch08, AC3T_Ch12, AC3T_Ch14; not met: AC3T_Ch10 (elements (3) ERD labels), AC3T_Ch11 (elements (3) ERD labels). The story is Done only when every criterion of it is met (G125), so it stays InProgress; the criteria are not edited and nothing is waived." .
ex:CR3_PageErd a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "Element 3 (ERD labels after Untangle) of the page criteria of chapters 10, 11 cannot be measured: what measures it where the research states no relationship?"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_Pages ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Found by the control run 2026-10-21. The page test 9.35.0 skips its feature on the labels shown after Untangle on the pages of chapters 10, 11, because the chapter research states no relationship between two sections, so there is nothing to label (skip lines as printed: {\"10\": [\"[SKIP] the filled ERD reads: overlapping label pairs under 15 percent of the labels, labels over an entity under 10 percent  the chapter's research states no relationship between two sections, so the ERD has no line and no label to measure (entities \", \"[SKIP] the on-choice labels mode shows only the chosen entity's labels  the chapter's research states no relationship between two sections, so the ERD has no label\"], \"11\": [\"[SKIP] the filled ERD reads: overlapping label pairs under 15 percent of the labels, labels over an entity under 10 percent  the chapter's research states no relationship between two sections, so the ERD has no line and no label to measure (entities \", \"[SKIP] the on-choice labels mode shows only the chosen entity's labels  the chapter's research states no relationship between two sections, so the ERD has no label\"]}). The skips equal the stored result of the pages as they stood (2 skipped each), so nothing got worse; but element 3 of their criteria asks that feature to report pass, and a skipped feature is not a pass. The criteria are therefore NOT MET on element 3 and are not edited or waived. THE OWNER'S QUESTION: for a page whose chapter states no relationship between two sections, what measures that the relationship labels are readable: (a) element 3 does not apply to such a page (the criterion for chapters 10, 11 then says so, a Shrink of the written standard), or (b) the chapter research states at least one relationship between two sections so the existing feature can run (a change of the research, which the standard excluded), or (c) another measure he names?" ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted  ;
    rdfs:comment "Owner's answer recorded 2026-10-22: Owner's answer of Thursday 2026-10-22 01:24 Istanbul (2026-10-21T22:24:00 UTC), as relayed by the course coordinator; the time at which the owner wrote it is not known to the builder session to the question of ex:CR3_PageErd, relayed by the course coordinator and recorded by the builder session, quoted: \"Sections are linked with each other at least by menu, possibly by semantic, syntactic, temporal, concepts, content or other relationships. You need to discover it by using the OEE relationship taxonomy and if necessary class categorization in a similar manner.\" This is option (b) of the question, widened: the relationships between sections are discovered and stated in the chapter research as links (object properties), not text. Under the standing rule that work following the owner's direction is recorded as owner-directed, it is not listed as an open owner confirmation. The question assumed option (a), a Shrink of the written standard; the decision is option (b) widened, which adds a deliverable to the scope, so the direction is Grow (Direction: Shrink in the question (option (a)), Grow in the decision (option (b) widened, a deliverable is added).) No criterion is changed or waived: AC3T_Ch10 and AC3T_Ch11 stay as written and are met when the new page passes element 3. Disposition stays Pending until the ScopeChange that admits the story is recorded in the Backlog version (G127 route)."@en .

ex:IA3_PageErd a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What the unmeasurable element 3 costs, measured before any decision"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR3_PageErd ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage3 ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:IA3_Pages ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "Affected: criteria AC3T_Ch10, AC3T_Ch11 and, through them, ST_Page_Template (stays InProgress until the owner decides and the criteria are met or changed by a recorded route). Not affected: the pages themselves (every other element is recorded), the Mission outcome, closureCommittedAt and the Achieved status of the third lineage, which this record does not touch. Cost of (a): one criterion revision by the change route, no page work. Cost of (b): a new research version per chapter, new pages and checks, the pages rebuilt (about the cost of this iteration for two chapters). Cost of (c): depends on the measure."  ;
    rdfs:comment "Impact assessment after the owner's answer (2026-10-22). Measured 2026-10-22 by the builder session from the newest page of each chapter (the relations the page test sees: page data relations between two different sections, counted by the same section map the page test 9.35.0 uses): chapter 10 has 17 sections and 0 relations between two sections; chapter 11 has 16 sections and 0; chapter 13 has 16 and 0; chapter 8 has 23 sections and 4 (16 sections with none); chapter 9 has 20 and 3 (14 with none); chapter 12 has 15 and 2 (12 with none); chapter 14 has 13 and 2 (10 with none); chapters 1 to 7 have every section linked (93, 50, 59, 39, 83, 110 and 52 section pairs). In chapters 1 to 7 the section relationship is NOT authored as a link between sections: it is the page-data builder's text co-mention ('mentions', evidence: the document's section on X names Y; 1,644 of the 1,683 cross-section relations of those chapters) plus a few 'operates on' relations that come from the domain link chx:hasOwner (a subproperty of RDODI's hasOwningConcept) between concept individuals of different sections (11, 4, 2, 3, 11, 4 and 4). The research of chapters 10 and 11 states no relationship between two sections: their domain T-Box holds subclass links inside sections and disjointness, their domain A-Box holds only the I/O examples (type, label, definition, source, input, output, hasIOExample); the OEE link discovery (oe_link_discovery) found only the syntactic pair input/output. The text co-mention does not arise in chapters 10 and 11 because their document text names no concept of another section. Route: the scope of the third lineage excludes a change of the research other than chapter 8 (ex:Excl3_NoConceptGates), so a new deliverable is added: a StageRevision from the Scope stage (G127), 7 versions (this one, retraction, four stages, and the iteration with the backlog in one) against the 'closed lineage and successor' alternative of about ten plus the owner's closure act. Work (planned, not begun): one story, one criterion per chapter (G133), seven tasks - for each of chapters 10 and 11 a research task (new research version whose section relationships are links, discovered with the OEE relationship taxonomy), a page task (the page-data builder reads the links as relations, the page is rebuilt as a new page version, the Stage 4 page ABox is rebuilt), a verify task - and one builder task that is shared (a new page-data builder version). Each page rebuild runs the page tests, about nine minutes per run. Iteration: ex:Iter_14, new, because the goal of ex:Iter_13 is frozen at its start and may not be extended; ex:Iter_13 stays open with ST_Page_Template only, its members unchanged, and closes when AC3T_Ch10 and AC3T_Ch11 are met by the verify tasks of the new iteration, or the owner rebaselines or recommits; closing it earlier would need a Rebaseline decided by the owner, which is not asked. Affected: AC3T_Ch10 and AC3T_Ch11 (met by the new pages), ST_Page_Template (closes after them), the Mission outcome, closureCommittedAt and the Achieved status of the third lineage are not touched. Risks: a section for which no relationship can be stated with a standard or declared relation is reported by name and not forced; the template draws every relation type that is not 'mentions' as 'operates on' and it is not changed; chapters 8, 9, 12, 13 and 14 have sections with no relationship and are not in this deliverable (an owner question). Not changed: any gate, test, threshold, criterion or template."@en .

ex:Revision_Lineage3_Scope3 a backlog:StageRevision ;
    rdfs:label "Revision of the third lineage from the Scope stage: the relationships between the sections of chapters 10 and 11 are stated in the research as links"@en ;
    backlog:revisesLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:revisesFromStage backlog:Stage_Scope ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_PageErd, ex:IA3_PageErd ;
    backlog:revisionReason "Owner's answer of Thursday 2026-10-22 01:24 Istanbul (2026-10-21T22:24:00 UTC), as relayed by the course coordinator; the time at which the owner wrote it is not known to the builder session to the question of ex:CR3_PageErd, relayed by the course coordinator and recorded by the builder session, quoted: \"Sections are linked with each other at least by menu, possibly by semantic, syntactic, temporal, concepts, content or other relationships. You need to discover it by using the OEE relationship taxonomy and if necessary class categorization in a similar manner.\" This is option (b) of the question, widened: the relationships between sections are discovered and stated in the chapter research as links (object properties), not text. Under the standing rule that work following the owner's direction is recorded as owner-directed, it is not listed as an open owner confirmation. The work adds a deliverable to the scope of the third lineage (relationships between sections stated in the research of chapters 10 and 11, and the pages rebuilt from them); the lineage is in its closed Backlog stage, and a deliverable added to a closed scope statement is a revision from the Scope stage (ruling G127). The change request ex:CR3_PageErd and its impact assessment ex:IA3_PageErd were completed first, in the previous version. This version retracts the Scope, Goal, Objective and Backlog outputs and rebuilds nothing; they are rebuilt one stage and one commit at a time; the goals, objectives, stories and tasks already in the register, Done ones included, re-enter by admission and are not re-dated. The retracted outputs and their digests stay as history (L-112). The interim versions are the declared transition (G129). The revision is recorded as decided by the builder role: the route is what the owner's direction needs; the stage revision itself he did not decide." ;
    backlog:retractsOutput ex:Out3_ScopeR3, ex:Out3_GoalR3, ex:Out3_ObjectiveR3, ex:Out3_BacklogR4 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:revisedAtCommit "4a2801d" .
ex:Out3_ScopeR3 backlog:outputRetracted true .
ex:Out3_GoalR3 backlog:outputRetracted true .
ex:Out3_ObjectiveR3 backlog:outputRetracted true .
ex:Out3_BacklogR4 backlog:outputRetracted true .

ex:Area3_SectionLinks a backlog:ScopeArea ;
    rdfs:label "The relationships between the sections of the chapters whose research states none"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:areaLocation "03-materials: the research folders (rdodi) and page folders of chapters 10 and 11; the page-data builder, the page builder and the Stage 4 builder in 08-tooling" ;
    backlog:areaMeasure "sections of chapters 10 and 11 with no relationship to another section: 33 of 33 today; after the work 0" ;
    backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Work .
ex:Del3_SectionLinks a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ;
    rdfs:label "The research of chapters 10 and 11 states how their sections relate, as links, and their pages show the relationships"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:derivesFromMissionClause "the research behind it and an interactive page"^^xsd:string ;
    backlog:hasDeliverableText "A new version of the research of chapters 10 and 11 (the domain T-Box, A-Box and SHACL as the chapter's package requires, the document and the research file) in which the relationships between the sections are STATED AS LINKS (object properties between the sections' individuals or classes; ruling G134: links, not text), discovered with the OEE relationship taxonomy (categories such as semantic, syntactic, temporal, containment, ordering and succession; class kinds where the kind rule needs them), each property declared in the domain T-Box with domain, range, label and kb:hasRelationshipCategory, a standard relation reused where one says it; every section of the chapter related to at least one other section; the page-data builder reads the links as page relations, the page is rebuilt as a new page version and its Stage 4 page ABox as a new file; the page test 9.35.0 runs its ERD labels feature and passes it with no skip. The OEE relationship taxonomy is oe-method/04-documentation/RELATIONSHIP_TAXONOMY_RESEARCH_v1_11_0.md (categories as kb:RelationshipCategory_* in oe-method/09-governance/oegov_abox_v1_36_0.ttl, properties kb:hasRelationshipCategory and kb:hasClassKind in oegov_tbox_v1_15_0.ttl); construction method BP-D58 (choose the relation: which category, is there a standard relation that says it, which pattern, what to declare), class kinds BP-D59, missing-link discovery BP-D57 (tool repo-tooling/oe_link_discovery_v1_1_0.py: syntactic, semantic, temporal families; file set = a T-Box and A-Box pair), kind rule check repo-tooling/oe_kind_rule_check_v1_1_0.py. OE v2.31.0 and v2.32.0 (ceremony of 2026-10-22: PROCEED, repo-tooling v1.77.0) add kind rules and two class kinds: they bind the ontology files and any research that declares a category or a kind; they do not bind the A-Box versions of this register. Measured 2026-10-22 by the builder session from the newest page of each chapter (the relations the page test sees: page data relations between two different sections, counted by the same section map the page test 9.35.0 uses): chapter 10 has 17 sections and 0 relations between two sections; chapter 11 has 16 sections and 0; chapter 13 has 16 and 0; chapter 8 has 23 sections and 4 (16 sections with none); chapter 9 has 20 and 3 (14 with none); chapter 12 has 15 and 2 (12 with none); chapter 14 has 13 and 2 (10 with none); chapters 1 to 7 have every section linked (93, 50, 59, 39, 83, 110 and 52 section pairs). In chapters 1 to 7 the section relationship is NOT authored as a link between sections: it is the page-data builder's text co-mention ('mentions', evidence: the document's section on X names Y; 1,644 of the 1,683 cross-section relations of those chapters) plus a few 'operates on' relations that come from the domain link chx:hasOwner (a subproperty of RDODI's hasOwningConcept) between concept individuals of different sections (11, 4, 2, 3, 11, 4 and 4). The research of chapters 10 and 11 states no relationship between two sections: their domain T-Box holds subclass links inside sections and disjointness, their domain A-Box holds only the I/O examples (type, label, definition, source, input, output, hasIOExample); the OEE link discovery (oe_link_discovery) found only the syntactic pair input/output. The text co-mention does not arise in chapters 10 and 11 because their document text names no concept of another section." ;
    backlog:deliverableForArea ex:Area3_SectionLinks ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Work ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_Functional .
ex:Scope3 backlog:requiresDeliverable ex:Del3_SectionLinks ;
    backlog:coversArea ex:Area3_SectionLinks ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_PageErd, ex:IA3_PageErd .
ex:Scope3 rdfs:comment "Revised 2026-10-22 by the stage revision Revision_Lineage3_Scope3 on the owner's answer of Thursday 2026-10-22 01:24 Istanbul (2026-10-21T22:24:00 UTC), as relayed by the course coordinator; the time at which the owner wrote it is not known to the builder session (quoted in the change request ex:CR3_PageErd). The statement above is unchanged (L-112). It now also requires ex:Del3_SectionLinks and covers the area ex:Area3_SectionLinks. The exclusion ex:Excl3_NoConceptGates (owner-decided) stands for every gate, test and threshold. Not in the deliverable and not changed: the page template, a page test, a criterion, a relation type the template cannot draw (it draws every type other than 'mentions' as 'operates on'), forcing a relationship that no taxonomy relation states, and the section relationships of chapters 8, 9, 12, 13 and 14 (reported as facts; extending to them is the owner's to decide)."@en .
ex:Excl3_NoConceptGates rdfs:comment "Note 2026-10-22: the concern 'a change of content, decks or research other than the chapter 8 examples' is lifted for the research of chapters 10 and 11 by the owner's answer of Thursday 2026-10-22 01:24 Istanbul (2026-10-21T22:24:00 UTC), as relayed by the course coordinator; the time at which the owner wrote it is not known to the builder session, as ex:Del3_SectionLinks; the exclusion stands for every other change of content, decks or research and for every gate, test and threshold."@en .

