ex:TK_SecLinks_Ch10_Research a backlog:ExecutionTask ; rdfs:label "State the relationships between the sections of chapter 10 as links in a new research version"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "TK_SecLinks_Ch10_Research" ; backlog:hasTitle "State the relationships between the sections of chapter 10 as links in a new research version" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Iter_14 ; backlog:admittedByOutput ex:Out3_BacklogR28 ; backlog:responsible ex:Executor_ClaudeCodeSession ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasTaskType backlog:TaskType_Build ; backlog:effectiveDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-21T23:42:23"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-21T23:51:14"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:lastAuditedAt "2026-10-22T00:09:19"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasExecutionModality backlog:Mode_Hybrid ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Ranked by its story's state; scoring both would double-count." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Discover the relationships between the 17 sections of chapter 10 with the OEE relationship taxonomy (read the research, the domain T-Box and A-Box, the document; run oe_link_discovery on the T-Box and A-Box pair; classify by category: semantic, syntactic, temporal, containment, ordering and succession, and by class kind where needed) and state them in a NEW research version as object-property links between the sections' individuals (the X_ individuals the page-data builder maps to sections) or classes, in the domain A-Box, with every property declared in the domain T-Box with domain, range, label and kb:hasRelationshipCategory, reusing a standard relation where one says it (as chapters 1 to 7 reuse rd:hasOwningConcept through chx:hasOwner); every section related to at least one other; no relationship stated only as text (ruling G134). Produce the new T-Box, A-Box, SHACL, document and research files as the chapter's package needs, run the Stage 3.F and Stage 4 gates and the Research chapter check on them. A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. No gate, test, threshold, criterion or page template is changed; STOP and report if any would be needed (including a relation type the template cannot draw). The OEE relationship taxonomy is oe-method/04-documentation/RELATIONSHIP_TAXONOMY_RESEARCH_v1_11_0.md (categories as kb:RelationshipCategory_* in oe-method/09-governance/oegov_abox_v1_36_0.ttl, properties kb:hasRelationshipCategory and kb:hasClassKind in oegov_tbox_v1_15_0.ttl); construction method BP-D58 (choose the relation: which category, is there a standard relation that says it, which pattern, what to declare), class kinds BP-D59, missing-link discovery BP-D57 (tool repo-tooling/oe_link_discovery_v1_1_0.py: syntactic, semantic, temporal families; file set = a T-Box and A-Box pair), kind rule check repo-tooling/oe_kind_rule_check_v1_1_0.py. OE v2.31.0 and v2.32.0 (ceremony of 2026-10-22: PROCEED, repo-tooling v1.77.0) add kind rules and two class kinds: they bind the ontology files and any research that declares a category or a kind; they do not bind the A-Box versions of this register. Satisfies the criterion ex:AC3L_Ch10." .

