ex:ST_Section_Links a backlog:Story ; rdfs:label "The research of chapters 10 and 11 states how their sections relate, as links, and their pages show the relationships"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "ST_Section_Links" ; backlog:hasTitle "The research of chapters 10 and 11 states how their sections relate, as links, and their pages show the relationships" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Iter_14 ; backlog:admittedByOutput ex:Out3_BacklogR28 ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ;
    backlog:asRole "SEN0401 instructor" ; backlog:wantsCapability "the relationships between the sections of chapters 10 and 11 stated in the research as links and shown on the ERD of their pages" ; backlog:soThat "a student sees how the sections of a chapter connect, the ERD labels can be measured, and the research, not the page builder, is where the relationships are stated" ;
    backlog:satisfiesDeliverable ex:Del3_SectionLinks ; backlog:pursuesObjective ex:Obj3_SectionsLinked ; backlog:hasAcceptanceCriterion ex:AC3L2_Ch10 ;
    backlog:effectiveDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD ; backlog:hasApplicableConcern backlog:Concern_Data ; backlog:responsible ex:Executor_ClaudeCodeSession ;
    backlog:decomposesInto ex:TK_SecLinks_Ch10_Research, ex:TK_SecLinks_Ch10_Page, ex:TK_SecLinks_PageData, ex:TK_SecLinks_Ch10_Verify, ex:TK_SecLinks_Ch11_Research, ex:TK_SecLinks_Ch11_Page, ex:TK_SecLinks_Ch11_Verify ;
    backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-21T23:42:23"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-22T17:31:35"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:lastAuditedAt "2026-10-24T10:22:59"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasExecutionModality backlog:Mode_Hybrid ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Not scored: the owner directed this work on 2026-10-22, so there is no ranking left to compute." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Owner's answer of Thursday 2026-10-22 01:24 Istanbul (2026-10-21T22:24:00 UTC), as relayed by the course coordinator; the time at which the owner wrote it is not known to the builder session to the question of ex:CR3_PageErd, relayed by the course coordinator and recorded by the builder session, quoted: \"Sections are linked with each other at least by menu, possibly by semantic, syntactic, temporal, concepts, content or other relationships. You need to discover it by using the OEE relationship taxonomy and if necessary class categorization in a similar manner.\" This is option (b) of the question, widened: the relationships between sections are discovered and stated in the chapter research as links (object properties), not text. Under the standing rule that work following the owner's direction is recorded as owner-directed, it is not listed as an open owner confirmation. One criterion per chapter (G133). Measured 2026-10-22 by the builder session from the newest page of each chapter (the relations the page test sees: page data relations between two different sections, counted by the same section map the page test 9.35.0 uses): chapter 10 has 17 sections and 0 relations between two sections; chapter 11 has 16 sections and 0; chapter 13 has 16 and 0; chapter 8 has 23 sections and 4 (16 sections with none); chapter 9 has 20 and 3 (14 with none); chapter 12 has 15 and 2 (12 with none); chapter 14 has 13 and 2 (10 with none); chapters 1 to 7 have every section linked (93, 50, 59, 39, 83, 110 and 52 section pairs). In chapters 1 to 7 the section relationship is NOT authored as a link between sections: it is the page-data builder's text co-mention ('mentions', evidence: the document's section on X names Y; 1,644 of the 1,683 cross-section relations of those chapters) plus a few 'operates on' relations that come from the domain link chx:hasOwner (a subproperty of RDODI's hasOwningConcept) between concept individuals of different sections (11, 4, 2, 3, 11, 4 and 4). The research of chapters 10 and 11 states no relationship between two sections: their domain T-Box holds subclass links inside sections and disjointness, their domain A-Box holds only the I/O examples (type, label, definition, source, input, output, hasIOExample); the OEE link discovery (oe_link_discovery) found only the syntactic pair input/output. The text co-mention does not arise in chapters 10 and 11 because their document text names no concept of another section." .
ex:ST_Section_Links backlog:standsAlone true .
ex:Obj3_ErdLabelsRun backlog:metricMovableBy ex:ST_Section_Links .
ex:Obj3_SectionsLinked backlog:metricMovableBy ex:ST_Section_Links .

