    backlog:hasAuditNote "Done, recorded 2026-10-22: delivered by the executor session SEN0401-I14-research-ch10 (commit d4dda4c); control run on the evidence bridge, serial, logs in 08-tooling/verify/iter14/ch10. Results as printed: Stage 4 gate runner v1_1_0 (current validator v1.13.0): verified -> OVERALL: PASS; chapter check Research v1_3_0 (pinned validator v1.6.0): verified -> RESULT Research/Ch10: PASS; section links declared, between sections, every section covered (sen0401_ch_seclinks_check v1_0_0): verified -> RESULT: PASS; every link annotated with the sentence that states it (sen0401_ch_seclinks_check v1_0_0 --evidence): NOT verified -> RESULT: FAIL; OE link discovery v1_1_0 (BP-D57, BP-D61 duplicate family): 0 beyond the baseline: verified -> VERDICT: PASS; OE kind rule check v1_1_0 (BP-D58, BP-D59): verified -> VERDICT: PASS; one property per category and super-property (floor of BP-D61), sen0401_lineage_research_check v1_0_0: NOT verified -> RESULT: FAIL (a measurable floor of BP-D61: one property per category and super-property; two properties in one group are one meaning unless they differ in cate. FINDING of the control (not an element of this task's text): (a) the research states one property per class pair, 26 properties for 28 links, with the same meaning stated more than once (five 'precedes' variants, six requirement variants, five comparison variants, two 'defend against an attack' variants): the owner's standing rule of 2026-10-21 is that real equals are one property with several labels (OE v2.27.0 BP-D61, v2.28.0 duplicate detector rule S6); the OE link discovery passes because it compares definitions word for word and finds no identical one, so it does not see this; the floor check 'singular' fails (groups of 4, 2, 5, 6 and 5 properties in one category and super-property); (b) the links carry no sentence that states them (0 of 28 annotated, chapter 11: 32 of 32). Both are repaired by a new task in the change route of the next versions, not by editing this delivery. Cause on the builder side: the brief generated for this task did not carry BP-D61 or the singularity rule; the brief tool v1_1_0 omitted it." .
ex:AC3L_Ch10 backlog:hasAuditNote "Control 2026-10-22 (record v0.163.0), research v1.1.0 of chapter 10: elements run by the bridge: Stage 4 gate runner v1_1_0 (current validator v1.13.0): verified -> OVERALL: PASS; chapter check Research v1_3_0 (pinned validator v1.6.0): verified -> RESULT Research/Ch10: PASS; section links declared, between sections, every section covered (sen0401_ch_seclinks_check v1_0_0): verified -> RESULT: PASS; every link annotated with the sentence that states it (sen0401_ch_seclinks_check v1_0_0 --evidence): NOT verified -> RESULT: FAIL; OE link discovery v1_1_0 (BP-D57, BP-D61 duplicate family): 0 beyond the baseline: verified -> VERDICT: PASS; OE kind rule check v1_1_0 (BP-D58, BP-D59): verified -> VERDICT: PASS; one property per category and super-property (floor of BP-D61), sen0401_lineage_research_check v1_0_0: NOT verified -> RESULT: FAIL (a measurable floor of BP-D61: one property per category and super-property; two properties in one group are one meaning unless they differ in cate. The criterion is not met yet: its page elements wait for the page tasks; the story stays InProgress. FINDING of the control (not an element of this task's text): (a) the research states one property per class pair, 26 properties for 28 links, with the same meaning stated more than once (five 'precedes' variants, six requirement variants, five comparison variants, two 'defend against an attack' variants): the owner's standing rule of 2026-10-21 is that real equals are one property with several labels (OE v2.27.0 BP-D61, v2.28.0 duplicate detector rule S6); the OE link discovery passes because it compares definitions word for word and finds no identical one, so it does not see this; the floor check 'singular' fails (groups of 4, 2, 5, 6 and 5 properties in one category and super-property); (b) the links carry no sentence that states them (0 of 28 annotated, chapter 11: 32 of 32). Both are repaired by a new task in the change route of the next versions, not by editing this delivery. Cause on the builder side: the brief generated for this task did not carry BP-D61 or the singularity rule; the brief tool v1_1_0 omitted it." .
