ex:CR3_Singular a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "Chapter 10 research: one property per meaning and a sentence on every link, found by the control of the research task"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_PageErd, ex:IA3_PageErd ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Raised Thursday 2026-10-22 (after 03:04 Istanbul, the last commit of the chapter 11 research session), as relayed by the course coordinator. Found by the control run of 2026-10-22 (register v0.163; logs in 08-tooling/verify/iter14/ch10): the chapter 10 research v1.1.0 (commit d4dda4c) states its 28 links with 26 properties, one per class pair, and the same meaning is stated more than once: five 'precedes' variants (precedesCompactBlockMode, precedesFeefilter, precedesHeadersRequest, precedesWtxidAnnouncement, relayNetworkPrecedesCompactBlocks), six requirement variants (buildsOn x3, requiresAddressExchange, requiresProtocolVersion, plaintextFramedBy), five comparison variants ('in the way of', 'differs in privacy from', 'shares its hash function with') and two 'defend against an attack' variants among four causal ones. The check 'singular' of sen0401_lineage_research_check v1_0_0 (a floor: no two properties share a category and a super-property, no two share a label) fails with groups of 4, 2, 5, 6 and 5; chapter 11 passes it with 6 general properties for 32 links. The OE link discovery passes chapter 10 because its duplicate family compares definitions word for word and finds no identical one. Second finding: the chapter 10 links carry no sentence that states them (0 of 28; chapter 11: 32 of 32, check 'annotated'). Cause on the builder side: the brief generated for the research task (sen0401_lineage_brief v1_1_0) did not carry BP-D61 or the singularity rule, and the criterion AC3L_Ch10 did not ask for the sentence. The rule applied is the owner's standing rule of 2026-10-21, as relayed by the coordinator on 2026-10-22: real equals (terms with the same meaning) are ONE property with several labels, not parallel properties (consolidate; OE v2.27.0 BP-D61 'one meaning, one term', v2.28.0 duplicate detector, rule S6). The delivered task stays Done (G125); the repair is a new Build task, ex:TK_SecLinks_Ch10_Consolidate, with its own criterion (G133: one criterion per unit; the criterion AC3L_Ch10 is not rewritten while the work under it runs), on the open story ex:ST_Section_Links. The deliverable ex:Del3_SectionLinks is unchanged: its text asks that the relationships be stated as links discovered with the taxonomy; one meaning one property is how the taxonomy and BP-D61 ask them to be stated. A new criterion is counted by the Backlog digest, so the route is a revision from the Backlog stage (G125 route 2), not from the Scope stage. Pending until the ScopeChange that admits the new criterion and task is recorded." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .

ex:IA3_Singular a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What the consolidation of the chapter 10 research costs, measured before it is started"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR3_Singular ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage3 ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:IA3_PageErd ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "Found by the control run of 2026-10-22 (register v0.163; logs in 08-tooling/verify/iter14/ch10): the chapter 10 research v1.1.0 (commit d4dda4c) states its 28 links with 26 properties, one per class pair, and the same meaning is stated more than once: five 'precedes' variants (precedesCompactBlockMode, precedesFeefilter, precedesHeadersRequest, precedesWtxidAnnouncement, relayNetworkPrecedesCompactBlocks), six requirement variants (buildsOn x3, requiresAddressExchange, requiresProtocolVersion, plaintextFramedBy), five comparison variants ('in the way of', 'differs in privacy from', 'shares its hash function with') and two 'defend against an attack' variants among four causal ones. The check 'singular' of sen0401_lineage_research_check v1_0_0 (a floor: no two properties share a category and a super-property, no two share a label) fails with groups of 4, 2, 5, 6 and 5; chapter 11 passes it with 6 general properties for 32 links. The OE link discovery passes chapter 10 because its duplicate family compares definitions word for word and finds no identical one. Second finding: the chapter 10 links carry no sentence that states them (0 of 28; chapter 11: 32 of 32, check 'annotated'). Cause on the builder side: the brief generated for the research task (sen0401_lineage_brief v1_1_0) did not carry BP-D61 or the singularity rule, and the criterion AC3L_Ch10 did not ask for the sentence. What moves: the Backlog digest of the third lineage once, when the stage is closed again (one more criterion, one more task); Scope, Goal and Objective digests do not move. New items: the criterion AC3L_Ch10_Singular, the Build task TK_SecLinks_Ch10_Consolidate (a new research version v1.2.0 as new files: one property per meaning with several labels, the same 28 link meanings kept, 17 of 17 sections covered, every link annotated with its sentence, the T-Box notes on standard relations such as BFO precedes and dcterms corrected where they are still true, all gates unchanged) planned into a NEW iteration ex:Iter_15 (the goal of ex:Iter_14 is frozen at its start; work added later goes to a new iteration or to the owner's rebaseline, which is not asked). Dependencies corrected: TK_SecLinks_PageData waited only for the chapter 10 research; it now waits for the consolidation and the chapter 11 research, because it reads the links of both and is tested on the consolidated chapter 10; TK_SecLinks_Ch10_Page now also waits for the consolidation. No page work has begun, so nothing is wasted; the chapter 10 page would otherwise have been built on 26 properties and rebuilt. Chapter 11 passes the same floor check and the sentence check and is not touched; its 'is followed by' (direct succession) and 'is earlier than' (order) differ in category and are kept as two meanings. The start of the ST_Section_Links story and the lineage status stay InProgress; the Done research tasks are re-admitted by admission, not re-dated. Interim: while the Backlog output is retracted the register shows the declared interim violations (G129). Nothing is waived and no gate, test, threshold or criterion is changed. Cost of waiting: pages built on parallel properties, a rule of the owner broken in the delivery. Cost of acting: four versions and one executor session of about ten minutes (the first research session took nine)." .

ex:Revision_Lineage3_Backlog6 a backlog:StageRevision ;
    rdfs:label "Revision of the third lineage from the Backlog stage: one meaning one property in the chapter 10 research"@en ;
    backlog:revisesLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:revisesFromStage backlog:Stage_Backlog ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_Singular, ex:IA3_Singular ;
    backlog:revisionReason "Found by the control run of 2026-10-22 (register v0.163; logs in 08-tooling/verify/iter14/ch10): the chapter 10 research v1.1.0 (commit d4dda4c) states its 28 links with 26 properties, one per class pair, and the same meaning is stated more than once: five 'precedes' variants (precedesCompactBlockMode, precedesFeefilter, precedesHeadersRequest, precedesWtxidAnnouncement, relayNetworkPrecedesCompactBlocks), six requirement variants (buildsOn x3, requiresAddressExchange, requiresProtocolVersion, plaintextFramedBy), five comparison variants ('in the way of', 'differs in privacy from', 'shares its hash function with') and two 'defend against an attack' variants among four causal ones. The check 'singular' of sen0401_lineage_research_check v1_0_0 (a floor: no two properties share a category and a super-property, no two share a label) fails with groups of 4, 2, 5, 6 and 5; chapter 11 passes it with 6 general properties for 32 links. The OE link discovery passes chapter 10 because its duplicate family compares definitions word for word and finds no identical one. Second finding: the chapter 10 links carry no sentence that states them (0 of 28; chapter 11: 32 of 32, check 'annotated'). Cause on the builder side: the brief generated for the research task (sen0401_lineage_brief v1_1_0) did not carry BP-D61 or the singularity rule, and the criterion AC3L_Ch10 did not ask for the sentence. The new acceptance criterion of the open story ex:ST_Section_Links is counted by the Backlog digest, so the Backlog stage is revised (G125 route 2): this version retracts the Backlog output Out3_BacklogR5 and rebuilds nothing; the next version rebuilds it, re-admitting the same items by admission, not re-dated. The change request CR3_Singular and the impact assessment IA3_Singular are in the previous version. The interim version is the declared transition (G129). Recorded as decided by the builder role: the owner's rule is the origin; the revision is the route that the rule needs." ;
    backlog:retractsOutput ex:Out3_BacklogR5 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:revisedAtCommit "d943d53" .
ex:Out3_BacklogR5 backlog:outputRetracted true .

ex:TS_ResearchCheck a backlog:ToolScript ; rdfs:label "research check v1_0_0 (singular, samepairs, annotated, seclinks, linkdisc, kindrule wrapper for the bridge)"@en ; backlog:scriptFileName "sen0401_lineage_research_check_v1_0_0.py" ; backlog:acceptsGraphPath false .
ex:TS_SeclinksCheck a backlog:ToolScript ; rdfs:label "section links check v1_0_0"@en ; backlog:scriptFileName "sen0401_ch_seclinks_check_v1_0_0.py" ; backlog:acceptsGraphPath false .
