ex:ST_Section_Links backlog:hasAuditNote "Control 2026-10-22 (record v0.173.0): AC3L_Ch10 NOT MET (elements (3) gates, (4) AC3T elements); AC3L_Ch11 NOT MET (elements (2) ERD, (3) gates, (4) AC3T elements). The story is Done only when every criterion is met (G125): it stays InProgress. TK_SecLinks_Ch10_Page and TK_SecLinks_Ch11_Page are Suspended, not Done. Research (links, consolidation) and PageData are Done and unaffected. ROOT CAUSE as facts. (1) The page test 9.35.0 asserts that any page whose chapter has relations between two sections shows 'mentioned-together' relations that the toggle removes (rels r2 > r3); the page-data builder derives 'mentions' only where another section's text names a concept label, and the new section links of chapters 10 and 11 are all links stated in the research, none a mention, so the assertion has nothing to remove; the old pages passed only because the test skipped that feature for them (NOREL: no relation between two sections). This is a test-design gap of the same family as the owner's open ruling on the chapter 13 test design. (2) The template 9.51.0 Untangle layout leaves boxes overlapping when many edges connect the section boxes (2 of 24 in chapter 10; the click crash in chapter 11 is an overlapped box). Changing either means a new test version or a new template version, which the written standard excludes; the executors correctly stopped, and no test, template, gate or threshold was changed. The change request ex:CR3_PageGates is open; no execution task is created until the owner decides." .
ex:CR3_PageGates a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "The pages of chapters 10 and 11 with section links fail page test 9.35.0 (a hard-coded assertion) and template 9.51.0 (Untangle overlaps): new test and template versions, or keep the old pages?"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_PageErd, ex:ST_Section_Links ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Found by the control 2026-10-22. ROOT CAUSE as facts. (1) The page test 9.35.0 asserts that any page whose chapter has relations between two sections shows 'mentioned-together' relations that the toggle removes (rels r2 > r3); the page-data builder derives 'mentions' only where another section's text names a concept label, and the new section links of chapters 10 and 11 are all links stated in the research, none a mention, so the assertion has nothing to remove; the old pages passed only because the test skipped that feature for them (NOREL: no relation between two sections). This is a test-design gap of the same family as the owner's open ruling on the chapter 13 test design. (2) The template 9.51.0 Untangle layout leaves boxes overlapping when many edges connect the section boxes (2 of 24 in chapter 10; the click crash in chapter 11 is an overlapped box). Changing either means a new test version or a new template version, which the written standard excludes; the executors correctly stopped, and no test, template, gate or threshold was changed. OPTION A (recommended by the coordinator): a new template version (an Untangle fix for dense section edges) and a new page-test version in which the assertion on mentioned-together relations applies only when the page has them, both as new files, with the old test and template kept as comparison; then ch10 and ch11 are rebuilt (new page versions), measured again, and the criteria can be met. OPTION B: keep the pages 9.77.0 of chapters 10 and 11; the section links stay in the research; the ERD-label element is recorded as unmeasurable and accepted by the owner. THE OWNER'S QUESTION: Do you approve building a new page template version and a new page-test version as NEW files (the old ones kept for comparison), so that the section-link pages of chapters 10 and 11 can be rebuilt and measured: the template with an Untangle fix for dense section edges, and the test with the 'mentioned-together relations' assertion applying only to a page that has such relations (yes or no)? If no, the pages 9.77.0 stay, the ERD-label element for chapters 10 and 11 is recorded as unmeasurable and accepted by you." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted  ;
    rdfs:comment "Owner's answer recorded 2026-10-22: Owner's answer of Thursday 2026-10-22 08:35 Istanbul (05:35 UTC), as relayed by the course coordinator; the time at which the owner wrote it is not known to the builder session to the question of ex:CR3_PageGates (Do you approve building a new page template version and a new page-test version as NEW files (the old ones kept for comparison), so that the section-link pages of chapters 10 and 11 can be rebuilt and measured: the template with an Untangle fix for dense section edges, and the test with the 'mentioned-together relations' assertion applying only to a page that has such relations (yes or no)?), relayed by the course coordinator and recorded by the builder session, quoted: \"Yes, proceed.\" This is option A of the request. Under the standing rule that work following the owner's direction is recorded as owner-directed, it is not listed as an open owner confirmation. Disposition stays Pending until the ScopeChange that admits the story is recorded in the Backlog version (G127 route)."@en .

