    rdfs:label "What the failing page tests cost, measured before any decision"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR3_PageGates ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage3 ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:IA3_PageErd ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "Affected: AC3L_Ch10 and AC3L_Ch11 (NOT MET), AC3T_Ch10 and AC3T_Ch11 (element 3 waiting on the new pages), ST_Section_Links and ST_Page_Template (stay InProgress), Iter_13 and Iter_14 (stay open; their ends are the owner's). Not affected: the research of chapters 10 and 11 (links and consolidation Done), the page data builder, the passing chapters 8, 12 and 14, the Mission outcome, closureCommittedAt and the Achieved status of the third lineage, which this record does not touch. The same test-design gap is likely to meet any other chapter later given section links (chapters 13, 8, 9, 12, 14; the earlier open owner question on extending the section links). Cost of A: one template version, one test version (the test and template are code of the shared tooling, so every later page test uses them; the old ones stay), a rebuild and control of two pages (about the cost of this iteration's page tasks plus a new Verify), and the chapters 8, 12, 14 pages need no change. Cost of B: no page work; ERD-label stays unmeasurable for two chapters with an owner acceptance recorded; the section links in the research are then shown on no page."  ;
    rdfs:comment "Impact assessment after the owner's answer (2026-10-22). Facts measured by the control of 2026-10-22 (register v0.173; logs in 08-tooling/verify/iter14/ch10 and ch11): page 9.78.0 of chapter 10 fails 4 of 370 features in each of the tests 9.34.0 and 9.35.0, which are 2 distinct features: (A) the ERD sections choice with the mentioned-together relations on by default (sections 17, relations 23 -> 23 with mentions off: the assertion r2 > r3 of line 1245 of 9.35.0 assumes that any page with a relation between two sections has 'mentions'; the page data holds 0 'mentions', because the builder derives them only where another section's text names a concept label, and the new section links are all 'operates on'); (B) the concept-map Untangle leaves 2 of 24 boxes overlapping (template 9.51.0, function rlUntangle). Page 9.78.0 of chapter 11 stops in both tests on a click timeout ('HeaderFields intercepts pointer events': the rect of the entity HeaderFields lies over the element the test clicks) after 161 passed features, fails the same assertion (A) (sections 16, relations 32 -> 32), and the executor's force-click diagnostic (a log, not a result) found 4 of 22 boxes overlapping; whether the crash comes from the layout (overlapping entities) or from the test is a fact the executor of the template task must establish. The ERD label features themselves run and pass on both pages (chapter 10: labels 23 -> 23, overlaps 0/0). Old pages (9.77.0) passed because the test skipped assertion (A) for them (no relation between two sections). Route: the scope excludes any change to a gate, a test or a threshold (ex:Excl3_NoGateChange, ex:Excl3_NoConceptGates) and a new template and new test versions are a new deliverable, so a StageRevision from the Scope stage (G127), seven versions (this one, the retraction, four stages, the fill), against the 'keep the old pages' alternative (option B), which costs no page work and leaves the ERD label element unmeasurable. Planned structure (not begun): a new story ST_Page_Gates in a NEW iteration ex:Iter_16 with T1 template (new version 9.51.1), T2 page tests (new versions 9.34.1 and 9.35.1), in parallel, and T3 regression (depends on T1 and T2; the new tests on the 14 shipped pages and on the pages of chapters 1, 8, 12 and 14 rebuilt on the new template); the existing tasks of ST_Section_Links in ex:Iter_14 then continue: T4 and T5 (the page tasks of chapters 10 and 11, now also depending on T1, T2 and T3, resumed after T_Suspend) and T6 (their Verify tasks). Why a new iteration: the goals of ex:Iter_14 and ex:Iter_15 are frozen at their start and adding work to them is the mid-sprint extension the owner ruled out on 2026-10-21 10:14 Istanbul; the tasks T4 to T6 stay in ex:Iter_14 with their story (a story is planned into one iteration only, L4). Disclosed consequence: the sprint goal of ex:Iter_14 says 'on the gates as they stand'; the owner's decision changes the test and the template, so that goal cannot be met as worded and the review of ex:Iter_14 will record it so; a rebaseline is the owner's. The criteria AC3L_Ch10 and AC3L_Ch11 name the tests 9.34.0 and 9.35.0 'unchanged'; they are not edited. Their successors AC3L2_Ch10 and AC3L2_Ch11 name the same five elements with the new test and template versions; the story ST_Section_Links points to the successors, the old criteria stay as history with their recorded result NOT MET. AC3T_Ch10 and AC3T_Ch11 (ex:Iter_13) name the same tests; their element 4 will be measured with the new test versions, justified by AC3P_Test (identical but for the named assertion); the note on each says so and nothing in them is edited. Not affected: the research of chapters 10 and 11 (Done), the passing chapters unless the regression shows a change, the Mission outcome, closureCommittedAt and the Achieved status of the third lineage. Risks: the template fix may change the layout of another page (the regression set rebuilds chapters 1, 8, 12 and 14 on the new template and runs the new tests: results equal to or better than stored); the new test must give the same result as the old on every page that has mentions (all 14 shipped pages run: old stored result against new run). Cost: about 11 hours of serial machine time (a page test run is about nine minutes; 14 shipped pages plus 4 rebuilt pages plus the two section-link pages), spread over one to two days."@en .

ex:Revision_Lineage3_Scope4 a backlog:StageRevision ;
    rdfs:label "Revision of the third lineage from the Scope stage: a new page template version and new page test versions, then the section-link pages rebuilt"@en ;
    backlog:revisesLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:revisesFromStage backlog:Stage_Scope ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_PageGates, ex:IA3_PageGates ;
    backlog:revisionReason "Owner's answer of Thursday 2026-10-22 08:35 Istanbul (05:35 UTC), as relayed by the course coordinator; the time at which the owner wrote it is not known to the builder session to the question of ex:CR3_PageGates (Do you approve building a new page template version and a new page-test version as NEW files (the old ones kept for comparison), so that the section-link pages of chapters 10 and 11 can be rebuilt and measured: the template with an Untangle fix for dense section edges, and the test with the 'mentioned-together relations' assertion applying only to a page that has such relations (yes or no)?), relayed by the course coordinator and recorded by the builder session, quoted: \"Yes, proceed.\" This is option A of the request. Under the standing rule that work following the owner's direction is recorded as owner-directed, it is not listed as an open owner confirmation. The work adds a deliverable (new template and test versions) and lifts, for the named changes only, the exclusions of any change to a gate or test; the lineage is in its closed Backlog stage, and a deliverable that is new is a StageRevision from the Scope stage (G127). This version retracts the Scope, Goal, Objective and Backlog outputs and rebuilds nothing; the next four versions rebuild them one stage each; the goals, objectives, stories and tasks already in the register, Done ones included, re-enter by admission and are not re-dated. The change request and its impact assessment were completed first. The interim versions are the declared transition (G129). Recorded as decided by the builder role: the route is what the owner's direction needs; the stage revision itself he did not decide." ;
    backlog:retractsOutput ex:Out3_ScopeR4, ex:Out3_GoalR4, ex:Out3_ObjectiveR4, ex:Out3_BacklogR6 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:revisedAtCommit "8620376" .
ex:Out3_ScopeR4 backlog:outputRetracted true .
ex:Out3_GoalR4 backlog:outputRetracted true .
ex:Out3_ObjectiveR4 backlog:outputRetracted true .
ex:Out3_BacklogR6 backlog:outputRetracted true .

