ex:Del3_PageGates a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ;
    rdfs:label "A page template version and page test versions that measure pages with section links, and the pages of chapters 10 and 11 rebuilt on them"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:derivesFromMissionClause "the research behind it and an interactive page"^^xsd:string ;
    backlog:hasDeliverableText "(1) A NEW page template file (version 9.51.1, over 9.51.0 which stays unchanged) whose concept-map Untangle leaves no two boxes overlapping on the pages of chapters 10 and 11 with section links, and in which the executor has established as a fact whether the click timeout of the page of chapter 11 ('HeaderFields intercepts pointer events') comes from the layout or from the test; (2) NEW page test files (9.34.1 over 9.34.0 and 9.35.1 over 9.35.0, which stay unchanged) that differ in exactly one assertion: the one on the mentioned-together relationships applies to a page that has such relationships, so that a page whose section relationships are all stated links is measured instead of failed by an assumption; every other assertion identical; (3) a regression measurement: the new tests give the stored result on the 14 shipped pages, and pages of chapters 1, 8, 12 and 14 rebuilt on the new template give a result equal to or better than the stored one; (4) the pages of chapters 10 and 11 rebuilt on the new template and measured with the new tests. Facts measured by the control of 2026-10-22 (register v0.173; logs in 08-tooling/verify/iter14/ch10 and ch11): page 9.78.0 of chapter 10 fails 4 of 370 features in each of the tests 9.34.0 and 9.35.0, which are 2 distinct features: (A) the ERD sections choice with the mentioned-together relations on by default (sections 17, relations 23 -> 23 with mentions off: the assertion r2 > r3 of line 1245 of 9.35.0 assumes that any page with a relation between two sections has 'mentions'; the page data holds 0 'mentions', because the builder derives them only where another section's text names a concept label, and the new section links are all 'operates on'); (B) the concept-map Untangle leaves 2 of 24 boxes overlapping (template 9.51.0, function rlUntangle). Page 9.78.0 of chapter 11 stops in both tests on a click timeout ('HeaderFields intercepts pointer events': the rect of the entity HeaderFields lies over the element the test clicks) after 161 passed features, fails the same assertion (A) (sections 16, relations 32 -> 32), and the executor's force-click diagnostic (a log, not a result) found 4 of 22 boxes overlapping; whether the crash comes from the layout (overlapping entities) or from the test is a fact the executor of the template task must establish. The ERD label features themselves run and pass on both pages (chapter 10: labels 23 -> 23, overlaps 0/0). Old pages (9.77.0) passed because the test skipped assertion (A) for them (no relation between two sections)." ;
    backlog:deliverableForArea ex:Area3_PageGates ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Work ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_Functional .
ex:Scope3 backlog:requiresDeliverable ex:Del3_PageGates ;
    backlog:coversArea ex:Area3_PageGates ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_PageGates, ex:IA3_PageGates .
ex:Scope3 rdfs:comment "Revised 2026-10-22 by the stage revision Revision_Lineage3_Scope4 on the owner's answer of Thursday 2026-10-22 08:35 Istanbul (05:35 UTC), as relayed by the course coordinator; the time at which the owner wrote it is not known to the builder session (quoted in the change request ex:CR3_PageGates). The statement above is unchanged (L-112). It now also requires ex:Del3_PageGates and covers the area ex:Area3_PageGates."@en .
ex:Excl3_NoGateChange rdfs:comment "Note 2026-10-22: the exclusion of any change to a gate, a test or a threshold is lifted for exactly two named changes by the owner's answer of Thursday 2026-10-22 08:35 Istanbul (05:35 UTC), as relayed by the course coordinator; the time at which the owner wrote it is not known to the builder session (ex:CR3_PageGates, option A): a new page-template file with an Untangle fix, and new page-test files that differ in one assertion; both as new files with the old ones kept, and measured against the stored results of the shipped pages. It stands for every other change: Stage 3.F, the Stage 4 gates, the chapter checks, the deck match check, every other assertion and threshold of the page tests."@en .
ex:Excl3_NoConceptGates rdfs:comment "Note 2026-10-22: the exclusion of a change of any test is lifted for the one named assertion by the owner's answer of Thursday 2026-10-22 08:35 Istanbul (05:35 UTC), as relayed by the course coordinator; the time at which the owner wrote it is not known to the builder session (ex:CR3_PageGates); the other parts of this exclusion stand."@en .

