ex:TS_GateCheck a backlog:ToolScript ; rdfs:label "gate check v1_0_0 (the exit-code form of the elements of the criteria of the page gates: new files, byte-identical old files, only-the-named-lines diffs, regression equality; written by the builder session before the control run, never run by an executor)"@en ; backlog:scriptFileName "sen0401_lineage_gate_check_v1_0_0.py" ; backlog:acceptsGraphPath false .
ex:TS_PageCheck2 a backlog:ToolScript ; rdfs:label "page check wrapper v1_1_0 (links, ERD labels, tests, counts, Stage 4 page ABox, nothing edited; page 9.79.0 and later by argument)"@en ; backlog:scriptFileName "sen0401_lineage_page_check_v1_1_0.py" ; backlog:acceptsGraphPath false .

ex:AC3P_Template a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; rdfs:label "The page template 9.51.1 is a new file that differs from 9.51.0 only in the Untangle layout code, and the concept map of the pages with section links leaves no two boxes overlapping"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Owner's answer of Thursday 2026-10-22 08:35 Istanbul (05:35 UTC), as relayed by the course coordinator; the time at which the owner wrote it is not known to the builder session: \"Yes, proceed.\" to the question: Do you approve building a new page template version and a new page-test version as NEW files (the old ones kept for comparison), so that the section-link pages of chapters 10 and 11 can be rebuilt and measured: the template with an Untangle fix for dense section edges, and the test with the 'mentioned-together relations' assertion applying only to a page that has such relations (yes or no)? Given the page template 9.51.0 (SHA-256 cab2ab8809507acf42805ad67b0c1181ce73d65edcc05e864d0ca5ade2e543a4) whose concept-map Untangle (function rlUntangle, from line 684 of the file) leaves boxes overlapping on pages with dense section edges (chapter 10: 2 of 24 boxes; chapter 11: 4 of 22 per the executor's diagnostic), when a NEW template file course_page_template_v9_51_1.html is made, then ALL of: (1) the file is new, the file 9.51.0 is byte-identical to the SHA-256 above, and the version comment names 9.51.1 and its reason; (2) the difference between 9.51.0 and 9.51.1 is limited to the layout code the executor names (the function rlUntangle and, only if the analysis of (4) shows it is the cause, erdUntangle), with the line ranges and the reason for each hunk stated in the report; no other function, text, style or threshold differs; (3) on the pages of chapters 10 and 11 rebuilt on 9.51.1, the concept-map Untangle leaves no two boxes overlapping, measured as the page test measures it (24 boxes and 22 boxes, overlaps 0); (4) the click timeout of the page of chapter 11 ('HeaderFields intercepts pointer events') is analysed and reported as a FACT with its measurements - whether it is the template layout (overlapping entities, one intercepting the pointer events) or a test artefact; a force-click, a changed click target or any workaround is never part of a result; (5) no gate, no test, no threshold and no criterion is changed by this task; results are reported as printed; if any element fails the template is named failing." ;
    backlog:measuredWithTool ex:TS_PageTest34b, ex:TS_PageTest35b, ex:TS_PageTemplateB, ex:TS_GateCheck, ex:TS_PageCheck2, ex:TS_PageTest35, ex:TS_PageTest34 ;
    backlog:measuredWithVersion "template 9.51.0 and tests 9.34.0 and 9.35.0 as comparison (SHA-256 recorded in the text); template 9.51.1; gate check v1_0_0; page check wrapper v1_1_0" ;
    backlog:satisfiedByArtifact "the new template or test files cited by SHA-256, the logs of the runs and the diffs, verified by the evidence bridge" ;
    backlog:coveredByCase ex:TC3P_G_Passes, ex:TC3P_G_Unchanged .

ex:AC3P_Test a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; rdfs:label "The page tests 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 are new files that differ from 9.34.0 and 9.35.0 only in the assertion on mentioned-together relationships"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Owner's answer of Thursday 2026-10-22 08:35 Istanbul (05:35 UTC), as relayed by the course coordinator; the time at which the owner wrote it is not known to the builder session: \"Yes, proceed.\" to the question: Do you approve building a new page template version and a new page-test version as NEW files (the old ones kept for comparison), so that the section-link pages of chapters 10 and 11 can be rebuilt and measured: the template with an Untangle fix for dense section edges, and the test with the 'mentioned-together relations' assertion applying only to a page that has such relations (yes or no)? Given the page tests 9.34.0 (SHA-256 545a7d9470c959e4a9d6a568370e6f51f4f7dcb45d84975aa1e6c8ecdcdd2675) and 9.35.0 (SHA-256 a8a39cc9b943cdd99a43f66d755fc6c7c22015131211e43009436125e7e113bf), whose assertion 'the ERD's sections choice draws one entity per section with the mentioned-together relationships on by default (the toggle removes them), and the page's schema stays the third choice' (9.35.0 line 1245; 9.34.0 the same feature) requires r2 > r3 on every page that has a relation between two sections, when NEW test files sen0401_page_test_v9_34_1.py and sen0401_page_test_v9_35_1.py are made, then ALL of: (1) the files are new and 9.34.0 and 9.35.0 are byte-identical to the SHA-256 above; (2) the difference from 9.34.0 and from 9.35.0 is limited to the version lines and comments and to that one assertion: on a page that has 'mentions' relations the assertion is unchanged (r2 > r3); on a page that has relations between two sections but no 'mentions' the assertion is r2 == r3 and r2 > 0 (the toggle has nothing to remove); the NOREL branch is unchanged; every other feature, skip, threshold and line is textually identical, shown by a diff and by the set of feature texts being equal; (3) the new tests are run on one page that has mentions (chapter 1, page 9.77.0 or the newest) and on the page 9.78.0 of chapter 10: the first gives the stored result, the second no longer fails on that assertion; (4) no gate, threshold or other test is changed; results are reported as printed; if any element fails the tests are named failing." ;
    backlog:measuredWithTool ex:TS_PageTest34b, ex:TS_PageTest35b, ex:TS_PageTemplateB, ex:TS_GateCheck, ex:TS_PageCheck2, ex:TS_PageTest35, ex:TS_PageTest34 ;
    backlog:measuredWithVersion "tests 9.34.0 and 9.35.0 as comparison (SHA-256 recorded in the text); tests 9.34.1 and 9.35.1; gate check v1_0_0; page check wrapper v1_1_0" ;
    backlog:satisfiedByArtifact "the new template or test files cited by SHA-256, the logs of the runs and the diffs, verified by the evidence bridge" ;
    backlog:coveredByCase ex:TC3P_G_Passes, ex:TC3P_G_Unchanged .

ex:AC3P_Regression a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; rdfs:label "The new template and tests give every shipped page the result its stored result has, and the pages of chapters 1, 8, 12 and 14 rebuilt on the new template an equal or better one"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Owner's answer of Thursday 2026-10-22 08:35 Istanbul (05:35 UTC), as relayed by the course coordinator; the time at which the owner wrote it is not known to the builder session: \"Yes, proceed.\". Given the new template 9.51.1 (task TK_PageGates_Template) and the new page tests 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 (task TK_PageGates_Test), when they are measured against the stored results of the pages, then ALL of: (1) the new tests 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 run on each of the 14 shipped pages (the newest page of each chapter as it stands; chapters 10 and 11: 9.77.0) give the result the old tests stored: widgets, features passed, failed, skipped and gates equal or better, and on a page that has mentions identical in failed and skipped; (2) the pages of chapters 1, 8, 12 and 14 are rebuilt (to a scratch folder, not shipped) on the template 9.51.1 with the page builder v4_14_0 and the page-data builder that built them, and the new tests give for each a result equal to or better than its stored result; (3) each run is kept as a log; a main-thread budget failure is run again up to three times, every run kept; a [FAIL] is a result; (4) no gate, test, threshold or committed file is changed; results are reported as printed; if any page differs the new versions are named failing and the differing features are listed." ;
    backlog:measuredWithTool ex:TS_PageTest34b, ex:TS_PageTest35b, ex:TS_PageTemplateB, ex:TS_GateCheck, ex:TS_PageCheck2, ex:TS_PageTest35, ex:TS_PageTest34 ;
    backlog:measuredWithVersion "tests 9.34.1 and 9.35.1; template 9.51.1; page builder v4_14_0; stored results test_results_abox of the shipped pages; gate check v1_0_0; page check wrapper v1_1_0" ;
    backlog:satisfiedByArtifact "the new template or test files cited by SHA-256, the logs of the runs and the diffs, verified by the evidence bridge" ;
    backlog:coveredByCase ex:TC3P_G_Passes, ex:TC3P_G_Unchanged .

ex:AC3L2_Ch10 a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; rdfs:label "The research of chapter 10 states how its sections relate as links, and its page, rebuilt on the new template, shows them with the ERD labels measured by the new page tests"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Owner's answer of Thursday 2026-10-22 08:35 Istanbul (05:35 UTC), as relayed by the course coordinator; the time at which the owner wrote it is not known to the builder session (change request ex:CR3_PageGates): \"Yes, proceed.\". Given the research of chapter 10 (17 sections, section links Done) and the page 9.78.0 (failing the page tests 9.34.0 and 9.35.0 on the assertion on mentions and on the Untangle overlap), when the page is rebuilt as a new page version (9.79.0) on the template 9.51.1 and the tests 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 are run, then ALL of: (1) links: every one of the 17 sections is related to at least one other section by a stated link, and no relationship is stated as text only; (2) ERD: the page tests 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 run their ERD label features (the filled ERD overlap and labels-over-entity reading, and the on-choice labels mode) with no skip and pass them, labels shown after Untangle at least 95 percent of the grid's, and the run ends without a crash; (3) gates: the Stage 4 gate runner v1_1_0 for 10 (reading the current validator v1.13.0) exits 0 with Stage3.F, Stage4.A, B, cov, sub and src PASS, and the Research, Deck and Page chapter checks v1_3_0 (reading the pinned validator v1.6.0) pass; (4) the five elements of the criterion AC3T_ChAC3L_Ch10 are measured on the new page and all pass: the template markers, pages_deck_match_verify with 0 not carried, the page tests 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 with counts equal to or better than the stored result of 9.77.0, the Stage 4 page ABox rebuilt as a new file and the stored page-test result as a new file; (5) no committed file is edited and no gate, test, threshold or criterion is changed beyond the two new test files and the new template file of this iteration; results are reported as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN) and a skip is not a pass; if any element fails the chapter is named failing and this criterion has no passing result." ;
    backlog:measuredWithTool ex:TS_PageTest34b, ex:TS_PageTest35b, ex:TS_PageTemplateB, ex:TS_GateCheck, ex:TS_PageCheck2, ex:TS_Stage4Gates, ex:TS_ChapterCheck, ex:TS_DeckMatch, ex:TS_RdodiValidatorCurrent, ex:TS_RdodiValidatorPinned, ex:TS_LinkDiscovery ;
    backlog:measuredWithVersion "page tests 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 (new files; identical to 9.34.0 and 9.35.0 in every feature except the one named assertion, proved by AC3P_Test); page template 9.51.1 (new file; identical to 9.51.0 except the named layout code, proved by AC3P_Template); Stage 4 gate runner v1_1_0 reading the CURRENT RDODI validator v1.13.0; chapter check v1_3_0 reading the PINNED RDODI validator v1.6.0; deck match check v1_0_0; page check wrapper v1_1_0; research check v1_0_0" ;
