ex:TK_PageGates_Template a backlog:ExecutionTask ; rdfs:label "Make a new page template version 9.51.1 whose Untangle leaves no two boxes overlapping on pages with dense section edges"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "TK_PageGates_Template" ; backlog:hasTitle "Make a new page template version 9.51.1 whose Untangle leaves no two boxes overlapping on pages with dense section edges" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Iter_16 ; backlog:admittedByOutput ex:Out3_BacklogR28 ; backlog:responsible ex:Executor_ClaudeCodeSession ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasTaskType backlog:TaskType_Build ; backlog:effectiveDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-22T06:54:06"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-22T07:00:09"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:lastAuditedAt "2026-10-22T08:07:00"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasExecutionModality backlog:Mode_Hybrid ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Ranked by its story's state; scoring both would double-count." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Write the NEW file 08-tooling/course_page_template_v9_51_1.html from course_page_template_v9_51_0.html (which stays byte-identical, SHA-256 cab2ab8809507acf42805ad67b0c1181ce73d65edcc05e864d0ca5ade2e543a4). The failing layout code is the concept map's Untangle, function rlUntangle (the force-directed relocation, from line 684 of the 9.51.0 file: repulsion within two box-lengths, springs along edges, a pull to the centre, chunks), which on the pages 9.78.0 of chapter 10 (2 of 24 boxes overlap after Untangle) and of chapter 11 (4 of 22 per the executor's force-click diagnostic) leaves boxes overlapping when many edges join the section boxes; the ERD's own layout is erdUntangle (line 1536). FIRST establish as a FACT, with measurements (positions of the overlapping rects, the entity HeaderFields on the page of chapter 11, which element is intercepted, which template function placed the boxes), whether the click timeout of the page of chapter 11 ('HeaderFields intercepts pointer events') comes from the template layout (entities overlapping so that one intercepts the pointer events: probably the same layout cause) or from the test; write the finding into your report; a force-click, a changed click target or any workaround is not allowed in a result. THEN change only the layout code the finding names (rlUntangle and, if it is the cause, erdUntangle), keeping the drawn shape, the Reset, the drag behaviour and the speed; no other function, text, style or threshold differs. The page builder v4_14_0 takes the template by argument or default: state how you built the pages (the template path you passed). Build scratch copies of the pages of chapters 10 and 11 (page 9.78.0 data, template 9.51.1) in a folder outside the repository and measure that no two concept-map boxes overlap after Untangle (the measure of the page test: boxes and overlaps), and that the click no longer times out; do NOT run the full page tests (the regression task does). Commit the new template file and a short evidence file (08-tooling/page-gates-evidence/template_v9_51_1.md) with the diff summary (functions, line ranges, reason) and the finding. A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate or a test beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN). Satisfies the criterion ex:AC3P_Template." .

ex:TK_PageGates_Test a backlog:ExecutionTask ; rdfs:label "Make new page test versions 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 whose assertion on mentioned-together relationships applies to a page that has such relationships"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "TK_PageGates_Test" ; backlog:hasTitle "Make new page test versions 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 whose assertion on mentioned-together relationships applies to a page that has such relationships" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Iter_16 ; backlog:admittedByOutput ex:Out3_BacklogR28 ; backlog:responsible ex:Executor_ClaudeCodeSession ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasTaskType backlog:TaskType_Build ; backlog:effectiveDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-22T06:54:06"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-22T07:45:28"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:lastAuditedAt "2026-10-22T08:07:00"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasExecutionModality backlog:Mode_Hybrid ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Ranked by its story's state; scoring both would double-count." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Write the NEW files 08-tooling/sen0401_page_test_v9_34_1.py and sen0401_page_test_v9_35_1.py from 9.34.0 and 9.35.0 (which stay byte-identical, SHA-256 545a7d9470c959e4a9d6a568370e6f51f4f7dcb45d84975aa1e6c8ecdcdd2675 and a8a39cc9b943cdd99a43f66d755fc6c7c22015131211e43009436125e7e113bf). The assertion is the feature \"the ERD's sections choice draws one entity per section with the mentioned-together relationships on by default (the toggle removes them), and the page's schema stays the third choice\" (9.35.0 line 1245): it requires r2 > r3 (relations drawn with mentions on against off) on any page that has a relation between two sections, which assumes such a page has 'mentions'; the page data of chapters 10 and 11 holds 0 'mentions' (the new section links are all 'operates on'). Change it so that: a page that has 'mentions' relations (type mentions between two different sections in the page data, counted as NOREL counts sections) keeps r2 > r3; a page that has relations between two sections but no 'mentions' requires r2 == r3 and r2 > 0; the NOREL branch is unchanged. Every other feature, skip, threshold and line stays textually identical except the version line, the version comment (state the owner's decision and the reason) and the lines this one assertion needs. Show it: a unified diff of each new file against its old file, and the proof that the set of feature texts (feat/skip calls) is equal. Run the new test 9.35.1 once on a scratch rebuild or the shipped page of chapter 1 (a page with mentions: result equal to its stored result) and once on page 9.78.0 of chapter 10 (the assertion passes; other features as they were); about nine minutes per run. Commit the new files and a short evidence file (08-tooling/page-gates-evidence/tests_v9_34_1_v9_35_1.md). A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate or a test beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN). Satisfies the criterion ex:AC3P_Test." .

ex:TK_PageGates_Regression a backlog:ExecutionTask ; rdfs:label "Measure the new template and the new page tests against the stored results of the existing pages"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "TK_PageGates_Regression" ; backlog:hasTitle "Measure the new template and the new page tests against the stored results of the existing pages" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Iter_16 ; backlog:admittedByOutput ex:Out3_BacklogR28 ; backlog:responsible ex:Executor_ClaudeCodeSession ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_Compliance ; backlog:hasTaskType backlog:TaskType_Verify ; backlog:effectiveDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-22T08:21:33"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-22T14:15:44"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:lastAuditedAt "2026-10-22T14:46:30"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasExecutionModality backlog:Mode_Hybrid ;
    backlog:dependsOn ex:TK_PageGates_Template, ex:TK_PageGates_Test ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Ranked by its story's state; scoring both would double-count." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "After the template (TK_PageGates_Template) and the tests (TK_PageGates_Test) are Done: (1) run the new tests 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 on each of the 14 shipped pages (the newest page of each chapter as it stands, key-substituted TEST copy by sen0401_lineage_page_test_run_v1_2_0.py with PAGE_TEST set; chapters 10 and 11: page 9.77.0) and compare with the stored result of that page (test_results_abox of its folder): equal or better; on a page that has mentions identical in failed and skipped; (2) rebuild the pages of chapters 1, 8, 12 and 14 into a scratch folder on the template 9.51.1 with the page builder v4_14_0 and the page-data builder that built each shipped page, run the new tests on each and compare with the stored result: equal to or better. Keep every run as a log under 08-tooling/page-gates-evidence/regression/ (a main-thread budget failure may be run again up to three times, every run kept; a [FAIL] is a result); do not ship the scratch pages. Report a table: page, stored widgets/features/failed/skipped, new run, equal/better/worse. If any page is worse, report it and stop: the versions are named failing. About 18 runs at nine minutes, run serially. A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate or a test beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN). Satisfies the criteria ex:AC3P_Regression (and, with the other two, ex:AC3P_Template and ex:AC3P_Test)." .

ex:ST_Page_Gates a backlog:Story ; rdfs:label "The page template and page tests measure a page with section links by what it has, as new versions with the old ones kept"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "ST_Page_Gates" ; backlog:hasTitle "The page template and page tests measure a page with section links by what it has, as new versions with the old ones kept" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Iter_16 ; backlog:admittedByOutput ex:Out3_BacklogR28 ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ;
    backlog:asRole "SEN0401 instructor" ; backlog:wantsCapability "a new page template version and new page test versions that differ from the old only in the named parts, shown equal on the shipped pages" ; backlog:soThat "the pages of chapters 10 and 11 with section links can be rebuilt and measured by the page tests without a test assumption that does not hold and without overlapping boxes, and no shipped page changes its result" ;
    backlog:satisfiesDeliverable ex:Del3_PageGates ; backlog:pursuesObjective ex:Obj3_PagesMeasured ; backlog:hasAcceptanceCriterion ex:AC3P_Template, ex:AC3P_Test, ex:AC3P_Regression ;
    backlog:effectiveDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD ; backlog:hasApplicableConcern backlog:Concern_Data ; backlog:responsible ex:Executor_ClaudeCodeSession ;
    backlog:decomposesInto ex:TK_PageGates_Template, ex:TK_PageGates_Test, ex:TK_PageGates_Regression ;
    backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-22T06:54:06"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-22T14:15:44"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:lastAuditedAt "2026-10-24T02:19:04"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasExecutionModality backlog:Mode_Hybrid ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Not scored: the owner directed this work on 2026-10-22, so there is no ranking left to compute." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Owner's answer of Thursday 2026-10-22 08:35 Istanbul (05:35 UTC), as relayed by the course coordinator; the time at which the owner wrote it is not known to the builder session to the question of ex:CR3_PageGates (Do you approve building a new page template version and a new page-test version as NEW files (the old ones kept for comparison), so that the section-link pages of chapters 10 and 11 can be rebuilt and measured: the template with an Untangle fix for dense section edges, and the test with the 'mentioned-together relations' assertion applying only to a page that has such relations (yes or no)?), relayed by the course coordinator and recorded by the builder session, quoted: \"Yes, proceed.\" This is option A of the request. Under the standing rule that work following the owner's direction is recorded as owner-directed, it is not listed as an open owner confirmation. One criterion per unit (G133). Facts measured by the control of 2026-10-22 (register v0.173; logs in 08-tooling/verify/iter14/ch10 and ch11): page 9.78.0 of chapter 10 fails 4 of 370 features in each of the tests 9.34.0 and 9.35.0, which are 2 distinct features: (A) the ERD sections choice with the mentioned-together relations on by default (sections 17, relations 23 -> 23 with mentions off: the assertion r2 > r3 of line 1245 of 9.35.0 assumes that any page with a relation between two sections has 'mentions'; the page data holds 0 'mentions', because the builder derives them only where another section's text names a concept label, and the new section links are all 'operates on'); (B) the concept-map Untangle leaves 2 of 24 boxes overlapping (template 9.51.0, function rlUntangle). Page 9.78.0 of chapter 11 stops in both tests on a click timeout ('HeaderFields intercepts pointer events': the rect of the entity HeaderFields lies over the element the test clicks) after 161 passed features, fails the same assertion (A) (sections 16, relations 32 -> 32), and the executor's force-click diagnostic (a log, not a result) found 4 of 22 boxes overlapping; whether the crash comes from the layout (overlapping entities) or from the test is a fact the executor of the template task must establish. The ERD label features themselves run and pass on both pages (chapter 10: labels 23 -> 23, overlaps 0/0). Old pages (9.77.0) passed because the test skipped assertion (A) for them (no relation between two sections)." .
ex:ST_Page_Gates backlog:standsAlone true .
ex:Obj3_PagesMeasured backlog:metricMovableBy ex:ST_Page_Gates, ex:ST_Section_Links .

