    backlog:hasAuditNote "Done, recorded 2026-10-22: delivered by the executor session SEN0401-I16-template (commits 2654ae9); control run on the evidence bridge, serial, logs in 08-tooling/verify/iter16. Results as printed: (1) new file, old byte-identical: MET [template 9.51.1 is a new file, 9.51.0 byte-identical, version comment names 9.51.1: verified -> 9.51.1 exists True; 9.51.0 byte-identical to cab2ab88... True; version comment names 9.51.1 True; 9.51.1 sha256 d8c236ac89a3aa343be9bd5756827f79cd7ccb172face35cb6d1c5f5866ece0a] | (2) diff limited to the named layout code: MET [difference 9.51.0 to 9.51.1 limited to the version comment and the function rlUntangle: verified -> rlUntangle spans lines 685-690 of 9.51.1; removed lines 2, added lines 2; added outside the version comment and rlUntangle: []; removed outside rlUntangle: []] | (3) no overlap on chapters 10 and 11: MET [chapter 10 concept map after drag and Untangle: no two boxes overlap on 9.51.1 (scratch build by the builder): verified -> chapter 10 concept map after drag and Untangle: template 9.51.0 boxes/overlaps (24, 2); template 9.51.1 boxes/overlaps (24, 0); chapter 11 concept map after drag and Untangle: no two boxes overlap on 9.51.1 (scratch build by the builder): verified -> chapter 11 concept map after drag and Untangle: template 9.51.0 boxes/overlaps (22, 4); template 9.51.1 boxes/overlaps (22, 0)] | (4) click timeout analysed as a fact: MET [the click timeout of chapter 11 is analysed as a fact: test sequence, control log and the executor's evidence: verified -> test 9.35.1 drags the first ERD entity (found True) and later clicks entity nth(_ti) (found True); the control log of chapter 11 shows HeaderFields intercepting pointer events (True); the executor's evidence states the cause as a test artef] | (5) nothing else changed: MET [template task: no committed file edited (every file of its commit added): verified -> commits 2654ae9: 5 file(s) added, 0 changed or removed []]. DONE WITH A FINDING: the text of this task asks to measure 'that the click no longer times out' on the scratch build; the premise (the timeout comes from the layout) is refuted by the measurement, so that sentence cannot be satisfied by a template; the criterion of the task, which asks the cause to be analysed and reported as a fact, is met. FACT (measured by the executors SEN0401-I16-template and SEN0401-I16-test and confirmed by the control's check): the click timeout of the page of chapter 11 ('HeaderFields intercepts pointer events') is a TEST ARTEFACT, not the template layout. The test 9.35.0 (line 1261; 9.35.1 lines 1256-1263; 9.34.1 line 1259) drags the first ERD entity 120 px right and 70 px down over HeaderFields, GenesisQuirks and BackLinks, and then clicks the SAME entity (nth(_ti), the first end of the first relationship); HeaderFields, drawn later, covers it and intercepts the pointer. Before the drag no two entities overlap (16 entities, 0 pairs); the click works on chapter 10 because its first relationship starts at a different entity; template 9.51.1 gives the identical result, so no template change can remove it." .
