    backlog:hasAuditNote "Done, recorded 2026-10-22: delivered by the executor session SEN0401-I16-test (commits a626896, 0cfd139, aa9c24b); control run on the evidence bridge, serial, logs in 08-tooling/verify/iter16. Results as printed: (1) new files, old byte-identical: MET [tests 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 are new files, 9.34.0 and 9.35.0 byte-identical: verified -> 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 exist True; 9.34.0 and 9.35.0 byte-identical to the recorded SHA-256 True] | (2) diff limited to the one assertion: MET [tests differ from the old only in version line, comments, HASMENT and the one assertion; feature texts equal: verified -> lines changed outside version, comments, HASMENT and the one assertion: []; feature texts (old, new, equal in order): [(4, 190, 190, True), (5, 193, 193, True)]] | (3) chapter 1 equal to stored, chapter 10 assertion passes: MET [test 9.35.1 on chapter 1 page 9.70.0 (builder's run): equal to the stored result: verified -> distinct features 186 (stored result of page 9.70.0 with test 9.35.0: 186), widgets ('122', '122') (stored 122); test 9.35.1 on chapter 10 page 9.78.0 (builder's run): the mentioned-together assertion passes, no other failure than the template's overlap feature: verified -> page_test_9_35_1_9_78_0_run1.log: exit-0 False widgets ('86', '86') fails ['[FAIL] relocate on the concept map: a dragged box carries every edge naming it and opens no card; Untangle leaves no two boxes overlapping; Reset retu', '[FAIL] rel] | (4) nothing else changed: MET [test task: no committed file edited (every file of its commits added): verified -> commits a626896, 0cfd139, aa9c24b: 17 file(s) added, 0 changed or removed []]. The assertion that the mentioned-together toggle removes relationships now applies by what the page has; on page 9.78.0 of chapter 10 it passes, and the one other failing feature is the concept-map overlap of the template 9.51.0, which the new template removes (control of TK_PageGates_Template). The chapter 11 page is still not measurable by 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 because of the click (see ex:CR3_PageClick)." .
ex:TK_PageGates_Regression backlog:hasAuditNote "Fact for the executor, found 2026-10-22: stale temporary folders (/tmp/sen0401_page_test_* and /tmp/sen0401_fx_*) of earlier sessions filled the root disk to 28 MB free and crashed browser runs ('Target crashed', 'Page crashed') of the test task. Before each batch of runs, delete these folders when older than 60 minutes (find /tmp -maxdepth 1 -name 'sen0401_page_test_*' -mmin +60 and the same for sen0401_fx_*), check df, keep the logs. A crash with a full disk is not a result." .
ex:ST_Page_Gates backlog:hasAuditNote "Control 2026-10-22 (record v0.182.0): TK_PageGates_Template and TK_PageGates_Test Done on bridge-verified evidence; AC3P_Template and AC3P_Test MET; AC3P_Regression waits for TK_PageGates_Regression. The story stays InProgress. FACT (measured by the executors SEN0401-I16-template and SEN0401-I16-test and confirmed by the control's check): the click timeout of the page of chapter 11 ('HeaderFields intercepts pointer events') is a TEST ARTEFACT, not the template layout. The test 9.35.0 (line 1261; 9.35.1 lines 1256-1263; 9.34.1 line 1259) drags the first ERD entity 120 px right and 70 px down over HeaderFields, GenesisQuirks and BackLinks, and then clicks the SAME entity (nth(_ti), the first end of the first relationship); HeaderFields, drawn later, covers it and intercepts the pointer. Before the drag no two entities overlap (16 entities, 0 pairs); the click works on chapter 10 because its first relationship starts at a different entity; template 9.51.1 gives the identical result, so no template change can remove it." .
ex:CR3_PageClick a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "The page test clicks an entity it has just dragged under another one: may the new test versions change a second thing so the chapter 11 page can be measured?"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_PageGates, ex:IA3_PageGates ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Found by the executors of Iter_16 and confirmed by the control 2026-10-22. FACT (measured by the executors SEN0401-I16-template and SEN0401-I16-test and confirmed by the control's check): the click timeout of the page of chapter 11 ('HeaderFields intercepts pointer events') is a TEST ARTEFACT, not the template layout. The test 9.35.0 (line 1261; 9.35.1 lines 1256-1263; 9.34.1 line 1259) drags the first ERD entity 120 px right and 70 px down over HeaderFields, GenesisQuirks and BackLinks, and then clicks the SAME entity (nth(_ti), the first end of the first relationship); HeaderFields, drawn later, covers it and intercepts the pointer. Before the drag no two entities overlap (16 entities, 0 pairs); the click works on chapter 10 because its first relationship starts at a different entity; template 9.51.1 gives the identical result, so no template change can remove it. The owner's approval of ex:CR3_PageGates covers one change of the test (the assertion on mentioned-together relationships); this is a second, different change, so it is asked, not assumed. THE OWNER'S QUESTION: May the new page-test versions 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 change a second thing: after dragging an entity in the ERD, the test clicks an entity that is not covered by another one (the first end of the first relationship that nothing lies on), so the chapter 11 page can be measured? (yes/no) IF NO: the chapter 11 page cannot pass the page tests 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 (the run stops on the click), the criterion AC3L2_Ch11 stays unmet and the chapter 11 page stays as shipped (9.77.0). IF YES: new test versions 9.34.2 and 9.35.2 as new files beside 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 (which stay as built), a new task, a new criterion that the new versions differ from 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 only in that click and give them the same results on the regression pages, and the chapter 11 page then rebuilt and measured with them; the route is a revision from the Scope stage again (a test change is lifted by the owner one change at a time). Chapter 10 is not affected: its click works." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Pending .
ex:IA3_PageClick a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What the second test change costs, measured before any decision"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR3_PageClick ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage3 ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:IA3_PageGates ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "Affected: AC3L2_Ch11 and, through it, TK_SecLinks_Ch11_Page and TK_SecLinks_Ch11_Verify, ST_Section_Links and ST_Page_Template (ex:AC3T_Ch11). Not affected: chapter 10 (its click works), the template 9.51.1, the tests 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 as built, the regression task TK_PageGates_Regression (which runs 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 on the other pages and may start now: no shipped page is a section-link page whose first relationship starts at a dragged entity that another covers; if one is, the regression reports it as a result), the Mission outcome, closureCommittedAt and the Achieved status of the third lineage. Cost of yes: a revision from the Scope stage (seven versions, about the cost of v0.174 to v0.180), one test task (two new files, one changed line each, one run each on chapters 1 and 11, about 20 minutes of machine time), a regression equality check of the new versions against the old on the regression pages (about 18 runs, 3 hours), then the chapter 11 page task. The ordering of the work in the iteration: the page tasks already wait for the regression task; the new test would be inserted before them. Cost of no: none in work; chapter 11's section links stay in the research but unmeasured on a page, and the ERD-label element of its criterion stays unmet. No execution task is created before the owner answers." .

