es, skipped features and gates as the executor's runs and the stored results: verified ->   equal ch14 9_34_1 9.80.0 widgets 68/68 features 185/185 gates 6/6 skipped 0/0; equal to the executor's run (widgets, features, skipped, gates): True]. RESULT: MET: all elements are met; DEVIATION disclosed, not waived: the executor appended the rows of the rebuilt chapters to its own table R16_table_9_35_1.md after committing it (commit b903613); the criterion says every output is a new file. The file is its own output of this task, not a gate, a test, a template, a stored result or a page, and the stop condition of the criterion names an edit 'beyond the named new files'; no result depends on it, because the control computed the comparison again from the kept logs (elements 1 to 3) and the earlier commit holds the table as first written. Sample rerun: the control reran serially, by itself, chapter 13 page 9.69.0 with test 9.35.1, chapter 11 page 9.77.0 with test 9.34.1 and chapter 14 rebuilt as 9.80.0 with test 9.34.1; logs in 08-tooling/verify/iter16/regress. Why a sample and not all 36: the criterion asks the executor to run, keep and compare; the control re-checks every kept run (36 of 36) by an independent comparison and re-executes the runs of the three classes in which the new test or template can differ from the old (a shipped page with mentions skipped, the chapter the pending change request is about, a page rebuilt on 9.51.1); the other shipped pages differ from the old runs by the test lines proved identical by AC3P_Test. Nothing is waived." .
