ex:TK_SecLinks_Ch10_Verify backlog:hasAcceptanceCriterion ex:AC3L2_Ch10 ; backlog:hasEvidence ex:Ev21C_markers, ex:Ev21C_deck, ex:Ev21C_link, ex:Ev21C_seclinks, ex:Ev21C_erd, ex:Ev21C_test34, ex:Ev21C_test35, ex:Ev21C_counts34, ex:Ev21C_counts35, ex:Ev21C_abox, ex:Ev21C_nochange, ex:Ev21C_stage4, ex:Ev21C_research, ex:Ev21C_deckchk, ex:Ev21C_pagechk, ex:Ev21C_annotated, ex:Ev21C_linkdisc, ex:Ev21C_kindrule, ex:Ev21C_singular, ex:Ev21C_samepairs, ex:Ev3C_File_f9f26117ce, ex:Ev3C_File_e3ab488668, ex:Ev3C_File_bff5946748, ex:Ev3C_File_e073f1e837, ex:Ev3C_File_52f725ade9, ex:Ev3C_File_c1d5eee946, ex:Ev3C_File_4dcce843f8, ex:Ev3C_File_37b6d401ec, ex:Ev3C_File_b4bdcfcdbf, ex:Ev3C_File_6742c9e055, ex:Ev3C_File_9576e7e5ce, ex:Ev3C_File_ea0db58d79, ex:Ev3C_File_3da0f229fe, ex:Ev3C_File_69ae300829, ex:Ev3C_File_acaed0656b, ex:Ev3C_File_b21f24d76d, ex:Ev3C_File_d4fcb41bc3, ex:Ev3C_File_3bbfd668a6, ex:Ev3C_File_601251d2eb, ex:Ev3C_File_0afa8828fd ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Done, recorded 2026-10-22: the checks of the task ran one after the other on the bridge after the task started; results as printed: markers -> const LBLRE=LBL.map: True | function edVars(): True | deck -> chapter 10 page 9_79_0: 21 items compared with lecture_v1_1_0.json and sen0401_ch10_stories_v1_2_0; not carried: 0 | link -> chapter 10: 16 register entries, 0 not carried | seclinks -> RESULT: PASS | erd -> 9.35.1 ERD label features, final run: on-choice labels mode PASS lines ['PASS']; filled ERD PASS lines ['PASS']; SKIP li | test34 -> 9_34_1: 1 run(s) kept, final page_test_9_34_1_run1.log: exit-0=True widgets=(86, 86) fails=0 | test35 -> 9_35_1: 1 run(s) kept, final page_test_9_35_1_run1.log: exit-0=True widgets=(86, 86) fails=0 | counts34 -> 9_34_1 final run: widgets (86, 86), features 185, gates 6, skipped 0 | stored test_results_abox_v9_77_0.json: widgets 86 | counts35 -> 9_35_1 final run: widgets (86, 86), features 185, gates 6, skipped 0 | stored test_results_abox_v9_77_0.json: widgets 86 | abox -> Stage 4 page ABox 03-materials/ch10/page/sen0401_ch10_page_abox_v9_79_0.ttl: True | stored page-test result 08-tooling/c | nochange -> commits b1943e7, 8386e4a, 2f2e9b7, e8bdc14, 23e155f: 17 file(s) added, 0 changed or removed [] | stage4 -> OVERALL: PASS | research -> RESULT Research/Ch10: PASS | deckchk -> RESULT Deck/Ch10: PASS | pagechk -> RESULT Page/Ch10: PASS | annotated -> RESULT: PASS | linkdisc -> VERDICT: PASS | kindrule -> VERDICT: PASS | singular -> RESULT: PASS (a measurable floor of BP-D61: one property per category and super-property; two properties in one group ar | samepairs -> RESULT: PASS. The page-test elements read the logs of the builder's control run of the same page files on the same day (08-tooling/verify/iter16/ch10, the page and its SHA-256 are unchanged since); the page tests were not run a second time. NOTE on tools: the criterion AC3L_Ch10_Singular names OE link discovery v1_1_0 and OE kind rule check v1_1_0; the working copy of the OE repository now holds newer versions (v1_2_0 and v1_3_0) and no longer holds the named ones, so the builder restored the two named files from the OE repository history (oe_link_discovery_v1_1_0.py from the commit before repo-tooling v1.81.0, oe_kind_rule_check_v1_1_0.py from the commit before repo-tooling v1.80.0) into a scratch tree (OEE_ROOT=/tmp/claude-0/s/oe_old, the rest symlinked to the current repo-tooling and oe-method) and ran exactly the named versions; the newer versions were not run." .

ex:Revision_Lineage3_Scope5 a backlog:StageRevision ;
    rdfs:label "Revision of the third lineage from the Scope stage: the chapter 5 and chapter 6 decks and pages are remedied"@en ;
    backlog:revisesLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:revisesFromStage backlog:Stage_Scope ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_Remedy56, ex:IA3_Remedy56 ;
    backlog:revisionReason "Owner's messages of Thursday 2026-10-22, relayed by the course coordinator and recorded by the builder session. 17:27 Istanbul (14:27 UTC), quoted: \"I need the chapter 5 and 6 urgently. The HTML file Playground code list is crazily extends outside of the page space. You put the code there not the name of the code. Chapter code is not listed as far as I see. I need a specific tab just to run the chapter code matching with the same order of the ppt. Additionally, multiple concepts are presented on the same page with downward flow. You can add one more step to the hierarchy and build the details in lower level panels. Repeating the same menu items on the tab and left hierarchical menu is not good when the tabs are not fitting on a single line. PPT is very poor in content and just listing codes with sub shapes and concept names. They cannot be presented nor understandable. They are certainly not matches with any standards of teaching materials.\" 17:30 Istanbul (14:30 UTC), quoted: \"I want you to remedy the weaknesses and provide me Chapter 5 and 6 PPT and Interactive pages ready to use.\" The 17:30 message authorises the scope: remedy the weaknesses and deliver the chapter 5 and chapter 6 decks and interactive pages ready to use. Under the standing rule that work following the owner's direction is recorded as owner-directed, it is not listed as an open owner confirmation. The end of the iteration is still the owner's. The work adds deliverables (rebuilt decks and pages of chapters 5 and 6, a new page template, a new page test and a deck check, all as new files); the lineage is in its closed Backlog stage, and a deliverable added to a closed scope statement is a revision from the Scope stage (ruling G127). The change request ex:CR3_Remedy56 and the impact assessment ex:IA3_Remedy56 were recorded first (v0.186). This version retracts the Scope, Goal, Objective and Backlog outputs and rebuilds nothing; the next four versions rebuild them one stage each, a sixth fills the last commit; the goals, objectives, stories and tasks already in the register, Done ones included, re-enter by admission and are not re-dated. The retracted outputs and their digests stay as history (L-112). The interim versions are the declared transition (G129). Recorded as decided by the builder role: the route is what the owner's direction needs; the stage revision itself he did not decide." ;
    backlog:retractsOutput ex:Out3_ScopeR5, ex:Out3_GoalR5, ex:Out3_ObjectiveR5, ex:Out3_BacklogR7 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:revisedAtCommit "2a3f6e2" .
ex:Out3_ScopeR5 backlog:outputRetracted true .
ex:Out3_GoalR5 backlog:outputRetracted true .
ex:Out3_ObjectiveR5 backlog:outputRetracted true .
ex:Out3_BacklogR7 backlog:outputRetracted true .

ex:Area3_Remedy56 a backlog:ScopeArea ;
    rdfs:label "The decks and interactive pages of chapters 5 and 6, and the tools that measure the teaching-material standard"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:areaLocation "03-materials: the deck and page folders of chapters 5 and 6; 08-tooling: the new template, builders, page test and deck check as new files" ;
    backlog:areaMeasure "chapters of 14 whose deck and page meet the written teaching-material standard: 0 of 2 (chapters 5 and 6) today; after the work 2" ;
    backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Work .
ex:Del3_Remedy56Tools a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ;
    rdfs:label "A deck standard check, a page test with the page-standard features, and a page template 9.52.0 with its builders, as new files with the old ones kept"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:derivesFromMissionClause "the research behind it and an interactive page"^^xsd:string ;
    backlog:hasDeliverableText "(1) the deck standard check v1_0_0 (a new file, python-pptx 1.0.2) that measures the elements D1 to D12 and reproduces the measured facts on the two existing decks; (2) the page test 9.36.0 (a new file over 9.35.1, which stays unchanged; every old feature identical, new features for the page standard) that fails the two existing pages on the measured defects; (3) the page template 9.52.0, the page builder v4_15_0 and the page-data builder v2_24_0 (new files over 9.51.1, v4_14_0 and v2_23_0, which stay unchanged); (4) a control set of pages built from the new template that gives the old tests their stored result. WRITTEN STANDARD (the owner's standing teaching-material rules, from his recorded preferences; each element is measurable and none is a taste). DECK: (D1) every slide is numbered; (D2) no long paragraph: no text box over 30 words, full sentences allowed (python-pptx 1.0.2 count); (D3) every code slide carries an explanation beside the code (each line group has a plain-language note) and the executed result as a visualization, not REPL text (100 percent of code slides); (D4) every key concept has an everyday analogy (100 percent of the chapter's key concepts, listed in the research); (D5) every story follows 5N1K (who, what, when, where, why, how) with real names, a real picture and a live further-reading link; (D6) every chart is a native chart object, never a picture; (D7) speaker notes are short (at most 60 words per slide); (D8) a resources slide with links (community, corpus, seminal works, tutorials, videos); (D9) one consistent background scheme, no switching between dark and light mid-deck; (D10) each divider names its concepts with one line of meaning and one visual; (D11) the deck covers the chapter's concepts of the research (coverage counted against the research's concept list, and the result stated); (D12) the code blocks do not wrap. PAGE: (P1) no horizontal overflow at 390 px and at 1366 px (Playwright 1.56.0 measures scrollWidth); (P2) the chapter-code tab lists the deck's code examples by NAME, in the deck's slide order, each one runnable in the page with the chapter library defined in the page, and the code in the editor not in the list; (P3) the tab bar and the left tree are synchronised and their label sets are disjoint, or the tab bar is a single row; (P4) no third level of tabs; one more level of panels in the hierarchy so that one panel holds one concept; (P5) a panel fits the screen without scrolling (height at most 1.0 screen at 1366x768, stated measure); (P6) no duplicated list on a screen; (P7) every diagram has zoom; (P8) the menu is uncrowded; (P9) text size control and adaptive layout on phone, tablet and large screens; (P10) executed code results are visualized; (P11) the page and the deck carry the same code and the same look. The existing page tests 9.34.1 and 9.35.1, the deck match check, the Stage 4 gates and the chapter checks still pass on the rebuilt page; no existing gate, test, template or threshold is edited or weakened." ;
    backlog:deliverableForArea ex:Area3_Remedy56 ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Work ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_Functional .
ex:Del3_Remedy56Decks a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ;
    rdfs:label "The decks of chapters 5 and 6 rebuilt to the deck standard, each with its chapter-code manifest"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:derivesFromMissionClause "the research behind it and an interactive page"^^xsd:string ;
    backlog:hasDeliverableText "The decks of chapter 5 and chapter 6 rebuilt as new files that pass every element D1 to D12 of the deck standard, each with the chapter-code manifest of its code examples in slide order. DECK STANDARD (checked by the deck standard check, python-pptx 1.0.2, one named result per element): D1 every slide is numbered; D2 no text box over 30 words; D3 every code slide has a plain-language explanation beside the code and the executed result as a visual (a native chart, a table or a drawn diagram), not REPL text; D4 every key concept of the chapter has an everyday analogy slide or box (the key concepts are listed in the chapter research); D5 every story has who, what, when, where, why and how, a real picture and a live link; D6 every chart is a native chart object, no chart picture; D7 speaker notes at most 60 words per slide; D8 a resources slide with links; D9 one background scheme, no dark/light switching mid-deck; D10 every divider names its concepts with one line of meaning and one visual; D11 coverage: the share of the chapter research concepts that appear on a slide, stated as measured, not below 90 percent; D12 no code line wraps. MEASURED FACTS (fact-finding agent of the coordinator, read-only, tools Playwright 1.56.0 and python-pptx 1.0.2, date 2026-10-22; the builder session did not re-measure them and states so). PAGE. The Playground is one select with 97 options (chapter 5) and 106 (chapter 6); its width is 4861 px and 5836 px, and it is still that wide at 390 px in a container 242 px wide. 83 of 97 and 92 of 106 option labels read 'Name: code', so the whole label is the code (longest 840 and 828 characters); the chapter items are 76 and 85. Of the page items 4 of 76 (chapter 5) and 0 of 85 (chapter 6) appear in the deck. The deck code blocks are 18 (9 slides) and 21 (13 slides); they call chapter-library functions (master, ckd_priv, parse_tx, weight, block_subsidy, WORDS, TV, ALICE and others) that the page does not define, so a deck REPL line cannot be pasted into the Playground; the Playground items follow concept order, not slide order. The Learn tab bar has a second row of 8 folder tabs that repeats the 8 left-tree folders (8 of 8 the same label); the Learn sub-tab bar has 10 tabs, wraps to 3 rows (chapter 5) and 2 rows (chapter 6) at 1366 px and scrolls sideways at 390 px. The group panes stack 2 to 7 h4 concepts and are 3751 to 10754 px (chapter 5) and 2544 to 7530 px (chapter 6) tall; the Lecture pane has 23 and 26 cards and is 4107 and 4875 px tall; the Stories are 4.1 and 6.4 screens. DECK. Chapter 5 has 23 slides (average 74 words, longest box 39 words); chapter 6 has 26 (average 81, longest box 56). Of the code slides 9 and 13 are two REPL transcripts plus 3 caption pills; the executed result is REPL text, not a visual. Native charts: 1 and 3. Stories with 5N1K and a picture: 3 and 4. Analogies: 0 in both decks. The dividers (4 and 5) hold concept names only. Speaker notes are 31 to 98 words. A resources slide and slide numbers are present. Ranked page defects: (1) Playground select width and raw code; (2) no slide-ordered chapter-code tab, and the slide code needs the chapter library the page lacks; (3) the tab bar repeats the tree; (4) group panes stack concepts with no panel level below the group; (5) Lecture and Stories flow over 4 to 7 screens. Ranked deck defects: (1) code slides are transcripts plus captions with no visual result; (2) no analogies; (3) thin coverage of the 111 concepts; (4) dividers are names only; (5) charts are sparse; (6) page and deck code do not correspond." ;
    backlog:deliverableForArea ex:Area3_Remedy56 ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Work ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_Functional .
ex:Del3_Remedy56Pages a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ;
    rdfs:label "The pages of chapters 5 and 6 rebuilt to the page standard, with the chapter-code tab in the deck's order"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:derivesFromMissionClause "the research behind it and an interactive page"^^xsd:string ;
    backlog:hasDeliverableText "The pages of chapter 5 and chapter 6 rebuilt as new files on the template 9.52.0 that pass the page test 9.36.0 and the page tests 9.34.1 and 9.35.1, the Stage 4 gate runner and the chapter checks, with the chapter-code tab in the deck's order. PAGE STANDARD (checked by the new page test 9.36.0, Playwright 1.56.0): P1 no horizontal overflow at 390 px and at 1366 px; P2 the chapter-code tab lists the deck's examples by NAME in the deck's slide order, each runnable in the page with the chapter library defined in the page and its result visualised, and the code lives in the editor, not in the list; P3 tabs and left tree are synchronised and their label sets are disjoint or the tab bar is one row; P4 no third level of tabs, and one more level of panels so that one panel holds one concept; P5 a panel is at most 1.0 screen high at 1366x768; P6 no list repeated on one screen; P7 every diagram has zoom; P8 the top-level menu is uncrowded (at most 8 top-level tabs); P9 a text-size control and an adaptive layout at 390, 768 and 1366 px; P10 executed code results are visualised; P11 the page declares the standard and the examples equal the deck's code manifest." ;
    backlog:deliverableForArea ex:Area3_Remedy56 ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Work ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_Functional .
ex:Scope3 backlog:requiresDeliverable ex:Del3_Remedy56Tools, ex:Del3_Remedy56Decks, ex:Del3_Remedy56Pages ;
    backlog:coversArea ex:Area3_Remedy56 ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_Remedy56, ex:IA3_Remedy56 .
ex:Scope3 rdfs:comment "Revised 2026-10-22 by the stage revision Revision_Lineage3_Scope5 on the owner's messages of Thursday 2026-10-22 17:27 and 17:30 Istanbul (14:27 and 14:30 UTC), as relayed by the course coordinator (quoted in the change request ex:CR3_Remedy56). The statement above is unchanged (L-112). It now also requires ex:Del3_Remedy56Tools, ex:Del3_Remedy56Decks and ex:Del3_Remedy56Pages and covers the area ex:Area3_Remedy56."@en .
ex:Excl3_NoGateChange rdfs:comment "Note 2026-10-22: the exclusion of any change to a gate, a test or a threshold is lifted for exactly the new files named in ex:Del3_Remedy56Tools (a new page template, new builders, a new page test that only ADDS features and keeps every feature of 9.35.1, and a new deck check), by the owner's words of Thursday 2026-10-22 17:27 and 17:30 Istanbul (14:27 and 14:30 UTC), as relayed by the course coordinator naming the defects they measure (ex:CR3_Remedy56). No existing file, gate, test, threshold or criterion is edited or weakened; the old files stay as comparison. The exclusion stands for everything else."@en .
ex:Excl3_NoConceptGates rdfs:comment "Note 2026-10-22: stands unchanged for the concept-inventory gates; the deck standard element D11 (coverage) is a new measure of its own and does not change them."@en .

