ex:Spec3R_P a backlog:Specification ;
    rdfs:label "What it is for a page meets the teaching standard"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:specifiesGoal ex:G3_Remedy56Pages ;
    backlog:hasSpecificationText "PAGE STANDARD (checked by the new page test 9.36.0, Playwright 1.56.0): P1 no horizontal overflow at 390 px and at 1366 px; P2 the chapter-code tab lists the deck's examples by NAME in the deck's slide order, each runnable in the page with the chapter library defined in the page and its result visualised, and the code lives in the editor, not in the list; P3 tabs and left tree are synchronised and their label sets are disjoint or the tab bar is one row; P4 no third level of tabs, and one more level of panels so that one panel holds one concept; P5 a panel is at most 1.0 screen high at 1366x768; P6 no list repeated on one screen; P7 every diagram has zoom; P8 the top-level menu is uncrowded (at most 8 top-level tabs); P9 a text-size control and an adaptive layout at 390, 768 and 1366 px; P10 executed code results are visualised; P11 the page declares the standard and the examples equal the deck's code manifest." ;
    backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_Derived ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner ; backlog:producedByStage ex:Out3_GoalR6 .
ex:Scen3R_P_Passes a backlog:TestScenario ; rdfs:label "A rebuilt chapter page passes every element of the standard when measured"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Nominal ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec3R_P ;
    backlog:hasScenarioText "Given the rebuilt file of chapter 5 or 6, when the check of the standard is run, then every element is met, nothing is skipped, and the run exits 0." .
ex:Scen3R_P_NotClaimed a backlog:TestScenario ; rdfs:label "An existing chapter page that fails an element is named failing and not claimed"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Rejection ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec3R_P ;
    backlog:hasScenarioText "Given the existing chapter 5 or 6 file (measured 2026-10-22), when the check of the standard is run on it, then the failing elements are named and the story carries no passing result for it." .

ex:Model3R_UseCase a backlog:ModelArtifact ; rdfs:label "Who uses the rebuilt chapter 5 and 6 materials"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasModelKind backlog:Kind_UseCaseDiagram ; backlog:hasModelLevel backlog:Level_Analysis ;
    backlog:declaresState "The instructor presents the deck of the chapter in class and opens the page of the chapter on the same code, in the same order, with the same look; a student runs each deck example from the chapter-code tab on a phone or a laptop, changes it and sees the result visualised, and finds one concept per panel without scrolling through a stack of concepts; independent checks (the deck standard check, the page test 9.36.0) measure the standard; the evidence bridge verifies the runs; the owner reads the register to see which chapter materials are ready." ;
    backlog:describesItem ex:G3_Remedy56Pages .

