    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasTaskType backlog:TaskType_Build ; backlog:effectiveDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-22T18:28:30"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-22T18:31:26"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:lastAuditedAt "2026-10-22T21:11:45"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasExecutionModality backlog:Mode_Hybrid ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Ranked by its story's state; scoring both would double-count." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Write the NEW file 08-tooling/sen0401_deck_standard_check_v1_0_0.py (python-pptx 1.0.2): one named, exit-coded result per element D1 to D12 of the deck standard, for a deck given by chapter number, printing the measured number for each. DECK STANDARD (checked by the deck standard check, python-pptx 1.0.2, one named result per element): D1 every slide is numbered; D2 no text box over 30 words; D3 every code slide has a plain-language explanation beside the code and the executed result as a visual (a native chart, a table or a drawn diagram), not REPL text; D4 every key concept of the chapter has an everyday analogy slide or box (the key concepts are listed in the chapter research); D5 every story has who, what, when, where, why and how, a real picture and a live link; D6 every chart is a native chart object, no chart picture; D7 speaker notes at most 60 words per slide; D8 a resources slide with links; D9 one background scheme, no dark/light switching mid-deck; D10 every divider names its concepts with one line of meaning and one visual; D11 coverage: the share of the chapter research concepts that appear on a slide, stated as measured, not below 90 percent; D12 no code line wraps. Define each element's measure in the file header (words per text box, what counts as a code slide, an analogy marker, a native chart, a story with 5N1K, coverage against the chapter research concept list 03-materials/chNN/rdodi). Prove it by running it on the two existing decks (chapters 5 and 6, newest files): it must reproduce the measured facts (chapter 5: 23 slides, 9 code slides, 1 native chart, 0 analogies, longest box 39 words; chapter 6: 26 slides, 13 code slides, 3 native charts, 0 analogies, longest box 56 words) and report the failing elements, which is the baseline. Keep the logs. Do not judge your own deck: you do not build a deck in this iteration. A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores: browser tests run one at a time and no build runs beside them. Planned session SEN0401-I17-deckcheck; estimated start T0 after the executors begin, about 1.5 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

