    backlog:hasAuditNote "Write the NEW files course_page_template_v9_52_0.html (from v9_51_1, which stays byte-identical), sen0401_page_build_v4_15_0.py (from v4_14_0) and sen0401_page_data_v2_24_0.py (from v2_23_0). The owner's defects (quoted in ex:CR3_Remedy56): the playground list extends outside the page and shows code, not names; chapter code is not listed; multiple concepts stack on one page; the tab bar repeats the left tree and wraps. The template must: (1) show the playground as a list of NAMES that fits its container at 390 and 1366 px, the code opening in the editor; (2) add the chapter-code tab fed by the chapter-code manifest of the page data (an ordered list of named examples, each runnable with the chapter library defined in the page; FIRST establish as a fact how the page runs code today and what runtime the chapter library needs, and report it); (3) add one more level to the hierarchy: a group holds panels, one concept per panel, the panel at most one screen high; (4) tabs show only the sub-menus of the selected tree item, never the tree's own folder labels again, and never a third tab level (a breadcrumb instead); (5) keep every existing behaviour, id and test hook of 9.51.1 and add the DOM contract. DOM CONTRACT shared by the template, the page test and the page tasks (so the independent test can find what the template builds): the chapter-code tab is the tab with attribute data-pane=\"chaptercode\"; its list items have data-cc-item, the NAME of the example in data-cc-name and the deck's order number in data-cc-order; an item opens the example in the editor element data-cc-editor with a run button data-cc-run and a result element data-cc-result; the left tree items have role=treeitem and the tabs role=tab; one concept panel is an element with data-panel; the playground list items have data-pg-item and show names only; a page that follows the standard declares <meta name=\"page-standard\" content=\"9.52\">. The page-data builder reads the manifest file 03-materials/chNN/page/chapter_code_chNN_v*.json (written by the deck task of that chapter; if it is absent the page has no chapter-code tab) and the panel structure from the research. Build scratch copies of chapters 1 and 10 on the new template with the new builders outside the repository and show they build. Do NOT write the page test or judge your own work: the independent test is the task TK_Remedy_PageTest. A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores: browser tests run one at a time and no build runs beside them. Planned session SEN0401-I17-template; estimated start T0 after the executors begin, about 4.5 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

