    backlog:hasAuditNote "After the template (TK_Remedy_Template) and the page test 9.36.0 (TK_Remedy_PageTest) are Done: build the pages of chapters 1 and 10 into a scratch folder on the template 9.52.0 with the new builders and run the page tests 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 on each (serially, a run is about nine minutes, every run kept): each result must equal or beat the stored result of the shipped page; and run 9.36.0 with FORCE_STANDARD=1 on them. Justification of the control set: the new template is a new file used only by pages built from it; the shipped pages stay on their files and are not rebuilt, so their results cannot move; the set shows the new template keeps the behaviour the old tests measure on a page with mentions (chapter 1) and a page with section links (chapter 10). A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores: browser tests run one at a time and no build runs beside them. Planned session builder; estimated start T0+4.5h after the executors begin, about 1.0 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

