ex:TK_Remedy_Deck_Ch06_Build a backlog:ExecutionTask ; rdfs:label "Rebuild the deck of chapter 6 against the deck standard and give it its chapter-code manifest"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "TK_Remedy_Deck_Ch06_Build" ; backlog:hasTitle "Rebuild the deck of chapter 6 against the deck standard and give it its chapter-code manifest" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Iter_17 ; backlog:admittedByOutput ex:Out3_BacklogR28 ; backlog:responsible ex:Executor_ClaudeCodeSession ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasTaskType backlog:TaskType_Build ; backlog:effectiveDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-22T18:28:30"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-22T19:03:12"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:lastAuditedAt "2026-10-22T21:00:29"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasExecutionModality backlog:Mode_Hybrid ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Ranked by its story's state; scoring both would double-count." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Build the deck of chapter 6 as a NEW file with a new version number from the chapter research and the earlier deck's assets, to the deck standard. The owner's words (quoted in ex:CR3_Remedy56): the deck is very poor in content, only lists codes with sub shapes and concept names, cannot be presented nor understood. DECK STANDARD (checked by the deck standard check, python-pptx 1.0.2, one named result per element): D1 every slide is numbered; D2 no text box over 30 words; D3 every code slide has a plain-language explanation beside the code and the executed result as a visual (a native chart, a table or a drawn diagram), not REPL text; D4 every key concept of the chapter has an everyday analogy slide or box (the key concepts are listed in the chapter research); D5 every story has who, what, when, where, why and how, a real picture and a live link; D6 every chart is a native chart object, no chart picture; D7 speaker notes at most 60 words per slide; D8 a resources slide with links; D9 one background scheme, no dark/light switching mid-deck; D10 every divider names its concepts with one line of meaning and one visual; D11 coverage: the share of the chapter research concepts that appear on a slide, stated as measured, not below 90 percent; D12 no code line wraps. Rules from the owner's standing teaching-material preferences: full sentences are fine but no long paragraphs; explanation beside every code listing; the executed result shown as a visualization (native chart, table or drawn diagram) next to each listing; an everyday analogy for each key concept; 5N1K stories with real names, a real picture and a live link; native charts only; numbered slides; a resources slide; short speaker notes; a smooth colour scheme. ALSO write the chapter-code manifest 03-materials/ch06/page/chapter_code_ch06_v1_0_0.json: the ordered list of the deck's code examples (order number = slide order, a short NAME, the code that runs in the page with the chapter library it needs, the expected result), because the page tab must list the same examples in the same order. The deck generator is a NEW tool file; the checker is the independent TK_Remedy_DeckCheck (not yours): run it when it exists and report every element as printed. A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores: browser tests run one at a time and no build runs beside them. Planned session SEN0401-I17-deck-ch06; estimated start T0 after the executors begin, about 5.5 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

