ex:TK_Remedy_Page_Ch05_Build a backlog:ExecutionTask ; rdfs:label "Rebuild the page of chapter 5 on the new template with the chapter-code tab"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "TK_Remedy_Page_Ch05_Build" ; backlog:hasTitle "Rebuild the page of chapter 5 on the new template with the chapter-code tab" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Iter_17 ; backlog:admittedByOutput ex:Out3_BacklogR28 ; backlog:responsible ex:Executor_ClaudeCodeSession ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasTaskType backlog:TaskType_Build ; backlog:effectiveDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD ; backlog:hasState backlog:Cancelled ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-22T21:58:35"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:lastAuditedAt "2026-10-23T05:51:16"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasRationale "Closed 2026-10-23T05:51:16 UTC by the change route of ex:CR3_ChipScroll (v0.217.0): the task is superseded by TK_Repair_Page_Ch05_Build, which carries the rebuild of the chapter 5 page on template 9.52.1; it is withdrawn, not Done, and its earlier result (page 9.80.0 NOT MET on the story chip) stays in the register as history." ;
    backlog:dependsOn ex:TK_Remedy_Template, ex:TK_Remedy_PageTest, ex:TK_Remedy_Deck_Ch05_Verify ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Ranked by its story's state; scoring both would double-count." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Build the page of chapter 5 as a NEW file with a new page version on the template 9.52.0 with the page builder v4_15_0 and the page-data builder v2_24_0 (state how you passed the template), from the chapter research, the deck's lecture export and stories, and the deck's chapter-code manifest. Run the page tests 9.36.0, 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 (the runner with PAGE_TEST), serially, store the result as a new test_results file, and build the Stage 4 page ABox with the Stage 4 builder. PAGE STANDARD (checked by the new page test 9.36.0, Playwright 1.56.0): P1 no horizontal overflow at 390 px and at 1366 px; P2 the chapter-code tab lists the deck's examples by NAME in the deck's slide order, each runnable in the page with the chapter library defined in the page and its result visualised, and the code lives in the editor, not in the list; P3 tabs and left tree are synchronised and their label sets are disjoint or the tab bar is one row; P4 no third level of tabs, and one more level of panels so that one panel holds one concept; P5 a panel is at most 1.0 screen high at 1366x768; P6 no list repeated on one screen; P7 every diagram has zoom; P8 the top-level menu is uncrowded (at most 8 top-level tabs); P9 a text-size control and an adaptive layout at 390, 768 and 1366 px; P10 executed code results are visualised; P11 the page declares the standard and the examples equal the deck's code manifest. DOM CONTRACT shared by the template, the page test and the page tasks (so the independent test can find what the template builds): the chapter-code tab is the tab with attribute data-pane=\"chaptercode\"; its list items have data-cc-item, the NAME of the example in data-cc-name and the deck's order number in data-cc-order; an item opens the example in the editor element data-cc-editor with a run button data-cc-run and a result element data-cc-result; the left tree items have role=treeitem and the tabs role=tab; one concept panel is an element with data-panel; the playground list items have data-pg-item and show names only; a page that follows the standard declares <meta name=\"page-standard\" content=\"9.52\">. A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores: browser tests run one at a time and no build runs beside them. Planned session SEN0401-I17-page-ch05; estimated start T0+5.5h after the executors begin, about 3.0 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

