ex:ST_Remedy_Tools a backlog:Story ; rdfs:label "The page standard and the deck standard are measured by new tools and a new page template, as new files, without moving any existing gate"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "ST_Remedy_Tools" ; backlog:hasTitle "The page standard and the deck standard are measured by new tools and a new page template, as new files, without moving any existing gate" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Iter_17 ; backlog:admittedByOutput ex:Out3_BacklogR28 ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ;
    backlog:asRole "SEN0401 instructor" ; backlog:wantsCapability "the page standard and the deck standard are measured by new tools and a new page template, as new files, without moving any existing gate" ; backlog:soThat "the instructor can teach chapter 5 and 6 tomorrow from a deck and a page that meet the written standard" ;
    backlog:satisfiesDeliverable ex:Del3_Remedy56Tools ; backlog:pursuesObjective ex:Obj3_Remedy56Pages ; backlog:hasAcceptanceCriterion ex:AC4R_DeckCheck, ex:AC4R_PageTest, ex:AC4R_Template ;
    backlog:effectiveDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD ; backlog:hasApplicableConcern backlog:Concern_Data ; backlog:responsible ex:Executor_ClaudeCodeSession ;
    backlog:decomposesInto ex:TK_Remedy_DeckCheck, ex:TK_Remedy_PageTest, ex:TK_Remedy_Template, ex:TK_Remedy_Regress ;
    backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-22T18:28:30"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-22T20:00:13"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:lastAuditedAt "2026-10-24T15:39:28"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasExecutionModality backlog:Mode_Hybrid ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Owner's messages of Thursday 2026-10-22, relayed by the course coordinator and recorded by the builder session. 17:27 Istanbul (14:27 UTC), quoted: \"I need the chapter 5 and 6 urgently. The HTML file Playground code list is crazily extends outside of the page space. You put the code there not the name of the code. Chapter code is not listed as far as I see. I need a specific tab just to run the chapter code matching with the same order of the ppt. Additionally, multiple concepts are presented on the same page with downward flow. You can add one more step to the hierarchy and build the details in lower level panels. Repeating the same menu items on the tab and left hierarchical menu is not good when the tabs are not fitting on a single line. PPT is very poor in content and just listing codes with sub shapes and concept names. They cannot be presented nor understandable. They are certainly not matches with any standards of teaching materials.\" 17:30 Istanbul (14:30 UTC), quoted: \"I want you to remedy the weaknesses and provide me Chapter 5 and 6 PPT and Interactive pages ready to use.\" The 17:30 message authorises the scope: remedy the weaknesses and deliver the chapter 5 and chapter 6 decks and interactive pages ready to use. Under the standing rule that work following the owner's direction is recorded as owner-directed, it is not listed as an open owner confirmation. The end of the iteration is still the owner's. One criterion per unit (G133). The Done stories of chapters 5 and 6 (ST_Deck_Ch05, ST_Deck_Ch06, ST_Page_Ch05, ST_Page_Ch06) stay Done and are not edited (G125). MEASURED FACTS (fact-finding agent of the coordinator, read-only, tools Playwright 1.56.0 and python-pptx 1.0.2, date 2026-10-22; the builder session did not re-measure them and states so). PAGE. The Playground is one select with 97 options (chapter 5) and 106 (chapter 6); its width is 4861 px and 5836 px, and it is still that wide at 390 px in a container 242 px wide. 83 of 97 and 92 of 106 option labels read 'Name: code', so the whole label is the code (longest 840 and 828 characters); the chapter items are 76 and 85. Of the page items 4 of 76 (chapter 5) and 0 of 85 (chapter 6) appear in the deck. The deck code blocks are 18 (9 slides) and 21 (13 slides); they call chapter-library functions (master, ckd_priv, parse_tx, weight, block_subsidy, WORDS, TV, ALICE and others) that the page does not define, so a deck REPL line cannot be pasted into the Playground; the Playground items follow concept order, not slide order. The Learn tab bar has a second row of 8 folder tabs that repeats the 8 left-tree folders (8 of 8 the same label); the Learn sub-tab bar has 10 tabs, wraps to 3 rows (chapter 5) and 2 rows (chapter 6) at 1366 px and scrolls sideways at 390 px. The group panes stack 2 to 7 h4 concepts and are 3751 to 10754 px (chapter 5) and 2544 to 7530 px (chapter 6) tall; the Lecture pane has 23 and 26 cards and is 4107 and 4875 px tall; the Stories are 4.1 and 6.4 screens. DECK. Chapter 5 has 23 slides (average 74 words, longest box 39 words); chapter 6 has 26 (average 81, longest box 56). Of the code slides 9 and 13 are two REPL transcripts plus 3 caption pills; the executed result is REPL text, not a visual. Native charts: 1 and 3. Stories with 5N1K and a picture: 3 and 4. Analogies: 0 in both decks. The dividers (4 and 5) hold concept names only. Speaker notes are 31 to 98 words. A resources slide and slide numbers are present. Ranked page defects: (1) Playground select width and raw code; (2) no slide-ordered chapter-code tab, and the slide code needs the chapter library the page lacks; (3) the tab bar repeats the tree; (4) group panes stack concepts with no panel level below the group; (5) Lecture and Stories flow over 4 to 7 screens. Ranked deck defects: (1) code slides are transcripts plus captions with no visual result; (2) no analogies; (3) thin coverage of the 111 concepts; (4) dividers are names only; (5) charts are sparse; (6) page and deck code do not correspond." .

