ex:Iter_17 a backlog:Iteration ; rdfs:label "Iteration 17: the chapter 5 and 6 decks and interactive pages remedied to the written standard"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "Iter_17" ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:iterationStart "2026-10-22T18:09:01"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:iterationEnd "2026-10-23T23:59:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasDurationSource "Proposed by the builder session on 2026-10-22: the start is the instant of the planning ceremony ex:PC3_Iter_17; the proposed end is Friday 2026-10-23 09:00 UTC (12:00 Istanbul); the owner decides the end and the hour of tomorrow's class is not known to the builder. Justification (estimates, not measurements). Parallel on the 2 cores at the start (T0): the deck check (about 1.5 h), the page test (about 3 h), the template and builders (about 4.5 h), the deck of chapter 5 (about 5 h) and the deck of chapter 6 (about 5.5 h) are independent builds with python-pptx and light rendering. The heavy part is the browser tests, which run one at a time: baseline runs of the page test (2), the control set (4 runs), the page tests per page (3 each), and the builder's control runs (3 per page); about 3 hours of serial test time in all. CRITICAL PATH: deck of chapter 5 (5 h) -> its verification (0.5 h) -> page of chapter 5 (about 3 h, also needs the template and the page test) -> its verification (about 1 h) = about 9.5 h after T0 for the page of chapter 5; chapter 6 follows the same path half an hour later and its tests queue behind those of chapter 5: about 11 h. Estimated from T0 (executors start, expected about 18:15 UTC = 21:15 Istanbul if they begin at once): deck chapter 5 ready about T0+5.5 h (23:45 UTC), deck chapter 6 about T0+6 h (00:15 UTC), page chapter 5 about T0+9.5 h (03:45 UTC = 06:45 Istanbul), page chapter 6 about T0+11 h (05:15 UTC = 08:15 Istanbul) if nothing fails. The margin to the proposed end (09:00 UTC) is about 3.75 h, enough for one repeat of a page task (about 3 h) but not for two; chapter 5 is delivered about 1.5 h before chapter 6 on purpose. Whether the end serves the class is the owner's to say." ;
    backlog:hasSprintGoal "The decks and the interactive pages of chapters 5 and 6 are rebuilt as new files that meet the written teaching-material standard (the deck standard D1 to D12 and the page standard P1 to P11), measured by an independent deck check and the page test 9.36.0 and verified by the evidence bridge, chapter 5 first; each unit that fails is named failing and is not Done. No existing file, gate, test or threshold is edited. Frozen at the planning ceremony." ;
    backlog:hasMember ex:ST_Remedy_Tools, ex:ST_Remedy_Deck_Ch05, ex:ST_Remedy_Page_Ch05, ex:ST_Remedy_Deck_Ch06, ex:ST_Remedy_Page_Ch06, ex:TK_Remedy_DeckCheck, ex:TK_Remedy_PageTest, ex:TK_Remedy_Template, ex:TK_Remedy_Regress, ex:TK_Remedy_Deck_Ch05_Build, ex:TK_Remedy_Deck_Ch05_Verify, ex:TK_Remedy_Deck_Ch06_Build, ex:TK_Remedy_Deck_Ch06_Verify, ex:TK_Remedy_Page_Ch05_Build, ex:TK_Remedy_Page_Ch05_Verify, ex:TK_Remedy_Page_Ch06_Build, ex:TK_Remedy_Page_Ch06_Verify .
ex:PB3R_Iter_17 a backlog:PlanBaseline ; rdfs:label "Plan baseline of iteration 17 when it was planned"@en ; backlog:baselineFor ex:Iter_17 ; backlog:baselinedAt "2026-10-22T18:09:01"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:isCurrentBaseline true ; backlog:hasBaselineStart "2026-10-22T18:09:01"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasBaselineEnd "2026-10-23T09:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime .
ex:PC3_Iter_17 a backlog:SprintPlanningCeremony ; rdfs:label "Planning of iteration 17: the chapter 5 and 6 remedy"@en ; backlog:ceremonyFor ex:Iter_17 ; backlog:heldAt "2026-10-22T18:09:01"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:includesPlanningEvent ex:Plan3R_ST_Remedy_Tools, ex:Plan3R_ST_Remedy_Deck_Ch05, ex:Plan3R_ST_Remedy_Page_Ch05, ex:Plan3R_ST_Remedy_Deck_Ch06, ex:Plan3R_ST_Remedy_Page_Ch06 ;
    rdfs:comment "Held 2026-10-22T18:09:01 by the builder session, after the owner's messages of Thursday 2026-10-22 17:27 and 17:30 Istanbul (14:27 and 14:30 UTC), as relayed by the course coordinator (ex:CR3_Remedy56): the five stories and their 12 tasks are committed to this iteration, whose goal is frozen at its start. No executor has started; work begun is recorded at the real start of each executor session, with its brief."@en .
ex:SC3_Remedy56 a backlog:ScopeChange ;
    rdfs:label "Scope grown by the chapter 5 and 6 decks and pages remedied, and the tools that measure the standard"@en ;
    backlog:fulfillsRequest ex:CR3_Remedy56 ; backlog:changesScope ex:Scope3 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner ;
    backlog:admitsItem ex:ST_Remedy_Tools, ex:ST_Remedy_Deck_Ch05, ex:ST_Remedy_Page_Ch05, ex:ST_Remedy_Deck_Ch06, ex:ST_Remedy_Page_Ch06 ;
    backlog:hasScopeChangeRationale "Owner's messages of Thursday 2026-10-22, relayed by the course coordinator and recorded by the builder session. 17:27 Istanbul (14:27 UTC), quoted: \"I need the chapter 5 and 6 urgently. The HTML file Playground code list is crazily extends outside of the page space. You put the code there not the name of the code. Chapter code is not listed as far as I see. I need a specific tab just to run the chapter code matching with the same order of the ppt. Additionally, multiple concepts are presented on the same page with downward flow. You can add one more step to the hierarchy and build the details in lower level panels. Repeating the same menu items on the tab and left hierarchical menu is not good when the tabs are not fitting on a single line. PPT is very poor in content and just listing codes with sub shapes and concept names. They cannot be presented nor understandable. They are certainly not matches with any standards of teaching materials.\" 17:30 Istanbul (14:30 UTC), quoted: \"I want you to remedy the weaknesses and provide me Chapter 5 and 6 PPT and Interactive pages ready to use.\" The 17:30 message authorises the scope: remedy the weaknesses and deliver the chapter 5 and chapter 6 decks and interactive pages ready to use. Under the standing rule that work following the owner's direction is recorded as owner-directed, it is not listed as an open owner confirmation. The end of the iteration is still the owner's. The boundary moved outward by five stories; the exclusion of any change to a gate or a test is lifted only for the new files named in ex:Del3_Remedy56Tools; nothing existing is edited or weakened." .
ex:CR3_Remedy56 rdfs:comment "Disposition set to Accepted on 2026-10-22 in the version that records the ScopeChange ex:SC3_Remedy56 and the five stories it admits; it was Pending before. The owner's message of Thursday 2026-10-22 17:27 and 17:30 Istanbul (14:27 and 14:30 UTC), as relayed by the course coordinator is the direction and authorises the scope; the end of the iteration is still his."@en .

