ex:AC4R_Deck_Ch05 backlog:hasAuditNote "Control 2026-10-22 (record v0.197.0), deck v3_1_0 of chapter 5, every element run by the evidence bridge and recorded as printed: (1) deck standard D1 to D12: MET [deck standard check v1_0_0: D1 to D12 all PASS (independent tool, python-pptx 1.0.2): verified -> SUMMARY PASS=12 FAIL=0 NOT_MEASURED=0 | failing: none RESULT PASS (exit 0)] | (2) Deck chapter check and deck match: MET [chapter check Deck/Ch05 v1_3_0: verified -> RESULT Deck/Ch05: PASS; deck match check v1_0_0: 0 not carried: verified -> chapter 05 page 9_74_0: 15 items compared with lecture_v1_2_0.json and sen0401_ch05_stories_v1_2_0; not carried: 0] | (3) manifest in slide order: MET [chapter-code manifest: order equals the order of the code slides, names unique, library hashes match: verified -> manifest chapter_code_ch05_v1_1_0.json | 27 examples | 27 code slides | deck 03-materials/ch05/SEN0401_Ch05_WalletRecovery_3e_v3_1_0.pptx | PASS order equals code-slide order, names unique, library hashes match] | (4) no committed file edited: MET [no committed file edited (every file of the three commits added): verified -> nochange commits 3fc6881,6db1751,e5d7761 | PASS every file of the commits was added, none modified or deleted]. RESULT: MET: all elements are met. RENDERED REVIEW by the builder session (independent of the executor): the deck was rendered with soffice to PDF and PNG (68 pages) and every page was viewed in contact sheets of 9 slides; every slide type was seen (title, story with picture and 5N1K, dividers, code slides with explanation and result, tables, native charts, diagrams, analogy slides, resources, closing). Result: no text overlap, no clipped text, no empty slide found; slide 33 (the coordinator's finding on v3_0_0) is correct in v3_1_0. A review by eye is not a machine result and is not counted as evidence; it is recorded here. Observations, not failures: the dividers repeat a six-concept list beside a numbered 'How they fit together' panel; several table slides leave empty space below the table. DISCLOSED: (a) the criterion text names the manifest chapter_code_ch05_v1_0_0.json; the executor wrote v1_1_0 with the deck v3_1_0 (v1_0_0 is kept and belongs to v3_0_0); the control measured the newest manifest. (b) The criterion element 'the order equals the order of the code slides, measured by the deck check' is measured by a new control file sen0401_deck_control_check_v1_0_0.py because the deck standard check does not read the manifest. (c) The overlap scan is the executor's own tool; it is run as evidence but my render review is the independent part. (d) The Verify task TK_Remedy_Deck_Ch05_Verify waits for TK_Remedy_DeckCheck (Done not yet controlled); it is not made Ready." .
