    backlog:hasAuditNote "Done, recorded 2026-10-22: delivered by the executor session SEN0401-I17-deck-ch05 (3 commits 3fc6881 to e5d7761; deck v3_1_0, v3_0_0 not controlled). The checks and their results are those of the evidence nodes and the note of AC4R_Deck_Ch05. RENDERED REVIEW by the builder session (independent of the executor): the deck was rendered with soffice to PDF and PNG (68 pages) and every page was viewed in contact sheets of 9 slides; every slide type was seen (title, story with picture and 5N1K, dividers, code slides with explanation and result, tables, native charts, diagrams, analogy slides, resources, closing). Result: no text overlap, no clipped text, no empty slide found; slide 33 (the coordinator's finding on v3_0_0) is correct in v3_1_0. A review by eye is not a machine result and is not counted as evidence; it is recorded here. Observations, not failures: the dividers repeat a six-concept list beside a numbered 'How they fit together' panel; several table slides leave empty space below the table. DISCLOSED: (a) the criterion text names the manifest chapter_code_ch05_v1_0_0.json; the executor wrote v1_1_0 with the deck v3_1_0 (v1_0_0 is kept and belongs to v3_0_0); the control measured the newest manifest. (b) The criterion element 'the order equals the order of the code slides, measured by the deck check' is measured by a new control file sen0401_deck_control_check_v1_0_0.py because the deck standard check does not read the manifest. (c) The overlap scan is the executor's own tool; it is run as evidence but my render review is the independent part. (d) The Verify task TK_Remedy_Deck_Ch05_Verify waits for TK_Remedy_DeckCheck (Done not yet controlled); it is not made Ready." .
