ex:AC4R_Deck_Ch06 backlog:hasAuditNote "Control 2026-10-22 (record v0.198.0), deck v2_1_0 of chapter 6, every element run by the evidence bridge and recorded as printed: (1) deck standard D1 to D12: MET [deck standard check v1_0_0: D1 to D12 all PASS (independent tool, python-pptx 1.0.2): verified -> SUMMARY PASS=12 FAIL=0 NOT_MEASURED=0 | failing: none RESULT PASS (exit 0)] | (2) Deck chapter check and deck match: MET [chapter check Deck/Ch06 v1_3_0: verified -> RESULT Deck/Ch06: PASS; deck match check v1_0_0: 0 not carried: verified -> chapter 06 page 9_75_0: 18 items compared with lecture_v1_2_0.json and sen0401_ch06_stories_v1_2_0; not carried: 0] | (3) manifest in slide order: MET [chapter-code manifest: order equals the order of the code slides, names unique, library hashes match: verified -> manifest chapter_code_ch06_v1_1_0.json | 18 examples | 18 code slides | deck SEN0401_Ch06_Transactions_3e_v2_1_0.pptx | PASS order equals code-slide order, names unique, library files exist, hashes match where stated] | (4) no committed file edited: MET [no committed file edited (every file of the three commits added): verified -> nochange commits 10e3fa8,f8bed0d | PASS every file of the commits was added, none modified or deleted]. RESULT: MET: all elements are met. RENDERED REVIEW by the builder session (independent of the executor): the deck was rendered with soffice to PDF and PNG (62 pages) and every page was viewed in contact sheets of 9 slides; every slide type was seen (title, story with picture and 5N1K, dividers, code slides with explanation and result, tables, native charts, diagrams, analogy slides, resources, closing). Result: no text overlap between text boxes, no clipped text, no empty slide found. One minor finding, not covered by any element of the standard and so not a failure, reported to the coordinator: on slide 51 (the subsidy chart) the data labels of the five tiny bars at the right end crowd each other. A review by eye is not a machine result and is not counted as evidence; it is recorded here. Observations, not failures: several concept-card slides (46, 52, 59 and others) leave empty space in the lower half. DISCLOSED: (a) the criterion text names the manifest chapter_code_ch06_v1_0_0.json; v1_0_0 was committed with the draft deck v2_0_0, so the executor wrote v1_1_0 with deck v2_1_0 (v1_0_0 is kept; the brief named v1_0_0); the control measured the newest manifest. (b) The criterion element 'the order equals the order of the code slides, measured by the deck check' is measured by a new control file sen0401_deck_control_check_v1_1_0.py because the deck standard check does not read the manifest (v1_1_0 of that file, because the chapter 6 manifest has a bare deck file name and states no SHA-256). (c) The overlap scan is the executor's own tool; it is run as evidence but my render review is the independent part. (d) The Verify task TK_Remedy_Deck_Ch06_Verify waits for TK_Remedy_DeckCheck (Done not yet controlled); it is not made Ready." .
