ex:TK_Remedy_Deck_Ch06_Verify backlog:hasAcceptanceCriterion ex:AC4R_Deck_Ch06 ; backlog:hasEvidence ex:Ev25c6_std, ex:Ev25c6_overlap, ex:Ev25c6_deckchk, ex:Ev25c6_match, ex:Ev25c6_manifest, ex:Ev25c6_nochange, ex:Ev3C_File_ead40d8a1a, ex:Ev3C_File_103d3fe3ce, ex:Ev3C_File_217e8d965e, ex:Ev3C_File_99655bb7e2, ex:Ev3C_File_f3e31b40ca, ex:Ev3C_File_50ae49c14e ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Done, recorded 2026-10-22: the checks of the task ran one after the other on the bridge after the task started; results as printed: deck standard check v1_0_0: D1 to D12 all PASS (independent tool, pyth: SUMMARY PASS=12 FAIL=0 NOT_MEASURED=0 | failing: none RESULT PASS (exit 0) | overlap scan v1_0_0: CLEAN (the executor's tool, not independent): RESULT CLEAN (0 findings) | chapter check Deck/Ch06 v1_3_0: RESULT Deck/Ch06: PASS | deck match check v1_0_0: 0 not carried: chapter 06 page 9_75_0: 18 items compared with lecture_v1_2_0.json and sen0401_ch06_stories_v1_2_0; not carried: 0 | chapter-code manifest: order equals the order of the code slides, name: manifest chapter_code_ch06_v1_1_0.json | 18 examples | 18 code slides | deck SEN0401_Ch06_Transactions_3e_v2_1_0.pptx | PASS order equals code-slide order, names unique, library files exist, hashes ma | no committed file edited (every file of the three commits added): nochange commits 10e3fa8,f8bed0d | PASS every file of the commits was added, none modified or deleted. READING (not a tool result; by the builder session, after the rendered review of the Build control, from the three roles of the owner's preference). Teaching academician: the deck follows the chapter's parts in order, each part opens with a divider that names its concepts, shows a map strip and gives the way the concepts fit together; every code slide pairs the listing with a plain-language note beside each line group and an executed result as a chart, table or diagram; stories carry 5N1K, a real picture and a live link. Reviewing faculty specialist: the code results are those the chapter library printed (the examples were re-run by the Deck chapter check and the manifest holds the expected values); the 62 slides, 18 code slides and 7 native charts are the measured facts of the deck standard check. Student: every concept card gives the meaning and an everyday comparison; slides are numbered; the closing slides summarise and point to practice. Findings kept: slide 51 chart labels crowd on the five smallest bars (recorded as a defect task of the chapter 6 deck, the coordinator decides)" .

ex:Imp_Ch5Lib a backlog:Impediment ; rdfs:label "The chapter 5 library needs hash primitives the page runtime lacks"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:impedes ex:TK_Remedy_Page_Ch05_Build ;
    backlog:raisedAt "2026-10-22T20:00:13"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasImpedimentOwner backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:hasImpedimentStatement "BLOCKS the chapter-code tab examples of chapter 5 unless handled: the library sen0401_ch05_wallet_lib_v1_1_0.py needs RIPEMD-160 and PBKDF2-HMAC, which the page's Pyodide 0.28.2 lacks (measured: hashlib.new('ripemd160') raises ValueError at line 49, hashlib.pbkdf2_hmac raises AttributeError at line 100), and it opens the BIP39 wordlist 08-tooling/ch05-evidence/bip39_english.txt (line 74). WHAT CLEARS IT: the chapter 5 page gets a pywheels file (pywheels_vX.json in the chapter's page-data folder, as chapters 8 to 14 have) whose wheel carries the library and the wordlist, and whose boot snippet is pure Python: a RIPEMD-160 and a PBKDF2-HMAC (built on hmac) registered before the library is imported. It is cleared when every example of the chapter-code tab runs in the page (page test 9.36.0 P2 passes). Source: 08-tooling/template952_logs/RUNTIME_FACTS.txt (measured by the executor SEN0401-I17-template on 2026-10-22, commit af9b390)." .
ex:Imp_Ch6Lib a backlog:Impediment ; rdfs:label "The chapter 6 library needs nothing the page runtime lacks"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:impedes ex:TK_Remedy_Page_Ch06_Build ;
    backlog:raisedAt "2026-10-22T20:00:13"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:resolvedAt "2026-10-22T21:21:44"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasImpedimentStatement "CLEARED: the question was whether the chapter 6 library needs primitives the page lacks. Measured: sen0401_ch06_tx_lib_v1_0_0.py imports hashlib and struct only (sha256; no RIPEMD-160, no PBKDF2), so it runs in the page's Pyodide as it is once packaged as a wheel with a boot snippet like chapters 8 to 14. The page task still has to build that pywheels file. Source: 08-tooling/template952_logs/RUNTIME_FACTS.txt (measured by the executor SEN0401-I17-template on 2026-10-22, commit af9b390). Cleared in the register by the builder session's check tpfacts (08-tooling/sen0401_remedy_check_v1_0_0.py) of the executor's report." .
ex:Imp_Manifest a backlog:Impediment ; rdfs:label "The chapter-code manifests of chapters 5 and 6 differ in shape"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:impedes ex:TK_Remedy_Page_Ch05_Build, ex:TK_Remedy_Page_Ch06_Build ;
    backlog:raisedAt "2026-10-22T20:00:13"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:resolvedAt "2026-10-22T21:21:44"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasImpedimentStatement "CLEARED: the manifests chapter_code_ch05_v1_1_0.json (fields order, id, name, slide, concepts, code, expected, library, prelude) and chapter_code_ch06_v1_1_0.json (order, id, name, slide, branch, library, needs, code, show with expression and expected) are not the same shape. The page test 9.36.0 reads only order and name; the page-data builder v2_24_0 accepts more (order or n, name or title, code, slide, expected or result or output, note, viz) and stops on a missing name or code, a repeated name or an order that runs backwards. So both manifests are usable as they are; the page task passes the manifest by its newest version in 03-materials/chNN/page. Cleared by the builder session's reading of the two files and the check manifest:05 and manifest:06 (08-tooling/sen0401_deck_control_check_v1_1_0.py)." .
