ex:CR3_ChipScroll a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "A story chip does not bring its story into view on the chapter 5 page: may the template get a new version 9.52.1 and the chapter 5 and 6 pages be rebuilt on it?"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_Remedy56, ex:AC4R_Page_Ch05, ex:AC4R_Page_Ch06 ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Requested Friday 2026-10-23, relayed by the course coordinator (the owner's standing direction of Thursday 2026-10-22 17:30 Istanbul: remedy the weaknesses and deliver the chapter 5 and 6 pages ready to use). MEASURED FACTS. The executor SEN0401-I17-page-ch05 reported the chapter 5 page 9.80.0 (commits c4002e1 to 0fb29ca, template 9.52.0, builders v4_15_0 and v2_24_0): the page tests 9.36.0, 9.35.1 and 9.34.1 each fail exactly one feature, 'a story chip on a concept opens that story in the Stories tab' (detail: story GoxColdFind, which lands at 2064 px, outside the 768 px viewport). Its diagnosis (confirmed by the builder session by reading template 9.52.0): the click handler of the story chips (the listener on the panes, button[data-story]) calls showTab('stories') and then scrollIntoView on the story at once; the pane height is fitted afterwards, so the scroll position is lost. The chapter 6 page 9.81.0 (executor SEN0401-I17-page-ch06, commits faf1b10 to ca2e510) passes all three tests, but it carries the same handler: the page tests click the first chip of the first concept that has one, and in chapter 6 that chip is the first story, which sits at the top of the pane and needs no scroll. So the defect is in template 9.52.0 and is latent in the chapter 6 page; the builder session re-ran the page tests on both pages on 2026-10-23 (results in the control version). The change grows the scope: a new template version, and new rebuilds of two pages that were delivered. Pending until the ScopeChange that admits the stories is recorded in the Backlog version." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .

ex:IA3_ChipScroll a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What repairing the story chip costs, measured before it is started"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR3_ChipScroll ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage3 ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:IA3_Remedy56 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "MEASURED FACTS. The executor SEN0401-I17-page-ch05 reported the chapter 5 page 9.80.0 (commits c4002e1 to 0fb29ca, template 9.52.0, builders v4_15_0 and v2_24_0): the page tests 9.36.0, 9.35.1 and 9.34.1 each fail exactly one feature, 'a story chip on a concept opens that story in the Stories tab' (detail: story GoxColdFind, which lands at 2064 px, outside the 768 px viewport). Its diagnosis (confirmed by the builder session by reading template 9.52.0): the click handler of the story chips (the listener on the panes, button[data-story]) calls showTab('stories') and then scrollIntoView on the story at once; the pane height is fitted afterwards, so the scroll position is lost. The chapter 6 page 9.81.0 (executor SEN0401-I17-page-ch06, commits faf1b10 to ca2e510) passes all three tests, but it carries the same handler: the page tests click the first chip of the first concept that has one, and in chapter 6 that chip is the first story, which sits at the top of the pane and needs no scroll. So the defect is in template 9.52.0 and is latent in the chapter 6 page; the builder session re-ran the page tests on both pages on 2026-10-23 (results in the control version). AFFECTED: TK_Remedy_Page_Ch05_Build (its criterion AC4R_Page_Ch05 names template 9.52.0 and the page 9.80.0 fails one feature of it, so the criterion cannot be met; the task is suspended, not edited, G125) and its Verify task; the chapter 6 page task (met on page 9.81.0, Done; not edited; its latent defect is carried by the new story); the template 9.52.0 (stays byte-identical; the Template task TK_Remedy_Template stays Done: its criterion was met as measured, and the defect is a finding beyond what the page tests measured). NOT AFFECTED: the decks, the page tests, the page-data builder, the pywheels files, the chapter-code manifests, every other chapter, the Mission outcome and the Achieved status. CHAPTER 6: the template change TOUCHES chapter 6, because the page 9.81.0 carries the same handler (it passes only because its first chip is the first story); the plan rebuilds the chapter 6 page on 9.52.1 so that both delivered pages are free of the defect; the rebuild is a separate story and task so it can be declined without blocking chapter 5. PLAN (route as ex:CR3_Remedy56, G127): a StageRevision from the Scope stage, seven versions; new iteration Iter_18 with three stories and six tasks: template 9.52.1 (executor, about 1 h) and its verification (builder, about 0.7 h); then the pages of chapters 5 and 6 rebuilt in parallel (executors, about 2 h each) and their verification (builder, about 1 h each, serial browser tests). Estimated from T0 (executor of the template starts at once): template ready about T0+1.5 h, page chapter 5 and chapter 6 about T0+4.5 h and T0+5 h; the machine has 2 cores, so browser tests queue. The proposed end is today Friday 2026-10-23 09:00 UTC (12:00 Istanbul), the owner's to decide. COST: new files only (one template, no new builder unless the default must change); old files byte-identical; no gate, test or threshold changes. A criterion that fails is named failing and its story is not Done; nothing is waived." .

ex:Revision_Lineage3_Scope6 a backlog:StageRevision ;
    rdfs:label "Revision of the third lineage from the Scope stage: the story chip repair (template 9.52.1 and the chapter 5 and 6 pages)"@en ;
    backlog:revisesLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:revisesFromStage backlog:Stage_Scope ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_ChipScroll, ex:IA3_ChipScroll ;
    backlog:revisionReason "The change request ex:CR3_ChipScroll (Friday 2026-10-23, relayed by the course coordinator (the owner's standing direction of Thursday 2026-10-22 17:30 Istanbul: remedy the weaknesses and deliver the chapter 5 and 6 pages ready to use)) adds deliverables (a new template version and two page rebuilds, as new files); the lineage is in its closed Backlog stage, and a deliverable added to a closed scope statement is a revision from the Scope stage (ruling G127). The request and its impact assessment ex:IA3_ChipScroll were recorded first. This version retracts the Scope, Goal, Objective and Backlog outputs and rebuilds nothing; the next four versions rebuild them one stage each, a sixth fills the last commit; the items already in the register, Done ones included, re-enter by admission and are not re-dated. The retracted outputs and their digests stay as history (L-112). The interim versions are the declared transition (G129). Recorded as decided by the builder role." ;
    backlog:retractsOutput ex:Out3_ScopeR6, ex:Out3_GoalR6, ex:Out3_ObjectiveR6, ex:Out3_BacklogR8 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:revisedAtCommit "4b82f3e" .
ex:Out3_ScopeR6 backlog:outputRetracted true .
ex:Out3_GoalR6 backlog:outputRetracted true .
ex:Out3_ObjectiveR6 backlog:outputRetracted true .
ex:Out3_BacklogR8 backlog:outputRetracted true .

ex:Del3_ChipScrollTemplate a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ;
    rdfs:label "A page template 9.52.1 that brings a story into view after the pane is fitted, as a new file with 9.52.0 kept"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:derivesFromMissionClause "the research behind it and an interactive page"^^xsd:string ;
    backlog:hasDeliverableText "The page template 9.52.1, a new file over 9.52.0 (which stays unchanged), whose story-chip click handler runs the scroll after the pane is fitted; every id, hook and behaviour of 9.52.0 stays. MEASURED FACTS. The executor SEN0401-I17-page-ch05 reported the chapter 5 page 9.80.0 (commits c4002e1 to 0fb29ca, template 9.52.0, builders v4_15_0 and v2_24_0): the page tests 9.36.0, 9.35.1 and 9.34.1 each fail exactly one feature, 'a story chip on a concept opens that story in the Stories tab' (detail: story GoxColdFind, which lands at 2064 px, outside the 768 px viewport). Its diagnosis (confirmed by the builder session by reading template 9.52.0): the click handler of the story chips (the listener on the panes, button[data-story]) calls showTab('stories') and then scrollIntoView on the story at once; the pane height is fitted afterwards, so the scroll position is lost. The chapter 6 page 9.81.0 (executor SEN0401-I17-page-ch06, commits faf1b10 to ca2e510) passes all three tests, but it carries the same handler: the page tests click the first chip of the first concept that has one, and in chapter 6 that chip is the first story, which sits at the top of the pane and needs no scroll. So the defect is in template 9.52.0 and is latent in the chapter 6 page; the builder session re-ran the page tests on both pages on 2026-10-23 (results in the control version). PAGE FEATURE (existing, from the page test 9.35.1 and kept in 9.36.0 and 9.34.1): a story chip on a concept opens that story in the Stories tab: after the click the Stories pane is visible and the story card is inside the viewport." ;
    backlog:deliverableForArea ex:Area3_Remedy56 ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Work ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_Functional .
ex:Del3_ChipScrollPages a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ;
    rdfs:label "The pages of chapters 5 and 6 rebuilt on template 9.52.1 so that every story chip opens its story in view"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:derivesFromMissionClause "the research behind it and an interactive page"^^xsd:string ;
    backlog:hasDeliverableText "The pages of chapter 5 and chapter 6 rebuilt as new files on template 9.52.1 with the builders v4_15_0 and v2_24_0, passing the page test 9.36.0 and the page tests 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 with no failure, the Stage 4 gate runner and the chapter checks. PAGE STANDARD (checked by the new page test 9.36.0, Playwright 1.56.0): P1 no horizontal overflow at 390 px and at 1366 px; P2 the chapter-code tab lists the deck's examples by NAME in the deck's slide order, each runnable in the page with the chapter library defined in the page and its result visualised, and the code lives in the editor, not in the list; P3 tabs and left tree are synchronised and their label sets are disjoint or the tab bar is one row; P4 no third level of tabs, and one more level of panels so that one panel holds one concept; P5 a panel is at most 1.0 screen high at 1366x768; P6 no list repeated on one screen; P7 every diagram has zoom; P8 the top-level menu is uncrowded (at most 8 top-level tabs); P9 a text-size control and an adaptive layout at 390, 768 and 1366 px; P10 executed code results are visualised; P11 the page declares the standard and the examples equal the deck's code manifest." ;
    backlog:deliverableForArea ex:Area3_Remedy56 ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Work ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_Functional .
ex:Scope3 backlog:requiresDeliverable ex:Del3_ChipScrollTemplate, ex:Del3_ChipScrollPages ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_ChipScroll, ex:IA3_ChipScroll .
ex:Scope3 rdfs:comment "Revised 2026-10-23 by the stage revision ex:Revision_Lineage3_Scope6 on the change request ex:CR3_ChipScroll (Friday 2026-10-23, relayed by the course coordinator (the owner's standing direction of Thursday 2026-10-22 17:30 Istanbul: remedy the weaknesses and deliver the chapter 5 and 6 pages ready to use)). The statement above is unchanged (L-112). It now also requires ex:Del3_ChipScrollTemplate and ex:Del3_ChipScrollPages in the area ex:Area3_Remedy56. No exclusion changes: the new template is a new file named in the deliverable and the exclusion of changes to gates, tests and thresholds still holds."@en .

