ex:G3_ChipScroll a backlog:Goal ;
    rdfs:label "On the chapter 5 and 6 pages every story chip brings its story into view"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope3 ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:Area3_Remedy56 ;
    backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Mission ; backlog:hasGoalPriority backlog:Priority_Must ;
    backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_Derived ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner ;
    backlog:hasGoalRationale "Derived from the revised scope and from the change request ex:CR3_ChipScroll: the owner uses the pages in class; a story chip that scrolls to nowhere is a defect of the teaching material. MEASURED FACTS. The executor SEN0401-I17-page-ch05 reported the chapter 5 page 9.80.0 (commits c4002e1 to 0fb29ca, template 9.52.0, builders v4_15_0 and v2_24_0): the page tests 9.36.0, 9.35.1 and 9.34.1 each fail exactly one feature, 'a story chip on a concept opens that story in the Stories tab' (detail: story GoxColdFind, which lands at 2064 px, outside the 768 px viewport). Its diagnosis (confirmed by the builder session by reading template 9.52.0): the click handler of the story chips (the listener on the panes, button[data-story]) calls showTab('stories') and then scrollIntoView on the story at once; the pane height is fitted afterwards, so the scroll position is lost. The chapter 6 page 9.81.0 (executor SEN0401-I17-page-ch06, commits faf1b10 to ca2e510) passes all three tests, but it carries the same handler: the page tests click the first chip of the first concept that has one, and in chapter 6 that chip is the first story, which sits at the top of the pane and needs no scroll. So the defect is in template 9.52.0 and is latent in the chapter 6 page; the builder session re-ran the page tests on both pages on 2026-10-23 (results in the control version)." ;
    backlog:producedByStage ex:Out3_GoalR7 .
ex:G3_ChipScroll rdfs:comment "Drafted by the builder session on 2026-10-23 from the change request ex:CR3_ChipScroll; the intent origin is therefore Derived."@en .
ex:Spec3C_P a backlog:Specification ;
    rdfs:label "What it is for a story chip to work"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:specifiesGoal ex:G3_ChipScroll ;
    backlog:hasSpecificationText "PAGE FEATURE (existing, from the page test 9.35.1 and kept in 9.36.0 and 9.34.1): a story chip on a concept opens that story in the Stories tab: after the click the Stories pane is visible and the story card is inside the viewport. MEASURED FACTS. The executor SEN0401-I17-page-ch05 reported the chapter 5 page 9.80.0 (commits c4002e1 to 0fb29ca, template 9.52.0, builders v4_15_0 and v2_24_0): the page tests 9.36.0, 9.35.1 and 9.34.1 each fail exactly one feature, 'a story chip on a concept opens that story in the Stories tab' (detail: story GoxColdFind, which lands at 2064 px, outside the 768 px viewport). Its diagnosis (confirmed by the builder session by reading template 9.52.0): the click handler of the story chips (the listener on the panes, button[data-story]) calls showTab('stories') and then scrollIntoView on the story at once; the pane height is fitted afterwards, so the scroll position is lost. The chapter 6 page 9.81.0 (executor SEN0401-I17-page-ch06, commits faf1b10 to ca2e510) passes all three tests, but it carries the same handler: the page tests click the first chip of the first concept that has one, and in chapter 6 that chip is the first story, which sits at the top of the pane and needs no scroll. So the defect is in template 9.52.0 and is latent in the chapter 6 page; the builder session re-ran the page tests on both pages on 2026-10-23 (results in the control version)." ;
    backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_Derived ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner ; backlog:producedByStage ex:Out3_GoalR7 .
ex:Scen3C_Passes a backlog:TestScenario ; rdfs:label "A page on template 9.52.1 brings every story into view when its chip is clicked"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Nominal ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec3C_P ;
    backlog:hasScenarioText "Given a page of chapter 5 or 6 built on template 9.52.1, when the page tests are run, then the story chip feature passes (the Stories pane is visible and the story is inside the viewport) and nothing else fails." .
ex:Scen3C_NotClaimed a backlog:TestScenario ; rdfs:label "A page on template 9.52.0 whose chip feature fails is named failing and not claimed"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Rejection ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec3C_P ;
    backlog:hasScenarioText "Given the chapter 5 page 9.80.0 on template 9.52.0 (measured 2026-10-23), when the page tests are run, then the story chip feature fails for GoxColdFind and the page carries no passing result." .

