ex:TS_PageTemplateD a backlog:ToolScript ; rdfs:label "page template 9.52.1 (new file over 9.52.0: the story chip scrolls after the pane is fitted)"@en ; backlog:scriptFileName "course_page_template_v9_52_1.html" ; backlog:acceptsGraphPath false .

ex:AC5R_Template a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; rdfs:label "The page template 9.52.1 is a new file that scrolls a story into view after the pane is fitted and changes nothing else"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Owner-directed work (ex:CR3_ChipScroll). Given the template 9.52.0 (byte-identical after the task) and the defect measured on the chapter 5 page 9.80.0, when the NEW file course_page_template_v9_52_1.html is written, then ALL of: (1) the file is new and 9.52.0 is byte-identical; (2) the unified diff of 9.52.1 over 9.52.0 shows only the story-chip click handler and the version marker, and every id and hook of 9.52.0 and the DOM contract are present; (3) a scratch page of chapter 5 built on 9.52.1 with the builders v4_15_0 and v2_24_0 (PAGE_TEMPLATE) passes the feature 'a story chip on a concept opens that story in the Stories tab' of the page tests 9.35.1 and 9.36.0 for the story GoxColdFind and the tests report no failure; (4) scratch pages of chapters 1 and 10 on 9.52.1 pass page test 9.36.0 P1, P3, P4, P5, P6, P8, P9; (5) no committed file is edited, no gate, test or threshold changed; results as printed; if any element fails the template is named failing. MEASURED FACTS. The executor SEN0401-I17-page-ch05 reported the chapter 5 page 9.80.0 (commits c4002e1 to 0fb29ca, template 9.52.0, builders v4_15_0 and v2_24_0): the page tests 9.36.0, 9.35.1 and 9.34.1 each fail exactly one feature, 'a story chip on a concept opens that story in the Stories tab' (detail: story GoxColdFind, which lands at 2064 px, outside the 768 px viewport). Its diagnosis (confirmed by the builder session by reading template 9.52.0): the click handler of the story chips (the listener on the panes, button[data-story]) calls showTab('stories') and then scrollIntoView on the story at once; the pane height is fitted afterwards, so the scroll position is lost. The chapter 6 page 9.81.0 (executor SEN0401-I17-page-ch06, commits faf1b10 to ca2e510) passes all three tests, but it carries the same handler: the page tests click the first chip of the first concept that has one, and in chapter 6 that chip is the first story, which sits at the top of the pane and needs no scroll. So the defect is in template 9.52.0 and is latent in the chapter 6 page; the builder session re-ran the page tests on both pages on 2026-10-23 (results in the control version). PAGE FEATURE (existing, from the page test 9.35.1 and kept in 9.36.0 and 9.34.1): a story chip on a concept opens that story in the Stories tab: after the click the Stories pane is visible and the story card is inside the viewport." ;
    backlog:measuredWithTool ex:TS_PageTemplateD, ex:TS_PageTest36, ex:TS_PageTest35b, ex:TS_PageBuilder415, ex:TS_PageData224 ;
    backlog:measuredWithVersion "page template 9.52.1 (new file over 9.52.0, which stays byte-identical); page builder v4_15_0 and page-data builder v2_24_0 (unchanged; the template is passed by PAGE_TEMPLATE, a builder v4_16_0 only if the default must change); page test 9.36.0 (Playwright 1.56.0); page tests 9.34.1 and 9.35.1; Stage 4 gate runner v1_1_0 reading the CURRENT RDODI validator v1.13.0; chapter check v1_3_0 reading the PINNED RDODI validator v1.6.0; deck match check v1_0_0; page check wrapper v1_3_0; Playwright 1.56.0" ;
    backlog:satisfiedByArtifact "the new files cited by SHA-256, the logs of the runs and the diffs, verified by the evidence bridge" ;
    backlog:coveredByCase ex:TC3C_T_Passes, ex:TC3C_T_NotClaimed .

ex:AC5R_Page_Ch05 a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; rdfs:label "The page of chapter 5 rebuilt on template 9.52.1 passes all three page tests, story chip included"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Owner-directed work (ex:CR3_ChipScroll). Given the page of chapter 5 (the earlier page and its deck), when the page is rebuilt as a new file with a new page version on the template 9.52.1 with the builders v4_15_0 and v2_24_0, then ALL of: (1) the page test 9.36.0 runs all its added features with no skip and passes them (P1, P2, P3, P4, P5, P6, P8, P9, P11) and every other feature, exit 0; (2) the page tests 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 report no failure and widgets, features and gates not below the stored result of the page 9.74.0 (chapter 5) or 9.75.0 (chapter 6), skipped not more; (3) the chapter-code tab equals the deck's chapter-code manifest in names and order and each example runs in the page and shows its result; (4) the Stage 4 gate runner v1_1_0 for 5 exits 0 with Stage3.F, Stage4.A, B, cov, sub and src PASS, the Research, Deck and Page chapter checks pass, the deck match check reports 0 not carried; (5) no committed file is edited, no gate, test or threshold changed; the Stage 4 page ABox and the stored page-test result are new files; results as printed; if any element fails the page is named failing and this criterion has no passing result. MEASURED FACTS. The executor SEN0401-I17-page-ch05 reported the chapter 5 page 9.80.0 (commits c4002e1 to 0fb29ca, template 9.52.0, builders v4_15_0 and v2_24_0): the page tests 9.36.0, 9.35.1 and 9.34.1 each fail exactly one feature, 'a story chip on a concept opens that story in the Stories tab' (detail: story GoxColdFind, which lands at 2064 px, outside the 768 px viewport). Its diagnosis (confirmed by the builder session by reading template 9.52.0): the click handler of the story chips (the listener on the panes, button[data-story]) calls showTab('stories') and then scrollIntoView on the story at once; the pane height is fitted afterwards, so the scroll position is lost. The chapter 6 page 9.81.0 (executor SEN0401-I17-page-ch06, commits faf1b10 to ca2e510) passes all three tests, but it carries the same handler: the page tests click the first chip of the first concept that has one, and in chapter 6 that chip is the first story, which sits at the top of the pane and needs no scroll. So the defect is in template 9.52.0 and is latent in the chapter 6 page; the builder session re-ran the page tests on both pages on 2026-10-23 (results in the control version). PAGE STANDARD (checked by the new page test 9.36.0, Playwright 1.56.0): P1 no horizontal overflow at 390 px and at 1366 px; P2 the chapter-code tab lists the deck's examples by NAME in the deck's slide order, each runnable in the page with the chapter library defined in the page and its result visualised, and the code lives in the editor, not in the list; P3 tabs and left tree are synchronised and their label sets are disjoint or the tab bar is one row; P4 no third level of tabs, and one more level of panels so that one panel holds one concept; P5 a panel is at most 1.0 screen high at 1366x768; P6 no list repeated on one screen; P7 every diagram has zoom; P8 the top-level menu is uncrowded (at most 8 top-level tabs); P9 a text-size control and an adaptive layout at 390, 768 and 1366 px; P10 executed code results are visualised; P11 the page declares the standard and the examples equal the deck's code manifest." ;
    backlog:measuredWithTool ex:TS_PageTemplateD, ex:TS_PageBuilder415, ex:TS_PageData224, ex:TS_PageTest36, ex:TS_Stage4Gates, ex:TS_ChapterCheck, ex:TS_DeckMatch, ex:TS_RdodiValidatorCurrent, ex:TS_RdodiValidatorPinned, ex:TS_PageTest34b, ex:TS_PageTest35b ;
    backlog:measuredWithVersion "page template 9.52.1 (new file over 9.52.0, which stays byte-identical); page builder v4_15_0 and page-data builder v2_24_0 (unchanged; the template is passed by PAGE_TEMPLATE, a builder v4_16_0 only if the default must change); page test 9.36.0 (Playwright 1.56.0); page tests 9.34.1 and 9.35.1; Stage 4 gate runner v1_1_0 reading the CURRENT RDODI validator v1.13.0; chapter check v1_3_0 reading the PINNED RDODI validator v1.6.0; deck match check v1_0_0; page check wrapper v1_3_0; Playwright 1.56.0" ;
