ex:TK_Repair_Template a backlog:ExecutionTask ; rdfs:label "Make page template 9.52.1: the story chip scrolls its story into view after the pane is fitted"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "TK_Repair_Template" ; backlog:hasTitle "Make page template 9.52.1: the story chip scrolls its story into view after the pane is fitted" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Iter_18 ; backlog:admittedByOutput ex:Out3_BacklogR28 ; backlog:responsible ex:Executor_ClaudeCodeSession ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasTaskType backlog:TaskType_Build ; backlog:effectiveDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-23T01:33:50"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-23T02:33:05"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:lastAuditedAt "2026-10-23T02:57:30"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasExecutionModality backlog:Mode_Hybrid ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Ranked by its story's state; scoring both would double-count." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Write the NEW file 08-tooling/course_page_template_v9_52_1.html from course_page_template_v9_52_0.html (which stays byte-identical). The defect (from the control of the chapter 5 page 9.80.0, register v0.205.0): MEASURED FACTS. The executor SEN0401-I17-page-ch05 reported the chapter 5 page 9.80.0 (commits c4002e1 to 0fb29ca, template 9.52.0, builders v4_15_0 and v2_24_0): the page tests 9.36.0, 9.35.1 and 9.34.1 each fail exactly one feature, 'a story chip on a concept opens that story in the Stories tab' (detail: story GoxColdFind, which lands at 2064 px, outside the 768 px viewport). Its diagnosis (confirmed by the builder session by reading template 9.52.0): the click handler of the story chips (the listener on the panes, button[data-story]) calls showTab('stories') and then scrollIntoView on the story at once; the pane height is fitted afterwards, so the scroll position is lost. The chapter 6 page 9.81.0 (executor SEN0401-I17-page-ch06, commits faf1b10 to ca2e510) passes all three tests, but it carries the same handler: the page tests click the first chip of the first concept that has one, and in chapter 6 that chip is the first story, which sits at the top of the pane and needs no scroll. So the defect is in template 9.52.0 and is latent in the chapter 6 page; the builder session re-ran the page tests on both pages on 2026-10-23 (results in the control version). THE CHANGE: in the click listener of the panes, run the scroll of the story after the pane height has been fitted (the template fits pane heights after showTab; defer the scroll until that fit is done, for example by calling it from the fit routine's completion or after two animation frames), and keep the highlight. Change nothing else: every id, hook, behaviour and the DOM contract of 9.52.0 stay (the unified diff against 9.52.0 must show only that handler and the version marker). If the builder's default template name has to change, write sen0401_page_build_v4_16_0.py as a new file over v4_15_0; otherwise leave the builders alone and name PAGE_TEMPLATE. PROOF to deliver and keep as logs: (1) the unified diff; (2) a scratch page of chapter 5 built on 9.52.1 (page data from the repository, outside the repository folders) passes the story-chip feature of the page test 9.35.1 for the story that failed (GoxColdFind), and the page tests 9.36.0 and 9.35.1 on it report no failure; (3) scratch pages of chapters 1 and 10 on 9.52.1 pass page test 9.36.0 P1, P3, P4, P5, P6, P8, P9 as they did on 9.52.0; (4) 9.52.0 is byte-identical (SHA-256 before and after). PAGE FEATURE (existing, from the page test 9.35.1 and kept in 9.36.0 and 9.34.1): a story chip on a concept opens that story in the Stories tab: after the click the Stories pane is visible and the story card is inside the viewport. A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores: browser tests run one at a time and no build runs beside them. Planned session SEN0401-I18-template; estimated start T0 after the executors begin, about 1.0 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

