    backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-23T03:02:58"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-23T05:41:33"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:lastAuditedAt "2026-10-24T02:19:07"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasExecutionModality backlog:Mode_Hybrid ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Not scored: the owner directed this work on 2026-10-22 and uses it tomorrow, so there is no ranking left to compute." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Requested Friday 2026-10-23, relayed by the course coordinator (the owner's standing direction of Thursday 2026-10-22 17:30 Istanbul: remedy the weaknesses and deliver the chapter 5 and 6 pages ready to use) (ex:CR3_ChipScroll). One criterion per unit (G133). The Done stories and tasks stay Done and are not edited (G125). MEASURED FACTS. The executor SEN0401-I17-page-ch05 reported the chapter 5 page 9.80.0 (commits c4002e1 to 0fb29ca, template 9.52.0, builders v4_15_0 and v2_24_0): the page tests 9.36.0, 9.35.1 and 9.34.1 each fail exactly one feature, 'a story chip on a concept opens that story in the Stories tab' (detail: story GoxColdFind, which lands at 2064 px, outside the 768 px viewport). Its diagnosis (confirmed by the builder session by reading template 9.52.0): the click handler of the story chips (the listener on the panes, button[data-story]) calls showTab('stories') and then scrollIntoView on the story at once; the pane height is fitted afterwards, so the scroll position is lost. The chapter 6 page 9.81.0 (executor SEN0401-I17-page-ch06, commits faf1b10 to ca2e510) passes all three tests, but it carries the same handler: the page tests click the first chip of the first concept that has one, and in chapter 6 that chip is the first story, which sits at the top of the pane and needs no scroll. So the defect is in template 9.52.0 and is latent in the chapter 6 page; the builder session re-ran the page tests on both pages on 2026-10-23 (results in the control version)." .

