ex:CR3_Charset a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "The delivered chapter 5 and 6 pages show their labels with garbled characters: may a template 9.52.2 declare the character set first, with a check, and the two pages be rebuilt on it?"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_ChipScroll, ex:AC5R_Page_Ch05, ex:AC5R_Page_Ch06 ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Requested Friday 2026-10-23 09:32 Istanbul, relayed by the course coordinator (the owner's defect report on the delivered chapter 5 and 6 pages). MEASURED FACTS. The owner reports that the delivered chapter 5 and 6 pages show the label '▸📁Wallet keys' as 'â–¸ðŸ“Wallet keys' (UTF-8 bytes read as Windows-1252). The coordinator measured the cause: in template 9.52.1, in 9.52.0 and in all older pages built from the 9.24 line, `<meta charset=\"utf-8\">` sits at byte 13587 of the file, behind a long header comment and other meta tags; a viewer that prescans only the first 1024 bytes for a charset does not find it and guesses Windows-1252. In the pages 9.82.0 of chapter 5 and chapter 6 the attribute charset=\"utf-8\" sits at byte 13584 (the coordinator's measure) and the tag `<meta charset=` starts at byte 13578 (the builder session's measure of the same files, 2026-10-23); the tag is the first thing a prescan reads. The other delivered pages (chapters 1 to 14 in the owner's archive) have the same defect. The change grows the scope: a new template version, a new check tool, and new rebuilds of two pages that were delivered. Pending until the ScopeChange that admits the stories is recorded in the Backlog version." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .

ex:IA3_Charset a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What declaring the character set first costs, measured before it is started"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR3_Charset ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage3 ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:IA3_ChipScroll ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "MEASURED FACTS. The owner reports that the delivered chapter 5 and 6 pages show the label '▸📁Wallet keys' as 'â–¸ðŸ“Wallet keys' (UTF-8 bytes read as Windows-1252). The coordinator measured the cause: in template 9.52.1, in 9.52.0 and in all older pages built from the 9.24 line, `<meta charset=\"utf-8\">` sits at byte 13587 of the file, behind a long header comment and other meta tags; a viewer that prescans only the first 1024 bytes for a charset does not find it and guesses Windows-1252. In the pages 9.82.0 of chapter 5 and chapter 6 the attribute charset=\"utf-8\" sits at byte 13584 (the coordinator's measure) and the tag `<meta charset=` starts at byte 13578 (the builder session's measure of the same files, 2026-10-23); the tag is the first thing a prescan reads. The other delivered pages (chapters 1 to 14 in the owner's archive) have the same defect. AFFECTED: the pages 9.82.0 of chapters 5 and 6 (delivered; replaced by new files 9.83.0, the old files stay); the Build task of the chapter 5 page of Iter_18 (Suspended, not edited, G125) and the Done tasks of the chapter 6 page and of the template 9.52.1 (not edited; the template 9.52.1 stays byte-identical). NOT AFFECTED: the decks, the page tests, the builders (unless the builder puts bytes before the template, then one new builder file), the pywheels files, the chapter-code manifests, every other chapter, the Mission outcome and the Achieved status. OTHER PAGES: the pages of chapters 1 to 14 in the owner's archive have the same defect (the tag at byte 13578 or later). They are NOT rebuilt by this request: the decision is tracked by the change request ex:CR3_CharsetOtherPages (Pending) and the closure caveat ex:Cav_CharsetOtherPages. PLAN (route as ex:CR3_ChipScroll, G127): a StageRevision from the Scope stage, seven versions; new iteration Iter_19 with four stories and eight tasks: the template 9.52.2 and the check (two executors, about 0.5 h each, in parallel) and their verification (builder, about 0.5 h each); then the pages of chapters 5 and 6 rebuilt in parallel (executors, about 1.5 h each) and their verification (builder, about 1 h each, serial browser tests). Estimated from T0 (both tool executors start at once): tools verified about T0+1.2 h, pages about T0+2.7 h and T0+3.2 h; the machine has 2 cores, so browser tests queue. The proposed end is today Friday 2026-10-23 23:59 UTC, the owner's to decide. COST: new files only (one template, one tool); old files byte-identical; no gate, test or threshold changes. A criterion that fails is named failing and its story is not Done; nothing is waived." .

ex:CR3_CharsetOtherPages a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "The pages of chapters 1 to 14 in the owner's archive declare their character set late: may they be rebuilt on template 9.52.2?"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_Charset ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Found Friday 2026-10-23 09:32 Istanbul, relayed by the course coordinator (the owner's defect report on the delivered chapter 5 and 6 pages). MEASURED FACTS. The owner reports that the delivered chapter 5 and 6 pages show the label '▸📁Wallet keys' as 'â–¸ðŸ“Wallet keys' (UTF-8 bytes read as Windows-1252). The coordinator measured the cause: in template 9.52.1, in 9.52.0 and in all older pages built from the 9.24 line, `<meta charset=\"utf-8\">` sits at byte 13587 of the file, behind a long header comment and other meta tags; a viewer that prescans only the first 1024 bytes for a charset does not find it and guesses Windows-1252. In the pages 9.82.0 of chapter 5 and chapter 6 the attribute charset=\"utf-8\" sits at byte 13584 (the coordinator's measure) and the tag `<meta charset=` starts at byte 13578 (the builder session's measure of the same files, 2026-10-23); the tag is the first thing a prescan reads. The other delivered pages (chapters 1 to 14 in the owner's archive) have the same defect. Only the pages of chapters 5 and 6 are rebuilt now (the owner uses them first). The other pages carry the same defect and stay as delivered until the owner decides whether to rebuild them: the decision is the disposition of this request. Pending." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Pending .

