ex:Del3_CharsetTemplate a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ;
    rdfs:label "A page template 9.52.2 that declares its character set within the first 1024 bytes, and a check that measures it, as new files with the older templates kept"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:derivesFromMissionClause "the research behind it and an interactive page"^^xsd:string ;
    backlog:hasDeliverableText "The page template 9.52.2, a new file over 9.52.1 (which stays unchanged, as do the older templates), whose first bytes are the character set declaration `<meta charset=\"utf-8\">` with the header comments after it, and a new check tool that measures the declaration; every id, hook and behaviour of 9.52.1 stays. MEASURED FACTS. The owner reports that the delivered chapter 5 and 6 pages show the label '▸📁Wallet keys' as 'â–¸ðŸ“Wallet keys' (UTF-8 bytes read as Windows-1252). The coordinator measured the cause: in template 9.52.1, in 9.52.0 and in all older pages built from the 9.24 line, `<meta charset=\"utf-8\">` sits at byte 13587 of the file, behind a long header comment and other meta tags; a viewer that prescans only the first 1024 bytes for a charset does not find it and guesses Windows-1252. In the pages 9.82.0 of chapter 5 and chapter 6 the attribute charset=\"utf-8\" sits at byte 13584 (the coordinator's measure) and the tag `<meta charset=` starts at byte 13578 (the builder session's measure of the same files, 2026-10-23); the tag is the first thing a prescan reads. The other delivered pages (chapters 1 to 14 in the owner's archive) have the same defect. PAGE FEATURE (new, measured by the new check): the file declares its character set so that a viewer which looks only at the first 1024 bytes finds it: the string `<meta charset=\"utf-8\">` occurs at a byte offset below 1024, and the first 1024 bytes decode as UTF-8 (a multibyte sequence cut by the end of the window is not an error; any other invalid byte is)." ;
    backlog:deliverableForArea ex:Area3_Remedy56 ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Work ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_Functional .
ex:Del3_CharsetPages a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ;
    rdfs:label "The pages of chapters 5 and 6 rebuilt on template 9.52.2 so that their character set is declared within the first 1024 bytes"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:derivesFromMissionClause "the research behind it and an interactive page"^^xsd:string ;
    backlog:hasDeliverableText "The pages of chapter 5 and chapter 6 rebuilt as new files on template 9.52.2 with the builders v4_15_0 and v2_24_0, passing the charset check, the page test 9.36.0 and the page tests 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 with no failure, the Stage 4 gate runner and the chapter checks. PAGE STANDARD (checked by the new page test 9.36.0, Playwright 1.56.0): P1 no horizontal overflow at 390 px and at 1366 px; P2 the chapter-code tab lists the deck's examples by NAME in the deck's slide order, each runnable in the page with the chapter library defined in the page and its result visualised, and the code lives in the editor, not in the list; P3 tabs and left tree are synchronised and their label sets are disjoint or the tab bar is one row; P4 no third level of tabs, and one more level of panels so that one panel holds one concept; P5 a panel is at most 1.0 screen high at 1366x768; P6 no list repeated on one screen; P7 every diagram has zoom; P8 the top-level menu is uncrowded (at most 8 top-level tabs); P9 a text-size control and an adaptive layout at 390, 768 and 1366 px; P10 executed code results are visualised; P11 the page declares the standard and the examples equal the deck's code manifest." ;
    backlog:deliverableForArea ex:Area3_Remedy56 ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Work ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_Functional .
ex:Scope3 backlog:requiresDeliverable ex:Del3_CharsetTemplate, ex:Del3_CharsetPages ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_Charset, ex:IA3_Charset .
ex:Scope3 rdfs:comment "Revised 2026-10-23 by the stage revision ex:Revision_Lineage3_Scope7 on the change request ex:CR3_Charset (Friday 2026-10-23 09:32 Istanbul, relayed by the course coordinator (the owner's defect report on the delivered chapter 5 and 6 pages)). The statement above is unchanged (L-112). It now also requires ex:Del3_CharsetTemplate and ex:Del3_CharsetPages in the area ex:Area3_Remedy56. No exclusion changes: the new template is a new file named in the deliverable and the exclusion of changes to gates, tests and thresholds still holds."@en .

