    backlog:hasGherkinText "Owner-directed work (ex:CR3_Charset). Given the template 9.52.1 (byte-identical after the task) and the defect measured on the pages 9.82.0, when the NEW file course_page_template_v9_52_2.html is written, then ALL of: (1) the file is new and the templates 9.52.0 and 9.52.1 and every older template are byte-identical; (2) `<meta charset=\"utf-8\">` occurs exactly once, at a byte offset below 1024, and the first 1024 bytes decode as UTF-8; (3) the unified diff of 9.52.2 over 9.52.1 shows only the moved tag, the moved header comments (the same lines in a new order) and the version marker, and every id and hook of 9.52.1 and the DOM contract are present; (4) a scratch page of chapter 5 built on 9.52.2 with the builders v4_15_0 and v2_24_0 (PAGE_TEMPLATE) has the tag below byte 1024 and passes the page test 9.36.0 with no failure; (5) no committed file is edited, no gate, test or threshold changed; results as printed; if any element fails the template is named failing. MEASURED FACTS. The owner reports that the delivered chapter 5 and 6 pages show the label '▸📁Wallet keys' as 'â–¸ðŸ“Wallet keys' (UTF-8 bytes read as Windows-1252). The coordinator measured the cause: in template 9.52.1, in 9.52.0 and in all older pages built from the 9.24 line, `<meta charset=\"utf-8\">` sits at byte 13587 of the file, behind a long header comment and other meta tags; a viewer that prescans only the first 1024 bytes for a charset does not find it and guesses Windows-1252. In the pages 9.82.0 of chapter 5 and chapter 6 the attribute charset=\"utf-8\" sits at byte 13584 (the coordinator's measure) and the tag `<meta charset=` starts at byte 13578 (the builder session's measure of the same files, 2026-10-23); the tag is the first thing a prescan reads. The other delivered pages (chapters 1 to 14 in the owner's archive) have the same defect. PAGE FEATURE (new, measured by the new check): the file declares its character set so that a viewer which looks only at the first 1024 bytes finds it: the string `<meta charset=\"utf-8\">` occurs at a byte offset below 1024, and the first 1024 bytes decode as UTF-8 (a multibyte sequence cut by the end of the window is not an error; any other invalid byte is)." ;
    backlog:measuredWithTool ex:TS_PageTemplateE, ex:TS_PageCharsetCheck, ex:TS_PageTest36, ex:TS_PageBuilder415, ex:TS_PageData224 ;
    backlog:measuredWithVersion "page template 9.52.2 (new file over 9.52.1, which stays byte-identical, as do 9.52.0 and every older template); page charset check v1_0_0 (a new tool, Python 3.13 standard library only); page builder v4_15_0 and page-data builder v2_24_0 (unchanged; the template is passed by PAGE_TEMPLATE, a builder v4_16_0 only if the builder puts anything before the template's first bytes); page test 9.36.0 (Playwright 1.56.0); page tests 9.34.1 and 9.35.1; Stage 4 gate runner v1_1_0 reading the CURRENT RDODI validator v1.13.0; chapter check v1_3_0 reading the PINNED RDODI validator v1.6.0; deck match check v1_0_0; page check wrapper v1_4_1; Playwright 1.56.0" ;
