ex:AC6R_Check a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; rdfs:label "The page charset check fails every page without a UTF-8 charset declaration in its first 1024 bytes and passes every page with one"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Owner-directed work (ex:CR3_Charset). Given the pages 9.82.0 of chapters 5 and 6 (known bad) and the template 9.52.1, when the NEW tool sen0401_page_charset_check_v1_0_0.py is written, then ALL of: (1) the tool is a new file using the standard library only and changes no file; (2) it exits non-zero and prints the tag offset 13578 on the pages 9.82.0 of chapters 5 and 6 and prints a failure on template 9.52.1; (3) it exits zero on a fixture with the tag at byte 0, on one with the tag at byte 1000 and on one whose UTF-8 character is cut by byte 1024; (4) it exits non-zero on a fixture with the tag at byte 1100, on one with the tag at byte 10 and an invalid byte before byte 1024, and on a missing file; (5) it exits zero only when every file given passes; no committed file is edited; results as printed; if any element fails the tool is named failing. MEASURED FACTS. The owner reports that the delivered chapter 5 and 6 pages show the label '▸📁Wallet keys' as 'â–¸ðŸ“Wallet keys' (UTF-8 bytes read as Windows-1252). The coordinator measured the cause: in template 9.52.1, in 9.52.0 and in all older pages built from the 9.24 line, `<meta charset=\"utf-8\">` sits at byte 13587 of the file, behind a long header comment and other meta tags; a viewer that prescans only the first 1024 bytes for a charset does not find it and guesses Windows-1252. In the pages 9.82.0 of chapter 5 and chapter 6 the attribute charset=\"utf-8\" sits at byte 13584 (the coordinator's measure) and the tag `<meta charset=` starts at byte 13578 (the builder session's measure of the same files, 2026-10-23); the tag is the first thing a prescan reads. The other delivered pages (chapters 1 to 14 in the owner's archive) have the same defect. PAGE FEATURE (new, measured by the new check): the file declares its character set so that a viewer which looks only at the first 1024 bytes finds it: the string `<meta charset=\"utf-8\">` occurs at a byte offset below 1024, and the first 1024 bytes decode as UTF-8 (a multibyte sequence cut by the end of the window is not an error; any other invalid byte is)." ;
    backlog:measuredWithTool ex:TS_PageCharsetCheck ;
    backlog:measuredWithVersion "page template 9.52.2 (new file over 9.52.1, which stays byte-identical, as do 9.52.0 and every older template); page charset check v1_0_0 (a new tool, Python 3.13 standard library only); page builder v4_15_0 and page-data builder v2_24_0 (unchanged; the template is passed by PAGE_TEMPLATE, a builder v4_16_0 only if the builder puts anything before the template's first bytes); page test 9.36.0 (Playwright 1.56.0); page tests 9.34.1 and 9.35.1; Stage 4 gate runner v1_1_0 reading the CURRENT RDODI validator v1.13.0; chapter check v1_3_0 reading the PINNED RDODI validator v1.6.0; deck match check v1_0_0; page check wrapper v1_4_1; Playwright 1.56.0" ;
