ex:TK_Charset_Template a backlog:ExecutionTask ; rdfs:label "Make page template 9.52.2: the character set is declared first, within the first 1024 bytes"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "TK_Charset_Template" ; backlog:hasTitle "Make page template 9.52.2: the character set is declared first, within the first 1024 bytes" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Iter_19 ; backlog:admittedByOutput ex:Out3_BacklogR28 ; backlog:responsible ex:Executor_ClaudeCodeSession ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasTaskType backlog:TaskType_Build ; backlog:effectiveDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-23T09:58:08"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-23T10:22:49"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:lastAuditedAt "2026-10-23T11:10:21"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasExecutionModality backlog:Mode_Hybrid ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Ranked by its story's state; scoring both would double-count." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Write the NEW file 08-tooling/course_page_template_v9_52_2.html from course_page_template_v9_52_1.html (which stays byte-identical, as do 9.52.0 and every older template). MEASURED FACTS. The owner reports that the delivered chapter 5 and 6 pages show the label '▸📁Wallet keys' as 'â–¸ðŸ“Wallet keys' (UTF-8 bytes read as Windows-1252). The coordinator measured the cause: in template 9.52.1, in 9.52.0 and in all older pages built from the 9.24 line, `<meta charset=\"utf-8\">` sits at byte 13587 of the file, behind a long header comment and other meta tags; a viewer that prescans only the first 1024 bytes for a charset does not find it and guesses Windows-1252. In the pages 9.82.0 of chapter 5 and chapter 6 the attribute charset=\"utf-8\" sits at byte 13584 (the coordinator's measure) and the tag `<meta charset=` starts at byte 13578 (the builder session's measure of the same files, 2026-10-23); the tag is the first thing a prescan reads. The other delivered pages (chapters 1 to 14 in the owner's archive) have the same defect. THE CHANGE: `<meta charset=\"utf-8\">` becomes the very first element of the file (the first bytes), and the template's header comments, which are long, move after it, so that the declaration lies within the first 1024 bytes; the version marker comment names 9.52.2. Change nothing else: every id, hook, behaviour and the DOM contract of 9.52.1 stay; the unified diff against 9.52.1 shows only the moved charset tag and the moved comments (same lines, new order) and the version marker. The tag must stay exactly once in the file. Then build one scratch page of chapter 5 on 9.52.2 outside the repository folders (builders v4_15_0 and v2_24_0, PAGE_TEMPLATE, PAGE_SCRATCH / PAGE_DATA_OUT) and show that the byte offset of the tag in the built page is below 1024: if the page builder puts anything before the template's first bytes and the offset is not below 1024, write sen0401_page_build_v4_16_0.py as a new file over v4_15_0 and say so. PROOF to deliver and keep as logs: (1) the unified diff; (2) SHA-256 of 9.52.0, 9.52.1 and 9.52.2 before and after; (3) the byte offset of the tag in the template and in the scratch page; (4) the page test 9.36.0 on the scratch page of chapter 5 reports no failure. DO NOT EDIT OR APPEND TO ANY FILE COMMITTED EARLIER, INCLUDING YOUR OWN LOG FILES: write each log once, after its run is complete, and commit it once (the control of the page 9.82.0 of chapter 5 found a log file of the executor appended in a later commit, which fails the element 'no committed file is edited'). PAGE FEATURE (new, measured by the new check): the file declares its character set so that a viewer which looks only at the first 1024 bytes finds it: the string `<meta charset=\"utf-8\">` occurs at a byte offset below 1024, and the first 1024 bytes decode as UTF-8 (a multibyte sequence cut by the end of the window is not an error; any other invalid byte is). A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores: browser tests run one at a time and no build runs beside them. Planned session SEN0401-I19-template; estimated start T0 after the executors begin, about 0.5 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

