ex:TK_Charset_Check a backlog:ExecutionTask ; rdfs:label "Make the page charset check: fail unless the character set is declared within the first 1024 bytes and they decode as UTF-8"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "TK_Charset_Check" ; backlog:hasTitle "Make the page charset check: fail unless the character set is declared within the first 1024 bytes and they decode as UTF-8" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Iter_19 ; backlog:admittedByOutput ex:Out3_BacklogR28 ; backlog:responsible ex:Executor_ClaudeCodeSession ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasTaskType backlog:TaskType_Build ; backlog:effectiveDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-23T09:58:08"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-23T10:05:46"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:lastAuditedAt "2026-10-23T10:41:45"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasExecutionModality backlog:Mode_Hybrid ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Ranked by its story's state; scoring both would double-count." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Write the NEW tool 08-tooling/sen0401_page_charset_check_v1_0_0.py (Python 3.13, standard library only): usage `python3 -B sen0401_page_charset_check_v1_0_0.py FILE...`; for each file it prints PASS or FAIL with the byte offset found, and the exit code is 0 only when EVERY file passes. A file passes only when BOTH hold: (1) the case-insensitive pattern of a meta charset declaration for utf-8 (`<meta charset=\"utf-8\">`, any quoting, spacing and case) is found within the first 1024 bytes, and (2) the first 1024 bytes decode as UTF-8; a multibyte sequence that is merely cut by the end of the 1024-byte window is NOT an error, any other invalid byte is. A missing file or no tag is FAIL, never skipped. MEASURED FACTS. The owner reports that the delivered chapter 5 and 6 pages show the label '▸📁Wallet keys' as 'â–¸ðŸ“Wallet keys' (UTF-8 bytes read as Windows-1252). The coordinator measured the cause: in template 9.52.1, in 9.52.0 and in all older pages built from the 9.24 line, `<meta charset=\"utf-8\">` sits at byte 13587 of the file, behind a long header comment and other meta tags; a viewer that prescans only the first 1024 bytes for a charset does not find it and guesses Windows-1252. In the pages 9.82.0 of chapter 5 and chapter 6 the attribute charset=\"utf-8\" sits at byte 13584 (the coordinator's measure) and the tag `<meta charset=` starts at byte 13578 (the builder session's measure of the same files, 2026-10-23); the tag is the first thing a prescan reads. The other delivered pages (chapters 1 to 14 in the owner's archive) have the same defect. PROOF to deliver and keep as logs: (a) the tool FAILS (exit non-zero, offset of the start of the tag printed: 13578 on both pages) on the shipped pages 03-materials/ch05/page/sen0401_ch05_page_v9_82_0.html and 03-materials/ch06/page/sen0401_ch06_page_v9_82_0.html and on the template 9.52.1; (b) it PASSES on three small fixture files you write beside the logs (a tag at byte 0, a tag at byte 1000, and a tag at byte 0 with a UTF-8 character cut by byte 1024); (c) it FAILS on a fixture with the tag at byte 1100, on a fixture with the tag at byte 10 and an invalid byte (0xFF) before byte 1024, and on a missing file; (d) the tool does not change any file. DO NOT EDIT OR APPEND TO ANY FILE COMMITTED EARLIER, INCLUDING YOUR OWN LOG FILES: write each log once, after its run is complete, and commit it once (the control of the page 9.82.0 of chapter 5 found a log file of the executor appended in a later commit, which fails the element 'no committed file is edited'). PAGE FEATURE (new, measured by the new check): the file declares its character set so that a viewer which looks only at the first 1024 bytes finds it: the string `<meta charset=\"utf-8\">` occurs at a byte offset below 1024, and the first 1024 bytes decode as UTF-8 (a multibyte sequence cut by the end of the window is not an error; any other invalid byte is). A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores: browser tests run one at a time and no build runs beside them. Planned session SEN0401-I19-check; estimated start T0 after the executors begin, about 0.5 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

