    backlog:hasReach "1"^^xsd:decimal ; backlog:hasImpact "0.5"^^xsd:decimal ; backlog:hasConfidence "0.8"^^xsd:decimal ; backlog:hasEffort "1.5"^^xsd:decimal ; backlog:hasDepFactor "1"^^xsd:decimal ;
    backlog:hasScoreValue "0.27"^^xsd:decimal ; backlog:scoredAt "2026-10-23T11:10:32"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:isAveragedFromMembers false ;
    backlog:hasScoreRationale "RICE with dependency factor (BP-D10): score = Reach x Impact x Confidence / Effort = 1 x 0.5 x 0.8 / 1.5 = 0.27; the dependency factor 1 is recorded beside it and the ORDERING KEY is the score times the dependency factor = 0.27. Reach 1 page. Impact 0.5 (low): the page passes all three page tests; the one failing element is formal (an appended log file). Confidence 0.8: measured by the control of v0.216.0. Effort 1.5 h: redo the log commit 0.5 h plus control 1.0 h. DepFactor 1: no open prerequisite. It ships the same charset defect as the page it would deliver, so the owner's rule puts the charset repair above it. FACTS: the owner's archive holds 14 chapter pages built on the one template line, each with the charset tag behind byte 1024 (the coordinator's measure); the builder session measured the tag at byte 13578 in the pages 9.82.0 of chapters 5 and 6; the owner reported garbled labels on pages he uses in class (2026-10-23 09:32 Istanbul). Recorded on the owner's instruction 'Repairs should change the priority of the PBIs or the tasks'; a new dated record, no earlier score is edited. Re-run after the completion of TK_Charset_Template and TK_Charset_Template_Verify (BP-D11); the prerequisites of both page rebuilds are now Done, so their dependency factor is 1; the item points to this record, the earlier record stays in the register unedited." .
