ex:CR3_Ch78 a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "Chapters 7 and 8 are urgent: may they get a deck, a chapter-code manifest and a page on the current standard, with a deck check that measures their research?"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_Charset, ex:CR3_Remedy56 ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Requested Friday 2026-10-23 16:06 Istanbul, relayed by the course coordinator (the owner's decision): chapters 6, 7 and 8 are urgent; chapter 6 is rebuilt already (Iteration 19). Chapters 7 and 8 need a deck, a chapter-code manifest and a page on the current standard (template 9.52.2, character set first). MEASURED FACTS (2026-10-23, by the builder session with the committed tools). Decks: the deck standard check v1_0_0 on the newest decks gives PASS=12 for chapters 5 and 6 and FAIL for every other chapter: chapters 1 to 4 fail D1, D2, D3, D4, D5, D7, D10, D11 (PASS=4); chapter 7 (26 slides, 14 code slides) fails the same eight (D1 25 of 26 numbered, D2 longest box 45 words, D3 3 of 14 code slides complete, D4 0 of 87 key concepts with an analogy, D5 0 of 3 stories complete, D7 longest note 100 words, D10 0 of 5 dividers complete, D11 32 of 87 research concepts shown = 36.8 percent); chapter 8 (26 slides, 16 code slides) and chapters 9 to 14 fail D1, D2, D3, D5, D7, D10 and the check returns NOT_MEASURED for D4 and D11 because their research files declare the key concepts as sen0414:PrimarySourceConcept while the check reads sen0401:PrimarySourceConcept (a skip is not a pass). Manifests: only chapters 5 and 6 have a chapter-code manifest. Pages: the charset check v1_0_0 passes the newest pages of chapters 5 and 6 (tag at byte 37) and fails the newest page of every other chapter (tag at byte 11172, or 11888 for chapter 10); the pages of chapters 7 and 8 (9.76.0, 9.77.0) are built on template 9.51.0 and have no chapter-code tab. Research, a deck and a page exist for all fourteen chapters; no chapter is unbuilt. The change grows the scope: two decks and two pages rebuilt as new files, and a new version of the deck check, because the present check cannot measure two of its twelve elements on chapter 8. Pending until the ScopeChange that admits the stories is recorded in the Backlog version." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .

ex:IA3_Ch78 a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What bringing chapters 7 and 8 to the current standard costs, measured before it is started"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR3_Ch78 ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage3 ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:IA3_Charset ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "MEASURED FACTS (2026-10-23, by the builder session with the committed tools). Decks: the deck standard check v1_0_0 on the newest decks gives PASS=12 for chapters 5 and 6 and FAIL for every other chapter: chapters 1 to 4 fail D1, D2, D3, D4, D5, D7, D10, D11 (PASS=4); chapter 7 (26 slides, 14 code slides) fails the same eight (D1 25 of 26 numbered, D2 longest box 45 words, D3 3 of 14 code slides complete, D4 0 of 87 key concepts with an analogy, D5 0 of 3 stories complete, D7 longest note 100 words, D10 0 of 5 dividers complete, D11 32 of 87 research concepts shown = 36.8 percent); chapter 8 (26 slides, 16 code slides) and chapters 9 to 14 fail D1, D2, D3, D5, D7, D10 and the check returns NOT_MEASURED for D4 and D11 because their research files declare the key concepts as sen0414:PrimarySourceConcept while the check reads sen0401:PrimarySourceConcept (a skip is not a pass). Manifests: only chapters 5 and 6 have a chapter-code manifest. Pages: the charset check v1_0_0 passes the newest pages of chapters 5 and 6 (tag at byte 37) and fails the newest page of every other chapter (tag at byte 11172, or 11888 for chapter 10); the pages of chapters 7 and 8 (9.76.0, 9.77.0) are built on template 9.51.0 and have no chapter-code tab. Research, a deck and a page exist for all fourteen chapters; no chapter is unbuilt. AFFECTED: the decks of chapters 7 (1.3.0) and 8 (1.1.0) and the pages 9.76.0 and 9.77.0 are replaced by new files (the old files stay); the deck check gets a new file v1_1_0 (v1_0_0 stays). NOT AFFECTED: the template 9.52.2, the page builders and tests, the pages and decks of every other chapter, the Mission outcome and the Achieved status. PLAN (route as ex:CR3_Charset, G127): a StageRevision from the Scope stage, seven versions; new iteration Iter_20 with five stories and ten tasks: the deck check v1_1_0 (an executor, about 0.5 h, verified about 0.5 h by the builder); the decks of chapters 7 and 8 (two executors in parallel, about 1.5 h each, verified about 0.5 h each by the builder); then the pages of chapters 7 and 8 (two executors, about 1.5 h each with three serial page-test runs each, verified about 1 h each by the builder with three serial runs). Measured from the chapters 5 and 6 work of 2026-10-22 and 23: the deck executor of chapter 6 needed 35 minutes, the page executor 62 minutes on an idle machine, a control run of one page test about 10 minutes. The machine has 2 cores shared with other sessions; browser tests run one at a time. Estimated from T0 (the executors of the deck check and of both decks start at once): decks verified about T0+2.0 h and T0+2.5 h; page of chapter 7 about T0+3.5 h, page of chapter 8 about T0+4.5 h, all on an idle machine; with the present machine load of other sessions the browser tests may take twice as long, so up to about T0+8 h. The proposed end is Saturday 2026-10-24 09:00 UTC, the owner's to decide. COST: new files only; old files byte-identical; no gate, test or threshold changes. A criterion that fails is named failing and its story is not Done; nothing is waived." .

ex:CR3_Retrofit a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "After chapters 7 and 8: bring chapters 1 to 4 and 9 to 14 to the same standard, in order"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_Ch78 ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Requested Friday 2026-10-23 16:06 Istanbul, relayed by the course coordinator (the owner's decision): after chapters 6, 7 and 8, return to all chapters starting with chapter 1 (retrofit: manifest, deck match, page with chapter-code tab and panels, character set) and after that build the remaining chapters. MEASURED FACTS (2026-10-23, by the builder session with the committed tools). Decks: the deck standard check v1_0_0 on the newest decks gives PASS=12 for chapters 5 and 6 and FAIL for every other chapter: chapters 1 to 4 fail D1, D2, D3, D4, D5, D7, D10, D11 (PASS=4); chapter 7 (26 slides, 14 code slides) fails the same eight (D1 25 of 26 numbered, D2 longest box 45 words, D3 3 of 14 code slides complete, D4 0 of 87 key concepts with an analogy, D5 0 of 3 stories complete, D7 longest note 100 words, D10 0 of 5 dividers complete, D11 32 of 87 research concepts shown = 36.8 percent); chapter 8 (26 slides, 16 code slides) and chapters 9 to 14 fail D1, D2, D3, D5, D7, D10 and the check returns NOT_MEASURED for D4 and D11 because their research files declare the key concepts as sen0414:PrimarySourceConcept while the check reads sen0401:PrimarySourceConcept (a skip is not a pass). Manifests: only chapters 5 and 6 have a chapter-code manifest. Pages: the charset check v1_0_0 passes the newest pages of chapters 5 and 6 (tag at byte 37) and fails the newest page of every other chapter (tag at byte 11172, or 11888 for chapter 10); the pages of chapters 7 and 8 (9.76.0, 9.77.0) are built on template 9.51.0 and have no chapter-code tab. Research, a deck and a page exist for all fourteen chapters; no chapter is unbuilt. Planned now, NOT started: Iteration 21 holds the ten chapters 1 to 4 and 9 to 14 in order (chapters 5 to 8 are done by Iterations 19 and 20), each as a deck story and a page story with its own criterion. Nothing is unbuilt in the fourteen chapters, so 'the remaining chapters' has no content beyond this retrofit; the owner's materials folder 'numbers' is the only other material and is not a chapter. Pending until the ScopeChange that admits the stories is recorded in the Backlog version." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .

ex:IA3_Retrofit a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What the retrofit of chapters 1 to 4 and 9 to 14 costs, estimated before it is planned into an iteration"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR3_Retrofit ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage3 ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:IA3_Ch78 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "MEASURED FACTS (2026-10-23, by the builder session with the committed tools). Decks: the deck standard check v1_0_0 on the newest decks gives PASS=12 for chapters 5 and 6 and FAIL for every other chapter: chapters 1 to 4 fail D1, D2, D3, D4, D5, D7, D10, D11 (PASS=4); chapter 7 (26 slides, 14 code slides) fails the same eight (D1 25 of 26 numbered, D2 longest box 45 words, D3 3 of 14 code slides complete, D4 0 of 87 key concepts with an analogy, D5 0 of 3 stories complete, D7 longest note 100 words, D10 0 of 5 dividers complete, D11 32 of 87 research concepts shown = 36.8 percent); chapter 8 (26 slides, 16 code slides) and chapters 9 to 14 fail D1, D2, D3, D5, D7, D10 and the check returns NOT_MEASURED for D4 and D11 because their research files declare the key concepts as sen0414:PrimarySourceConcept while the check reads sen0401:PrimarySourceConcept (a skip is not a pass). Manifests: only chapters 5 and 6 have a chapter-code manifest. Pages: the charset check v1_0_0 passes the newest pages of chapters 5 and 6 (tag at byte 37) and fails the newest page of every other chapter (tag at byte 11172, or 11888 for chapter 10); the pages of chapters 7 and 8 (9.76.0, 9.77.0) are built on template 9.51.0 and have no chapter-code tab. Research, a deck and a page exist for all fourteen chapters; no chapter is unbuilt. ESTIMATE per chapter (executor and builder hours): deck 1.5 h build plus 0.5 h verification, page 1.5 h build plus 1.0 h verification = 4.5 h; ten chapters = 45 hours of work, of which the browser tests (three runs by the executor, three by the builder, about 10 minutes each on an idle machine = about 1 h per page) are serial: about 10 hours of browser time. With three executors in parallel and the machine as it is today the retrofit is about 2 days of wall-clock (planned Sunday 2026-10-25 to Monday 2026-10-26, from the end of Iteration 20); the estimates are not measurements. ORDER: chapters 1, 2, 3, 4, then 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14 (chapters 5 and 6 are done, 7 and 8 are in Iteration 20). NOT STARTED: no executor is briefed, no work begun is recorded; the stories are Proposed. COST: new files only." .

ex:Revision_Lineage3_Scope8 a backlog:StageRevision ;
    rdfs:label "Revision of the third lineage from the Scope stage: chapters 7 and 8 urgent, then the retrofit of chapters 1 to 14"@en ;
    backlog:revisesLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:revisesFromStage backlog:Stage_Scope ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_Ch78, ex:IA3_Ch78, ex:CR3_Retrofit, ex:IA3_Retrofit ;
    backlog:revisionReason "The change requests ex:CR3_Ch78 and ex:CR3_Retrofit (Friday 2026-10-23 16:06 Istanbul, relayed by the course coordinator (the owner's decision)) add deliverables (decks and pages of chapters 7 and 8 and a new deck check version, and the planned retrofit of ten more chapters, all as new files); the lineage is in its closed Backlog stage, and a deliverable added to a closed scope statement is a revision from the Scope stage (ruling G127). The requests and their impact assessments ex:IA3_Ch78 and ex:IA3_Retrofit were recorded first. This version retracts the Scope, Goal, Objective and Backlog outputs and rebuilds nothing; the next four versions rebuild them one stage each, a sixth fills the last commit; the items already in the register, Done ones included, re-enter by admission and are not re-dated. The retracted outputs and their digests stay as history (L-112). The interim versions are the declared transition (G129). Recorded as decided by the builder role." ;
    backlog:retractsOutput ex:Out3_ScopeR8, ex:Out3_GoalR8, ex:Out3_ObjectiveR8, ex:Out3_BacklogR10 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:revisedAtCommit "6cfde86" .
ex:Out3_ScopeR8 backlog:outputRetracted true .
ex:Out3_GoalR8 backlog:outputRetracted true .
ex:Out3_ObjectiveR8 backlog:outputRetracted true .
ex:Out3_BacklogR10 backlog:outputRetracted true .

ex:Del3_Ch78Decks a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ;
    rdfs:label "The decks of chapters 7 and 8 rebuilt to the deck standard with their chapter-code manifests, and a deck check that measures the key concepts of every chapter's research, as new files"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:derivesFromMissionClause "the research behind it and an interactive page"^^xsd:string ;
    backlog:hasDeliverableText "The decks of chapter 7 and chapter 8 as new files with new version numbers meeting the deck standard D1 to D12 with a chapter-code manifest each, and a new deck standard check v1_1_0 (v1_0_0 stays) that reads the key concepts of the research whichever class declares them. MEASURED FACTS (2026-10-23, by the builder session with the committed tools). Decks: the deck standard check v1_0_0 on the newest decks gives PASS=12 for chapters 5 and 6 and FAIL for every other chapter: chapters 1 to 4 fail D1, D2, D3, D4, D5, D7, D10, D11 (PASS=4); chapter 7 (26 slides, 14 code slides) fails the same eight (D1 25 of 26 numbered, D2 longest box 45 words, D3 3 of 14 code slides complete, D4 0 of 87 key concepts with an analogy, D5 0 of 3 stories complete, D7 longest note 100 words, D10 0 of 5 dividers complete, D11 32 of 87 research concepts shown = 36.8 percent); chapter 8 (26 slides, 16 code slides) and chapters 9 to 14 fail D1, D2, D3, D5, D7, D10 and the check returns NOT_MEASURED for D4 and D11 because their research files declare the key concepts as sen0414:PrimarySourceConcept while the check reads sen0401:PrimarySourceConcept (a skip is not a pass). Manifests: only chapters 5 and 6 have a chapter-code manifest. Pages: the charset check v1_0_0 passes the newest pages of chapters 5 and 6 (tag at byte 37) and fails the newest page of every other chapter (tag at byte 11172, or 11888 for chapter 10); the pages of chapters 7 and 8 (9.76.0, 9.77.0) are built on template 9.51.0 and have no chapter-code tab. Research, a deck and a page exist for all fourteen chapters; no chapter is unbuilt. DECK STANDARD (checked by the deck standard check, python-pptx 1.0.2, one named result per element): D1 every slide is numbered; D2 no text box over 30 words; D3 every code slide has a plain-language explanation beside the code and the executed result as a visual (a native chart, a table or a drawn diagram), not REPL text; D4 every key concept of the chapter has an everyday analogy slide or box (the key concepts are listed in the chapter research); D5 every story has who, what, when, where, why and how, a real picture and a live link; D6 every chart is a native chart object, no chart picture; D7 speaker notes at most 60 words per slide; D8 a resources slide with links; D9 one background scheme, no dark/light switching mid-deck; D10 every divider names its concepts with one line of meaning and one visual; D11 coverage: the share of the chapter research concepts that appear on a slide, stated as measured, not below 90 percent; D12 no code line wraps." ;
    backlog:deliverableForArea ex:Area3_Remedy56 ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Work ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_Functional .

ex:Del3_Ch78Pages a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ;
    rdfs:label "The pages of chapters 7 and 8 rebuilt on template 9.52.2 with the chapter-code tab and the character set first"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:derivesFromMissionClause "the research behind it and an interactive page"^^xsd:string ;
    backlog:hasDeliverableText "The pages of chapter 7 and chapter 8 as new files on template 9.52.2 with the builders v4_15_0 and v2_24_0, passing the charset check, the page test 9.36.0 and the page tests 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 with no failure, the Stage 4 gate runner and the chapter checks. PAGE STANDARD (checked by the new page test 9.36.0, Playwright 1.56.0): P1 no horizontal overflow at 390 px and at 1366 px; P2 the chapter-code tab lists the deck's examples by NAME in the deck's slide order, each runnable in the page with the chapter library defined in the page and its result visualised, and the code lives in the editor, not in the list; P3 tabs and left tree are synchronised and their label sets are disjoint or the tab bar is one row; P4 no third level of tabs, and one more level of panels so that one panel holds one concept; P5 a panel is at most 1.0 screen high at 1366x768; P6 no list repeated on one screen; P7 every diagram has zoom; P8 the top-level menu is uncrowded (at most 8 top-level tabs); P9 a text-size control and an adaptive layout at 390, 768 and 1366 px; P10 executed code results are visualised; P11 the page declares the standard and the examples equal the deck's code manifest." ;
