ex:Del3_RetrofitDecks a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ;
    rdfs:label "The decks of chapters 1 to 4 and 9 to 14 rebuilt to the deck standard with their chapter-code manifests (planned, not started)"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:derivesFromMissionClause "the research behind it and an interactive page"^^xsd:string ;
    backlog:hasDeliverableText "The decks of chapters 1, 2, 3, 4, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13 and 14 as new files meeting the deck standard D1 to D12 with a chapter-code manifest each, in this order. Planned in Iteration 21; no executor is briefed. MEASURED FACTS (2026-10-23, by the builder session with the committed tools). Decks: the deck standard check v1_0_0 on the newest decks gives PASS=12 for chapters 5 and 6 and FAIL for every other chapter: chapters 1 to 4 fail D1, D2, D3, D4, D5, D7, D10, D11 (PASS=4); chapter 7 (26 slides, 14 code slides) fails the same eight (D1 25 of 26 numbered, D2 longest box 45 words, D3 3 of 14 code slides complete, D4 0 of 87 key concepts with an analogy, D5 0 of 3 stories complete, D7 longest note 100 words, D10 0 of 5 dividers complete, D11 32 of 87 research concepts shown = 36.8 percent); chapter 8 (26 slides, 16 code slides) and chapters 9 to 14 fail D1, D2, D3, D5, D7, D10 and the check returns NOT_MEASURED for D4 and D11 because their research files declare the key concepts as sen0414:PrimarySourceConcept while the check reads sen0401:PrimarySourceConcept (a skip is not a pass). Manifests: only chapters 5 and 6 have a chapter-code manifest. Pages: the charset check v1_0_0 passes the newest pages of chapters 5 and 6 (tag at byte 37) and fails the newest page of every other chapter (tag at byte 11172, or 11888 for chapter 10); the pages of chapters 7 and 8 (9.76.0, 9.77.0) are built on template 9.51.0 and have no chapter-code tab. Research, a deck and a page exist for all fourteen chapters; no chapter is unbuilt." ;
    backlog:deliverableForArea ex:Area3_Remedy56 ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Work ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_Functional .

