    backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_Derived ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner ;
    backlog:hasGoalRationale "Derived from the revised scope and the change request ex:CR3_Retrofit: after chapters 6, 7 and 8 all chapters follow in order. MEASURED FACTS (2026-10-23, by the builder session with the committed tools). Decks: the deck standard check v1_0_0 on the newest decks gives PASS=12 for chapters 5 and 6 and FAIL for every other chapter: chapters 1 to 4 fail D1, D2, D3, D4, D5, D7, D10, D11 (PASS=4); chapter 7 (26 slides, 14 code slides) fails the same eight (D1 25 of 26 numbered, D2 longest box 45 words, D3 3 of 14 code slides complete, D4 0 of 87 key concepts with an analogy, D5 0 of 3 stories complete, D7 longest note 100 words, D10 0 of 5 dividers complete, D11 32 of 87 research concepts shown = 36.8 percent); chapter 8 (26 slides, 16 code slides) and chapters 9 to 14 fail D1, D2, D3, D5, D7, D10 and the check returns NOT_MEASURED for D4 and D11 because their research files declare the key concepts as sen0414:PrimarySourceConcept while the check reads sen0401:PrimarySourceConcept (a skip is not a pass). Manifests: only chapters 5 and 6 have a chapter-code manifest. Pages: the charset check v1_0_0 passes the newest pages of chapters 5 and 6 (tag at byte 37) and fails the newest page of every other chapter (tag at byte 11172, or 11888 for chapter 10); the pages of chapters 7 and 8 (9.76.0, 9.77.0) are built on template 9.51.0 and have no chapter-code tab. Research, a deck and a page exist for all fourteen chapters; no chapter is unbuilt." ;
    backlog:producedByStage ex:Out3_GoalR9 .
ex:G3_Retrofit rdfs:comment "Drafted by the builder session on 2026-10-23 from the change request ex:CR3_Retrofit; the intent origin is therefore Derived."@en .
ex:Spec3I_Retrofit a backlog:Specification ;
    rdfs:label "What it is for a chapter to meet the deck and page standard"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:specifiesGoal ex:G3_Retrofit ;
    backlog:hasSpecificationText "The same standard as for chapters 7 and 8, chapter by chapter in the order 1, 2, 3, 4, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14. DECK STANDARD (checked by the deck standard check, python-pptx 1.0.2, one named result per element): D1 every slide is numbered; D2 no text box over 30 words; D3 every code slide has a plain-language explanation beside the code and the executed result as a visual (a native chart, a table or a drawn diagram), not REPL text; D4 every key concept of the chapter has an everyday analogy slide or box (the key concepts are listed in the chapter research); D5 every story has who, what, when, where, why and how, a real picture and a live link; D6 every chart is a native chart object, no chart picture; D7 speaker notes at most 60 words per slide; D8 a resources slide with links; D9 one background scheme, no dark/light switching mid-deck; D10 every divider names its concepts with one line of meaning and one visual; D11 coverage: the share of the chapter research concepts that appear on a slide, stated as measured, not below 90 percent; D12 no code line wraps. PAGE STANDARD (checked by the new page test 9.36.0, Playwright 1.56.0): P1 no horizontal overflow at 390 px and at 1366 px; P2 the chapter-code tab lists the deck's examples by NAME in the deck's slide order, each runnable in the page with the chapter library defined in the page and its result visualised, and the code lives in the editor, not in the list; P3 tabs and left tree are synchronised and their label sets are disjoint or the tab bar is one row; P4 no third level of tabs, and one more level of panels so that one panel holds one concept; P5 a panel is at most 1.0 screen high at 1366x768; P6 no list repeated on one screen; P7 every diagram has zoom; P8 the top-level menu is uncrowded (at most 8 top-level tabs); P9 a text-size control and an adaptive layout at 390, 768 and 1366 px; P10 executed code results are visualised; P11 the page declares the standard and the examples equal the deck's code manifest." ;
    backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_Derived ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner ; backlog:producedByStage ex:Out3_GoalR9 .
ex:Spec3I_Retrofit_Pass a backlog:TestScenario ; rdfs:label "A retrofitted chapter meets the standard"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Nominal ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec3I_Retrofit ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given a retrofitted chapter, when the checks are run, then every element passes as for chapters 7 and 8." .
ex:Spec3I_Retrofit_Fail a backlog:TestScenario ; rdfs:label "A chapter whose page declares the character set late is not claimed"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Rejection ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec3I_Retrofit ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given the page of chapter 1 (version 9.70.0, tag at byte 11172), when the charset check is run, then it fails and the chapter carries no passing result." .

