ex:TS_DeckStdCheck11 a backlog:ToolScript ; rdfs:label "deck standard check v1_1_0 (new tool: reads the key concepts of the research whichever class declares them)"@en ; backlog:scriptFileName "sen0401_deck_standard_check_v1_1_0.py" ; backlog:acceptsGraphPath false .

ex:AC7_DeckCheck a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; rdfs:label "The deck standard check v1_1_0 measures the key concepts of every chapter's research and changes nothing else"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Owner-directed work (ex:CR3_Ch78). Given the deck standard check v1_0_0 (byte-identical after the task) and the research files of chapters 5 to 14, when the NEW file sen0401_deck_standard_check_v1_1_0.py is written, then ALL of: (1) the file is new and v1_0_0 is byte-identical (SHA-256 before and after); (2) the diff against v1_0_0 is limited to the reading of the key-concept class (sen0401:PrimarySourceConcept and sen0414:PrimarySourceConcept); (3) on chapters 5, 6 and 7 every element gives the same result and the same measured numbers as v1_0_0; (4) on chapters 8 to 14 the elements D4 and D11 give a measured number and PASS or FAIL instead of NOT_MEASURED, and the concept counts are chapter 8: 46, 9: 38, 10: 62, 11: 43, 12: 43, 13: 29, 14: 69; (5) no committed file is edited, no gate, test or threshold changed; the logs are kept; results as printed; if any element fails the file is named failing. MEASURED FACT. The v1_0_0 check returns NOT_MEASURED for D4 and D11 on chapters 8 to 14 ('no research concept list found'); a skip is not a pass. DECK STANDARD (checked by the deck standard check, python-pptx 1.0.2, one named result per element): D1 every slide is numbered; D2 no text box over 30 words; D3 every code slide has a plain-language explanation beside the code and the executed result as a visual (a native chart, a table or a drawn diagram), not REPL text; D4 every key concept of the chapter has an everyday analogy slide or box (the key concepts are listed in the chapter research); D5 every story has who, what, when, where, why and how, a real picture and a live link; D6 every chart is a native chart object, no chart picture; D7 speaker notes at most 60 words per slide; D8 a resources slide with links; D9 one background scheme, no dark/light switching mid-deck; D10 every divider names its concepts with one line of meaning and one visual; D11 coverage: the share of the chapter research concepts that appear on a slide, stated as measured, not below 90 percent; D12 no code line wraps." ;
    backlog:measuredWithTool ex:TS_DeckStdCheck11, ex:TS_DeckStdCheck ;
    backlog:measuredWithVersion "deck standard check v1_0_0 (python-pptx 1.0.2) and, for chapters 8 to 14, its new version v1_1_0; Deck chapter check v1_3_0 reading the PINNED RDODI validator v1.6.0; deck match check v1_0_0; deck control check v1_1_0 (the manifest equals the deck's code slides); python-pptx 1.0.2" ;
    backlog:satisfiedByArtifact "the new files cited by SHA-256, the logs of the runs and the diffs, verified by the evidence bridge" ;
    backlog:coveredByCase ex:TC3I_K_Passes, ex:TC3I_K_NotClaimed .

ex:AC7_Deck_Ch07 a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; rdfs:label "The deck of chapter 7 meets the deck standard D1 to D12 and carries its chapter-code manifest"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Owner-directed work (ex:CR3_Ch78, Friday 2026-10-23 16:06 Istanbul, relayed by the course coordinator (the owner's decision)). Given the newest deck of chapter 7 (03-materials/ch07/SEN0401_Ch07_AuthorizationAuthentication_3e_v1_3_0.pptx, unchanged) and its research, when the deck is rebuilt as a new file (version v2.0.0) with its chapter-code manifest chapter_code_ch07_v1_0_0.json, then ALL of: (1) the deck standard check v1_0_0 for chapter 7 reports every element D1 to D12 met and exits 0 (no NOT_MEASURED); (2) the Deck chapter check v1_3_0 for Deck/Ch07 passes and the deck match check reports 0 not carried; (3) the manifest lists the deck's code examples in slide order, by name, and the order equals the order of the code slides (measured by the deck control check v1_1_0); (4) no committed file is edited, including the executor's own logs (written once); results as printed; if any element fails the deck is named failing and this criterion has no passing result. MEASURED FACTS (2026-10-23, by the builder session with the committed tools). Decks: the deck standard check v1_0_0 on the newest decks gives PASS=12 for chapters 5 and 6 and FAIL for every other chapter: chapters 1 to 4 fail D1, D2, D3, D4, D5, D7, D10, D11 (PASS=4); chapter 7 (26 slides, 14 code slides) fails the same eight (D1 25 of 26 numbered, D2 longest box 45 words, D3 3 of 14 code slides complete, D4 0 of 87 key concepts with an analogy, D5 0 of 3 stories complete, D7 longest note 100 words, D10 0 of 5 dividers complete, D11 32 of 87 research concepts shown = 36.8 percent); chapter 8 (26 slides, 16 code slides) and chapters 9 to 14 fail D1, D2, D3, D5, D7, D10 and the check returns NOT_MEASURED for D4 and D11 because their research files declare the key concepts as sen0414:PrimarySourceConcept while the check reads sen0401:PrimarySourceConcept (a skip is not a pass). Manifests: only chapters 5 and 6 have a chapter-code manifest. Pages: the charset check v1_0_0 passes the newest pages of chapters 5 and 6 (tag at byte 37) and fails the newest page of every other chapter (tag at byte 11172, or 11888 for chapter 10); the pages of chapters 7 and 8 (9.76.0, 9.77.0) are built on template 9.51.0 and have no chapter-code tab. Research, a deck and a page exist for all fourteen chapters; no chapter is unbuilt. DECK STANDARD (checked by the deck standard check, python-pptx 1.0.2, one named result per element): D1 every slide is numbered; D2 no text box over 30 words; D3 every code slide has a plain-language explanation beside the code and the executed result as a visual (a native chart, a table or a drawn diagram), not REPL text; D4 every key concept of the chapter has an everyday analogy slide or box (the key concepts are listed in the chapter research); D5 every story has who, what, when, where, why and how, a real picture and a live link; D6 every chart is a native chart object, no chart picture; D7 speaker notes at most 60 words per slide; D8 a resources slide with links; D9 one background scheme, no dark/light switching mid-deck; D10 every divider names its concepts with one line of meaning and one visual; D11 coverage: the share of the chapter research concepts that appear on a slide, stated as measured, not below 90 percent; D12 no code line wraps." ;
    backlog:measuredWithTool ex:TS_DeckStdCheck, ex:TS_ChapterCheck, ex:TS_DeckMatch, ex:TS_RdodiValidatorPinned ;
