    backlog:hasGherkinText "Owner-directed work (ex:CR3_Retrofit, Friday 2026-10-23 16:06 Istanbul, relayed by the course coordinator (the owner's decision)). Given the newest deck of chapter 3 (03-materials/ch03/SEN0401_Ch03_BitcoinCore_3e_v2_3_0.pptx, unchanged) and its research, when the deck is rebuilt as a new file (version the new version) with its chapter-code manifest chapter_code_ch03_v1_0_0.json, then ALL of: (1) the deck standard check v1_0_0 for chapter 3 reports every element D1 to D12 met and exits 0 (no NOT_MEASURED); (2) the Deck chapter check v1_3_0 for Deck/Ch03 passes and the deck match check reports 0 not carried; (3) the manifest lists the deck's code examples in slide order, by name, and the order equals the order of the code slides (measured by the deck control check v1_1_0); (4) no committed file is edited, including the executor's own logs (written once); results as printed; if any element fails the deck is named failing and this criterion has no passing result. MEASURED FACTS: see ex:IA3_Ch78. DECK STANDARD (checked by the deck standard check, python-pptx 1.0.2, one named result per element): D1 every slide is numbered; D2 no text box over 30 words; D3 every code slide has a plain-language explanation beside the code and the executed result as a visual (a native chart, a table or a drawn diagram), not REPL text; D4 every key concept of the chapter has an everyday analogy slide or box (the key concepts are listed in the chapter research); D5 every story has who, what, when, where, why and how, a real picture and a live link; D6 every chart is a native chart object, no chart picture; D7 speaker notes at most 60 words per slide; D8 a resources slide with links; D9 one background scheme, no dark/light switching mid-deck; D10 every divider names its concepts with one line of meaning and one visual; D11 coverage: the share of the chapter research concepts that appear on a slide, stated as measured, not below 90 percent; D12 no code line wraps." ;
