    backlog:hasGherkinText "Owner-directed work (ex:CR3_Retrofit, Friday 2026-10-23 16:06 Istanbul, relayed by the course coordinator (the owner's decision)). Given the rebuilt deck of chapter 14 with its manifest and the newest page of chapter 14 (03-materials/ch14/page/sen0401_ch14_page_v9_77_0.html), when the page is rebuilt as a new file with the page version above the newest page 9.77.0 on the template 9.52.2 with the builders v4_15_0 and v2_24_0, then ALL of: (1) the charset check exits 0 on the page (the tag below byte 1024, the first 1024 bytes decode as UTF-8); (2) the page test 9.36.0 runs all its added features with no skip and passes them (P1, P2, P3, P4, P5, P6, P8, P9, P11) and every other feature, exit 0, and the page tests 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 report no failure and widgets, features and gates not below the stored result of the page 9.77.0, skipped not more; (3) the chapter-code tab equals the deck's chapter-code manifest in names and order and each example runs in the page and shows its result; (4) the Stage 4 gate runner v1_1_0 for 14 exits 0 with Stage3.F, Stage4.A, B, cov, sub and src PASS, the Research, Deck and Page chapter checks pass, the deck match check reports 0 not carried; (5) no committed file is edited (an executor's own log is written once), no gate, test or threshold changed; the Stage 4 page ABox and the stored page-test result are new files; results as printed; if any element fails the page is named failing and this criterion has no passing result. MEASURED FACTS: see ex:IA3_Ch78. PAGE STANDARD (checked by the new page test 9.36.0, Playwright 1.56.0): P1 no horizontal overflow at 390 px and at 1366 px; P2 the chapter-code tab lists the deck's examples by NAME in the deck's slide order, each runnable in the page with the chapter library defined in the page and its result visualised, and the code lives in the editor, not in the list; P3 tabs and left tree are synchronised and their label sets are disjoint or the tab bar is one row; P4 no third level of tabs, and one more level of panels so that one panel holds one concept; P5 a panel is at most 1.0 screen high at 1366x768; P6 no list repeated on one screen; P7 every diagram has zoom; P8 the top-level menu is uncrowded (at most 8 top-level tabs); P9 a text-size control and an adaptive layout at 390, 768 and 1366 px; P10 executed code results are visualised; P11 the page declares the standard and the examples equal the deck's code manifest." ;
    backlog:measuredWithTool ex:TS_PageTemplateE, ex:TS_PageCharsetCheck, ex:TS_PageBuilder415, ex:TS_PageData224, ex:TS_PageTest36, ex:TS_Stage4Gates, ex:TS_ChapterCheck, ex:TS_DeckMatch, ex:TS_RdodiValidatorCurrent, ex:TS_RdodiValidatorPinned, ex:TS_PageTest34b, ex:TS_PageTest35b ;
