ex:TK_Ch78_DeckCheck a backlog:ExecutionTask ; rdfs:label "Make the deck standard check v1_1_0: read the research key concepts of chapters 8 to 14"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "TK_Ch78_DeckCheck" ; backlog:hasTitle "Make the deck standard check v1_1_0: read the research key concepts of chapters 8 to 14" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Iter_20 ; backlog:admittedByOutput ex:Out3_BacklogR28 ; backlog:responsible ex:Executor_ClaudeCodeSession ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasTaskType backlog:TaskType_Build ; backlog:effectiveDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-23T18:55:21"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-23T19:07:37"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:lastAuditedAt "2026-10-23T19:10:52"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasExecutionModality backlog:Mode_Hybrid ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Ranked by its story's state; scoring both would double-count." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Write the NEW file 08-tooling/sen0401_deck_standard_check_v1_1_0.py from sen0401_deck_standard_check_v1_0_0.py (which stays byte-identical): the only change is that the key concepts of the chapter research are read both when they are declared as sen0401:PrimarySourceConcept and when they are declared as sen0414:PrimarySourceConcept (the research files of chapters 8 to 14 use the second); every other element, threshold and message is unchanged. THE DEFECT, measured 2026-10-23: the v1_0_0 check returns NOT_MEASURED for D4 (analogy per key concept) and D11 (coverage) on chapters 8 to 14 with 'no research concept list found', because it matches the class sen0401:PrimarySourceConcept and finds none in those files (chapter 8: 46 concepts under sen0414:, chapter 9: 38, 10: 62, 11: 43, 12: 43, 13: 29, 14: 69). A skip is not a pass, so no deck of those chapters can be shown to meet the standard without this change. PROOF to deliver and keep as logs: (a) the unified diff against v1_0_0; (b) SHA-256 of v1_0_0 before and after; (c) v1_1_0 gives, on chapters 5, 6 and 7, the same PASS/FAIL and the same measured numbers as v1_0_0 for every element; (d) on chapters 8 to 14 D4 and D11 are now measured (a number, PASS or FAIL) instead of NOT_MEASURED, with the concept count per chapter as stated above. DO NOT EDIT OR APPEND TO ANY FILE COMMITTED EARLIER, INCLUDING YOUR OWN LOG FILES: write each log once, after its run is complete, and commit it once (the control of the page 9.82.0 of chapter 5 found a log file of the executor appended in a later commit and named that element not met). A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores: browser tests run one at a time and no build runs beside them. Planned session SEN0401-I20-deckcheck; estimated start T0 (T0 = the first executor start of the iteration), about 0.5 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

