    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasTaskType backlog:TaskType_Build ; backlog:effectiveDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD ; backlog:hasState backlog:Cancelled ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-23T18:55:21"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:lastAuditedAt "2026-10-24T09:14:56"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasRationale "Closed 2026-10-24T09:14:56 UTC by the change route of ex:CR3_Repair20 (v0.252.0): the task is superseded by TK_Ch07_Deck_Reissue, which re-issues the deck of chapter 7 as v2_1_0 in new files; it is withdrawn, not Done, and its result (deck v2_0_0: element (4) not met, the commit 27d36a5 edited files of ed03d15) stays in the register as history." ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Ranked by its story's state; scoring both would double-count." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Rebuild the deck of chapter 7 as a NEW file (the newest deck is 03-materials/ch07/SEN0401_Ch07_AuthorizationAuthentication_3e_v1_3_0.pptx; it stays unchanged) with a new version number (v2_0_0) from the chapter research 03-materials/ch07/rdodi and the earlier deck's assets, to the deck standard. The owner's words on the chapter 5 and 6 decks (quoted in ex:CR3_Remedy56) apply: a deck must be presentable and understandable. DECK STANDARD (checked by the deck standard check, python-pptx 1.0.2, one named result per element): D1 every slide is numbered; D2 no text box over 30 words; D3 every code slide has a plain-language explanation beside the code and the executed result as a visual (a native chart, a table or a drawn diagram), not REPL text; D4 every key concept of the chapter has an everyday analogy slide or box (the key concepts are listed in the chapter research); D5 every story has who, what, when, where, why and how, a real picture and a live link; D6 every chart is a native chart object, no chart picture; D7 speaker notes at most 60 words per slide; D8 a resources slide with links; D9 one background scheme, no dark/light switching mid-deck; D10 every divider names its concepts with one line of meaning and one visual; D11 coverage: the share of the chapter research concepts that appear on a slide, stated as measured, not below 90 percent; D12 no code line wraps. Rules from the owner's standing teaching-material preferences: full sentences are fine but no long paragraphs; explanation beside every code listing; the executed result shown as a visualization (native chart, table or drawn diagram) next to each listing; an everyday analogy for each key concept; 5N1K stories with real names, a real picture and a live link; native charts only; numbered slides; a resources slide with links for further reading and watching; short speaker notes; a smooth colour scheme. Follow the way the decks of chapters 5 and 6 were built (their generator files in 08-tooling/ch05-deck and ch06-deck are the pattern; write your own generator as a NEW tool file). ALSO write the chapter-code manifest 03-materials/ch07/page/chapter_code_ch07_v1_0_0.json in the form of chapter_code_ch06_v1_1_0.json: the ordered list of the deck's code examples (order number = slide order, a short NAME, the code that runs in the page with the chapter library it needs, the expected result), because the page tab must list the same examples in the same order. The checker is the independent the deck standard check v1_0_0, not you: run it when it exists and report every element as printed. DO NOT EDIT OR APPEND TO ANY FILE COMMITTED EARLIER, INCLUDING YOUR OWN LOG FILES: write each log once, after its run is complete, and commit it once (the control of the page 9.82.0 of chapter 5 found a log file of the executor appended in a later commit and named that element not met). A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores: browser tests run one at a time and no build runs beside them. Planned session SEN0401-I20-deck-ch07; estimated start T0 (T0 = the first executor start of the iteration), about 1.5 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

