enerator files in 08-tooling/ch05-deck and ch06-deck are the pattern; write your own generator as a NEW tool file). ALSO write the chapter-code manifest 03-materials/ch12/page/chapter_code_ch12_v1_0_0.json in the form of chapter_code_ch06_v1_1_0.json: the ordered list of the deck's code examples (order number = slide order, a short NAME, the code that runs in the page with the chapter library it needs, the expected result), because the page tab must list the same examples in the same order. The checker is the independent the deck standard check v1_1_0 (a new tool made by TK_Ch78_DeckCheck: it reads the key concepts of the research whichever way they are declared), not you: run it when it exists and report every element as printed. DO NOT EDIT OR APPEND TO ANY FILE COMMITTED EARLIER, INCLUDING YOUR OWN LOG FILES: write each log once, after its run is complete, and commit it once (the control of the page 9.82.0 of chapter 5 found a log file of the executor appended in a later commit and named that element not met). A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores: browser tests run one at a time and no build runs beside them. Planned session SEN0401-I21-deck-ch12; estimated start S+14.0h (S = the start of the iteration, planned and not yet held), about 1.5 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

