ex:TS_PageTest37 a backlog:ToolScript ; rdfs:label "page test 9.37.0 (new file over 9.36.0: the P2 step waits until the result no longer shows the placeholder Running...; every other feature unchanged)"@en ; backlog:scriptFileName "sen0401_page_test_v9_37_0.py" ; backlog:acceptsGraphPath false .

ex:AC7R_Deck_Ch07 a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; rdfs:label "The deck of chapter 7 is re-issued as v2_1_0 in new files and meets the deck standard with no committed file edited"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Owner-directed work (ex:CR3_Repair20, Saturday 2026-10-24, the course coordinator's order after the controls of the same day (v0.244.0) and the owner's rule that repairs re-rank the open items). Given the deck of chapter 7 v2_0_0 (controlled 2026-10-24: all elements met except that 27d36a5 edited files of ed03d15 in place) and the chapter research, when the deck is RE-ISSUED as the NEW files 03-materials/ch07/SEN0401_Ch07_AuthorizationAuthentication_3e_v2_1_0.pptx, 08-tooling/ch07-deck/deck_build_v2_1_0.py, deck_plan_v2_1_0.json and the shipped copy sen0401_ch07_deck_v2_1_0.pptx (the manifest chapter_code_ch07_v1_0_0.json stays; a changed order or name of the code slides needs a new manifest version), then ALL of: (1) the deck standard check reports every element D1 to D12 met and exits 0, no NOT_MEASURED; (2) the Deck chapter check v1_3_0 for Deck/Ch07 passes, the deck overlap check is clean and the deck match check reports 0 not carried; (3) the manifest lists the deck's code examples in slide order and the order equals the order of the code slides (deck control check v1_1_0); (4) every commit of the executor in this task adds files only (the nochange check over its commits prints status A for every file; no file of an earlier commit, the executor's own logs and the v2_0_0 files included, is modified; each log is written once, after its run is complete, and committed once); (5) results are reported as printed; if any element fails the deck is named failing and this criterion has no passing result. MEASURED (control of 2026-10-24, register v0.244.0, logs in 08-tooling/verify/iter20/deck_ch07_bridge): the deck of chapter 7 v2_0_0 (61 slides, 15 examples, executor commits ed03d15 and 27d36a5): deck standard check D1 to D12 PASS=12 FAIL=0, overlap check clean, Deck chapter check PASS, manifest equals the 15 code slides, deck match check 0 not carried, every slide viewed zoomed; the element 'no committed file edited' is NOT MET: the commit 27d36a5 modified in place four files that the commit ed03d15 had added (03-materials/ch07/SEN0401_Ch07_AuthorizationAuthentication_3e_v2_0_0.pptx, 08-tooling/ch07-deck/deck_build_v2_0_0.py, deck_plan_v2_0_0.json, sen0401_ch07_deck_v2_0_0.pptx; the nochange check prints status M for each). DECK STANDARD (checked by the deck standard check, python-pptx 1.0.2, one named result per element): D1 every slide is numbered; D2 no text box over 30 words; D3 every code slide has a plain-language explanation beside the code and the executed result as a visual (a native chart, a table or a drawn diagram), not REPL text; D4 every key concept of the chapter has an everyday analogy slide or box (the key concepts are listed in the chapter research); D5 every story has who, what, when, where, why and how, a real picture and a live link; D6 every chart is a native chart object, no chart picture; D7 speaker notes at most 60 words per slide; D8 a resources slide with links; D9 one background scheme, no dark/light switching mid-deck; D10 every divider names its concepts with one line of meaning and one visual; D11 coverage: the share of the chapter research concepts that appear on a slide, stated as measured, not below 90 percent; D12 no code line wraps." ;
    backlog:measuredWithTool ex:TS_DeckStdCheck, ex:TS_ChapterCheck, ex:TS_DeckMatch, ex:TS_RdodiValidatorPinned ;
    backlog:measuredWithVersion "deck standard check v1_0_0 (python-pptx 1.0.2) and, for chapters 8 to 14, its new version v1_1_0; Deck chapter check v1_3_0 reading the PINNED RDODI validator v1.6.0; deck match check v1_0_0; deck control check v1_1_0 (the manifest equals the deck's code slides); python-pptx 1.0.2" ;
    backlog:satisfiedByArtifact "the new files cited by SHA-256, the logs of the runs, the diffs and the fixtures, verified by the evidence bridge" ;
    backlog:coveredByCase ex:TC3R_D_Passes, ex:TC3R_D_NotClaimed .
