    backlog:hasAuditNote "RE-ISSUE the deck of chapter 7 as v2_1_0: write the NEW files 03-materials/ch07/SEN0401_Ch07_AuthorizationAuthentication_3e_v2_1_0.pptx, 08-tooling/ch07-deck/deck_build_v2_1_0.py, deck_plan_v2_1_0.json and the shipped copy sen0401_ch07_deck_v2_1_0.pptx, with the content of v2_0_0 (the control viewed all 61 slides and found no overflow; the deck standard check, overlap, Deck chapter check, manifest and deck match check all passed on v2_0_0, so the content stays). THE DEFECT: your commit 27d36a5 edited in place four files that your commit ed03d15 had added (the v2_0_0 deck, its build script, its plan and its shipped copy); the criterion's element (4) allows no edit of a committed file, your own earlier commit included. Do it so that every commit of this task adds files only: build in a scratch folder, check there, then copy the finished files in ONE commit; write each log once, after its run is complete, and commit it once; never touch any v2_0_0 file, any file of ed03d15 or 27d36a5, or the manifest (a changed manifest is a new version v1_1_0, only if the order or names of the code slides change). Run the deck standard check, the deck overlap check, the Deck chapter check v1_3_0 and the manifest check on the new deck and report each as printed. MEASURED (control of 2026-10-24, register v0.244.0, logs in 08-tooling/verify/iter20/deck_ch07_bridge): the deck of chapter 7 v2_0_0 (61 slides, 15 examples, executor commits ed03d15 and 27d36a5): deck standard check D1 to D12 PASS=12 FAIL=0, overlap check clean, Deck chapter check PASS, manifest equals the 15 code slides, deck match check 0 not carried, every slide viewed zoomed; the element 'no committed file edited' is NOT MET: the commit 27d36a5 modified in place four files that the commit ed03d15 had added (03-materials/ch07/SEN0401_Ch07_AuthorizationAuthentication_3e_v2_0_0.pptx, 08-tooling/ch07-deck/deck_build_v2_0_0.py, deck_plan_v2_0_0.json, sen0401_ch07_deck_v2_0_0.pptx; the nochange check prints status M for each). DO NOT EDIT OR APPEND TO ANY FILE COMMITTED EARLIER, INCLUDING YOUR OWN LOG FILES: write each log once, after its run is complete, and commit it once (the control of the page 9.82.0 of chapter 5 found a log file of the executor appended in a later commit and named that element not met). A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores: browser tests run one at a time and no build runs beside them. Planned session SEN0401-I20-deck-ch07-r2; estimated start T0 (T0 = the first executor start of the iteration), about 1.0 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

