ct: the template placeholder is correct behaviour for a reader and lighter example code would change the teaching content to suit the test; a defective gate is repaired by a new test file (the precedent of 9.34.1 and 9.35.1), so a new test file 9.37.0 is made. It enters no criterion until the owner answers the question that is asked. DO NOT EDIT OR APPEND TO ANY FILE COMMITTED EARLIER, INCLUDING YOUR OWN LOG FILES: write each log once, after its run is complete, and commit it once (the control of the page 9.82.0 of chapter 5 found a log file of the executor appended in a later commit and named that element not met). A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores: browser tests run one at a time and no build runs beside them. Planned session SEN0401-I22-pagetest; estimated start T0 (T0 = the first executor start of the iteration), about 1.0 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

