e example opens in the editor, runs in the page with the chapter library defined in the page, and shows a visualised result (P10) 0 of 1 examples ran; 1 defects ['1 Fixture example: Page.wait_for_func [FAIL] P2 every chapter-code exa] | (4) chapters 5 and 6 same as 9.36.0, chapter 8 reported as printed: MET [chapter 5 page 9.83.0 under 9.37.0: 398 passed, 0 failed (the same as 9.36.0): verified -> page 05: exit 0, widgets ('113', '113'), features passed 398, failed 0 RESULT: PASS; chapter 6 page 9.83.0 under 9.37.0: 398 passed, 0 failed (the same as 9.36.0): verified -> page 06: exit 0, widgets ('121', '121'), features passed 398, failed 0 RESULT: PASS; chapter 8 page 9.85.0 under 9.37.0: 394 passed, 0 failed (P2 as printed): verified -> page 08: exit 0, widgets ('127', '127'), features passed 394, failed 0 RESULT: PASS] | (5) no committed file edited: MET [no committed file edited: all 32 files of the three commits are added (status A): verified -> 32 files, not added: [] RESULT: PASS]. RESULT: MET: all elements are met. The builder re-ran the three fixtures under 9.37.0, fixture a under 9.36.0 and the pages 9.83.0 of chapters 5 and 6 and 9.85.0 of chapter 8 under 9.37.0 itself, under flock /tmp/page_test.lock, one at a time (logs in 08-tooling/verify/iter22/pagetest937); the bridge ran the exit-code checks over those logs, the files and the git history. Chapters 5 and 6 under 9.36.0 are the recorded runs of register v0.2 (398 passed, 0 failed each). The page 9.85.0 of chapter 8 under 9.36.0 fails P2 only (examples 17 and 18; executor and builder logs); under 9.37.0 it gives 394 passed, 0 failed." .
