ex:CR3_Repair21 a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "Page criteria of chapters 7 and 8 restated on the page test 9.37.0, and the regression criterion carried, by the lineage under the owner standing rule of 2026-10-24"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_Repair20 ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "RULE: Saturday 2026-10-24, decided by the lineage's own change route under the owner's standing rule of the same day (relayed by the course coordinator): a lineage never waits on questions unrelated to its work; when the answerer is not a person, the lineage's agentic system decides without a handover; work the lineage enforces but the actual work misses must be dealt with; progress must not need expensive switch-overs. MEASURED (control of the page test 9.37.0, register v0.258.0, evidence bridge, logs in 08-tooling/verify/iter22/pagetest937 and pagetest937_bridge, every page run by the builder under flock /tmp/page_test.lock, one at a time): the page test 9.36.0 is byte-identical (SHA-256 85afebf6..., git log shows only d4880a3); the diff to 9.37.0 holds the version string, one comment and the P2 wait; fixture a (slow example with a visual) passes P2 under 9.37.0 and fails under 9.36.0 (the race); fixture b (text only) fails P2 under 9.37.0 with 'result is text, not a visualisation'; fixture c (never ends) fails P2 within the 90 s bound; the pages 9.83.0 of chapters 5 and 6 give 398 passed 0 failed under 9.37.0 (the same as under 9.36.0); the page 9.85.0 of chapter 8 gives 394 passed 0 failed under 9.37.0 and failed P2 on examples 17 and 18 under 9.36.0 (the root cause is recorded in AC7R_PageTest937: the placeholder 'Running...' read as a result after 300 ms). The race is a defect of the gate, not a waiver: the criteria are restated on 9.37.0 and every other element, threshold and the no-skip rule are kept. The criteria of the pages of chapters 7 and 8 (ex:AC7_Page_Ch07, ex:AC7_Page_Ch08) name the page test 9.36.0, whose P2 wait is a defect; the question whether the criteria may name 9.37.0 was asked of the owner and is not awaited under the rule: the race is a defect in the gate, not a waiver. The change grows the scope by one deliverable: the restated page criteria with new stories, and the regression criterion on the current template; nothing existing is edited; the old criteria stay as history. Pending until the ScopeChange that admits the stories is recorded in the Backlog version." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .

ex:IA3_Repair21 a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What the restated page criteria cost and what they unblock, measured before they are started"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR3_Repair21 ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage3 ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:IA3_Repair20 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "MEASURED (control of the page test 9.37.0, register v0.258.0, evidence bridge, logs in 08-tooling/verify/iter22/pagetest937 and pagetest937_bridge, every page run by the builder under flock /tmp/page_test.lock, one at a time): the page test 9.36.0 is byte-identical (SHA-256 85afebf6..., git log shows only d4880a3); the diff to 9.37.0 holds the version string, one comment and the P2 wait; fixture a (slow example with a visual) passes P2 under 9.37.0 and fails under 9.36.0 (the race); fixture b (text only) fails P2 under 9.37.0 with 'result is text, not a visualisation'; fixture c (never ends) fails P2 within the 90 s bound; the pages 9.83.0 of chapters 5 and 6 give 398 passed 0 failed under 9.37.0 (the same as under 9.36.0); the page 9.85.0 of chapter 8 gives 394 passed 0 failed under 9.37.0 and failed P2 on examples 17 and 18 under 9.36.0 (the root cause is recorded in AC7R_PageTest937: the placeholder 'Running...' read as a result after 300 ms). The race is a defect of the gate, not a waiver: the criteria are restated on 9.37.0 and every other element, threshold and the no-skip rule are kept. AFFECTED: ST_Ch07_Page and ST_Ch08_Page (their criteria name 9.36.0; the stories are withdrawn in the next version after their replacements exist), ST_Ch07_Deck (superseded by the re-issue), the three old stories of Iterations 17 and 18 (settled by the same route), ST_Remedy_Tools (its regression criterion is carried). NOT AFFECTED: the template, the builders, the tests 9.34.1, 9.35.1, 9.36.0 and 9.37.0 (no file edited), every other deck and page, the Mission outcome and the Achieved status. PLAN (route as ex:CR3_Repair20, G127): a StageRevision from the Scope stage, seven versions; then one version for the withdrawals and the old stories, one for the ranking (BP-D10), one for work begun. New iteration Iter_23 (start at planning, proposed end Sunday 2026-10-25 12:00 UTC) with three stories and five tasks: the page of chapter 7 (about 1.5 h executor, 1.0 h verification), the finish of the page 9.85.0 of chapter 8 (about 1.0 h and 0.5 h), the regression on template 9.52.2 (about 1.0 h, builder). COST: new files only; a failing criterion is named failing; nothing is waived. ORDER: the two page builds start at once (their dependencies are Done: the deck v2_1_0 and the page test 9.37.0 are controlled MET); browser runs are serialised by the lock." .

ex:Revision_Lineage3_Scope10 a backlog:StageRevision ;
    rdfs:label "Revision of the third lineage from the Scope stage: the page criteria of chapters 7 and 8 restated on 9.37.0"@en ;
    backlog:revisesLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:revisesFromStage backlog:Stage_Scope ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_Repair21, ex:IA3_Repair21 ;
    backlog:revisionReason "The change request ex:CR3_Repair21 (Saturday 2026-10-24, decided by the lineage's own change route under the owner's standing rule of the same day (relayed by the course coordinator): a lineage never waits on questions unrelated to its work; when the answerer is not a person, the lineage's agentic system decides without a handover; work the lineage enforces but the actual work misses must be dealt with; progress must not need expensive switch-overs) adds a deliverable (the restated page criteria and their stories); the lineage is in its closed Backlog stage, and a deliverable added to a closed scope statement is a revision from the Scope stage (ruling G127). The request and its impact assessment ex:IA3_Repair21 were recorded first. This version retracts the Scope, Goal, Objective and Backlog outputs and rebuilds nothing; the next four versions rebuild them one stage each, a sixth fills the last commit; the items already in the register, Done ones included, re-enter by admission and are not re-dated. The retracted outputs and their digests stay as history (L-112). The interim versions are the declared transition (G129). Recorded as decided by the builder role under the owner's standing rule." ;
    backlog:retractsOutput ex:Out3_ScopeR10, ex:Out3_GoalR10, ex:Out3_ObjectiveR10, ex:Out3_BacklogR12 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:revisedAtCommit "be96680" .
