ex:Del3_Repair21 a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ;
    rdfs:label "The page criteria of chapters 7 and 8 restated on the page test 9.37.0, the page of chapter 7 built on the re-issued deck, the page 9.85.0 of chapter 8 finished, and the regression criterion carried onto the current template"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:derivesFromMissionClause "the research behind it and an interactive page"^^xsd:string ;
    backlog:hasDeliverableText "The page of chapter 7 built as a new file on the re-issued deck v2_1_0 and its manifest v1_1_0, the page 9.85.0 of chapter 8 given its checks, stored result and Stage 4 ABox as new files, both measured by the page test 9.37.0 (a new file; 9.36.0 stays) with every other element of the old criteria kept; the regression of the template 9.52.2 on the old page tests measured on pages of chapters 1 and 10. MEASURED (control of the page test 9.37.0, register v0.258.0, evidence bridge, logs in 08-tooling/verify/iter22/pagetest937 and pagetest937_bridge, every page run by the builder under flock /tmp/page_test.lock, one at a time): the page test 9.36.0 is byte-identical (SHA-256 85afebf6..., git log shows only d4880a3); the diff to 9.37.0 holds the version string, one comment and the P2 wait; fixture a (slow example with a visual) passes P2 under 9.37.0 and fails under 9.36.0 (the race); fixture b (text only) fails P2 under 9.37.0 with 'result is text, not a visualisation'; fixture c (never ends) fails P2 within the 90 s bound; the pages 9.83.0 of chapters 5 and 6 give 398 passed 0 failed under 9.37.0 (the same as under 9.36.0); the page 9.85.0 of chapter 8 gives 394 passed 0 failed under 9.37.0 and failed P2 on examples 17 and 18 under 9.36.0 (the root cause is recorded in AC7R_PageTest937: the placeholder 'Running...' read as a result after 300 ms). The race is a defect of the gate, not a waiver: the criteria are restated on 9.37.0 and every other element, threshold and the no-skip rule are kept. RULE: Saturday 2026-10-24, decided by the lineage's own change route under the owner's standing rule of the same day (relayed by the course coordinator): a lineage never waits on questions unrelated to its work; when the answerer is not a person, the lineage's agentic system decides without a handover; work the lineage enforces but the actual work misses must be dealt with; progress must not need expensive switch-overs." ;
    backlog:deliverableForArea ex:Area3_Remedy56 ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Work ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_Functional .
ex:Scope3 backlog:requiresDeliverable ex:Del3_Repair21 ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_Repair21, ex:IA3_Repair21 .
ex:Scope3 rdfs:comment "Revised 2026-10-24 by the stage revision ex:Revision_Lineage3_Scope10 on the change request ex:CR3_Repair21 (Saturday 2026-10-24, decided by the lineage's own change route under the owner's standing rule of the same day (relayed by the course coordinator): a lineage never waits on questions unrelated to its work; when the answerer is not a person, the lineage's agentic system decides without a handover; work the lineage enforces but the actual work misses must be dealt with; progress must not need expensive switch-overs). The statement above is unchanged (L-112). It now also requires one deliverable in the area ex:Area3_Remedy56 (the restated page criteria). No exclusion changes: new files only; the exclusion of changes to gates, tests and thresholds still holds (9.37.0 is a new test file; the criteria name it by this change route, no gate is loosened)."@en .

