ex:AC8R_Page_Ch07 a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; rdfs:label "The page of chapter 7 meets the page standard on the page test 9.37.0 (restated), with its character set first"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "RESTATED by ex:CR3_Repair21 from ex:AC7_Page_Ch07 (Saturday 2026-10-24, decided by the lineage's own change route under the owner's standing rule of the same day (relayed by the course coordinator): a lineage never waits on questions unrelated to its work; when the answerer is not a person, the lineage's agentic system decides without a handover; work the lineage enforces but the actual work misses must be dealt with; progress must not need expensive switch-overs). The only changes: the page test named is 9.37.0 instead of 9.36.0 (MEASURED (control of the page test 9.37.0, register v0.258.0, evidence bridge, logs in 08-tooling/verify/iter22/pagetest937 and pagetest937_bridge, every page run by the builder under flock /tmp/page_test.lock, one at a time): the page test 9.36.0 is byte-identical (SHA-256 85afebf6..., git log shows only d4880a3); the diff to 9.37.0 holds the version string, one comment and the P2 wait; fixture a (slow example with a visual) passes P2 under 9.37.0 and fails under 9.36.0 (the race); fixture b (text only) fails P2 under 9.37.0 with 'result is text, not a visualisation'; fixture c (never ends) fails P2 within the 90 s bound; the pages 9.83.0 of chapters 5 and 6 give 398 passed 0 failed under 9.37.0 (the same as under 9.36.0); the page 9.85.0 of chapter 8 gives 394 passed 0 failed under 9.37.0 and failed P2 on examples 17 and 18 under 9.36.0 (the root cause is recorded in AC7R_PageTest937: the placeholder 'Running...' read as a result after 300 ms). The race is a defect of the gate, not a waiver: the criteria are restated on 9.37.0 and every other element, threshold and the no-skip rule are kept.) and the deck and its manifest are those of the re-issue (controlled MET in v0.257.0); nothing else is loosened. The old criterion stays as history and is not met. Owner-directed work (ex:CR3_Ch78, Friday 2026-10-23 16:06 Istanbul, relayed by the course coordinator (the owner's decision)). Given the RE-ISSUED deck of chapter 7 v2_1_0 (03-materials/ch07/SEN0401_Ch07_AuthorizationAuthentication_3e_v2_1_0.pptx, controlled MET in v0.257.0) with its manifest chapter_code_ch07_v1_1_0.json (a NEW file written first by the task: the same 15 examples in the same order and names as chapter_code_ch07_v1_0_0.json, whose deck field names v2_0_0, with the deck field naming v2_1_0) and the newest page of chapter 7 (03-materials/ch07/page/sen0401_ch07_page_v9_76_0.html), when the page is rebuilt as a new file with the page version 9.84.0 on the template 9.52.2 with the builders v4_15_0 and v2_24_0, then ALL of: (1) the charset check exits 0 on the page (the tag below byte 1024, the first 1024 bytes decode as UTF-8); (2) the page test 9.37.0 runs all its added features with no skip and passes them (P1, P2, P3, P4, P5, P6, P8, P9, P11) and every other feature, exit 0, and the page tests 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 report no failure and widgets, features and gates not below the stored result of the page 9.76.0, skipped not more; (3) the chapter-code tab equals the deck's chapter-code manifest in names and order and each example runs in the page and shows its result; (4) the Stage 4 gate runner v1_1_0 for 7 exits 0 with Stage3.F, Stage4.A, B, cov, sub and src PASS, the Research, Deck and Page chapter checks pass, the deck match check reports 0 not carried; (5) no committed file is edited (an executor's own log is written once), no gate, test or threshold changed; the Stage 4 page ABox and the stored page-test result are new files; results as printed; if any element fails the page is named failing and this criterion has no passing result. MEASURED FACTS (2026-10-23, by the builder session with the committed tools). Decks: the deck standard check v1_0_0 on the newest decks gives PASS=12 for chapters 5 and 6 and FAIL for every other chapter: chapters 1 to 4 fail D1, D2, D3, D4, D5, D7, D10, D11 (PASS=4); chapter 7 (26 slides, 14 code slides) fails the same eight (D1 25 of 26 numbered, D2 longest box 45 words, D3 3 of 14 code slides complete, D4 0 of 87 key concepts with an analogy, D5 0 of 3 stories complete, D7 longest note 100 words, D10 0 of 5 dividers complete, D11 32 of 87 research concepts shown = 36.8 percent); chapter 8 (26 slides, 16 code slides) and chapters 9 to 14 fail D1, D2, D3, D5, D7, D10 and the check returns NOT_MEASURED for D4 and D11 because their research files declare the key concepts as sen0414:PrimarySourceConcept while the check reads sen0401:PrimarySourceConcept (a skip is not a pass). Manifests: only chapters 5 and 6 have a chapter-code manifest. Pages: the charset check v1_0_0 passes the newest pages of chapters 5 and 6 (tag at byte 37) and fails the newest page of every other chapter (tag at byte 11172, or 11888 for chapter 10); the pages of chapters 7 and 8 (9.76.0, 9.77.0) are built on template 9.51.0 and have no chapter-code tab. Research, a deck and a page exist for all fourteen chapters; no chapter is unbuilt. PAGE STANDARD (checked by the new page test 9.37.0, Playwright 1.56.0): P1 no horizontal overflow at 390 px and at 1366 px; P2 the chapter-code tab lists the deck's examples by NAME in the deck's slide order, each runnable in the page with the chapter library defined in the page and its result visualised, and the code lives in the editor, not in the list; P3 tabs and left tree are synchronised and their label sets are disjoint or the tab bar is one row; P4 no third level of tabs, and one more level of panels so that one panel holds one concept; P5 a panel is at most 1.0 screen high at 1366x768; P6 no list repeated on one screen; P7 every diagram has zoom; P8 the top-level menu is uncrowded (at most 8 top-level tabs); P9 a text-size control and an adaptive layout at 390, 768 and 1366 px; P10 executed code results are visualised; P11 the page declares the standard and the examples equal the deck's code manifest." ;
    backlog:measuredWithTool ex:TS_PageTemplateE, ex:TS_PageCharsetCheck, ex:TS_PageBuilder415, ex:TS_PageData224, ex:TS_PageTest37, ex:TS_Stage4Gates, ex:TS_ChapterCheck, ex:TS_DeckMatch, ex:TS_RdodiValidatorCurrent, ex:TS_RdodiValidatorPinned, ex:TS_PageTest34b, ex:TS_PageTest35b ;
    backlog:measuredWithVersion "page template 9.52.2 (course_page_template_v9_52_2.html, built and controlled in Iteration 19); page charset check v1_0_0; page builder v4_15_0 and page-data builder v2_24_0 (unchanged; the template is passed by PAGE_TEMPLATE); page test 9.37.0 (new file over 9.37.0, controlled in v0.258.0; Playwright 1.56.0); page tests 9.34.1 and 9.35.1; Stage 4 gate runner v1_1_0 reading the CURRENT RDODI validator v1.13.0; chapter check v1_3_0 reading the PINNED RDODI validator v1.6.0; deck match check v1_0_0; page check wrapper v1_5_0; Playwright 1.56.0" ;
    backlog:satisfiedByArtifact "the new files cited by SHA-256, the logs of the runs and the diffs, verified by the evidence bridge" ;
    backlog:coveredByCase ex:TC8R_Ch07_Passes, ex:TC8R_Ch07_NotClaimed .

