ex:TK_Ch07_Page_Build_R a backlog:ExecutionTask ; rdfs:label "Build the page of chapter 7 on the re-issued deck with the chapter-code tab"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "TK_Ch07_Page_Build_R" ; backlog:hasTitle "Build the page of chapter 7 on the re-issued deck with the chapter-code tab" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Iter_23 ; backlog:admittedByOutput ex:Out3_BacklogR28 ; backlog:responsible ex:Executor_ClaudeCodeSession ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasTaskType backlog:TaskType_Build ; backlog:effectiveDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-24T15:53:08"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-24T17:13:15"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:lastAuditedAt "2026-10-24T18:32:35"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasExecutionModality backlog:Mode_Hybrid ;
    backlog:dependsOn ex:TK_Ch07_Deck_Reissue_Verify, ex:TK_Charset_Template_Verify, ex:TK_Charset_Check_Verify, ex:TK_PageTest937_Verify ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Ranked by its story's state; scoring both would double-count." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "RESTATED page task of chapter 7 (it replaces TK_Ch07_Page_Build, withdrawn by the same route ex:CR3_Repair21: the criterion now names the page test 9.37.0, which repairs the race of 9.36.0 on the placeholder 'Running...'; MEASURED (control of the page test 9.37.0, register v0.258.0, evidence bridge, logs in 08-tooling/verify/iter22/pagetest937 and pagetest937_bridge, every page run by the builder under flock /tmp/page_test.lock, one at a time): the page test 9.36.0 is byte-identical (SHA-256 85afebf6..., git log shows only d4880a3); the diff to 9.37.0 holds the version string, one comment and the P2 wait; fixture a (slow example with a visual) passes P2 under 9.37.0 and fails under 9.36.0 (the race); fixture b (text only) fails P2 under 9.37.0 with 'result is text, not a visualisation'; fixture c (never ends) fails P2 within the 90 s bound; the pages 9.83.0 of chapters 5 and 6 give 398 passed 0 failed under 9.37.0 (the same as under 9.36.0); the page 9.85.0 of chapter 8 gives 394 passed 0 failed under 9.37.0 and failed P2 on examples 17 and 18 under 9.36.0 (the root cause is recorded in AC7R_PageTest937: the placeholder 'Running...' read as a result after 300 ms). The race is a defect of the gate, not a waiver: the criteria are restated on 9.37.0 and every other element, threshold and the no-skip rule are kept.) FIRST write the NEW manifest 03-materials/ch07/page/chapter_code_ch07_v1_1_0.json: a copy of chapter_code_ch07_v1_0_0.json (which stays unchanged) whose 'deck' field names SEN0401_Ch07_AuthorizationAuthentication_3e_v2_1_0.pptx; its 15 examples, their order and their names are unchanged (measured equal to the code slides of the deck v2_1_0 in the control of v0.257.0). Run the deck control check v1_1_0 (manifest) against it and the deck v2_1_0 (if the check takes the manifest from the deck name alone, state how you ran it; do not edit the check). THEN build the page from the deck v2_1_0 (the lecture export and the stories made from it) and this manifest. Build the page of chapter 7 again as a NEW file with the new page version 9.84.0 on the template 9.52.2 (course_page_template_v9_52_2.html, pass it with PAGE_TEMPLATE) with the page builder v4_15_0 and the page-data builder v2_24_0, from the chapter research, the deck's lecture export and stories, and the NEW manifest chapter_code_ch07_v1_1_0.json (written first, see the start of this note) (state how you passed the template and how the lecture export and stories were made; the pages of chapters 5 and 6 are the pattern: their build logs are in 08-tooling/ch05-page and ch06-page). Run the page charset check on the page (it must pass), run the page tests 9.37.0, 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 (the runner with PAGE_TEST), serially, store the result as a new test_results file, and build the Stage 4 page ABox with the Stage 4 builder. PAGE STANDARD (checked by the new page test 9.37.0, Playwright 1.56.0): P1 no horizontal overflow at 390 px and at 1366 px; P2 the chapter-code tab lists the deck's examples by NAME in the deck's slide order, each runnable in the page with the chapter library defined in the page and its result visualised, and the code lives in the editor, not in the list; P3 tabs and left tree are synchronised and their label sets are disjoint or the tab bar is one row; P4 no third level of tabs, and one more level of panels so that one panel holds one concept; P5 a panel is at most 1.0 screen high at 1366x768; P6 no list repeated on one screen; P7 every diagram has zoom; P8 the top-level menu is uncrowded (at most 8 top-level tabs); P9 a text-size control and an adaptive layout at 390, 768 and 1366 px; P10 executed code results are visualised; P11 the page declares the standard and the examples equal the deck's code manifest. DOM CONTRACT shared by the template, the page test and the page tasks (so the independent test can find what the template builds): the chapter-code tab is the tab with attribute data-pane=\"chaptercode\"; its list items have data-cc-item, the NAME of the example in data-cc-name and the deck's order number in data-cc-order; an item opens the example in the editor element data-cc-editor with a run button data-cc-run and a result element data-cc-result; the left tree items have role=treeitem and the tabs role=tab; one concept panel is an element with data-panel; the playground list items have data-pg-item and show names only; a page that follows the standard declares <meta name=\"page-standard\" content=\"9.52\">. DO NOT EDIT OR APPEND TO ANY FILE COMMITTED EARLIER, INCLUDING YOUR OWN LOG FILES: write each log once, after its run is complete, and commit it once (the control of the page 9.82.0 of chapter 5 found a log file of the executor appended in a later commit and named that element not met). A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores: browser tests run one at a time and no build runs beside them. Planned session SEN0401-I23-page-ch07; estimated start S (T0 = the first executor start of the iteration), about 1.5 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

