    backlog:hasAuditNote "Re-run serially, each browser run under `flock /tmp/page_test.lock`: the charset check and the page tests 9.37.0, 9.34.1 and 9.35.1, the Stage 4 gate runner v1_1_0, the Research, Deck and Page chapter checks, the deck match check and the manifest equality (the chapter-code tab equals the deck's code order, from chapter_code_ch07_v1_1_0.json); record every result as printed. MEASURED (control of the page test 9.37.0, register v0.258.0, evidence bridge, logs in 08-tooling/verify/iter22/pagetest937 and pagetest937_bridge, every page run by the builder under flock /tmp/page_test.lock, one at a time): the page test 9.36.0 is byte-identical (SHA-256 85afebf6..., git log shows only d4880a3); the diff to 9.37.0 holds the version string, one comment and the P2 wait; fixture a (slow example with a visual) passes P2 under 9.37.0 and fails under 9.36.0 (the race); fixture b (text only) fails P2 under 9.37.0 with 'result is text, not a visualisation'; fixture c (never ends) fails P2 within the 90 s bound; the pages 9.83.0 of chapters 5 and 6 give 398 passed 0 failed under 9.37.0 (the same as under 9.36.0); the page 9.85.0 of chapter 8 gives 394 passed 0 failed under 9.37.0 and failed P2 on examples 17 and 18 under 9.36.0 (the root cause is recorded in AC7R_PageTest937: the placeholder 'Running...' read as a result after 300 ms). The race is a defect of the gate, not a waiver: the criteria are restated on 9.37.0 and every other element, threshold and the no-skip rule are kept. Planned session builder; estimated start S+1.5h (T0 = the first executor start of the iteration), about 1.0 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

