_PageTest937: the placeholder 'Running...' read as a result after 300 ms). The race is a defect of the gate, not a waiver: the criteria are restated on 9.37.0 and every other element, threshold and the no-skip rule are kept. DO NOT EDIT OR APPEND TO ANY FILE COMMITTED EARLIER, INCLUDING YOUR OWN LOG FILES: write each log once, after its run is complete, and commit it once (the control of the page 9.82.0 of chapter 5 found a log file of the executor appended in a later commit and named that element not met). Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores: browser tests run one at a time and no build runs beside them. Planned session SEN0401-I23-page-ch08; estimated start S (T0 = the first executor start of the iteration), about 1.0 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

