ex:Iter_23 rdfs:comment "Ranking of 2026-10-24T18:44:13 (BP-D10, RICE with dependency factor; the scores are the records ex:Rank41_*): 1. Section links of chapter 11: the remainder of the story of Iteration 14 (ordering key 0.80); 2. Page test 9.37.0: work Done, awaits the review of Iteration 22 (ordering key 0.80); 3. Regression of the template 9.52.2 on the old page tests (carried criterion) (ordering key 0.60); 4. Page 9.85.0 of chapter 8 finished: work Done, awaits the review of Iteration 23 (ordering key 0.40); 5. Page of chapter 7 built on the re-issued deck: work Done, awaits the review of Iteration 23 (ordering key 0.40); 6. Deck of chapter 7 re-issued as v2_1_0: work Done, awaits the review of Iteration 22 (ordering key 0.40); 7. Retrofit: deck and manifest of chapter 4 (ordering key 0.40); 8. Retrofit: deck and manifest of chapter 3 (ordering key 0.40); 9. Retrofit: deck and manifest of chapter 2 (ordering key 0.40); 10. Retrofit: deck and manifest of chapter 1 (ordering key 0.40); 11. Retrofit: deck and manifest of chapter 14 (ordering key 0.20); 12. Retrofit: deck and manifest of chapter 13 (ordering key 0.20); 13. Retrofit: deck and manifest of chapter 12 (ordering key 0.20); 14. Retrofit: deck and manifest of chapter 11 (ordering key 0.20); 15. Retrofit: deck and manifest of chapter 10 (ordering key 0.20); 16. Retrofit: deck and manifest of chapter 9 (ordering key 0.20); 17. Retrofit: page of chapter 14 on template 9.52.2 (ordering key 0.16); 18. Retrofit: page of chapter 13 on template 9.52.2 (ordering key 0.16); 19. Retrofit: page of chapter 12 on template 9.52.2 (ordering key 0.16); 20. Retrofit: page of chapter 11 on template 9.52.2 (ordering key 0.16); 21. Retrofit: page of chapter 10 on template 9.52.2 (ordering key 0.16); 22. Retrofit: page of chapter 9 on template 9.52.2 (ordering key 0.16); 23. Retrofit: page of chapter 4 on template 9.52.2 (ordering key 0.16); 24. Retrofit: page of chapter 3 on template 9.52.2 (ordering key 0.16); 25. Retrofit: page of chapter 2 on template 9.52.2 (ordering key 0.16); 26. Retrofit: page of chapter 1 on template 9.52.2 (ordering key 0.16). The urgent items (impact 3, the owner's priority input of 2026-10-23 16:06) rank ahead of the retrofit; pages carry the dependency factor 0.5 until their deck is Done. The inputs are stated in each record; the scale values (impact levels, the dependency factor 0.5) are stipulations of the method's scale and are disclosed as such."@en .

ex:CR3_Retro24 a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "Retrofit of all chapters on the measured state: restated criteria, the story-layout repair of chapters 5 to 8, the template 9.52.3, the chapter 1 verify script, planned in five iterations"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_Retrofit, ex:CR3_Repair21 ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Requested Sunday 2026-10-25, decided by the lineage's own change route under the owner's standing orders (retrofit all chapters starting with chapter 1; repairs re-rank the open items; a lineage never waits on unrelated questions). MEASURED (the lineage agent's baseline, 2026-10-25, tool sen0401_lineage_baseline_v1_0_0.py, one log per run in 08-tooling/verify/iter24/baseline, committed before this change): DECKS: the deck standard check v1_1_0 gives 12 of 12 elements PASS for chapters 5 to 8 and 4 PASS, 8 FAIL (D1, D2, D3, D4, D5, D7, D10, D11) for every one of chapters 1 to 4 and 9 to 14; the deck overlap check v1_0_0 is clean on the decks of chapters 5 to 14 and reports overlaps (text over a picture, a table over text) on chapters 1 to 4. MANIFESTS: a chapter-code manifest exists for chapters 5 to 8 only (27, 18, 15 and 20 examples; the control check manifest:NN exits 0; no example's first output line starts with an error name) and for no other chapter. PAGES: the newest pages of chapters 5 to 8 declare the standard 9.52, have the chapter-code tab and pass the charset check; the newest pages of the other ten chapters have no chapter-code tab, no standard declaration and fail the charset check (tag behind byte 1024). STORY LAYOUT (the owner's rule, new tool sen0401_story_layout_probe_v1_0_0.py, 1366x768, 1400x900 and 390x844, logs in 08-tooling/verify/iter24/storylayout): the pages of chapters 5, 6, 7 and 8 FAIL it (a photograph as tall as the screen pushes the narrative below the first screen: 4 of 9, 3 of 12, 2 of 9 and 3 of 9 stories); the cause is the template 9.52.2 (.simgrow img with width 100 percent and height auto, no height cap). GATES: the Stage 4 gate runner v1_1_0 gives OVERALL PASS for all fourteen chapters; the Research chapter check v1_3_0 exits 0 for chapters 2 to 14 and CRASHES for chapter 1 (no file sen0401_ch01_verify_v*.py exists; the check names the verify script as a part). NOT MEASURED here: the page test 9.37.0 on the old pages (they lack the chapter-code tab, so P2 and P11 cannot pass) - the page test is run on every rebuilt page. The criteria of the retrofit stories of Iteration 21 (ex:AC7_Deck_ChNN, ex:AC7_Page_ChNN) name the page test 9.36.0 and the template 9.52.2 and lack the rules the owner added since: no text overlap in a deck, no manifest example that starts with an error name, the story text on the first screen at three viewports, the page ABox as a new file. A rule added after a story is written does not reach into it (G133), so the repair is new work by the change route. The change grows the scope by one deliverable (the restated criteria, the template 9.52.3, the story-layout repair of the pages of chapters 5 to 8, the chapter 1 verify script); nothing existing is edited. Pending until the ScopeChange that admits the stories is recorded in the Backlog version." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .

ex:IA3_Retro24 a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What the retrofit costs on the measured state, and in what order it runs"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR3_Retro24 ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage3 ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:IA3_Retrofit ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "MEASURED (the lineage agent's baseline, 2026-10-25, tool sen0401_lineage_baseline_v1_0_0.py, one log per run in 08-tooling/verify/iter24/baseline, committed before this change): DECKS: the deck standard check v1_1_0 gives 12 of 12 elements PASS for chapters 5 to 8 and 4 PASS, 8 FAIL (D1, D2, D3, D4, D5, D7, D10, D11) for every one of chapters 1 to 4 and 9 to 14; the deck overlap check v1_0_0 is clean on the decks of chapters 5 to 14 and reports overlaps (text over a picture, a table over text) on chapters 1 to 4. MANIFESTS: a chapter-code manifest exists for chapters 5 to 8 only (27, 18, 15 and 20 examples; the control check manifest:NN exits 0; no example's first output line starts with an error name) and for no other chapter. PAGES: the newest pages of chapters 5 to 8 declare the standard 9.52, have the chapter-code tab and pass the charset check; the newest pages of the other ten chapters have no chapter-code tab, no standard declaration and fail the charset check (tag behind byte 1024). STORY LAYOUT (the owner's rule, new tool sen0401_story_layout_probe_v1_0_0.py, 1366x768, 1400x900 and 390x844, logs in 08-tooling/verify/iter24/storylayout): the pages of chapters 5, 6, 7 and 8 FAIL it (a photograph as tall as the screen pushes the narrative below the first screen: 4 of 9, 3 of 12, 2 of 9 and 3 of 9 stories); the cause is the template 9.52.2 (.simgrow img with width 100 percent and height auto, no height cap). GATES: the Stage 4 gate runner v1_1_0 gives OVERALL PASS for all fourteen chapters; the Research chapter check v1_3_0 exits 0 for chapters 2 to 14 and CRASHES for chapter 1 (no file sen0401_ch01_verify_v*.py exists; the check names the verify script as a part). NOT MEASURED here: the page test 9.37.0 on the old pages (they lack the chapter-code tab, so P2 and P11 cannot pass) - the page test is run on every rebuilt page. AFFECTED: the 20 retrofit stories and 40 tasks of Iteration 21 and ST_Section_Links_Ch11 with its Verify task (withdrawn in the version after the replacements exist; none started, none Done); the Done pages of chapters 5 to 8 stay Done and are not edited (G125): their story-layout defect is repaired by new stories on new page files. NOT AFFECTED: every committed file; the tools; the Mission outcome. PLAN (route as ex:CR3_Repair21, G127): a StageRevision from the Scope stage, seven versions; one version for the withdrawals, one for the ranking (BP-D10), one for work begun. ORDER (the owner's: chapter 1 first; repairs re-rank, G147): the template 9.52.3 gates every page, so it runs first with the decks of chapters 1 to 3 (three executors at once): Iter_24 decks 1, 2, 3 and the template; Iter_25 the story-layout repair of the pages 5 to 8, the deck of chapter 4 and the chapter 1 verify script; Iter_26 the pages 1 to 4; Iter_27 chapters 9 to 11; Iter_28 chapters 12 to 14. Iterations 25 to 28 are planned, not started (their ceremonies are held when each starts). ESTIMATES (not measurements, G120): deck 1.5 h build plus 0.5 h verify, page 1.5 h plus 1.0 h, template 1.5 h plus 1.0 h, verify script 1.0 h plus 0.5 h; browser runs about 9 minutes each, serial under the lock on two cores; at most three executors at once. COST: new files only; a failing criterion is named failing; nothing is waived." .

ex:Revision_Lineage3_Scope11 a backlog:StageRevision ;
    rdfs:label "Revision of the third lineage from the Scope stage: the retrofit of all chapters on the measured state"@en ;
    backlog:revisesLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:revisesFromStage backlog:Stage_Scope ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_Retro24, ex:IA3_Retro24 ;
    backlog:revisionReason "The change request ex:CR3_Retro24 (Sunday 2026-10-25, decided by the lineage's own change route under the owner's standing orders (retrofit all chapters starting with chapter 1; repairs re-rank the open items; a lineage never waits on unrelated questions)) adds a deliverable; the lineage is in its closed Backlog stage, and a deliverable added to a closed scope statement is a revision from the Scope stage (ruling G127). The request and its impact assessment ex:IA3_Retro24 were recorded first. This version retracts the Scope, Goal, Objective and Backlog outputs and rebuilds nothing; the next four versions rebuild them one stage each, a sixth fills the last commit; the items already in the register, Done ones included, re-enter by admission and are not re-dated. The retracted outputs and their digests stay as history (L-112). The interim versions are the declared transition (G129)." ;
    backlog:retractsOutput ex:Out3_ScopeR11, ex:Out3_GoalR11, ex:Out3_ObjectiveR11, ex:Out3_BacklogR13 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:revisedAtCommit "c0283d9" .
ex:Out3_ScopeR11 backlog:outputRetracted true .
ex:Out3_GoalR11 backlog:outputRetracted true .
ex:Out3_ObjectiveR11 backlog:outputRetracted true .
ex:Out3_BacklogR13 backlog:outputRetracted true .

