ex:AC9_Deck_Ch01 a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; rdfs:label "The deck of chapter 1 meets the deck standard D1 to D12, overlap-free, with a chapter-code manifest without error-first examples"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Owner-directed work (ex:CR3_Retro24, Sunday 2026-10-25, decided by the lineage's own change route under the owner's standing orders (retrofit all chapters starting with chapter 1; repairs re-rank the open items; a lineage never waits on unrelated questions)). Given the newest deck of chapter 1 (03-materials/ch01/SEN0401_Ch01_Introduction_3e_v2_11_0.pptx, unchanged) and its research, when the deck is rebuilt as a new file (a version above the newest) with its chapter-code manifest, then ALL of: (1) the deck standard check v1_1_0 for chapter 1 reports every element D1 to D12 met, no NOT_MEASURED, exit 0; (2) the deck overlap check v1_0_0 exits 0 on the deck (no text over a picture, table or other text, none beyond the slide edge); (3) the chapter-code manifest 03-materials/ch01/page/chapter_code_ch01_v1_0_0.json exists, lists the deck's code examples in slide order by name, the deck control check v1_1_0 (manifest:01) exits 0, and NO example's first output line starts with an error name (such as TypeError, ValueError, KeyError, Traceback): an example that teaches an error shows a first line that names what it does, then the error, because the page test 9.37.0 reads a first line that starts with an error name as a failed run; (4) the Deck chapter check v1_3_0 for Deck/Ch01 passes and the deck match check reports 0 not carried; (5) no committed file is edited, including the executor's own logs (each written once); results as printed; if any element fails the deck is named failing and this criterion has no passing result. MEASURED (the lineage agent's baseline, 2026-10-25, tool sen0401_lineage_baseline_v1_0_0.py, one log per run in 08-tooling/verify/iter24/baseline, committed before this change): DECKS: the deck standard check v1_1_0 gives 12 of 12 elements PASS for chapters 5 to 8 and 4 PASS, 8 FAIL (D1, D2, D3, D4, D5, D7, D10, D11) for every one of chapters 1 to 4 and 9 to 14; the deck overlap check v1_0_0 is clean on the decks of chapters 5 to 14 and reports overlaps (text over a picture, a table over text) on chapters 1 to 4. MANIFESTS: a chapter-code manifest exists for chapters 5 to 8 only (27, 18, 15 and 20 examples; the control check manifest:NN exits 0; no example's first output line starts with an error name) and for no other chapter. PAGES: the newest pages of chapters 5 to 8 declare the standard 9.52, have the chapter-code tab and pass the charset check; the newest pages of the other ten chapters have no chapter-code tab, no standard declaration and fail the charset check (tag behind byte 1024). STORY LAYOUT (the owner's rule, new tool sen0401_story_layout_probe_v1_0_0.py, 1366x768, 1400x900 and 390x844, logs in 08-tooling/verify/iter24/storylayout): the pages of chapters 5, 6, 7 and 8 FAIL it (a photograph as tall as the screen pushes the narrative below the first screen: 4 of 9, 3 of 12, 2 of 9 and 3 of 9 stories); the cause is the template 9.52.2 (.simgrow img with width 100 percent and height auto, no height cap). GATES: the Stage 4 gate runner v1_1_0 gives OVERALL PASS for all fourteen chapters; the Research chapter check v1_3_0 exits 0 for chapters 2 to 14 and CRASHES for chapter 1 (no file sen0401_ch01_verify_v*.py exists; the check names the verify script as a part). NOT MEASURED here: the page test 9.37.0 on the old pages (they lack the chapter-code tab, so P2 and P11 cannot pass) - the page test is run on every rebuilt page. DECK STANDARD (checked by the deck standard check, python-pptx 1.0.2, one named result per element): D1 every slide is numbered; D2 no text box over 30 words; D3 every code slide has a plain-language explanation beside the code and the executed result as a visual (a native chart, a table or a drawn diagram), not REPL text; D4 every key concept of the chapter has an everyday analogy slide or box (the key concepts are listed in the chapter research); D5 every story has who, what, when, where, why and how, a real picture and a live link; D6 every chart is a native chart object, no chart picture; D7 speaker notes at most 60 words per slide; D8 a resources slide with links; D9 one background scheme, no dark/light switching mid-deck; D10 every divider names its concepts with one line of meaning and one visual; D11 coverage: the share of the chapter research concepts that appear on a slide, stated as measured, not below 90 percent; D12 no code line wraps." ;
