ex:AC9_Page_Ch05 a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; rdfs:label "The page of chapter 5 on template 9.52.4 passes the page tests 9.37.0, 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 and the story layout at three viewports, with its character set first"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Owner-directed work (ex:CR3_Retro24, Sunday 2026-10-25, decided by the lineage's own change route under the owner's standing orders (retrofit all chapters starting with chapter 1; repairs re-rank the open items; a lineage never waits on unrelated questions)). Given the deck of chapter 5 with its chapter-code manifest and the newest page of chapter 5 (03-materials/ch05/page/sen0401_ch05_page_v9_83_0.html, unchanged), when the page is rebuilt as a new file with a page version above 9.83.0 on the template 9.52.4 with the builders v4_15_0 and v2_24_0, then ALL of: (1) the charset check v1_0_0 exits 0 on the page (the tag below byte 1024, the first 1024 bytes decode as UTF-8); (2) the page test 9.37.0 runs all its features with no skip and passes them (exit 0), and the page tests 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 report no failure and widgets, features and gates not below the stored result of the page 9.83.0, skipped not more; (3) the STORY LAYOUT probe sen0401_story_layout_probe_v1_0_0.py prints RESULT PASS: for EVERY story of the Stories tab, at 1366x768, 1400x900 and 390x844, the tallest photograph is shorter than the viewport and the story's narrative paragraph begins within the first screen; (4) the chapter-code tab equals the deck's chapter-code manifest in names and order and each example runs in the page and shows its result; (5) the Stage 4 gate runner v1_1_0 for 05 exits 0 with Stage3.F, Stage4.A, B, cov, sub and src PASS, the Research, Deck and Page chapter checks pass, the deck match check reports 0 not carried; (6) the Stage 4 page ABox and the stored page-test result are new files; (7) no committed file is edited (an executor's own log is written once), no gate, test or threshold changed; results as printed; if any element fails the page is named failing and this criterion has no passing result. MEASURED (the lineage agent's baseline, 2026-10-25, tool sen0401_lineage_baseline_v1_0_0.py, one log per run in 08-tooling/verify/iter24/baseline, committed before this change): DECKS: the deck standard check v1_1_0 gives 12 of 12 elements PASS for chapters 5 to 8 and 4 PASS, 8 FAIL (D1, D2, D3, D4, D5, D7, D10, D11) for every one of chapters 1 to 4 and 9 to 14; the deck overlap check v1_0_0 is clean on the decks of chapters 5 to 14 and reports overlaps (text over a picture, a table over text) on chapters 1 to 4. MANIFESTS: a chapter-code manifest exists for chapters 5 to 8 only (27, 18, 15 and 20 examples; the control check manifest:NN exits 0; no example's first output line starts with an error name) and for no other chapter. PAGES: the newest pages of chapters 5 to 8 declare the standard 9.52, have the chapter-code tab and pass the charset check; the newest pages of the other ten chapters have no chapter-code tab, no standard declaration and fail the charset check (tag behind byte 1024). STORY LAYOUT (the owner's rule, new tool sen0401_story_layout_probe_v1_0_0.py, 1366x768, 1400x900 and 390x844, logs in 08-tooling/verify/iter24/storylayout): the pages of chapters 5, 6, 7 and 8 FAIL it (a photograph as tall as the screen pushes the narrative below the first screen: 4 of 9, 3 of 12, 2 of 9 and 3 of 9 stories); the cause is the template 9.52.2 (.simgrow img with width 100 percent and height auto, no height cap). GATES: the Stage 4 gate runner v1_1_0 gives OVERALL PASS for all fourteen chapters; the Research chapter check v1_3_0 exits 0 for chapters 2 to 14 and CRASHES for chapter 1 (no file sen0401_ch01_verify_v*.py exists; the check names the verify script as a part). NOT MEASURED here: the page test 9.37.0 on the old pages (they lack the chapter-code tab, so P2 and P11 cannot pass) - the page test is run on every rebuilt page. STORY RULE (the owner's): the text of a story is visible without scrolling past a full-height photograph; check EVERY story at 1366x768, 1400x900 and 390x844 with the narrative starting within the first screen. The template 9.52.2 has no height cap on story photographs (.simgrow img{width:100%;height:auto}); the template 9.52.4 caps them. PAGE STANDARD (checked by the new page test 9.36.0, Playwright 1.56.0): P1 no horizontal overflow at 390 px and at 1366 px; P2 the chapter-code tab lists the deck's examples by NAME in the deck's slide order, each runnable in the page with the chapter library defined in the page and its result visualised, and the code lives in the editor, not in the list; P3 tabs and left tree are synchronised and their label sets are disjoint or the tab bar is one row; P4 no third level of tabs, and one more level of panels so that one panel holds one concept; P5 a panel is at most 1.0 screen high at 1366x768; P6 no list repeated on one screen; P7 every diagram has zoom; P8 the top-level menu is uncrowded (at most 8 top-level tabs); P9 a text-size control and an adaptive layout at 390, 768 and 1366 px; P10 executed code results are visualised; P11 the page declares the standard and the examples equal the deck's code manifest." ;
