ex:AC9_Template a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; rdfs:label "The template 9.52.3 passes the story layout probe on the pages of chapters 5 to 8 and changes nothing else"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Owner-directed work (ex:CR3_Retro24, Sunday 2026-10-25, decided by the lineage's own change route under the owner's standing orders (retrofit all chapters starting with chapter 1; repairs re-rank the open items; a lineage never waits on unrelated questions)). Given the template 9.52.2 and the pages of chapters 5 to 8, when the NEW template 9.52.3 is made, then ALL of: (1) 9.52.2 is byte-identical (SHA-256 before and after); (2) the diff against 9.52.2 is limited to the rules of the Stories tab; (3) scratch pages of chapters 5, 6, 7 and 8 built from the present page data with the page builder v4_15_0 and PAGE_TEMPLATE=9.52.3 pass the story layout probe v1_0_0 (RESULT PASS, every story at 1366x768, 1400x900 and 390x844); (4) REGRESSION (carried from the withdrawn criterion AC8R_Regress of ST_Remedy_Regress_R, restated on 9.52.3, not waived): the page tests 9.37.0, 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 on the scratch page of chapter 5, and the page tests 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 on scratch pages of chapters 1 and 10 built from 9.52.3, each give the stored result of the shipped page of that chapter or better (equal or beat, as the regression criterion required); (5) no committed file is edited; results as printed; if any element fails the template is named failing. MEASURED (the lineage agent's baseline, 2026-10-25, tool sen0401_lineage_baseline_v1_0_0.py, one log per run in 08-tooling/verify/iter24/baseline, committed before this change): DECKS: the deck standard check v1_1_0 gives 12 of 12 elements PASS for chapters 5 to 8 and 4 PASS, 8 FAIL (D1, D2, D3, D4, D5, D7, D10, D11) for every one of chapters 1 to 4 and 9 to 14; the deck overlap check v1_0_0 is clean on the decks of chapters 5 to 14 and reports overlaps (text over a picture, a table over text) on chapters 1 to 4. MANIFESTS: a chapter-code manifest exists for chapters 5 to 8 only (27, 18, 15 and 20 examples; the control check manifest:NN exits 0; no example's first output line starts with an error name) and for no other chapter. PAGES: the newest pages of chapters 5 to 8 declare the standard 9.52, have the chapter-code tab and pass the charset check; the newest pages of the other ten chapters have no chapter-code tab, no standard declaration and fail the charset check (tag behind byte 1024). STORY LAYOUT (the owner's rule, new tool sen0401_story_layout_probe_v1_0_0.py, 1366x768, 1400x900 and 390x844, logs in 08-tooling/verify/iter24/storylayout): the pages of chapters 5, 6, 7 and 8 FAIL it (a photograph as tall as the screen pushes the narrative below the first screen: 4 of 9, 3 of 12, 2 of 9 and 3 of 9 stories); the cause is the template 9.52.2 (.simgrow img with width 100 percent and height auto, no height cap). GATES: the Stage 4 gate runner v1_1_0 gives OVERALL PASS for all fourteen chapters; the Research chapter check v1_3_0 exits 0 for chapters 2 to 14 and CRASHES for chapter 1 (no file sen0401_ch01_verify_v*.py exists; the check names the verify script as a part). NOT MEASURED here: the page test 9.37.0 on the old pages (they lack the chapter-code tab, so P2 and P11 cannot pass) - the page test is run on every rebuilt page. STORY RULE (the owner's): the text of a story is visible without scrolling past a full-height photograph; check EVERY story at 1366x768, 1400x900 and 390x844 with the narrative starting within the first screen. The template 9.52.2 has no height cap on story photographs (.simgrow img{width:100%;height:auto}); the template 9.52.3 caps them." ;
