th colour scheme (the matching look of the page). Follow the way the decks of chapters 5 to 8 were built (their generator files in 08-tooling/ch05-deck to ch08-deck are the pattern; write your own generator as a NEW tool file). ALSO write the chapter-code manifest 03-materials/ch10/page/chapter_code_ch10_v1_0_0.json in the form of chapter_code_ch08_v1_0_0.json: the ordered list of the deck's code examples (order number = slide order, a short NAME, the code that runs in the page with the chapter library it needs, the expected result). Slide code is exactly one chapter-code page tab: the manifest equals the deck's code boxes. NO example may have a first output line that starts with an error name (TypeError, ValueError, KeyError, Traceback ...): an example that teaches an error first prints a plain line, then the error is caught and printed after it. Run `python3 -B 08-tooling/sen0401_deck_control_check_v1_1_0.py manifest:10`, the deck standard check v1_1_0 and the deck overlap check v1_0_0 on your deck and fix until they pass. The checker is the independent tools, not you: report every element as printed. DO NOT EDIT OR APPEND TO ANY FILE COMMITTED EARLIER, INCLUDING YOUR OWN LOG FILES: write each log once, after its run is complete, and commit it once (the control of the page 9.82.0 of chapter 5 found a log file of the executor appended in a later commit and named that element not met). A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores: browser tests run one at a time and no build runs beside them. Planned session SEN0401-I27-deck-ch10; estimated start S (S = the start of the iteration, planned and not yet held), about 1.5 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start;