    backlog:hasAuditNote "Build the page of chapter 5 again as a NEW file with a page version above the newest page (03-materials/ch05/page/sen0401_ch05_page_v9_83_0.html) on the template 9.52.4 (course_page_template_v9_52_4.html, pass it with PAGE_TEMPLATE) with the page builder v4_15_0 and the page-data builder v2_24_0, from the chapter research, the deck's lecture export and stories (the deck stays as it is: it already meets the deck standard), and the deck's chapter-code manifest (state which file). State how you passed the template and how the lecture export and stories were made (the pages of chapters 5 to 8 are the pattern: their build logs are in 08-tooling/ch05-page to ch08-page). Run the page charset check (it must pass), the page tests 9.37.0, 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 (the runner with PAGE_TEST, serially, each under `flock /tmp/page_test.lock`), and the story layout probe `flock /tmp/page_test.lock python3 -B 08-tooling/sen0401_story_layout_probe_v1_0_0.py 05 <page version> <log>`; store the page-test result as a new test_results file, and build the Stage 4 page ABox with the page ABox builder v2_1_0. STORY RULE (the owner's): the text of a story is visible without scrolling past a full-height photograph; check EVERY story at 1366x768, 1400x900 and 390x844 with the narrative starting within the first screen. The template 9.52.2 has no height cap on story photographs (.simgrow img{width:100%;height:auto}); the template 9.52.4 caps them. PAGE STANDARD (checked by the new page test 9.36.0, Playwright 1.56.0): P1 no horizontal overflow at 390 px and at 1366 px; P2 the chapter-code tab lists the deck's examples by NAME in the deck's slide order, each runnable in the page with the chapter library defined in the page and its result visualised, and the code lives in the editor, not in the list; P3 tabs and left tree are synchronised and their label sets are disjoint or the tab bar is one row; P4 no third level of tabs, and one more level of panels so that one panel holds one concept; P5 a panel is at most 1.0 screen high at 1366x768; P6 no list repeated on one screen; P7 every diagram has zoom; P8 the top-level menu is uncrowded (at most 8 top-level tabs); P9 a text-size control and an adaptive layout at 390, 768 and 1366 px; P10 executed code results are visualised; P11 the page declares the standard and the examples equal the deck's code manifest. DOM CONTRACT shared by the template, the page test and the page tasks (so the independent test can find what the template builds): the chapter-code tab is the tab with attribute data-pane=\"chaptercode\"; its list items have data-cc-item, the NAME of the example in data-cc-name and the deck's order number in data-cc-order; an item opens the example in the editor element data-cc-editor with a run button data-cc-run and a result element data-cc-result; the left tree items have role=treeitem and the tabs role=tab; one concept panel is an element with data-panel; the playground list items have data-pg-item and show names only; a page that follows the standard declares <meta name=\"page-standard\" content=\"9.52\">. DO NOT EDIT OR APPEND TO ANY FILE COMMITTED EARLIER, INCLUDING YOUR OWN LOG FILES: write each log once, after its run is complete, and commit it once (the control of the page 9.82.0 of chapter 5 found a log file of the executor appended in a later commit and named that element not met). A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores: browser tests run one at a time and no build runs beside them. Planned session SEN0401-I25-page-ch05; estimated start S (S = the start of the iteration, planned and not yet held), about 1.5 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

