ex:AC9_Deck_Ch04 backlog:hasAuditNote "Control 2026-10-25 (record v0.292.0), deck of chapter 4, every element run by the evidence bridge and recorded as printed: (1) deck standard check D1 to D12: MET [deck standard check v1_1_0: every element D1 to D12 met, no NOT_MEASUR: verified -> SUMMARY PASS=12 FAIL=0 NOT_MEASURED=0 | failing: none RESULT PASS (exit 0)] | (2) overlap check: MET [deck overlap check v1_0_0: exit 0 (no overlap, nothing beyond the slid: verified -> RESULT CLEAN (0 findings)] | (3) manifest equals the code slides, no error-first example: MET [deck control check v1_1_0 manifest: order equals the order of the code: verified -> manifest chapter_code_ch04_v1_0_0.json | 21 examples | 21 code slides | deck SEN0401_Ch04_KeysAndAddresses_3e_v3_4_0.pptx | PASS order equals code-slide order, names unique, library files exist, hashes match where stated; error-first scan: no manifest example has a first output line that sta: verified -> manifest chapter_code_ch04_v1_0_0.json | 21 examples | error-first examples: [] RESULT PASS] | (4) Deck chapter check: MET [Deck chapter check v1_3_0 (examples re-run, fixtures refused, layout, : verified -> deck: 03-materials/ch04/SEN0401_Ch04_KeysAndAddresses_3e_v3_4_0.pptx deck check: deck_check_v3_4_0.py deck_notes_check 1.0.0: 47 slides, 47 with notes written for the reader RESULT Deck/Ch04: PASS] | (5) no committed file edited: MET [no committed file is edited (every file of the executor's commits adde: verified -> nochange commits 2a6c41b,296511e | PASS every file of the commits was added, none modified or deleted]. RESULT: MET: all elements are met. The deck match check is not an element run here: the lecture export and page data of the chapter do not exist until its page task (Iteration 26). The slides were rendered (LibreOffice PDF, contact sheets of all slides) and read by the builder as a reading, not a tool result: cream scheme throughout, numbered slides, native charts, stories with picture and link strips. Not measured: the arc check v1_1_0 refuses this deck as it refuses the deck of chapter 8 (it demands a 26-slide standard); it is not an element of the criterion. CONTROL FINDINGS (chapter 4, 2026-10-25): (a) the arc check run with --slides 47 refuses ONE thing: the agenda entry '(slides 45-47)' starts at slide 45, the summary, which is not a section slide; by the check's rule 2 that is a real, minor deviation of the deck (the other refusals of the unflagged run come from the 26-slide demand and a stale reading of the plan); it is not an element of AC9_Deck_Ch04 and is not waived: it is carried to the arc-check repair ex:CR3_ArcCheck (Iteration 27), which decides whether a closing summary needs a section slide or the agenda a different range. (b) The executor's links check reported 3 of 10 not answering; the control opened them: https://bips.dev/173/ and https://bips.dev/350/ answer 200 from this machine, the YouTube oEmbed of the Computerphile video NF1pwjL9-DE answers with its title (the watch URL answers 429 to scripted requests); the links are the right ones (BIP 173, BIP 350, Elliptic Curves - Computerphile); a bot-blocking answer is an item unreachable from a script, said openly, not a wrong link. The deck match check v1_0_0 reported 15 compared, 0 not carried by the executor; it is not an element run here." .
