    backlog:hasAuditNote "Repair the research set of chapter 1 as NEW files (the research files of 03-materials/ch01/rdodi stay unchanged; new versions above the newest): (1) cite the publication P23 (RFC 3986) where the research uses it, or drop it with a stated reason; (2) reach the findings minimum of 8 (the library's) with findings that are true and sourced, not padding; (3) after the repair the form of the chapter 2 verify script (the shared library sen0401_research_verify_lib_v1_0_0.py, not edited) passes on the chapter 1 research, so a NEW version of the chapter 1 verify script above v1_0_0 adopts that form and keeps the quotation, number and example checks; (4) the Research chapter check v1_3_0 for Research/Ch01 exits 0 and the Stage 4 gate runner v1_1_0 for 01 exits 0; the validators (CURRENT v1.13.0 for Stage 4, PINNED v1.6.0 for the chapter check) pass on the new research; (5) the research is consistent (HermiT) and nothing else in the repository is edited. DO NOT EDIT OR APPEND TO ANY FILE COMMITTED EARLIER, INCLUDING YOUR OWN LOG FILES: write each log once, after its run is complete, and commit it once (the control of the page 9.82.0 of chapter 5 found a log file of the executor appended in a later commit and named that element not met). A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores: browser tests run one at a time and no build runs beside them. Planned session SEN0401-I26-research-ch01; estimated start S (T0 = the first executor start of the iteration), about 2.0 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

