ex:AC9_ArcCheck backlog:hasAuditNote "Control 2026-10-25 (record v0.314.0), the arc check, chapter-free (28), every element run by the evidence bridge and recorded as printed: (1) v1_1_0 byte-identical: MET [lineage agent's own check: v1_1_0 is byte-identica: verified -> RESULT PASS] | (2) diff limited to the length reading and the closing-part range: MET [lineage agent's own check: the diff v1_1_0 to v1_2: verified -> RESULT PASS] | (3) chapters 1, 4, 8: the two refusals gone, the remaining ones listed with their rule, no rule weakened: MET [lineage agent's own check: on chapters 1, 4, 8 the: verified -> RESULT PASS; lineage agent's own check: on every chapter with a: verified -> RESULT PASS] | (4) wrong-agenda fixture still refused: MET [lineage agent's own check: fixtures with a range s: verified -> RESULT PASS] | (5) no committed file edited: MET [no committed file is edited (every file of the exe: verified -> nochange commits 1bcd5ec,91b9f25,295061c | PASS every file of the commits was added, none modified or deleted]. RESULT: MET: all elements are met. CONTROL FINDINGS (lineage agent): v1_1_0 SHA-256 unchanged and one commit only; diff 11 changed lines, all in the two named changes. COMPARE on every chapter with an arc plan (v1_1_0 given the deck length versus v1_2_0): the only refusal lost is the closing-range refusal of chapter 4; none added; chapters 2 and 5 differ only in the number printed in 'the standard is N' (neutralised); chapter 3 crashes with the same IndexError in both versions (a defect of both, not changed, not part of the criterion). Own fixtures (range inside a section, closing range at slide 44 inside a section, --slides 40 against 47 slides): all refused, exit 1; real chapter 4 deck exits 0. Rules NOT weakened: the closing range is accepted only as the LAST range and only when it starts at the summary slide before the single resources slide. OPEN FINDINGS the repaired check now shows (outside the criterion, none waived): (a) chapter 5: the check reads 08-tooling/ch05-deck, whose newest deck file is a stale 23-slide deck against a 68-slide plan (80 refusals), while the delivered deck is 03-materials/ch05 v3_1_0: a defect of the tool's file lookup, to be planned; (b) chapter 10 deck (delivered, Done): 9 of 49 slides have notes of 5 sentences against the arc rule of 2 to 4; chapter 1 deck: 3 refusals (agenda ranges end at 59 against 62 slides, two resources slides, one notes slide); chapter 7: 1 notes refusal; these are deck findings against the arc check's own rule, which no deck criterion names. Executor disclosure kept: stray file arc_check_v1_1_0_ch.txt in 91b9f25 (holds chapter 8 only, naming slip, left unedited; correct logs added in 295061c)." .
