    backlog:hasAuditNote "Done, recorded 2026-10-25: delivered by the executor session SEN0401-I28-arccheck (3 commits 1bcd5ec to 295061c). The checks and their results are those of the evidence nodes and the note of AC9_ArcCheck. CONTROL FINDINGS (lineage agent): v1_1_0 SHA-256 unchanged and one commit only; diff 11 changed lines, all in the two named changes. COMPARE on every chapter with an arc plan (v1_1_0 given the deck length versus v1_2_0): the only refusal lost is the closing-range refusal of chapter 4; none added; chapters 2 and 5 differ only in the number printed in 'the standard is N' (neutralised); chapter 3 crashes with the same IndexError in both versions (a defect of both, not changed, not part of the criterion). Own fixtures (range inside a section, closing range at slide 44 inside a section, --slides 40 against 47 slides): all refused, exit 1; real chapter 4 deck exits 0. Rules NOT weakened: the closing range is accepted only as the LAST range and only when it starts at the summary slide before the single resources slide. OPEN FINDINGS the repaired check now shows (outside the criterion, none waived): (a) chapter 5: the check reads 08-tooling/ch05-deck, whose newest deck file is a stale 23-slide deck against a 68-slide plan (80 refusals), while the delivered deck is 03-materials/ch05 v3_1_0: a defect of the tool's file lookup, to be planned; (b) chapter 10 deck (delivered, Done): 9 of 49 slides have notes of 5 sentences against the arc rule of 2 to 4; chapter 1 deck: 3 refusals (agenda ranges end at 59 against 62 slides, two resources slides, one notes slide); chapter 7: 1 notes refusal; these are deck findings against the arc check's own rule, which no deck criterion names. Executor disclosure kept: stray file arc_check_v1_1_0_ch.txt in 91b9f25 (holds chapter 8 only, naming slip, left unedited; correct logs added in 295061c)." .
