ex:CR3_ArcFindings a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "Repair of the arc-check findings: the check finds the delivered deck and never crashes, and the decks of chapters 1, 7 and 10 are accepted by it"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_ArcCheck, ex:CR3_Retro24 ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "MEASURED 2026-10-25 by the control of the arc check v1_2_0 (register v0.314.0, logs 08-tooling/verify/iter24/bridge_arccheck28): (a) for chapter 5 the check reads 08-tooling/ch05-deck, whose newest deck file is a stale 23-slide deck against a 68-slide plan (80 refusals) while the delivered deck is 03-materials/ch05 v3_1_0; (b) for chapter 3 it crashes with IndexError (a plan and a deck of different lengths) in v1_1_0 and v1_2_0; (c) chapter 1 deck v3_0_0: 3 refusals (agenda ranges end at slide 59 of 62, two resources slides 19 and 61, one notes slide outside the 2 to 4 sentence rule); (d) chapter 7 deck: 1 notes refusal (slide 35); (e) chapter 10 deck v2_0_0: 9 of 49 slides have notes of 5 sentences against the rule of 2 to 4. None of these is an element of the criteria the decks were controlled on (AC9_Deck_Ch01, _Ch10), so those stay met; the arc check's own rule is the written standard they now fail. Gaps are said openly and are not waived; they are filled through change management in the active lineage. Pending until the ScopeChange of the revision that admits the four stories into Iteration 29." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .

ex:IA3_ArcFindings a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What the arc-check findings repair costs and what it touches"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR3_ArcFindings ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "MEASURED 2026-10-25 by the control of the arc check v1_2_0 (register v0.314.0, logs 08-tooling/verify/iter24/bridge_arccheck28): (a) for chapter 5 the check reads 08-tooling/ch05-deck, whose newest deck file is a stale 23-slide deck against a 68-slide plan (80 refusals) while the delivered deck is 03-materials/ch05 v3_1_0; (b) for chapter 3 it crashes with IndexError (a plan and a deck of different lengths) in v1_1_0 and v1_2_0; (c) chapter 1 deck v3_0_0: 3 refusals (agenda ranges end at slide 59 of 62, two resources slides 19 and 61, one notes slide outside the 2 to 4 sentence rule); (d) chapter 7 deck: 1 notes refusal (slide 35); (e) chapter 10 deck v2_0_0: 9 of 49 slides have notes of 5 sentences against the rule of 2 to 4. None of these is an element of the criteria the decks were controlled on (AC9_Deck_Ch01, _Ch10), so those stay met; the arc check's own rule is the written standard they now fail. AFFECTED: one new tool file (arc check v1_3_0) and three new deck versions (chapters 1, 7, 10, each with the manifest unchanged unless the examples change). NOT AFFECTED: the controlled criteria of the decks (they stay met), every committed file. ESTIMATE (G120): 2.5 h tool, 2.0 h + 1.0 h + 1.5 h decks, each plus verification." .

ex:Revision_Lineage3_Scope13 a backlog:StageRevision ;
    rdfs:label "Revision of the third lineage from the Scope stage: the repair of the arc-check findings"@en ;
    backlog:revisesLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:revisesFromStage backlog:Stage_Scope ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_ArcFindings, ex:IA3_ArcFindings ;
    backlog:revisionReason "The change request ex:CR3_ArcFindings (Sunday 2026-10-25, decided by the lineage's own change route (gaps found are filled through change management in the active lineage; the coordinator relayed the owner's standing orders; nothing is waived)) adds a deliverable (the repair of the arc-check findings); the lineage is in its closed Backlog stage, and a deliverable added to a closed scope statement is a revision from the Scope stage (ruling G127). The request and its assessment were recorded first. This version retracts the Scope, Goal, Objective and Backlog outputs and rebuilds nothing; the next four versions rebuild them one stage each, a sixth fills the last commit; the items already in the register, Done ones included, re-enter by admission and are not re-dated (L-112). The interim versions are the declared transition (G129)." ;
    backlog:retractsOutput ex:Out3_ScopeR13, ex:Out3_GoalR13, ex:Out3_ObjectiveR13, ex:Out3_BacklogR15 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:revisedAtCommit "5a04c0a" .
ex:Out3_ScopeR13 backlog:outputRetracted true .
ex:Out3_GoalR13 backlog:outputRetracted true .
ex:Out3_ObjectiveR13 backlog:outputRetracted true .
ex:Out3_BacklogR15 backlog:outputRetracted true .

