ex:AC9_ArcLookup a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; rdfs:label "The arc check v1_3_0 finds the delivered deck and refuses a plan/deck mismatch without crashing, and changes nothing else"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Owner-directed work (ex:CR3_ArcFindings, Sunday 2026-10-25, decided by the lineage's own change route (gaps found are filled through change management in the active lineage; the coordinator relayed the owner's standing orders; nothing is waived)). Given the arc check v1_2_0 (unchanged), when the NEW file v1_3_0 is made, then ALL of: (1) v1_2_0 is byte-identical (SHA-256 before and after); (2) the diff is limited to the deck lookup and the mismatch refusal; (3) on chapters 1 to 14 no refusal that v1_2_0 gives for the same deck file is lost, and chapters 3 and 5 give no crash and no stale-deck verdict; (4) a plan/deck mismatch fixture is refused with exit 1 and a message naming both lengths; (5) no committed file is edited; results as printed. MEASURED 2026-10-25 by the control of the arc check v1_2_0 (register v0.314.0, logs 08-tooling/verify/iter24/bridge_arccheck28): (a) for chapter 5 the check reads 08-tooling/ch05-deck, whose newest deck file is a stale 23-slide deck against a 68-slide plan (80 refusals) while the delivered deck is 03-materials/ch05 v3_1_0; (b) for chapter 3 it crashes with IndexError (a plan and a deck of different lengths) in v1_1_0 and v1_2_0; (c) chapter 1 deck v3_0_0: 3 refusals (agenda ranges end at slide 59 of 62, two resources slides 19 and 61, one notes slide outside the 2 to 4 sentence rule); (d) chapter 7 deck: 1 notes refusal (slide 35); (e) chapter 10 deck v2_0_0: 9 of 49 slides have notes of 5 sentences against the rule of 2 to 4. None of these is an element of the criteria the decks were controlled on (AC9_Deck_Ch01, _Ch10), so those stay met; the arc check's own rule is the written standard they now fail." ;
    backlog:measuredWithTool ex:TS_ArcCheck13 ;
    backlog:measuredWithVersion "arc check v1_3_0 (python-pptx); v1_2_0 byte-identical" ;
    backlog:satisfiedByArtifact "the new files cited by SHA-256, the logs of the runs, verified by the evidence bridge" ;
    backlog:coveredByCase ex:TC9A_ArcLookup_Passes, ex:TC9A_ArcLookup_NotClaimed .
ex:TC9A_ArcLookup_Passes a backlog:TestCase ; rdfs:label "Run the checks of the criterion"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
