    backlog:hasGherkinText "Owner-directed work (ex:CR3_ArcFindings, Sunday 2026-10-25, decided by the lineage's own change route (gaps found are filled through change management in the active lineage; the coordinator relayed the owner's standing orders; nothing is waived)). Given the chapter 1 deck delivered (unchanged), when a NEW deck version is made, then ALL of: (1) arc check v1_2_0 on the new deck exits 0; (2) deck standard check v1_1_0, overlap check, deck control check manifest, error-first scan and Deck chapter check v1_3_0 exit 0; (3) the delivered deck and every committed file are unchanged (nochange); results as printed; if any element fails the deck is named failing. REPAIR: agenda ranges to the last slide, one resources slide, notes of the one slide shortened. MEASURED 2026-10-25 by the control of the arc check v1_2_0 (register v0.314.0, logs 08-tooling/verify/iter24/bridge_arccheck28): (a) for chapter 5 the check reads 08-tooling/ch05-deck, whose newest deck file is a stale 23-slide deck against a 68-slide plan (80 refusals) while the delivered deck is 03-materials/ch05 v3_1_0; (b) for chapter 3 it crashes with IndexError (a plan and a deck of different lengths) in v1_1_0 and v1_2_0; (c) chapter 1 deck v3_0_0: 3 refusals (agenda ranges end at slide 59 of 62, two resources slides 19 and 61, one notes slide outside the 2 to 4 sentence rule); (d) chapter 7 deck: 1 notes refusal (slide 35); (e) chapter 10 deck v2_0_0: 9 of 49 slides have notes of 5 sentences against the rule of 2 to 4. None of these is an element of the criteria the decks were controlled on (AC9_Deck_Ch01, _Ch10), so those stay met; the arc check's own rule is the written standard they now fail." ;
