ex:TK_ArcLookup_Build a backlog:ExecutionTask ; rdfs:label "Build: The deck arc check finds the delivered deck of a chapter and refuses a plan/deck mismatch instead of crashing, as a new tool version"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "TK_ArcLookup_Build" ; backlog:hasTitle "Build: The deck arc check finds the delivered deck of a chapter and refuses a plan/deck mismatch instead of crashing, as a new tool version" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Iter_29 ; backlog:admittedByOutput ex:Out3_BacklogR28 ; backlog:responsible ex:Executor_ClaudeCodeSession ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasTaskType backlog:TaskType_Build ; backlog:effectiveDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-25T11:47:02"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-25T11:47:32"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:lastAuditedAt "2026-10-25T11:49:35"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasExecutionModality backlog:Mode_Hybrid ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Ranked by its story's state; scoring both would double-count." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Make the NEW file 08-tooling/sen0401_deck_arc_check_v1_3_0.py from v1_2_0 (which stays byte-identical, SHA-256 before and after): (1) the deck to check is the newest deck of the chapter in 03-materials/chNN (by version in the file name) when SEN0401_DECK is not set, falling back to 08-tooling/chNN-deck only when 03-materials has none; (2) when the plan and the deck disagree in length, or any slide index of the plan is not in the deck, the check REFUSES with a message that names both lengths and exits 1; it never raises an IndexError; every other rule and message is unchanged. PROOF kept as logs: unified diff; SHA-256 of v1_2_0 before and after; v1_3_0 on chapters 1 to 14 (list the refusals, none lost that v1_2_0 gave for the same deck file); chapter 3 and chapter 5 now give a refusal or pass, never a crash or a stale-deck verdict; fixtures: a plan/deck length mismatch is refused. DO NOT EDIT OR APPEND TO ANY FILE COMMITTED EARLIER, INCLUDING YOUR OWN LOG FILES: write each log once, after its run is complete, and commit it once (the control of the page 9.82.0 of chapter 5 found a log file of the executor appended in a later commit and named that element not met). A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores: browser tests run one at a time and no build runs beside them. Planned session SEN0401-I29-arclookup; estimated start S (S = the start of the iteration, planned and not yet held), about 2.5 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

