    backlog:hasGherkinText "Owner-directed work (ex:CR3_Ch12Research, Sunday 2026-10-25, decided by the lineage's own change route (gaps found are filled through change management in the active lineage; the coordinator relayed the owner's standing orders; nothing is waived)). Given the chapter 12 research v1_0_1 (unchanged), when the research is corrected as new files, then ALL of: (1) the primary-source concepts are those of chapter 12 and none equals a chapter 11 concept by label without a stated reason (the lineage agent's own scan against every other chapter); (2) the Research chapter check for Research/Ch12 exits 0; (3) the Stage 4 gate runner for 12 exits 0 and lists its NOT_MEASURED items as such; (4) HermiT is consistent; (5) no committed file is edited; results as printed; if any element fails the research is named failing. MEASURED 2026-10-25 by the executor of TK_Ch12_Deck_Build_R24 (commits 40fac1a, c9d1985) and confirmed by the lineage agent in the control (register v0.329.0): the 41 primary-source concepts of 03-materials/ch12/rdodi/sen0401_ch12_research_v1_0_1.ttl are identical by label to the 41 of the chapter 11 research (41 of 41); no other pair of chapters overlaps (scan of chapters 1 to 14). The deck standard check reads these concepts for D4 and D11, so the chapter 12 deck v2_0_0 shows eight slides titled From chapter 11 (slides 43 to 50) that teach none of chapter 12 and cover only 39 real chapter 12 concepts; the criterion AC9_Deck_Ch12 names the checks and is MET, the defect is a gap of the research set, not of that criterion." ;
