    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Ranked by its story's state; scoring both would double-count." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Correct the research set of chapter 12 as NEW files (the research files of 03-materials/ch12/rdodi stay unchanged; new versions above the newest): the primary-source concepts are those of chapter 12 (Mining and Consensus), read from the chapter text and the saved sources, each with a label, a comment in a complete sentence and a citation, none taken from the chapter 11 research; the other parts of the research (publications, findings, stories, scorecard) are kept unless a statement is wrong, and every change is listed in a version note. After the repair: the Research chapter check v1_3_0 for Research/Ch12 exits 0; the Stage 4 gate runner v1_1_0 for 12 exits 0 (NOT_MEASURED items listed as such, not as passes); the chapter 12 verify script, if one exists, is not edited and a new version is made only where its checks need the new file; no concept equals a concept of the chapter 11 research by label unless chapter 12 itself teaches it (list the shared ones with the reason); HermiT consistent. DO NOT EDIT OR APPEND TO ANY FILE COMMITTED EARLIER, INCLUDING YOUR OWN LOG FILES: write each log once, after its run is complete, and commit it once (the control of the page 9.82.0 of chapter 5 found a log file of the executor appended in a later commit and named that element not met). A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores: browser tests run one at a time and no build runs beside them. Planned session SEN0401-I30-research-ch12; estimated start S (S = the start of the iteration, planned and not yet held), about 3.0 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

