ex:AC9_Deck_Ch13 backlog:hasAuditNote "Control 2026-10-25 (record v0.340.0), deck of chapter 13, every element run by the evidence bridge and recorded as printed: (1) deck standard check D1 to D12: MET [deck standard check v1_1_0: every element D1 to D12 met, no NOT_MEASUR: verified -> SUMMARY PASS=12 FAIL=0 NOT_MEASURED=0 | failing: none RESULT PASS (exit 0)] | (2) overlap check: MET [deck overlap check v1_0_0: exit 0 (no overlap, nothing beyond the slid: verified -> RESULT CLEAN (0 findings)] | (3) manifest equals the code slides, no error-first example: MET [deck control check v1_1_0 manifest: order equals the order of the code: verified -> manifest chapter_code_ch13_v1_0_0.json | 28 examples | 28 code slides | deck SEN0401_Ch13_BitcoinSecurity_3e_v2_0_0.pptx | PASS order equals code-slide order, names unique, library files exist, hashes match where stated; error-first scan: no manifest example has a first output line that sta: verified -> manifest chapter_code_ch13_v1_0_0.json | 28 examples | error-first examples: [] RESULT PASS] | (4) Deck chapter check: MET [Deck chapter check v1_3_0 (examples re-run, fixtures refused, layout, : verified -> deck: 03-materials/ch13/SEN0401_Ch13_BitcoinSecurity_3e_v2_0_0.pptx deck check: deck_check_v1_0_0.py deck_notes_check 1.0.0: 55 slides, 55 with notes written for the reader RESULT Deck/Ch13: PASS] | (5) no committed file edited: MET [no committed file is edited (every file of the executor's commits adde: verified -> nochange commits 2e03836,8f62c97 | PASS every file of the commits was added, none modified or deleted]. RESULT: MET: all elements are met. The deck match check is not an element run here: the lecture export and page data of the chapter do not exist until its page task (Iteration 26). The slides were rendered (LibreOffice PDF, contact sheets of all slides) and read by the builder as a reading, not a tool result: cream scheme throughout, numbered slides, native charts, stories with picture and link strips. Not measured: the arc check v1_1_0 refuses this deck as it refuses the deck of chapter 8 (it demands a 26-slide standard); it is not an element of the criterion. Slide reading by the lineage agent (soffice render, 55 slides, sheets 08-tooling/verify/iter24/ctl_deck13): numbered, 6 native charts, four stories with pictures and link bars, concept slides with everyday analogies, resources slide present. Links: the lineage agent's own curl re-check of all 14 links returned 200 (14 of 14). OPEN OWNER CONTENT DECISION, not decided by the lineage: three of the four story pictures (Mt. Gox letter, Casascius hologram, Trezor Model T) are stand-ins labelled as such on the slide, only the Shamir portrait is the real person; the owner's rule asks real pictures for stories; listed with the stand-in pictures of chapter 2. Other executor disclosures kept: deck match check reads the old page and export (NOT_MEASURED, falls to the page task); examples cut where the wheel lacks files (mempool blocks, BIP 39 word list and vectors, Shamir 1979 paper) and rewritten self-contained (genesis hash rebuilt from the header, a BIP 39 vector against a literal); R-values are one recorded run of Bitcoin Core 31.1 and said so on the slides; earlier failures (logo byte-copy fixture, slide 11 takeaway overflow, table and caption overlap) were fixed before the final runs, only final runs are logged." .
