ex:AC9_Ch05ArcPlan a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; rdfs:label "The arc check v1_3_0 reads the chapter 5 plan in its schema and every remaining refusal is a stated rule"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Owner-directed work (ex:CR3_ArcFindings2, Sunday 2026-10-25, decided by the lineage's own change route (gaps found are filled through change management in the active lineage; the coordinator relayed the owner's standing orders; nothing is waived)). Given the plan file deck_plan_v3_1_0.json (unchanged) and the delivered chapter 5 deck, when a NEW plan file deck_plan_v3_2_0.json is made, then ALL of: (1) the plan has as many slides as the deck file and in the same order; (2) the arc check v1_3_0 on chapter 5 refuses nothing for a missing kind or section, and every refusal that remains is listed with its rule; (3) the deck, the old plan and every committed file are unchanged (nochange); results as printed. MEASURED 2026-10-25 by the executor of TK_ArcLookup_Build (commits 663e649, 0ec94c4) and confirmed by the lineage agent in the control (register v0.343.0): the arc check v1_3_0 on the delivered decks shows (a) chapter 5: 82 refusals because its plan file 08-tooling/ch05-deck/deck_plan_v3_1_0.json is in the remedy schema (slides without the kinds title, closing and section that the arc check reads), a plan-schema finding and not a finding about the deck; (b) chapter 13 deck v2_0_0: one notes refusal (notes of 5 sentences against the rule of 2 to 4); (c) chapter 12 deck v2_0_0: one notes refusal of the same kind. The decks of chapters 1, 7 and 10 are planned in Iteration 29 (ex:CR3_ArcFindings). None of these is an element of the criteria the decks were controlled on, so those stay met." ;
