ex:AC9_Deck_Ch14 backlog:hasAuditNote "Control 2026-10-25 (record v0.361.0), deck of chapter 14, every element run by the evidence bridge and recorded as printed: (1) deck standard check D1 to D12: MET [deck standard check v1_1_0: every element D1 to D12 met, no NOT_MEASUR: verified -> SUMMARY PASS=12 FAIL=0 NOT_MEASURED=0 | failing: none RESULT PASS (exit 0)] | (2) overlap check: MET [deck overlap check v1_0_0: exit 0 (no overlap, nothing beyond the slid: verified -> RESULT CLEAN (0 findings)] | (3) manifest equals the code slides, no error-first example: MET [deck control check v1_1_0 manifest: order equals the order of the code: verified -> manifest chapter_code_ch14_v1_0_0.json | 19 examples | 19 code slides | deck SEN0401_Ch14_SecondLayerApplications_3e_v2_0_0.pptx | PASS order equals code-slide order, names unique, library files exist, hashes match where stated; error-first scan: no manifest example has a first output line that sta: verified -> manifest chapter_code_ch14_v1_0_0.json | 19 examples | error-first examples: [] RESULT PASS] | (4) Deck chapter check: MET [Deck chapter check v1_3_0 (examples re-run, fixtures refused, layout, : verified -> deck: 03-materials/ch14/SEN0401_Ch14_SecondLayerApplications_3e_v2_0_0.pptx deck check: deck_check_v1_0_0.py deck_notes_check 1.0.0: 47 slides, 47 with notes written for the reader RESULT Deck/Ch14: PASS] | (5) no committed file edited: MET [no committed file is edited (every file of the executor's commits adde: verified -> nochange commits e189d73,aeda513 | PASS every file of the commits was added, none modified or deleted]. RESULT: MET: all elements are met. The deck match check is not an element run here: the lecture export and page data of the chapter do not exist until its page task (Iteration 26). The slides were rendered (LibreOffice PDF, contact sheets of all slides) and read by the builder as a reading, not a tool result: cream scheme throughout, numbered slides, native charts, stories with picture and link strips. Not measured: the arc check v1_1_0 refuses this deck as it refuses the deck of chapter 8 (it demands a 26-slide standard); it is not an element of the criterion. Slide reading by the lineage agent (soffice render, 47 slides, sheets 08-tooling/verify/iter24/ctl_deck14): numbered, 5 native charts, four stories with pictures and link bars, concept cards with everyday analogies, resources slide present. Links: the lineage agent's own curl re-check returned 200 for 13 of 14 links; the 14th (the Spillman list post on lists.linuxfoundation.org) answers 418 to a browser user agent and 200 to the plain curl agent: bot blocking by the site, the link works; recorded openly. FIRST CONTROL RUN FAILED FOR AN ENVIRONMENT CAUSE: the disk was full (0 MB free) and the fixture part of the Deck chapter check died with OSError 28; the first prepare run was deleted and rerun after space was freed; the logs kept are of the clean rerun (6 verified, 0 unverified). ROOT CAUSE of the full disk, measured: the Deck chapter check v1_3_0 leaves its fixture copies in /tmp/sen0401_fx_* (34 directories, 1.7 GB; 16 of them older than 30 minutes were removed by the lineage agent to continue, 18 recent ones left because executors may be running); the repair is a new chapter check version that removes them, to be planned. Executor disclosures kept: research lists 69 labels, the checker counts 61 after merging 8 repeats (research not edited); the wheel lacks the BOLT 4 onion test file and the mempool statistics so examples use only the wheel; the Spillman story link points to the original list post (header spells Spilman, the module and the book Spillman); story pictures are the earlier deck's own files with captions saying what they are (Papa John's is a commemorative plaque, the Lightning picture is a source figure); title shortened to Chapter 14: Second-Layer Apps for overlap; deck match check reads the old page and export (NOT_MEASURED)." .
