ex:AC9_TmpCleanup a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; rdfs:label "The Deck chapter check v1_4_0 leaves no temporary folder and changes nothing else"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Owner-directed work (ex:CR3_TmpLeak, Sunday 2026-10-25, decided by the lineage's own change route (gaps found are filled through change management in the active lineage; the coordinator relayed the owner's standing orders; nothing is waived)). Given the deck fixtures tool v1_2_0 and the chapter check v1_3_0 (both unchanged), when the NEW files fixtures v1_3_0 and chapter check v1_4_0 are made, then ALL of: (1) v1_2_0 and v1_3_0 are byte-identical (SHA-256 before and after); (2) after one run of Deck/Ch09 and one of Research/Ch09 no folder sen0401_fx_* or hermit_* is left that was not there before; (3) the old and the new chapter check print the same lines on Deck/Ch09, Deck/Ch12 and Research/Ch09 except the version line and exit with the same code; (4) a fixture that must be refused is still refused; (5) no committed file is edited; results as printed. MEASURED 2026-10-25 by the lineage agent while controlling the chapter 14 deck (register v0.361.0): the root disk had 0 MB free; the control run of the Deck chapter check v1_3_0 died in its fixture part with OSError 28 (No space left on device) and the first control run was discarded and rerun. Cause: 34 directories /tmp/sen0401_fx_* (1.7 GB), the output folders of the deck fixtures tool (sen0401_deck_fixtures_v1_2_0.py line 149, tempfile.mkdtemp, never removed), left by every run of the Deck chapter check; the same leak is named in the briefs' DISK paragraph for /tmp/sen0401_page_test_*. 16 folders older than 30 minutes were removed by the lineage agent to continue; 18 recent ones were left in case executors were running." ;
    backlog:measuredWithTool ex:TS_ChapterCheck ;
    backlog:measuredWithVersion "Deck chapter check v1_4_0 (system python3, python-pptx), old v1_3_0 for the comparison" ;
    backlog:satisfiedByArtifact "the new files cited by SHA-256, the logs of the runs, verified by the evidence bridge" ;
    backlog:coveredByCase ex:TC9E_TmpCleanup_Passes, ex:TC9E_TmpCleanup_NotClaimed .
