ex:TK_TmpCleanup_Build a backlog:ExecutionTask ; rdfs:label "Build: The Deck chapter check leaves no temporary folder, as new tool versions"@en ; backlog:hasIdentifier "TK_TmpCleanup_Build" ; backlog:hasTitle "Build: The Deck chapter check leaves no temporary folder, as new tool versions" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Iter_32 ; backlog:admittedByOutput ex:Out3_BacklogR28 ; backlog:responsible ex:Executor_ClaudeCodeSession ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasTaskType backlog:TaskType_Build ; backlog:effectiveDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-25T12:03:00"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-25T12:06:05"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:lastAuditedAt "2026-10-25T12:14:29"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasExecutionModality backlog:Mode_Hybrid ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Ranked by its story's state; scoring both would double-count." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Make NEW tool files so that the Deck chapter check leaves no temporary folder: (1) 08-tooling/sen0401_deck_fixtures_v1_3_0.py from v1_2_0 (which stays byte-identical, SHA-256 before and after): the output folder it creates with tempfile.mkdtemp is removed when it finishes, whatever the result, unless it is given an output folder or --keep; its refusals, messages and exit codes are unchanged; (2) 08-tooling/sen0401_lineage_chapter_check_v1_4_0.py from v1_3_0 (which stays byte-identical) that uses the fixtures v1_3_0 and removes the folders of its own HermiT part (prefix hermit_) as well; every check, message and exit code is otherwise unchanged. PROOF kept as logs: unified diffs; SHA-256 of v1_2_0 and v1_3_0 before and after; the count of /tmp/sen0401_fx_* and /tmp/hermit_* before and after one run of Deck/Ch09 and one of Research/Ch09 with the new versions (no new folder remains); the results of the old and the new chapter check on Deck/Ch09, Deck/Ch12 and Research/Ch09 are equal line by line except the version line; a fixture the check should refuse is still refused. DO NOT EDIT OR APPEND TO ANY FILE COMMITTED EARLIER, INCLUDING YOUR OWN LOG FILES: write each log once, after its run is complete, and commit it once (the control of the page 9.82.0 of chapter 5 found a log file of the executor appended in a later commit and named that element not met). A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores: browser tests run one at a time and no build runs beside them. Planned session SEN0401-I32-tmpcleanup; estimated start S (S = the start of the iteration, planned and not yet held), about 2.0 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

