ex:AC9_ArcFix_Ch13 backlog:hasAuditNote "Control 2026-10-25 (record v0.382.0), every element run by the evidence bridge and recorded as printed: (1) arc check v1_3_0 on the new deck exits 0: MET [verified -> sen0401_deck_arc_check 1.3.0 (chapter 13): 55 slides, sections [5, 15, 26, 33, 42, 48], story slides [22, 41, 45, 47], resources slide [54], notes 25..60 words (mean 44); 0 refusal(s), 0 warning(s)] | (2) deck standard, overlap, manifest, error-first scan and Deck chapter check: MET [verified -> sen0401_deck_standard_check v1.1.0 | python-pptx 1.0.2 | chapter 13 | deck 03-materials/ch13/SEN0401_Ch13_BitcoinSecurity_3e_v2_1_0.pptx FACTS slides=55 code_slides=28 native_charts=6 analogies=41 lon; verified -> RESULT CLEAN (0 findings); verified -> manifest chapter_code_ch13_v1_0_0.json | 28 examples | 28 code slides | deck SEN0401_Ch13_BitcoinSecurity_3e_v2_0_0.pptx | PASS order equals code-slide order, names unique, library files exist, hashes; verified -> manifest chapter_code_ch13_v1_0_0.json | 28 examples | error-first examples: [] RESULT PASS; verified -> deck: 03-materials/ch13/SEN0401_Ch13_BitcoinSecurity_3e_v2_1_0.pptx deck check: deck_check_v1_0_0.py 28 examples re-run on 55 slides; 0 mismatch(es) stale fixtures: ['fixture_stale_expr_v1_0_0.pptx'] ] | (3) the delivered deck and every committed file unchanged: MET [verified -> nochange commits 3aa2117,3e40605,5589854 | PASS every file of the commits was added, none modified or deleted]. RESULT: MET. Reading of the changed slides 38 and 44 (by the lineage agent, from the files): the shapes and texts of all 55 slides of v2_1_0 equal those of v2_0_0 (python-pptx compared type, position and text of every shape); only the notes of slides 38 and 44 differ, each now three sentences with the same facts (example 22 and 25 of the chapter code tab, the line's height at zero, two points, the 850,000 coins and the 36 percent cut), so no rendering of the slide faces was needed. The deck v2_1_0 supersedes v2_0_0 (kept, unchanged); the chapter-code manifest is unchanged and its deck field still names v2_0_0 (the slide numbers are identical). The plan v2_1_0 was made too, because the arc check reads the notes from the plan. The error-first scan of the executor was an inline script whose first attempt read nonexistent keys and checked nothing (that attempt is kept); the control ran the committed scan tool. No browser, no lock." .
