ex:AC9_Ch05DeckFix a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; rdfs:label "The chapter 5 deck is accepted by the arc check v1_3_0 as a new version and stays met on its earlier checks"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Owner-directed work (ex:CR3_Ch05DeckFix, Sunday 2026-10-25, decided by the lineage's own change route (gaps found are filled through change management in the active lineage; the coordinator relayed the owner's standing orders; nothing is waived)). Given the chapter 5 deck v3_1_0 delivered (unchanged) and the plan v3_2_0, when a NEW deck version and a NEW plan are made, then ALL of: (1) the arc check v1_3_0 on chapter 5 exits 0 with no refusal; (2) deck standard check v1_1_0, overlap check, deck control check manifest, error-first scan and Deck chapter check v1_4_0 exit 0; (3) the delivered deck, the plans v3_1_0 and v3_2_0 and every committed file are unchanged (nochange); results as printed; if any element fails the deck is named failing. MEASURED 2026-10-25 by the executor of TK_Ch05_ArcPlan_Build (commits 635eed8, 67e8fc6) and confirmed by the lineage agent in the control of the plan (register v0.383.0): with the new plan file 08-tooling/ch05-deck/deck_plan_v3_2_0.json (68 slides, as many as the delivered deck v3_1_0, same order) the arc check v1_3_0 on chapter 5 prints 10 refusals, 0 warnings, exit 1, and no longer refuses a missing kind or section. The 10 refusals are findings about the delivered deck: (1) the last slide 68 is light (FAF6EF), not the dark closing slide; (2) the agenda range that starts at slide 65 does not start at a section slide (sections 7, 12, 19, 31, 43, 53, 57; slide 65 is the summary, 66 the check, 67 the resources); (3) six slides titled 'Everyday pictures' (15, 30, 40, 42, 51, 52) have no takeaway strip; (4) slide 66 'Check yourself' is not a summary slide; (5) the notes of slides 13, 21 and 65 are outside the limit of 2 to 4 sentences and 100 words (5, 5 and 6 sentences). None of these is an element of the criteria the chapter 5 deck was controlled on, so that control stays met; the findings are carried openly, not waived." ;
    backlog:measuredWithTool ex:TS_ArcCheck13 ;
    backlog:measuredWithVersion "arc check v1_3_0; deck standard check v1_1_0; deck overlap check v1_0_0; deck control check v1_1_0; Deck chapter check v1_4_0 (system python3, python-pptx)" ;
    backlog:satisfiedByArtifact "the new files cited by SHA-256, the logs of the runs, verified by the evidence bridge" ;
    backlog:coveredByCase ex:TC9F_Ch05DeckFix_Passes, ex:TC9F_Ch05DeckFix_NotClaimed .
