    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Ranked by its story's state; scoring both would double-count." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Make a NEW deck 03-materials/ch05/SEN0401_Ch05_WalletRecovery_3e_v3_2_0.pptx and a NEW plan 08-tooling/ch05-deck/deck_plan_v3_3_0.json (the delivered deck v3_1_0 and the plans v3_1_0 and v3_2_0 stay byte-identical: SHA-256 before and after) that remove the ten refusals of the arc check v1_3_0 for the reasons it gives: (1) the last slide is the dark closing slide; (2) the summary slide comes before the check and the resources slide and the agenda range at the end starts at a section slide (the sections and the order of the content slides are otherwise as delivered); (3) each of the six 'Everyday pictures' slides (15, 30, 40, 42, 51, 52 of the delivered deck) carries a takeaway strip, written from the slide's own content; (4) the notes of slides 13, 21 and 65 are cut to 2 to 4 sentences within 100 words with the same facts. Nothing else of the content, the examples, the charts, the pictures and the story slides changes; the chapter-code manifest is unchanged in its examples and keeps its slide numbers if no example slide moves (if one moves, a NEW manifest file records the new numbers). Build with the deck engine and builder of the delivered deck (read them first). PROOF kept as logs: the arc check v1_3_0 on chapter 5 exits 0 with no refusal; deck standard check v1_1_0 (D1 to D12), deck overlap check v1_0_0, deck control check manifest:05, error-first scan, Deck chapter check v1_4_0 all exit 0; the slides changed are rendered and read; nochange (every file of your commits added). DO NOT EDIT OR APPEND TO ANY FILE COMMITTED EARLIER, INCLUDING YOUR OWN LOG FILES: write each log once, after its run is complete, and commit it once. A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. Planned session SEN0401-I33-deck-ch05fix; estimated start S (S = the start of the iteration, planned and not yet held), about 4.0 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

