ex:CR3_TemplateRedo a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "Repair of the in-place edits of the page template 9.52.3, as a new template file"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_Retro24 ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "MEASURED 2026-10-25 by the lineage agent in the control of the template task (register v0.394.0, tool sen0401_template_control_check_v1_0_0.py): the committed file 08-tooling/course_page_template_v9_52_3.html was EDITED by its executor three times after its first commit (fb1d9f8, 36eeb95, 8a1922f; revisions 2, 3, 4), each after a failed check, instead of being made as new versions, and the log of its first failed batch was deleted before it was saved; the executor disclosed this. The rule is that a committed file is never edited, and element (5) of the criterion AC9_Template says so; it is NOT MET, as the control of the page 9.82.0 of chapter 5 named an appended log not met. The other four elements are met by the content of the final file (SHA-256 44bcb3e7...564d): 9.52.2 unchanged, the diff limited to the story rules, the story layout probe PASS on the scratch pages of chapters 5 to 8, the regression on the scratch pages of chapters 5, 1 and 10 at or above the stored results. Nothing is waived: the template task is Suspended, and the template is delivered again as a NEW file that is never edited. Gaps are said openly and are not waived; they are filled through change management in the active lineage. Pending until the ScopeChange of the revision that admits the story into Iteration 34." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .

