    rdfs:label "What the template repair costs and what it touches"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR3_TemplateRedo ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "MEASURED 2026-10-25 by the lineage agent in the control of the template task (register v0.394.0, tool sen0401_template_control_check_v1_0_0.py): the committed file 08-tooling/course_page_template_v9_52_3.html was EDITED by its executor three times after its first commit (fb1d9f8, 36eeb95, 8a1922f; revisions 2, 3, 4), each after a failed check, instead of being made as new versions, and the log of its first failed batch was deleted before it was saved; the executor disclosed this. The rule is that a committed file is never edited, and element (5) of the criterion AC9_Template says so; it is NOT MET, as the control of the page 9.82.0 of chapter 5 named an appended log not met. The other four elements are met by the content of the final file (SHA-256 44bcb3e7...564d): 9.52.2 unchanged, the diff limited to the story rules, the story layout probe PASS on the scratch pages of chapters 5 to 8, the regression on the scratch pages of chapters 5, 1 and 10 at or above the stored results. Nothing is waived: the template task is Suspended, and the template is delivered again as a NEW file that is never edited. AFFECTED: a new template file and the page items that name the template. NOT AFFECTED: the controlled criteria of the decks (they stay met), the content of the template (unchanged), the old templates, every committed file. ESTIMATE (G120): 1.5 h executor plus 0.5 h verification. The page items of Iterations 25 to 28 name the template and its Verify task: they are re-pointed to 9.52.4 in the rebuilt Backlog (their text only; no criterion is edited in meaning, none has evidence)." .

