    backlog:hasAuditNote "Make the NEW file 08-tooling/course_page_template_v9_52_4.html as a byte-identical copy of the committed 08-tooling/course_page_template_v9_52_3.html (final content, SHA-256 44bcb3e7b29a4917b8673c5cf08e79bd516a66ad3e21e4985a3884918f98564d), in ONE commit, and never edit it afterwards (the files 9.52.2 and 9.52.3 stay byte-identical: SHA-256 before and after). No content change is made or wanted: the bytes that were verified are the bytes that ship, under a name whose history shows no in-place edit. PROOF kept as logs, each written once after its run is complete: SHA-256 of 9.52.2, 9.52.3 and 9.52.4 before and after (9.52.4 equal to 9.52.3); scratch pages of chapters 1, 5, 6, 7, 8 and 10 built from 9.52.4 and from 9.52.3 with the page builder v4_15_0 (PAGE_TEMPLATE, PAGE_SCRATCH, the newest page version of each chapter) are byte-identical in pairs (SHA-256 of each); the story layout probe v1_0_0 on the scratch pages of chapters 5 to 8 built from 9.52.4 (under flock /tmp/page_test.lock) prints RESULT PASS; nochange (the commit only adds one file). DO NOT EDIT OR APPEND TO ANY FILE COMMITTED EARLIER, INCLUDING YOUR OWN LOG FILES. A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores: browser tests run one at a time under the lock. Planned session SEN0401-I34-template9524; estimated start S (S = the start of the iteration, planned and not yet held), about 1.5 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

