ex:AC9_Ch05DeckFix backlog:hasAuditNote "Not carried (2026-10-25): its story is withdrawn, because element (1) cannot be met without breaking D9 or declaring a false background; the criterion stands as written, not edited, not waived. Replaced by ex:AC9_Ch05DeckFix2." .

ex:CR3_Ch05DeckFix2 a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "Second attempt at the chapter 5 deck findings, with the contradiction of the gates and the broken plan named"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_Retro24 ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "MEASURED 2026-10-25 by the lineage agent (register v0.404.0, after the executor of TK_Ch05_DeckFix_Build stopped without committing): (A) THE GATES CONTRADICT: the arc check v1_3_0 rule 1 refuses a last slide that is not the dark closing slide (it tests the plan's declaration kind closing and bg dark), and the deck standard check v1_1_0 element D9 (one background scheme, the owner's rule against switching dark and light) fails a deck with one dark slide among light ones (1 dark, 67 light, 1 switch). The decks of chapters 4, 6, 8, 12, 13 and 14 pass both only because their plans DECLARE bg dark for a last slide that is really light (FAF6EF); the plan of chapter 5 v3_2_0 declares it as it is (light), so the arc check refuses it. No deck can satisfy both gates with true declarations. A gate is not changed without the owner's explicit word (scope exclusion): the contradiction is recorded as the pending change request ex:CR3_GateArcDark and is carried, not worked around. (B) THE NEW PLAN BROKE ANOTHER CHECK: the plan file deck_plan_v3_2_0.json (control of TK_Ch05_ArcPlan_Build, register v0.384.0) is in the arc check's schema but dropped fields that the deck check, the picture check and the fixtures tool read from the NEWEST plan file (picture names, chart items, expressions): the Deck chapter check v1_4_0 on chapter 5 fails the part fixtures of every owner check refused (FAILED ok_image_reencoded, stale_chart, stale_expr, stale_image_swap; with the plan v3_2_0 hidden the same tool says every stale fixture refused, the control accepted). The control of that task did not run the chapter check; this is stated as a gap of the lineage's control and carried by this story. (C) THE REMAINING ARC FINDINGS (10 refusals with the plan v3_2_0): six slides without takeaway strip (15, 30, 40, 42, 51, 52), notes of slides 13, 21, 65 over the limit, the agenda range at slide 65 and the summary slide not immediately before the resources slide (the summary comes before the resources slide, after the check yourself slide). Gaps are said openly and are not waived; they are filled through change management in the active lineage. Pending until the ScopeChange of the revision that admits the story into Iteration 35." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .

ex:IA3_Ch05DeckFix2 a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What the chapter 5 deck repair costs and what it touches"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR3_Ch05DeckFix2 ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "MEASURED 2026-10-25 by the lineage agent (register v0.404.0, after the executor of TK_Ch05_DeckFix_Build stopped without committing): (A) THE GATES CONTRADICT: the arc check v1_3_0 rule 1 refuses a last slide that is not the dark closing slide (it tests the plan's declaration kind closing and bg dark), and the deck standard check v1_1_0 element D9 (one background scheme, the owner's rule against switching dark and light) fails a deck with one dark slide among light ones (1 dark, 67 light, 1 switch). The decks of chapters 4, 6, 8, 12, 13 and 14 pass both only because their plans DECLARE bg dark for a last slide that is really light (FAF6EF); the plan of chapter 5 v3_2_0 declares it as it is (light), so the arc check refuses it. No deck can satisfy both gates with true declarations. A gate is not changed without the owner's explicit word (scope exclusion): the contradiction is recorded as the pending change request ex:CR3_GateArcDark and is carried, not worked around. (B) THE NEW PLAN BROKE ANOTHER CHECK: the plan file deck_plan_v3_2_0.json (control of TK_Ch05_ArcPlan_Build, register v0.384.0) is in the arc check's schema but dropped fields that the deck check, the picture check and the fixtures tool read from the NEWEST plan file (picture names, chart items, expressions): the Deck chapter check v1_4_0 on chapter 5 fails the part fixtures of every owner check refused (FAILED ok_image_reencoded, stale_chart, stale_expr, stale_image_swap; with the plan v3_2_0 hidden the same tool says every stale fixture refused, the control accepted). The control of that task did not run the chapter check; this is stated as a gap of the lineage's control and carried by this story. (C) THE REMAINING ARC FINDINGS (10 refusals with the plan v3_2_0): six slides without takeaway strip (15, 30, 40, 42, 51, 52), notes of slides 13, 21, 65 over the limit, the agenda range at slide 65 and the summary slide not immediately before the resources slide (the summary comes before the resources slide, after the check yourself slide). AFFECTED: a new deck and a new plan file. NOT AFFECTED: the controlled criteria of the decks (they stay met), the delivered deck, the old plans, every committed file. ESTIMATE (G120): 4.0 h plus 1.0 h verification. The first attempt (ST_Ch05_DeckFix) is withdrawn: its executor stopped without committing because its criterion could not be met as written." .

ex:CR3_GateArcDark a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "Gate defect: the arc check rule 1 (dark closing slide) contradicts the deck standard element D9 (one background scheme)"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_Ch05DeckFix2 ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "MEASURED 2026-10-25 by the lineage agent (register v0.404.0, after the executor of TK_Ch05_DeckFix_Build stopped without committing): (A) THE GATES CONTRADICT: the arc check v1_3_0 rule 1 refuses a last slide that is not the dark closing slide (it tests the plan's declaration kind closing and bg dark), and the deck standard check v1_1_0 element D9 (one background scheme, the owner's rule against switching dark and light) fails a deck with one dark slide among light ones (1 dark, 67 light, 1 switch). The decks of chapters 4, 6, 8, 12, 13 and 14 pass both only because their plans DECLARE bg dark for a last slide that is really light (FAF6EF); the plan of chapter 5 v3_2_0 declares it as it is (light), so the arc check refuses it. No deck can satisfy both gates with true declarations. A gate is not changed without the owner's explicit word (scope exclusion): the contradiction is recorded as the pending change request ex:CR3_GateArcDark and is carried, not worked around. (B) THE NEW PLAN BROKE ANOTHER CHECK: the plan file deck_plan_v3_2_0.json (control of TK_Ch05_ArcPlan_Build, register v0.384.0) is in the arc check's schema but dropped fields that the deck check, the picture check and the fixtures tool read from the NEWEST plan file (picture names, chart items, expressions): the Deck chapter check v1_4_0 on chapter 5 fails the part fixtures of every owner check refused (FAILED ok_image_reencoded, stale_chart, stale_expr, stale_image_swap; with the plan v3_2_0 hidden the same tool says every stale fixture refused, the control accepted). The control of that task did not run the chapter check; this is stated as a gap of the lineage's control and carried by this story. (C) THE REMAINING ARC FINDINGS (10 refusals with the plan v3_2_0): six slides without takeaway strip (15, 30, 40, 42, 51, 52), notes of slides 13, 21, 65 over the limit, the agenda range at slide 65 and the summary slide not immediately before the resources slide (the summary comes before the resources slide, after the check yourself slide). DECISION NEEDED FROM THE OWNER (his explicit word, because a gate is changed only on it): which rule gives way - the arc check accepts a light closing slide (a new arc check version), or the deck standard allows one dark closing slide (a new standard check version). Until he says, no gate is changed, the plans of chapters 4, 6, 8, 12, 13 and 14 keep their declaration (bg dark for a last slide that is light) as a recorded false declaration, and the lineage does not wait." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Pending .

