    backlog:hasAuditNote "Make a NEW deck 03-materials/ch05/SEN0401_Ch05_WalletRecovery_3e_v3_2_0.pptx and a NEW plan 08-tooling/ch05-deck/deck_plan_v3_3_0.json (the delivered deck v3_1_0 and the plans v3_1_0 and v3_2_0 stay byte-identical: SHA-256 before and after). Do the work of the stopped session SEN0401-I33-deck-ch05fix, whose uncommitted files in the working tree are a start you may read but must rebuild and prove yourself: (1) each of the six 'Everyday pictures' slides (15, 30, 40, 42, 51, 52 of the delivered deck) carries a takeaway strip written from the slide's own content; (2) the notes of the slides 13, 21 and 65 are cut to 2 to 4 sentences within 100 words with the same facts; (3) the summary slide stands immediately before the resources slide (the check yourself slide comes before the summary; no example slide moves, so the chapter-code manifest and its slide numbers hold; if one moves, a NEW manifest file records it); (4) the last slide stays LIGHT like the rest of the deck and the plan v3_3_0 declares it as it is (kind closing, bg light): do NOT make it dark and do NOT write bg dark for a light slide - the deck standard check D9 and the owner's rule forbid a switch, and a false declaration is forbidden; the arc check v1_3_0 will therefore print exactly ONE refusal, 'the last slide is not the dark closing slide', which is the recorded gate contradiction ex:CR3_GateArcDark and is carried, not hidden; (5) THE PLAN v3_3_0 KEEPS EVERY FIELD THAT THE OTHER CHECKS READ FROM THE NEWEST PLAN FILE (take the fields of deck_plan_v3_1_0.json - picture names, chart items, expressions, fact rows, link groups - and ADD the arc check's kinds, takeaway and analogy fields to them; do not drop any). Build with the deck engine and builders of the delivered deck (read them first). PROOF kept as logs, each written once after its run is complete: the arc check v1_3_0 on chapter 5 (exactly one refusal, rule 1, exit 1); deck standard check v1_1_0 (D1 to D12 all PASS, exit 0); deck overlap check; deck control check manifest:05; error-first scan; the Deck chapter check v1_4_0 on Deck/Ch05 exits 0 (EVERY part, including fixtures of every owner check refused and control accepted, run with the NEWEST plan in the folder); the same chapter check run on the delivered deck v3_1_0 with the plan v3_3_0 beside it; the changed slides rendered and read; nochange (every file of your commits added). DO NOT EDIT OR APPEND TO ANY FILE COMMITTED EARLIER, INCLUDING YOUR OWN LOG FILES: write each log once, after its run is complete, and commit it once. A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. No gate, test or threshold is edited or worked around. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. Commit your work to main (pull --rebase before push). Planned session SEN0401-I35-deck-ch05fix2; estimated start S (S = the start of the iteration, planned and not yet held), about 4.0 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

