    backlog:hasAuditNote "Make a NEW deck of chapter 14 (the next version above the delivered v2_0_0; the executor's uncommitted files deck_storylink_v2_0_1.py, deck_plan_v2_0_1.json, sen0401_ch14_deck_v2_0_1.pptx in 08-tooling/ch14-deck and 03-materials/ch14 are a start you KEEP and finish: do not discard them) and a NEW plan, in which (1) the story SpillmanChannels shows the host of its READ link (web.archive.org) on its story slide (slide 23) as visible text beside the live link, and (2) the notes of the slides 22, 40 and 42 are cut to 2 to 4 sentences within 100 words with the same facts and the pointer to the chapter code example kept. Nothing else of the content changes; no slide is added, removed or moved, so the chapter-code manifest and its slide numbers hold. THE NEW PLAN KEEPS EVERY FIELD OF THE NEWEST PLAN (copy it and change only those fields). The delivered deck v2_0_0 stays byte-identical (SHA-256 2571a40a...4d89 before and after). PROOF kept as logs written into the repository (not /tmp), each written once after its run is complete: the story check v1_0_0 on chapter 14 prints no refusal; the arc check v1_3_0 on chapter 14 exits 0 with no refusal; deck standard check v1_1_0 (D1 to D12), deck overlap check, deck control check manifest:14, error-first scan, and the Deck chapter check v1_4_0 on Deck/Ch14 (every part, with the newest plan) exit 0; slides 22, 23, 40 and 42 rendered and read; nochange (every file of your commits added). DO NOT EDIT OR APPEND TO ANY FILE COMMITTED EARLIER, INCLUDING YOUR OWN LOG FILES: write each log once, after its run is complete, and commit it once. A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. No gate, test or threshold is edited. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. Commit your work to main (pull --rebase before push). Planned session SEN0401-I37-deck-ch14link2; estimated start S (S = the start of the iteration, planned and not yet held), about 2.5 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

