ex:AC9_Page_Ch02 backlog:hasAuditNote "Control findings 2026-10-26 (v0.472.0), added because the record of v0.470.0 lacks them (error of the lineage agent: the findings text was not passed in that call; the element results of v0.470.0 stand). The control's own runs were made under /tmp/page_test.lock, serially. Page tests 9.37.0, 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 all exit 0 on the FIRST control run (103/103 widgets, no FAIL, no skip, at or above the stored results of the page 9.71.0 in page-gates-evidence/regression; no rerun; every log kept). Story layout probe PASS (9 checks). Page reading (own screenshots at 1366x768 and 390x844 of stories 1 to 3): photo capped beside the text, narrative on the first screen, links and takeaway visible; story 3 uses the Bitcoin logo as a stand-in picture, which the page labels as such (weaker than a photograph). Chapter check Page/Ch02 takes the newest page file (9.72.0, checked on disk); the test names the page before it (9.71.0) as the shipped page; the tool does not print the tested version itself. Chapter-code tab equals the manifest v1_0_0 (14 examples) and its 14 code slides equal those of the newest deck v3_0_0. Deck match v1_0_0: 16 items, 0 not carried. Link check: the control counted the 13 hyperlinks of the newest deck and found every address in the page; NO link was fetched, the live state is NOT verified. Also run, not an element of the criterion: pages_link_verify v1_0_0 reports 1 of 12 entries of the chapter 2 link register not carried (the video 'But how does bitcoin actually work?', youtube bBC-nXj3Ng4); that video is on no slide of deck v3_0_0 and its address IS in the page, so it is a difference between the older register and the deck, not a missing link of the page. The executor's disclosures (seven old resource entries kept unmatched, the new tool pywheels_make_v1_0_0.py, some logs named without 'v') are noted and not judged by the criterion. The control tool sen0401_page_control_check_v1_3_0.py is a new file (stored logs also looked up in page-gates-evidence/regression); the control's brief path was first wrong (iter25) and was corrected in the new file control68." .

