ex:AC9_Page_Ch01 backlog:hasAuditNote "Control 2026-10-26 (record v0.474.0), every element run by the evidence bridge and recorded as printed: (1) charset check exits 0: MET [verified -> PASS /home/claude/sen0401/03-materials/ch01/page/sen0401_ch01_page_v9_72_0.html: tag at byte 37; first 1024 bytes decode as UTF-8 RESULT charset: PASS] | (2) page tests 9.37.0, 9.34.1, 9.35.1 at the stored results or better: MET [verified -> ch01 9_72_0 test 9_37_0 run ctl_ch01_page_9_72_0_test_9_37_0.full.log : widgets (122, 122) features 198 gates 6 skips 0 FAIL 0 [] | stored page 9_70_0 (122, 186, 6, 0) -> ok   verdict of 9_37_0 = the ] | (3) story layout probe PASS on every story at three viewports: MET [verified -> rative top 280.796875, images 1 PASS story 9 at 1400x900: photo height 234 of 900, narrative top 376.328125, images 1 PASS story 1 at 390x844: photo height 67 of 844, narrative top 463.78125, images 1] | (4) chapter-code tab equals the manifest, slides equal the deck: MET [verified -> manifest chapter_code_ch01_v1_0_0.json 15 examples; page tab 15 ; order, name, code, slide, expected equal (fields compared: the keys the page tab carries and the manifest has): True newest deck SEN04] | (5) Stage 4 gates, chapter checks Research, Deck and Page, deck match (the deck links check of the control is reported as a finding, not an element: it is outside the criterion): MET [verified -> sourced (tier-C residual: fluent-filler-with-source not caught) [PASS       ] Stage3.src: 118 real-sourced, 0 invalid (generator-stamp/absent) [PASS       ] Stage4.A: 2382 triples [PASS       ] Stage4; verified -> t                                                PASS   HermiT consistent                                            PASS RESULT Research/Ch01: PASS * Owlready2 * Running HermiT...     java -Xmx2000M ; verified -> e fixture refused, the control accepted SEN0401_Ch01_Introduction_3e_v3_1_0.pptx: 62 slides, 10.00 x 5.62 in   text frames estimated to overflow their box: 0   shapes reaching outside the slide: 0   s; verified -> d:false};const dx=+tr[0],dy=+tr[1];const edges=[...svg.querySelectorAll('line[data-a]')].filter(e=>e.dataset.a===a.id||e.dataset.b===a.id);const ok=edges.every((e,i)=>{const end=a.mine[i][0],b=a.mine[; verified -> chapter 01 page 9_72_0: 30 items compared with lecture_v3_1_0.json and sen0401_ch01_stories_v1_6_0; not carried: 0 RESULT match: PASS] | (6) page ABox and stored result are new files: MET [verified -> 03-materials/ch01/page/sen0401_ch01_page_abox_v9_72_0.ttl added by ['152f52a'] modified by [] 08-tooling/ch01-page/test_results_abox_v9_72_0.json added by ['9dc7ca8'] modified by [] 03-materials/ch01/] | (7) no committed file is edited: MET [verified -> commits dc6b237,d80defd,df0b8fc,f73f26d,19a23b0,9dc7ca8,152f52a | files not added: none RESULT nochange: PASS]. RESULT: MET. Control's own runs under /tmp/page_test.lock, serial. Page tests 9.37.0 (122/122 widgets, 198 features), 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 (122/122, 186 features) all exit 0 on the FIRST control run: no FAIL, no skip, gates 6, at or above the stored results of the page 9.70.0 (the last page that passed; the page 9.71.0 FAILED 9.37.0 on example 11 and has no stored result; it stays committed and failing, as the executor says). The executor deleted all /tmp/sen0401_page_test_* folders; none of the control's runs was in flight then, and the control's runs are complete (logs in verify/iter32/ctl_page01). Story layout probe PASS, 27 checks (9 stories x 3 viewports), run by the control (the executor did not repeat it). The Page/Ch01 check was run by the control under the lock; the executor's run was without the lock. Page reading (own screenshots at 1366x768 and 390x844 of stories 1, 2 and 9): photo capped beside the text, narrative on the first screen; the last story uses a real portrait. Chapter check Page/Ch01 takes the newest page file (9.72.0, checked on disk); the test names the page before it (9.71.0, the failed one) as the shipped page; the tool does not print the tested version itself. SHIM JUDGEMENT: the page's Pyodide has no hashlib.pbkdf2_hmac; the boot snippet defines it with hmac only when it is missing. The control ran the shim code against the real function on 28 cases (sha512, sha256, sha1; 1 to 4096 rounds; digest lengths none, 10, 16, 64, 70, 100; empty and bytearray inputs): 0 differences, and ran the chapter library's stretch on the example-11 phrase with 1, 10 and 2048 rounds both ways: identical seeds (64d8279a, 297e090a, 5eb00bbd). The shim does not change what the example computes; it makes the same function available where the browser lacks it. It is slower in the browser than a native one (pure Python loop), which the page test measured within its budget. Chapter-code tab equals the manifest v1_0_0 (15 examples) and its 15 code slides equal those of deck v3_1_0; the manifest names deck v3_0_0 (the examples are unchanged; disclosed). Deck match v1_0_0: 0 not carried. FINDING, not an element of the criterion: the control's own deck-link check found 4 hyperlinks of deck slide 19 (the Source links of the Kenya, Cyprus, Greece and Venezuela cases; the Ukraine link is carried) that are NOT in the page. The same links were not in the page 9.70.0 either and slide 19 held them already in deck v3_0_0, so it is an old gap and not a regression; the deck match tool v1_0_0 checks READ cards and the resources slide only, so it cannot see it. It is reported openly and not waived; it is to be filled by a story of the change route (the control check of the later pages runs the same deck-link check). Other pages: chapter 2 carried 13 of 13, chapters 5 to 8 carried all. NO link was fetched, so the live state of any link is NOT verified. Control tool: page control check v1_4_0 is a new file (STORED_PAGE names the reference page); the control's own deck-link check was left out of the element list of control70 because it is outside the criterion, its failing log is kept in the evidence." .
