s=[...svg.querySelectorAll('line[data-a]')].filter(e=>e.dataset.a===a.id||e.dataset.b===a.id);const ok=edges.every((e,i)=>{const end=a.mine[i][0],b=a.min; verified -> chapter 04 page 9_74_0: 16 items compared with lecture_v3_4_0.json and sen0401_ch04_stories_v1_2_0; not carried: 0 RESULT match: PASS; verified -> deck SEN0401_Ch04_KeysAndAddresses_3e_v3_4_0.pptx : 13 hyperlinks; 0 address not in the page: [] RESULT links: PASS] | (6) page ABox and stored result are new files: MET [verified -> 03-materials/ch04/page/sen0401_ch04_page_abox_v9_74_0.ttl added by ['4845ef0'] modified by [] 08-tooling/ch04-page/test_results_abox_v9_74_0.json added by ['8a901da'] modified by [] 03-materials/ch04/] | (7) no committed file is edited: MET [verified -> commits fb30072,3350e36,8a901da,4845ef0 | files not added: none RESULT nochange: PASS]. RESULT: MET. Deck-link check: 10 of 10 deck hyperlinks carried on the page (the control's own count). Page version: newest page file is 9_74_0; the page test names 9_73_0 as the shipped page (the page below it). My own runs under the lock: 9.37.0 (90 of 90 widgets, 199 features, 6 gates), 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 (90 of 90, 187, 6) all exit 0 on the first run, FAIL 0, skips 0, at or above stored page 9_73_0. My first prepare ran while 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 were still queued, so its regr element read them as missing; the bridge logs of that attempt are kept in bridge_pg04_first_unordered and the prepare was rerun after all three runs ended (12 verified, 0 unverified). Probe 9 checks pass, 0 failed; Stage 4 OVERALL PASS; chapter checks pass; manifest equals page tab (21 examples) and deck v3_4_0 code slides; deck match 0 not carried. Story 2 at 390x844, own screenshot: photo 67 px tall, who/where/when/read and the narrative text begin by about 330 of 844 px and fill the screen; the probe figure 796.8 belongs to its narrative-end element (the pull quote), not to the start of the text, so the narrow-width worry does not apply. Executor disclosure: the execut