ex:CR3_TemplateErd a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "The page template: the sections ERD can cover a dragged entity (the chapter 11 page 9.79.0 fails its page tests)"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_Retro24 ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "MEASURED 2026-10-26: the executor of the chapter 11 page (session SEN0401-I27-page-ch11, commits 8cfc35e, 95b5833, 06e8e67) reported that the page 9.79.0, built on the template 9.52.4, makes all three page tests 9.37.0, 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 stop with exit 1 (TimeoutError: Locator.click, 30 s, in the ERD step, no results file; 162 features had passed, 0 failed). The lineage agent's own run of the page test 9.37.0 on the page 9.79.0 under the lock (register v0.496.0) stops the same way: RESULT FAIL, and the click log names the element that intercepts the pointer events, the entity box of the field HeaderFields. CAUSE, measured by the executor's ERD diagnostic and by the lineage agent's ERD collision probe (sen0401_erd_collision_probe_v1_0_0.py): the test drags the first entity of the sections ERD and then taps the centre of the entity of the first relationship; in the chapter 11 sections ERD (16 entities, boxes 110 to 136 px wide, pitch 149) the entity BlockContainer has its centre at (497,492), inside the box of HeaderFields (x 479 to 589, y 399 to 497), which is drawn above it, so the tap is intercepted. The ERD code is the same in the templates 9.52.0 and 9.52.4. Probe on the newest page of every chapter (the probe was run under the lock, one browser, viewport 1400x900): the pages of the chapters 1 to 10 (built on 9.52.4 or earlier) are CLEAR (21, 14, 17, 13, 18, 22, 19, 23, 20 and 17 entities); the chapter 11 page 9.79.0 is a COLLISION; the existing older pages of the chapters 12, 13 and 14 (v9_77_0, v9_69_0, v9_77_0; 15, 16 and 13 entities, boxes 110 to 152 px) are CLEAR but are NOT built on the layout their rebuild will have, and the chapter 13 page has as many entities (16) as chapter 11, so a collision in the rebuilt pages of the chapters 12 to 14 cannot be excluded. The chapter 1 follow-up page (21 entities, CLEAR on 9.72.0, the same data) is not affected. RULING (relayed by the coordinator): the page tests are gates and stay unchanged; the template is not a gate and is repaired as a NEW file (9.52.5), never by editing 9.52.4; the ERD layout must leave a dragged entity uncovered; the page items of the chapters 12 to 14 name the new template; the chapter 11 page is rebuilt as the next page version. The page 9.79.0 is delivered and failing; nothing is waived. Gaps are said openly and are not waived; they are filled through change management in the active lineage. Pending until the ScopeChange of the revision that admits the story into Iteration 38." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .

ex:IA3_TemplateErd a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What the ERD template repair and the chapter 11 page rebuild costs and what it touches"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR3_TemplateErd ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "MEASURED 2026-10-26: the executor of the chapter 11 page (session SEN0401-I27-page-ch11, commits 8cfc35e, 95b5833, 06e8e67) reported that the page 9.79.0, built on the template 9.52.4, makes all three page tests 9.37.0, 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 stop with exit 1 (TimeoutError: Locator.click, 30 s, in the ERD step, no results file; 162 features had passed, 0 failed). The lineage agent's own run of the page test 9.37.0 on the page 9.79.0 under the lock (register v0.496.0) stops the same way: RESULT FAIL, and the click log names the element that intercepts the pointer events, the entity box of the field HeaderFields. CAUSE, measured by the executor's ERD diagnostic and by the lineage agent's ERD collision probe (sen0401_erd_collision_probe_v1_0_0.py): the test drags the first entity of the sections ERD and then taps the centre of the entity of the first relationship; in the chapter 11 sections ERD (16 entities, boxes 110 to 136 px wide, pitch 149) the entity BlockContainer has its centre at (497,492), inside the box of HeaderFields (x 479 to 589, y 399 to 497), which is drawn above it, so the tap is intercepted. The ERD code is the same in the templates 9.52.0 and 9.52.4. Probe on the newest page of every chapter (the probe was run under the lock, one browser, viewport 1400x900): the pages of the chapters 1 to 10 (built on 9.52.4 or earlier) are CLEAR (21, 14, 17, 13, 18, 22, 19, 23, 20 and 17 entities); the chapter 11 page 9.79.0 is a COLLISION; the existing older pages of the chapters 12, 13 and 14 (v9_77_0, v9_69_0, v9_77_0; 15, 16 and 13 entities, boxes 110 to 152 px) are CLEAR but are NOT built on the layout their rebuild will have, and the chapter 13 page has as many entities (16) as chapter 11, so a collision in the rebuilt pages of the chapters 12 to 14 cannot be excluded. The chapter 1 follow-up page (21 entities, CLEAR on 9.72.0, the same data) is not affected. RULING (relayed by the coordinator): the page tests are gates and stay unchanged; the template is not a gate and is repaired as a NEW file (9.52.5), never by editing 9.52.4; the ERD layout must leave a dragged entity uncovered; the page items of the chapters 12 to 14 name the new template; the chapter 11 page is rebuilt as the next page version. The page 9.79.0 is delivered and failing; nothing is waived. AFFECTED: a new page template file and a new chapter 11 page, and the page items of the chapters 12 to 14 that name the template 9.52.4 (re-pointed to 9.52.5). NOT AFFECTED: the controlled criteria of the decks (they stay met), the delivered deck, the old plans, every committed file. ESTIMATE (G120): 2.0 h plus 1.0 h verification." .

ex:Revision_Lineage3_Scope23 a backlog:StageRevision ;
    rdfs:label "Revision of the third lineage from the Scope stage: the ERD template repair and the chapter 11 page rebuild"@en ;
    backlog:revisesLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:revisesFromStage backlog:Stage_Scope ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_TemplateErd, ex:IA3_TemplateErd ;
    backlog:revisionReason "The change request ex:CR3_TemplateErd (Monday 2026-10-26, decided by the lineage's own change route (gaps found are filled through change management in the active lineage; the coordinator relayed the owner's standing orders and the ruling that the template is repaired as a new file and the chapter 11 page rebuilt; no question to the owner is needed; nothing is waived)) adds a deliverable (the ERD template repair and the chapter 11 page rebuild); the lineage is in its closed Backlog stage, and a deliverable added to a closed scope statement is a revision from the Scope stage (ruling G127). The request and its assessment were recorded first. This version retracts the Scope, Goal, Objective and Backlog outputs and rebuilds nothing; the next four versions rebuild them one stage each, a sixth fills the last commit; the items already in the register, Done ones included, re-enter by admission and are not re-dated (L-112). The interim versions are the declared transition (G129)." ;
    backlog:retractsOutput ex:Out3_ScopeR23, ex:Out3_GoalR23, ex:Out3_ObjectiveR23, ex:Out3_BacklogR25 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:revisedAtCommit "7ad0132" .
