    backlog:hasGoalRationale "Derived from the revised scope and the change request: MEASURED 2026-10-26: the executor of the chapter 11 page (session SEN0401-I27-page-ch11, commits 8cfc35e, 95b5833, 06e8e67) reported that the page 9.79.0, built on the template 9.52.4, makes all three page tests 9.37.0, 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 stop with exit 1 (TimeoutError: Locator.click, 30 s, in the ERD step, no results file; 162 features had passed, 0 failed). The lineage agent's own run of the page test 9.37.0 on the page 9.79.0 under the lock (register v0.496.0) stops the same way: RESULT FAIL, and the click log names the element that intercepts the pointer events, the entity box of the field HeaderFields. CAUSE, measured by the executor's ERD diagnostic and by the lineage agent's ERD collision probe (sen0401_erd_collision_probe_v1_0_0.py): the test drags the first entity of the sections ERD and then taps the centre of the entity of the first relationship; in the chapter 11 sections ERD (16 entities, boxes 110 to 136 px wide, pitch 149) the entity BlockContainer has its centre at (497,492), inside the box of HeaderFields (x 479 to 589, y 399 to 497), which is drawn above it, so the tap is intercepted. The ERD code is the same in the templates 9.52.0 and 9.52.4. Probe on the newest page of every chapter (the probe was run under the lock, one browser, viewport 1400x900): the pages of the chapters 1 to 10 (built on 9.52.4 or earlier) are CLEAR (21, 14, 17, 13, 18, 22, 19, 23, 20 and 17 entities); the chapter 11 page 9.79.0 is a COLLISION; the existing older pages of the chapters 12, 13 and 14 (v9_77_0, v9_69_0, v9_77_0; 15, 16 and 13 entities, boxes 110 to 152 px) are CLEAR but are NOT built on the layout their rebuild will have, and the chapter 13 page has as many entities (16) as chapter 11, so a collision in the rebuilt pages of the chapters 12 to 14 cannot be excluded. The chapter 1 follow-up page (21 entities, CLEAR on 9.72.0, the same data) is not affected. RULING (relayed by the coordinator): the page tests are gates and stay unchanged; the template is not a gate and is repaired as a NEW file (9.52.5), never by editing 9.52.4; the ERD layout must leave a dragged entity uncovered; the page items of the chapters 12 to 14 name the new template; the chapter 11 page is rebuilt as the next page version. The page 9.79.0 is delivered and failing; nothing is waived." ;
