    backlog:hasAuditNote "Make the NEW file 08-tooling/course_page_template_v9_52_5.html from the committed 08-tooling/course_page_template_v9_52_4.html (never edited; SHA-256 before and after) with ONE kind of change: the layout and the drag handling of the SECTIONS ERD, so that after any entity is dragged no entity box lies on top of the centre of another entity box, which is where the page test 9.37.0 (and 9.34.1, 9.35.1) taps (the element on top at the centre of every entity must be that entity). Choose the repair by measurement, for example a wider pitch or a grid laid out wide enough for the widest chapter, or bringing the dragged entity to the front and settling it into a free slot; the page tests, the page builder v4_15_0, the page-data builder v2_24_0 and every other part of the template stay as they are. Everything else of the template is byte-identical: the diff 9.52.4 to 9.52.5 is saved as a log and touches only the ERD layout and drag code. PROOF kept as logs written into the repository (not /tmp), each written once after its run is complete, the browser ONLY under `flock /tmp/page_test.lock`: SHA-256 of 9.52.2, 9.52.3, 9.52.4 and 9.52.5 before and after; the diff of 9.52.4 to 9.52.5; scratch pages of the chapters 1, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9 and 10 (newest page version of each, builder v4_15_0 with PAGE_TEMPLATE and PAGE_SCRATCH) built from 9.52.4 and from 9.52.5, whose difference is only the changed ERD code (save the diff of each pair); the ERD collision probe v1_0_0 (08-tooling/sen0401_erd_collision_probe_v1_0_0.py, committed by the lineage agent) on the scratch pages of the chapters 1 and 5 to 10 built from 9.52.5 and on a scratch page of the chapter 11 built from 9.52.5 with the chapter 11 inputs of the page 9.79.0 (the page data, manifest and lecture the executor committed): every line must print CLEAR; the page tests 9.37.0, 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 (runner sen0401_lineage_page_test_run_v1_2_0.py with PAGE_TEST, FULL_LOG, serially) on ONE scratch page rebuilt with 9.52.5 (the chapter 10 page 9.80.0), exit 0, widgets, features and gates not below the stored results of the page 9.80.0; the story layout probe v1_0_0 on the scratch pages of the chapters 5 to 8 and 10 built from 9.52.5: RESULT PASS; nochange (the commit only adds files). DO NOT EDIT OR APPEND TO ANY FILE COMMITTED EARLIER, INCLUDING YOUR OWN LOG FILES, AND DO NOT EDIT THE PAGE TESTS, THE PROBES OR THEIR THRESHOLDS. A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores and little disk: the browser runs one test at a time under the lock; remove only the temporary folders your own runs created and name them in your report. Commit your work to main (pull --rebase before push). Planned session SEN0401-I39-template9525; estimated start S (S = the start of the iteration, planned and not yet held), about 3.0 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

