    backlog:hasScoreRationale "RICE with dependency factor (BP-D10): score = Reach x Impact x Confidence / Effort = 14 x 2 x 0.8 / 4.0 = 5.60; the dependency factor 1 is recorded beside it and the ORDERING KEY is the score times the dependency factor = 5.60 (ties break in the owner's chapter order). Reach 14 chapters (every page of the course is built from the template; the pages 1 to 10 are measured clear, the pages 11 to 14 are at risk). Impact 2 (high): the failing page cannot be delivered and the pages of the chapters 12 to 14 can fail the same way. Confidence 0.8. Effort 4.0 h: 3.0 h executor plus 1.0 h verification. DepFactor 1: no open prerequisite. FACTS: ex:CR3_TemplateErd: the page tests of the chapter 11 page 9.79.0 crash in the ERD step because the sections ERD of the template 9.52.4 can draw one entity box over the centre of another (measured by the executor and by the control; probe 08-tooling/sen0401_erd_collision_probe_v1_0_0.py); the chapter 11 page is failing; the pages of the chapters 12 to 14 are rebuilt on the template 9.52.5, so their items wait for the template story. A repair re-ranks the open items (G147); a new dated record, no earlier score is edited." .
