ex:CR3_Ch13Ex12 a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "The chapter 13 page: example 12 prints Bitcoin Core wallet messages with the prefix Error: that the page test 9.37.0 reads as a run error"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_Retro24 ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "MEASURED 2026-10-27: the executor of the chapter 13 page (session SEN0401-I28-page-ch13, commits 5c4806a, 36d86b7) built the page 9.81.0 (template 9.52.5, builders v4_15_0 and v2_24_0, manifest v1_0_0 with 28 examples, lecture export of deck 2.1.0) and reported that the page test 9.37.0 prints RESULT FAIL (390 passed, 2 failed, widgets 84/84): the one defect line is 'P2 every chapter-code example ... 28 of 28 examples ran; 1 defects [12 A locked wallet shows the balance but cannot spend ...]'. The lineage agent's own run of 9.37.0 on the page 9.81.0 under the lock (register v0.520.0) gives the same: 390 passed, 2 failed (the same line twice). The page tests 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 and the other checks of the executor passed (368/0, story probe 12/0, ERD CLEAR, charset PASS, deck links 14 of 14, deck match 0 not carried, Pyodide preflight 28 of 28). CAUSE, read in the test and measured: the page test 9.37.0 treats a result of an example whose first 160 characters contain the text Error: as a run error. Example 12 of chapter 13 (slide 24 of the deck, manifest v1_0_0) is the only example of all chapter-code manifests whose expected output begins with the Bitcoin Core wallet message prefix: (1.0, 'Error: Please enter the wallet') and 'Error: The wallet passphrase entered was incorrect.' (measured over every chapter_code manifest; the chapter 14 manifest has none). The prefix is part of the node's text, not a run error of the page. RULING (relayed by the coordinator): the page test stays unchanged (a gate); the repair is a new manifest version, and a new deck version where the deck shows the same text, whose example 12 output does not carry the prefix, if that fits the teaching. FIT: the teaching of example 12 is that a locked wallet still shows its balance (1.0) but refuses to spend with the message Please enter the wallet passphrase ... and that a wrong passphrase gives The wallet passphrase entered was incorrect.; the prefix Error: adds nothing to it (the error codes -13 and -14 on the slide stay), so removing it with the string method removeprefix in the example code keeps the lesson, and the code still runs on the real stored result. The page 9.81.0 is delivered and failing; nothing is waived. Gaps are said openly and are not waived; they are filled through change management in the active lineage. Pending until the ScopeChange of the revision that admits the story into Iteration 40." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .

ex:IA3_Ch13Ex12 a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What the chapter 13 deck example repair and the chapter 13 page rebuild costs and what it touches"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR3_Ch13Ex12 ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "MEASURED 2026-10-27: the executor of the chapter 13 page (session SEN0401-I28-page-ch13, commits 5c4806a, 36d86b7) built the page 9.81.0 (template 9.52.5, builders v4_15_0 and v2_24_0, manifest v1_0_0 with 28 examples, lecture export of deck 2.1.0) and reported that the page test 9.37.0 prints RESULT FAIL (390 passed, 2 failed, widgets 84/84): the one defect line is 'P2 every chapter-code example ... 28 of 28 examples ran; 1 defects [12 A locked wallet shows the balance but cannot spend ...]'. The lineage agent's own run of 9.37.0 on the page 9.81.0 under the lock (register v0.520.0) gives the same: 390 passed, 2 failed (the same line twice). The page tests 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 and the other checks of the executor passed (368/0, story probe 12/0, ERD CLEAR, charset PASS, deck links 14 of 14, deck match 0 not carried, Pyodide preflight 28 of 28). CAUSE, read in the test and measured: the page test 9.37.0 treats a result of an example whose first 160 characters contain the text Error: as a run error. Example 12 of chapter 13 (slide 24 of the deck, manifest v1_0_0) is the only example of all chapter-code manifests whose expected output begins with the Bitcoin Core wallet message prefix: (1.0, 'Error: Please enter the wallet') and 'Error: The wallet passphrase entered was incorrect.' (measured over every chapter_code manifest; the chapter 14 manifest has none). The prefix is part of the node's text, not a run error of the page. RULING (relayed by the coordinator): the page test stays unchanged (a gate); the repair is a new manifest version, and a new deck version where the deck shows the same text, whose example 12 output does not carry the prefix, if that fits the teaching. FIT: the teaching of example 12 is that a locked wallet still shows its balance (1.0) but refuses to spend with the message Please enter the wallet passphrase ... and that a wrong passphrase gives The wallet passphrase entered was incorrect.; the prefix Error: adds nothing to it (the error codes -13 and -14 on the slide stay), so removing it with the string method removeprefix in the example code keeps the lesson, and the code still runs on the real stored result. The page 9.81.0 is delivered and failing; nothing is waived. AFFECTED: a new chapter 13 deck file and a new chapter 13 page; the chapter 14 page is NOT affected (no example of any other chapter prints Error:, measured). NOT AFFECTED: the controlled criteria of the decks (they stay met), the delivered deck, the old plans, every committed file. ESTIMATE (G120): 2.0 h plus 1.0 h verification." .

