    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Iter_40 ; backlog:admittedByOutput ex:Out3_BacklogR28 ; backlog:responsible ex:Executor_ClaudeCodeSession ;
    backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasTaskType backlog:TaskType_Build ; backlog:effectiveDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD ; backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:startedAt "2026-10-27T00:39:09Z"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:finishedAt "2026-10-27T00:45:08"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:lastAuditedAt "2026-10-27T00:48:27"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:hasExecutionModality backlog:Mode_Hybrid ;
    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Ranked by its story's state; scoring both would double-count." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Make the NEW deck file SEN0401_Ch13_BitcoinSecurity_3e_v2_2_0.pptx (in 03-materials/ch13) from the committed deck v2_1_0 (never edited; SHA-256 before and after) with ONE kind of change: example 12 on slide 24 (A locked wallet still shows the balance) shows its two messages WITHOUT the prefix Error: . In the example code the two message strings are cut with .removeprefix('Error: ') (for example msg = l['send']['error'].split('message: ')[1].removeprefix('Error: ') and the same for the wrong-passphrase message), so that the printed outputs read (1.0, 'Please enter the wallet') and 'The wallet passphrase entered was incorrect.'; the slide text, the notes and any quoted output of that example agree with it (keep what the slide says true for what the code prints). No other slide, example, link, note or picture changes. New files: the deck plan v2_2_0 and the example files your deck builder needs (new version numbers), the example output file for the examples run on the stored result, and the deck file. Also make the NEW chapter-code manifest 03-materials/ch13/page/chapter_code_ch13_v1_1_0.json from v1_0_0 (never edited) with only example 12 changed to the same code and the expected outputs (1.0, 'Please enter the wallet') and 'The wallet passphrase entered was incorrect.' (its other expected outputs, 3 and 0, stay); the manifest's slide numbers and code lines equal the code on the deck slides. PROOF kept as logs written into the repository (not /tmp), each written once after its run is complete: SHA-256 of deck v2_1_0 and the manifest v1_0_0 before and after; the diff of the extracted slide text and notes of v2_1_0 against v2_2_0 (only slide 24, only example 12); the run of all 28 examples of the manifest v1_1_0 on the stored results (28 of 28 run, every output equal to the expected output); the deck check of the chapter and the chapter check Deck/Ch13 (PASS); the count of the deck's hyperlinks (14 in v2_1_0, all kept); the deck match check; the manifest's code equals the code in the deck for every example; the check that no result of the manifest carries the text Error: in its first 160 characters; nochange (the commit only adds files). DO NOT EDIT OR APPEND TO ANY FILE COMMITTED EARLIER, INCLUDING YOUR OWN LOG FILES, AND DO NOT EDIT THE PAGE TESTS, THE PROBES OR THEIR THRESHOLDS. A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores and little disk: a browser, if you use one, runs one task at a time under `flock /tmp/page_test.lock`; remove only the temporary folders your own runs created and name them in your report. Commit your work to main (pull --rebase before push). Planned session SEN0401-I40-deck13fix; estimated start S (S = the start of the iteration, planned and not yet held), about 2.0 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

