    backlog:hasAuditNote "Make a NEW page of chapter 13 with a page version above 9.81.0 (9.82.0), as new files only, on the template 9.52.5 (PAGE_TEMPLATE names 08-tooling/course_page_template_v9_52_5.html) with the page builder v4_15_0 and the page-data builder v2_24_0, the NEW chapter-code manifest v1_2_0, the lecture export of the NEW deck v2_3_0 (the deck story ST_Deck13_Charts must be Done first) and the stories v1.3.0 that the executor committed for 9.81.0 (new files with new version numbers where a file must change; the page 9.81.0 and every committed file stay unchanged). State the deck version the page is built from in the page data and in your report: it must be the newest deck, 2.3.0. The page must meet the criterion AC9_Page_Ch13's measures, and the page test 9.37.0 must now exit 0. PROOF kept as logs written into the repository (not /tmp), each written once after its run is complete: the charset check; the Pyodide preflight of all 28 examples (the boot snippet pywheels_v1_2_0 as in 9.81.0; keep the log of EVERY run); the ERD collision probe v1_0_0 on the new page (CLEAR); the page tests 9.37.0, 9.34.1 and 9.35.1 (the runner with PAGE_TEST, serially, each under `flock /tmp/page_test.lock`; a main-thread budget failure may be rerun up to three times, every run kept); the story layout probe under the lock; the Stage 4 gate runner v1_1_0 for 13; the chapter checks Research, Deck and Page (the Page check under the lock); the deck match check v1_0_0; a count of the newest deck's hyperlinks against the page (all present; save the count); the page ABox and the stored result as new files; nochange (every file of your commits added). STATE which page version and which deck version each check tested. DO NOT EDIT OR APPEND TO ANY FILE COMMITTED EARLIER, INCLUDING YOUR OWN LOG FILES. No gate, test or threshold is edited. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold beyond the named new files. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. The browser runs ONLY under the lock; remove only the temporary folders your own runs created and name them in your report. Commit your work to main (pull --rebase before push). Planned session SEN0401-I40-page-ch13b; estimated start S (S = the start of the iteration, planned and not yet held), about 3.0 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

