ex:AC9_Deck13_Ex12 backlog:hasAuditNote "Control 2026-10-27 (record v0.531.0), every element run by the evidence bridge and recorded as printed: (1) the deck v2_1_0 and the manifest v1_0_0 are byte-identical: MET [verified -> 03-materials/ch13/SEN0401_Ch13_BitcoinSecurity_3e_v2_1_0.pptx before(46d1284) 89fb2d8ac55e1abf3fd3fbf89f54c79d97ec9f01a081bb80e2996f72d75b06dd after 89fb2d8ac55e1abf3fd3fbf89f54c79d97ec9f01a081bb80e29] | (2) only example 12 on slide 24 differs in text and notes: MET [verified -> part lists equal: True (259 parts); differing parts: ['docProps/core.xml', 'ppt/slides/slide24.xml']; allowed: ['docProps/core.xml', 'ppt/notesSlides/notesSlide24.xml', 'ppt/slides/slide24.xml'] parts; verified -> slides 55 and 55; slides whose text or notes differ: [24] --- v2_1_0 +++ v2_2_0 @@ -7 +7 @@ ->>> shown = l['balance_visible'] +>>> u = R['b4_unlocked'] @@ -10 +10 @@ ->>> spend = msg[:30] +>>> msg = m] | (3) 28 of 28 examples run, every output equals its expected output, none carries Error:, the manifest code equals the deck code: MET [verified -> python 3.14.6; 28 examples, 61 result texts; defects: [] run28 RESULT PASS; verified -> python 3.14.6; 28 examples, 61 result texts; defects: [] noerr RESULT PASS; verified -> baseline v1_0_0 against v2_1_0: 28 examples, 0 unequal [] v1_1_0 against v2_2_0: 28 examples, 0 unequal [] manifest ex12 code: l = R['b4_locked'] u = R['b4_unlocked'] msg = l['send']['error'].split('m] | (4) 14 hyperlinks kept, Deck chapter check, deck standard, overlap, arc, manifest and error-first scan pass: MET [verified -> distinct addresses v2_1_0: 14, v2_2_0: 14; only in old: []; only in new: [] links RESULT PASS; verified -> deck: 03-materials/ch13/SEN0401_Ch13_BitcoinSecurity_3e_v2_2_0.pptx deck check: deck_check_v1_0_0.py 28 examples re-run on 55 slides; 0 mismatch(es) stale fixtures: ['fixture_stale_expr_v1_0_0.pptx'] ; verified -> sen0401_deck_standard_check v1.1.0 | python-pptx 1.0.2 | chapter 13 | deck 03-materials/ch13/SEN0401_Ch13_BitcoinSecurity_3e_v2_2_0.pptx FACTS slides=55 code_slides=28 native_charts=6 analogies=41 lon; verified -> RESULT CLEAN (0 findings); verified -> sen0401_deck_arc_check 1.3.0 (chapter 13): 55 slides, sections [5, 15, 26, 33, 42, 48], story slides [22, 41, 45, 47], resources slide [54], notes 25..60 words (mean 44); 0 refusal(s), 0 warning(s); verified -> manifest chapter_code_ch13_v1_1_0.json | 28 examples | 28 code slides | deck SEN0401_Ch13_BitcoinSecurity_3e_v2_2_0.pptx | PASS order equals code-slide order, names unique, library files exist, hashes; verified -> manifest chapter_code_ch13_v1_1_0.json | 28 examples | error-first examples: [] RESULT PASS] | (5) no committed file is edited: MET [verified -> nochange commits 1cb991f,ab541ce,98e965c | PASS every file of the commits was added, none modified or deleted]. RESULT: MET. CONTROL NOTES (2026-10-27): the control used its own tool sen0401_deck13_control_check_v1_0_0.py, not the executor's proof script. Executor deviations read and accepted: the one-line removeprefix statement (70 characters) exceeds the deck standard limit D12 of 56, so it is two statements (the standard passes); the variables shown and spend were dropped so the listing fits and the last row is (l['balance_visible'], msg[:23]), which prints (1.0, 'Please enter the wallet'); the manifest fields manifest, deck and deck_version name the new files; the deck has 15 link entries and 14 distinct addresses (one paper on two slides). The deck match check v1_0_0 compares the page with the lecture export, so it belongs to the page story. GAPS FOUND (not elements of AC9_Deck13_Ex12, so they do not change this result, and nothing is waived): (a) the deck check v1_1_0, run by the control under Python 3.14.6 on v2_2_0 and on v2_1_0, refuses the chart ppt/charts/chart2.xml on slide 21 (example 10): no data labels; the same check passes the decks of chapters 12 and 14; (b) the body text of slide 24 still says the wrong passphrase gives the cut text 'The wallet passphrase entered wa' while the code now prints the whole message. Both are filled through change management in the active lineage (new change request, new deck version). The page test 9.37.0 was not run on this deck; it is the job of the page rebuild." .
