ex:CR3_Ch13Chart a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "The chapter 13 deck v2_2_0: the chart on slide 21 has no data labels and the body text of slide 24 contradicts what its code prints"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_Retro24 ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "MEASURED 2026-10-27: the control of the chapter 13 deck v2_2_0 (register v0.531.0, story ST_Deck13_Ex12 Done) ran the deck check v1_1_0 (sen0401_deck_check_v1_1_0.py, under Python 3.14.6 as it requires) on the deck v2_2_0 and on the deck v2_1_0: both print REFUSED ('chart ppt/charts/chart2.xml', 'has no data labels'), the chart of slide 21 (example 10); the same check run on the newest decks of chapters 12 and 14 prints 0 mismatches. The defect is therefore in the chapter 13 deck, older than the work of the executor, and byte-identical in v2_2_0 (found by the executor of ST_Deck13_Ex12 and confirmed by the control). SECOND GAP, found by the control in the text diff: the body text of slide 24 still says that the wrong passphrase gives the cut text The wallet passphrase entered wa, while the code of example 12 now prints the whole message The wallet passphrase entered was incorrect. (the slide must say what its code prints). BELONGS TO THE MISSION: the mission is teaching material of every chapter that meets the written standard (charts are native objects with explained values; what a slide says must be what its code prints); the deck check is the standard's executable form and passes the other chapters. FIT: the repair is a new deck v2_3_0 (and a manifest v1_2_0 that names it, code unchanged); no check is weakened, no owner decision is needed. ORDER: the not yet started page rebuild ST_Ch13_PageRebuild would otherwise be built from a deck that is replaced at once, so its items name the deck v2_3_0 and the manifest v1_2_0 and wait for the Verify task of the new story; the chapter 14 page is not affected. The page 9.81.0 is delivered and failing; nothing is waived. Gaps are said openly and are not waived; they are filled through change management in the active lineage. Pending until the ScopeChange of the revision that admits the story into Iteration 41." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .

