    backlog:notYetScoreable true ; backlog:hasScoreabilityReason "Ranked by its story's state; scoring both would double-count." ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Make the NEW deck file SEN0401_Ch13_BitcoinSecurity_3e_v2_3_0.pptx (in 03-materials/ch13) from the committed deck v2_2_0 (never edited; SHA-256 before and after) with TWO changes only: (1) the native chart ppt/charts/chart2.xml on slide 21 (example 10) carries data labels, as every chart of the standard does, so that the deck check v1_1_0 stops refusing it; the plotted values and the chart type stay as they are, and the five other charts keep their labels; (2) the body text of slide 24 says what the code of example 12 prints: the wrong passphrase gives The wallet passphrase entered was incorrect. (the whole message, not a cut). No other slide, example, link, note or picture changes. New files: the deck plan v2_3_0, the deck builder files that must change (new version numbers), the example files your builder needs, and the deck file. Also make the NEW chapter-code manifest 03-materials/ch13/page/chapter_code_ch13_v1_2_0.json from v1_1_0 (never edited) with ONLY the fields manifest, deck and deck_version changed to name the new files (chapter_code_ch13_v1_2_0, the deck v2_3_0, 2.3.0); every example, code, expected output and the setup stay byte-identical in content. PROOF kept as logs written into the repository (not /tmp), each written once after its run is complete: SHA-256 of deck v2_2_0 and manifest v1_1_0 before and after; the diff of the extracted slide text and notes of v2_2_0 against v2_3_0 (only slide 24, only that sentence) and the list of differing package parts (only the chart part, slide 21 and 24 parts, the properties part); the deck check v1_1_0 under Python 3.14.6 on v2_3_0: 28 examples, 0 mismatches, exit 0 (the check is NOT edited or weakened); the run of all 28 examples of the manifest v1_2_0 on the stored results (28 of 28, every output equal to its expected output, none with Error: in its first 160 characters); the deck standard check v1_1_0, the overlap check, the arc check, the chapter check Deck/Ch13 and the manifest check; the count of the deck's hyperlinks (14 distinct addresses, all kept); the manifest differs from v1_1_0 only in the three fields; nochange (the commit only adds files). DO NOT EDIT OR APPEND TO ANY FILE COMMITTED EARLIER, INCLUDING YOUR OWN LOG FILES, AND DO NOT EDIT THE PAGE TESTS, THE CHECKS OR THEIR THRESHOLDS. A committed file is never edited: every output is a new file with a new version number. STOP and report if the task cannot be satisfied without editing a committed file, a gate, a test or a threshold. Report every result as printed (PASS, FAIL, NOT_MEASURED, CANNOT_RUN); a skip is not a pass. The machine has 2 cores and little disk: remove only the temporary folders your own runs created and name them in your report. Commit your work to main (pull --rebase before push). Planned session SEN0401-I41-deck13charts; estimated start S (S = the start of the iteration, planned and not yet held), about 2.0 hours (an estimate, G120: nobody has witnessed a start; the real start is recorded at work begun)." .

