ex:CR3_Ch13Links a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "The chapter 13 research states no relationship between two sections, so the ERD label features of the page tests are skipped and the page cannot meet its criterion"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_Retro24 ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "MEASURED 2026-10-27: the executor of the chapter 13 page rebuild (session SEN0401-I40-page-ch13b, commits f8983f3, 7df32bc, 67ac57a, 8400ee5, 2d44a5d, 8e2e77d) built the page 9.82.0 from the deck 2.3.0 and the manifest v1_2_0 and reported the page tests 9.37.0 (392 passed, 0 failed, widgets 84/84), 9.34.1 (368/0) and 9.35.1 (368/0); in its log the page test 9.37.0 prints two [SKIP] lines: 'the filled ERD reads: overlapping label pairs ...' and 'the on-choice labels mode shows only the chosen entity's labels', each with the reason 'the chapter's research states no relationship between two sections, so the ERD has no line and no label to measure (entities 16)'. The lineage agent's own run of 9.37.0 on the page 9.81.0 prints the same two lines. CAUSE, measured in the page data: the page data of the chapter 13 pages hold 78 relations, all 'is a kind of' inside sections, and 0 relations between two sections (research sen0401_ch13_research_v1_0_2.ttl); the page data of chapters 10 and 11 hold 'builds on', 'has consequence', 'is earlier than' and 'operates on' relations between sections after the stories ST_Section_Links (chapter 10) and the research versions v1_2_0 and v1_1_0, and their page tests print 0 skips. THE CRITERION AND THE OWNER'S DECISION: the criterion of the page (AC9_PageRebuild_Ch13, element 2) says 'no FAIL, no skip', and a skip is not a pass. The owner decided on 2026-10-22 (option b of the change request ex:CR3_PageErd, widened) that the relationships between the sections of a chapter are discovered with the OEE relationship taxonomy and STATED IN THE CHAPTER RESEARCH AS LINKS, never as text; chapters 10 and 11 were done on that decision, chapter 13 was not covered by it when its research was written. The page cannot meet its criterion until the research of chapter 13 states how its 16 sections relate. RULING (standing): the page tests are gates and stay unchanged; the research is repaired as a NEW version; the page is rebuilt on it as the next page version. The page 9.82.0 is delivered; nothing is waived. Gaps are said openly and are not waived; they are filled through change management in the active lineage. Pending until the ScopeChange of the revision that admits the story into Iteration 42." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Pending .

ex:IA3_Ch13Links a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What the chapter 13 research section links and the chapter 13 page rebuild on them costs and what it touches"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR3_Ch13Links ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "MEASURED 2026-10-27: the executor of the chapter 13 page rebuild (session SEN0401-I40-page-ch13b, commits f8983f3, 7df32bc, 67ac57a, 8400ee5, 2d44a5d, 8e2e77d) built the page 9.82.0 from the deck 2.3.0 and the manifest v1_2_0 and reported the page tests 9.37.0 (392 passed, 0 failed, widgets 84/84), 9.34.1 (368/0) and 9.35.1 (368/0); in its log the page test 9.37.0 prints two [SKIP] lines: 'the filled ERD reads: overlapping label pairs ...' and 'the on-choice labels mode shows only the chosen entity's labels', each with the reason 'the chapter's research states no relationship between two sections, so the ERD has no line and no label to measure (entities 16)'. The lineage agent's own run of 9.37.0 on the page 9.81.0 prints the same two lines. CAUSE, measured in the page data: the page data of the chapter 13 pages hold 78 relations, all 'is a kind of' inside sections, and 0 relations between two sections (research sen0401_ch13_research_v1_0_2.ttl); the page data of chapters 10 and 11 hold 'builds on', 'has consequence', 'is earlier than' and 'operates on' relations between sections after the stories ST_Section_Links (chapter 10) and the research versions v1_2_0 and v1_1_0, and their page tests print 0 skips. THE CRITERION AND THE OWNER'S DECISION: the criterion of the page (AC9_PageRebuild_Ch13, element 2) says 'no FAIL, no skip', and a skip is not a pass. The owner decided on 2026-10-22 (option b of the change request ex:CR3_PageErd, widened) that the relationships between the sections of a chapter are discovered with the OEE relationship taxonomy and STATED IN THE CHAPTER RESEARCH AS LINKS, never as text; chapters 10 and 11 were done on that decision, chapter 13 was not covered by it when its research was written. The page cannot meet its criterion until the research of chapter 13 states how its 16 sections relate. RULING (standing): the page tests are gates and stay unchanged; the research is repaired as a NEW version; the page is rebuilt on it as the next page version. The page 9.82.0 is delivered; nothing is waived. AFFECTED: a new chapter 13 research version, a new chapter 13 page 9.83.0; the deck v2_3_0 and the manifest v1_2_0 are NOT affected (STOP if they would have to change); the chapter 14 page is NOT affected. NOT AFFECTED: the controlled criteria of the decks (they stay met), the delivered deck, the old plans, every committed file. ESTIMATE (G120): 2.0 h plus 1.0 h verification." .

